2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE I only know what I posted from Ilene. 
2 NOTE Do you know who is who in this photo?
2 NOTE From Ilene Kanfer Murray:
3 CONT This is the only photo I have of Hymie Rose. The family story was that he returned to Poritsk before WWII to visit cousins and this was taken before he came home. I have found him on a manifest back to the U.S. in September 1936, 
3 CONC so I assume it was for this trip. The only people I can positively identify are the young man in the far left, who is Yosef Plach, brother to my grandmother, Reitse Plach Kanfer, and the old woman next to Hymie, who is Reitse and 
3 CONC Yosef's mother, Chaya Leah Plitt Plach Greidinger, my great-grandmother. I don't think any of them survived the Holocaust.
