1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert COLIERE
2 CONT
2 CONT *     * Father: James COLIERE
2 CONT *     * Mother: Isabella LEVESON
2 CONT *     * Birth: 1515,
2 CONT *     * Death: before July 12, 1586 
2 CONT *    * Partnership with: Joyce SCRIMSHIRE     Marriage: 1536, Darlaston,England
2 CONT *         o Child: Thurston COLLYER Birth: 1542, Darlaston,England
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors of Robert COLIERE
2 CONT
2 CONT                   /-Robert COLIERE
2 CONT         /-James COLIERE
2 CONT         |         |         /-John DODDINGTON
2 CONT         |         \-Isabella DODDINGTON
2 CONT         |                   \-Elizabeth HUSSEY Robert COLIERE
2 CONT         \-Isabella LEVESON
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Robert COLIERE
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Robert COLIERE
2 CONT *   =Joyce SCRIMSHIRE  Marriage: 1536, Darlaston,England
2 CONT *       2 Thurston COLLYER
2 CONT *         =Elizabeth TUNSTALL  Marriage: 1563
2 CONT *             3 Robert COLLYER
2 CONT *               =Mary Margery STRANGE  Marriage: 14 Mar 1587, London,England
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT (son of James Coleire) of Darlaston was born c. 1515 and died c 1587. Heir of Darlaston, Yarlett, Stone and Antelope. Robert purchased Hilderston Manor (100 houses) from Edmund Ld. Sheffield. Licence granted in 1549 to Robe
2 CONC rt Collyer of Darlaston (Lord of the manor of Stone) for a market in the town of Stone. A Coat of Arms was conceded to Robert Collyer of Darlaston by letter patent dated 1558 - 1st Elizabeth from William Henry Clariencienex, King 
2 CONC at Arms. Married first wife in 1536, Joyce, daughter of Scrimshire of Norbury. Second wife, March 1, 1553, Agnes, daughter of Sir Thomas Venables of Kinderton and Chester County
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT (son of James Coleire) of Darlaston was born c. 1515 and died c 1587.  Heir of Darlaston, Yarlett, Stone and Antelope.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert purchased Hilderston Manor (100 houses) from Edmund Ld. Sheffield.  Licence granted in 1549 to Robert Collyer of Darlaston (Lord of the manor of Stone) for a market in the town of Stone. A Coat of Arms was conceded to Rober
2 CONC t Collyer of Darlaston by letter patent dated 1558 - 1st Elizabeth from William Henry Clariencienex, King at Arms. Married first wife in 1536, Joyce, daughter of Scrimshire of Norbury.  Second wife, March 1, 1553, Agnes, daughter 
2 CONC of Sir Thomas Venables of Kinderton and Chester County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue :
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b 1554;
2 CONT # James, 1538-1597; 
2 CONT # Richard;
2 CONT # Robert;
2 CONT # Margaret; 
2 CONT # Letitia (Lettice); 
2 CONT # Isabel (Isabella); 
2 CONT # Mary; 
2 CONT # Gratia; 
2 CONT # Cecily (Cecelia); 
2 CONT # Agnes (Anne); 
2 CONT # Christopher, b 1558; 
2 CONT # Thurston
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT (son of James Coleire) of Darlaston was born c. 1515 and died c 1587. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Heir of Darlaston, Yarlett, Stone and Antelope. 
2 CONT Robert purchased Hilderston Manor (100 houses) from Edmund Ld. Sheffield. 
2 CONT Licence granted in 1549 to Robert Collyer of Darlaston (Lord of the manor of Stone) for a market in the town of Stone. A Coat of Arms was conceded to Robert Collyer of Darlaston by letter patent dated 1558 - 1st Elizabeth from Wil
2 CONC liam Henry Clariencienex, King at Arms. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married first wife in 1536, Joyce, daughter of Scrimshire of Norbury. Second wife, March 1, 1553, Agnes, daughter of Sir Thomas Venables of Kinderton and Chester County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family with 1st wife Joyce Skrymsher m.1536:
2 CONT 1. Margaret Collier
2 CONT 2. James Collier b. 1538, d. c 1597
2 CONT 3. Letitia Collier b. c 1540
2 CONT 4. Thurston Collier b. c 1542
2 CONT 5. Richard Collier b. c 1544
2 CONT 6. Isabel Collier b. c 1546
2 CONT 7. Mary Collier b. c 1548
2 CONT 8. Grace Collier b. c 1550
2 CONT 9. Elizabeth Collier b. c 1550, d. 14 Oct 1594
2 CONT 10. Cecilia Collier b. c 1552
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family with 2nd wife Agnes Venables m.1553
2 CONT 1. Margery Collier b. c 1552
2 CONT 2. Elizabeth Collier b. c 1554, d. 1594
2 CONT 3. Mary Collier b. c 1556
2 CONT 4. Christopher Collier b. c 1558
2 CONT 5. Leticia Collier b. c 1563
2 CONT 6. Richard Collier b. c 1567
2 CONT 7. Thurston Collier b. c 1569
2 CONT 8. Agnes Collier b. c 1574
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 3
2 CONT 3.	SIR ROBERT COLIERE (COLLYER), was born about 1515 in Stone, Staffordshire, England, and died about 1587 in Stone, Staffordshire, England.  He was the son of James Colie're, 1490-1544 and Isabella Leveson, 1494-1544, and as thei
2 CONC r first-born son, became heir and Lord of the Manors Darlaston, Yarlet and Antelope.
2 CONT 	  Records show that a license was granted in 1549 to "Robert Collyer of Darlaston", (Lord of the Manor of Stone) for a market in the town of Stone. 
2 CONT 	 In 1558 a Peerage and Coat of Arms was conceded to "Robert Collyer of Darlaston" by letter patent - Queen Elizabeth I from William Henry Clariencienex, King of Arms.
2 CONT 	Robert married (1.) Joyce Scrimshire in 1536 in Darlaston, Staffordshire, England.  Joyce was born about 1514 in Stone, Staffordshire, England, and died before 1553 at Darlaston Manor, Staffordshire, England, the daughter of Thom
2 CONC as Scrimshire and Mary Swinehead.  After her death, he married (2.) Agnes Venables on 1 March, 1553.  Agnes was born about 1533 in Kinderton, Cheshire, England, and died about 1586 at Darlaston Manor, Stone, Staffordshire, England
2 CONC , the daughter of Sir Thomas Venables and Maud Needham.  Between the two wives, Robert was the father of thirteen children.  Little information was found about their children and many of the birth dates are estimated, taking into 
2 CONC consideration the birth dates of other children that are known, the marriage dates of the two wives, and birth and death dates of Robert, Joyce and Agnes.
2 CONT 	 The spelling of the surnamein the next generation  is most commonly spelled "Collyer" or "Colyer", although "Colie're" and "Coliere" are still seen, even when identifying siblings who may spell their names differently.  Since Co
2 CONC llyer was most commonly used in the 4th generation, or at least the following children were transitioning toward that spelling, I am using it for all the siblings.  If any reader would like to do their own research, however, I wou
2 CONC ld still suggest using all the variations of the name since some, even in the case of Robert Coliere of this generation, were identified with both spellings of the surname.
2 CONT [https://abahaiglossary.org/TNG/img/FTM%20MEDIA/Collier%20Family%20History-%2012%20Generations.docx
2 CONT Source
2 CONT abahaiglossary.org was first indexed by Google in November 2016]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Sir Robert Collier
2 CONT AKA COLLYER
