1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name show as "Thomas" in at least one source.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT A William Carpenter married at St. Thomas the Martyr, Salisbury, Wiltshire, 18 April 1605, Mary Bath (not Batt, as per various informal sources) (WiltPaR 5:22). Christopher Batt, a tanner of [New] Sarum (i.e., Salisbury), Wiltshir
2 CONC e, was one of the Carpenters' fellow passengers on the Bevis. Records of the Batt family of Salisbury, however, indicate that he and a Mary Batt of appropriate age (baptized at St. Thomas 7 Aug. 1584, daughter of Richard and Agnes
2 CONC  (Danyell) Batt) "would be no more than distant cousins" (NEHGR 14:336; Martin, citing NEHGR 51:181– 88, 348– 57, 52:44– 51, 321– 22). It has not been established that William1 Carpenter was the man of that name who married Mary B
2 CONC ath.
