2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT *'''Thomas Venables, Esq.
2 CONT *'''M, #69841, b. 1544, d. 8 December 1606
2 CONT *Father      Thomas Venables b. c 1514, d. Jun 1580
2 CONT *Mother     Matilda Needham b. c 1515
2 CONT *'''     Thomas Venables, Esq. was born in 1544 at of Kinderton, Cheshire, England. He married Ann Gargrave, daughter of Sir Cotton Gargrave, Sheriff of Yorkshire, Burgess of Boroughbridge and Anne (Agnes) Waterton, on 15 July 159
2 CONC 9. Thomas Venables, Esq. died on 8 December 1606 at Kinderton, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT *'''Family      Ann Gargrave b. c 1573
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Peter Venables b. c 1603, d. 1669
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2324.htm#i69841 _____________________
2 CONT *VENABLES, Sir Thomas (by 1513-80), of Kinderton, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. by 1513, 1st s. of Sir William Venables by Eleanor, da. and coh. of Richard Cotton of Ridware, Staffs. m. Maud, da. of Sir Robert Needham of Shavington, Salop, 3s. 3da. suc. fa. 31 July 1540. Kntd. 11 May 1544.1
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Venables died on 19 duly 1580. '''His eldest son Thomas, who was 38 when he succeeded to the estates, married as his first wife a daughter of Sir William Brereton I,''' and his second son, Anthony, also married into the family. A
2 CONC  daughter married another Cheshire gentleman, Peter, son and heir of Sir Piers Legh of Lyme.3
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/venables-sir-thomas-1513-80 __________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire (1978)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.74
2 CONT **	BRERETON--BARON BRERETON.
2 CONT *    .... etc.
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, Knt., of Brereton, who m. Jane,
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n95/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.75
2 CONT *eldest dau. of Sir Peter Warburton, by Elizabeth Wynynton, his wife, and by her (who m. 2ndly, Sir Lawrence Smith, of Hough), had issue.
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM (SIR), his heir.
2 CONT **	I. Mary.
2 CONT **'''	II. Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Venables, Esq., of Kenderton, and d. June, 1591.
2 CONT **	III. Jane, m. to John Legh, Esq., of Boothes.
2 CONT **	IV. Anne, m. to Sir Thomas Smith, Mayor of Chester, 1596, sheriff of the county in 1600.
2 CONT **	V. Susanna.
2 CONT *Sir William, who was buried at Brereton, 4 September, 1559, was s. by his son, .... etc. ______________________________
2 CONT *	Brackley, Viscount (E, 1616 - 1829)
2 CONT *	1. Sir Thomas Egerton (dspm. and vp. Aug 1599 ; bur. at Doddleston, co. Chester), mar. Elizabeth Venables, '''1st dau. of Thomas Venables, of Kinderton, co. Chester, by his first wife Elizabeth Brereton, sister of William [Brere
2 CONC ton], 1st Baron Brereton, and 1st dau. of Sir William Brereton, of Brereton, co. Chester''', and had issue:
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/brackley1616.htm?zoom_highlight=brereton - SEARCH - BRERETON ______________________________
2 CONT *'''The history of the county palatine and city of Chester: .... Vol. III.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyp03orme
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyp03orme#page/51/mode/1up
2 CONT **	BRERETON AND HOLT OF BRERETON. Pg.51-52
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, kt. buried at Brereton Sept. 4, 1559. = JANE, eldest daughter of sir Peter Warburton, by his wife Elizabeth Wynynton, remarried to sir Lawrence Smith of Hough, at Brereton Jan. 20, 1560-1.; ch: 
2 CONC (Pg.52 MARY, '''ELIZABETH (m. Thomas Venables)''', JANE (m. John Legh), ANNE (m. sir Thomas Smith), SUSANNA, Sir WILLIAM (m. MARGARET Savage) BRERETON.
2 CONT **https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyp03orme#page/52/mode/1up
2 CONT **MARY, bapt. Dec. 4, 1552, at Brereton.
2 CONT **'''ELIZABETH, wife of Thomas Venables, of Kinderton, esq. died June 1591, buried at Middlewich.'''
2 CONT **JANE, .... etc. ___________________________
2 CONT *EGERTON, Thomas II (1574-99), of Dodleston, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. 1574, 1st s. of (Sir) Thomas Egerton I by his 1st w. educ. L. Inn 1588; Brasenose, Oxf. 1589, BA 1592. m. by 1591, Elizabeth, da. of '''Thomas Venables of Kinderton''', 3da. Kntd. 1597.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/egerton-thomas-ii-1574-99 ____________________
2 CONT *Peter Venables (22 April 1604 – 13 February 1669 ) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1640 and 1669. He supported the Royalist cause in the English Civil War. [1]
2 CONT *Venables was the son of '''Thomas Venables, baron of Kinderton, and his wife Anne Gargreave''', daughter of Sir Cotton Gargreave of Nostoll, Yorkshire. He was High Sheriff of Cheshire in 1634.[2]
2 CONT *In November 1640, Venables was elected Member of Parliament for Cheshire in the Long Parliament.[3] He supported the King in the Civil War and was disabled from sitting on 22 January 1644.
2 CONT *In 1661, Venables was elected MP for Cheshire in the Cavalier Parliament and held the seat until his death.[4]
2 CONT *Venables died at the age of 64.
2 CONT *Venables married firstly Mary Wilbraham, daughter of Sir Richard Wilbraham of Woodhey and secondly Frances Cholmondeley sister of Sir Robert Cholmondeley.[2]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Venables_(MP) ______________________
2 CONT *VENABLES, Peter (1604-69), of Kinderton, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. 22 Apr. 1604, '''3rd but o. surv. s. of Thomas Venables of Kinderton, being 1st s. by 2nd w. Anne, da. of Sir cotton Cotton Gargrave''' of Nostell, Yorks. educ. L. Inn 1620. m. (1) c.1622, Mary, da. of Sir Richard Wilbraham, 1
2 CONC st Bt., of Woodhey, Cheshire, 1s. d.v.p.; (2) settlement 11 Sept. 1628, Frances, da. of Sir Hugh Cholmondeley of Cholmondeley, Cheshire, 4s. (2 d.v.p.) 2da. suc. fa. 1605.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/venables-peter-1604-69 __________________________
