1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Family and Education '''b. c.1560, 1st s. of Robert Colyer of Darlaston by his 2nd w. Agnes, da. of Sir Thomas Venables of Kinderton, Cheshire. m. 1586, Jane, da. of Robert Needham of Shenton, Notts., 1s. suc. fa. 1586.'''1
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT Freeman, Newcastle-under-Lyme 1586.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography The Colyer family, established in the vicinity of Stone, Staffordshire, during the reign of Henry VII, did well out of the dissolution of the monasteries. Inheriting the manors of Darlaston, Stone, Yerlett and Hilderston
2 CONC e with about 6,500 acres of land, Colyer at once began to sell out. In his first year he disposed of 100 houses and 1,000 acres of land for £480. Each year more went until, by his death, he had nothing left save a house in Stone c
2 CONC alled Newhall and three small properties. Over a period of ten years he realised £2,200. His reasons are unknown.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He was returned at Newcastle-under-Lyme through the influence of the mayor Ralph Smythe, who had married Colyer’s sister Margaret. The Robert Colyer then on the town council was presumably a relative. '''Colyer died intestate 14 J
2 CONC uly 1597, leaving a nine year-old son'''.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1558-1603 Author: R.C.G. Notes 1. C142/215/253; J. C. Wedgwood, Staffs. Parl. Hist. (Wm. Salt Arch. Soc.), i. 385. 2. Erdeswick’s Surv. Staffs. 33-5, 38, 50, 509; C142/215/253; Colls. Hist. Staffs. (Wm. Salt Arch. Soc
2 CONC . xiii), 259; (xv), 170, 171, 172, 181, 182, 191, 192; (xvi), 102, 103, 132, 146, 156, 163; Wards 7/24/184. 3. T. Pape, Newcastle-under-Lyme, 16, 46, 206; Wards 7/24/184     
2 CONT
2 CONT James siblings : -
2 CONT
2 CONT        1. 	Margaret Collier
2 CONT   	2. 	James Collier b. 1538, d. c 1597
2 CONT   	3. 	Letitia Collier b. c 1540
2 CONT   	4. 	Thurston Collier b. c 1542
2 CONT   	5. 	Richard Collier b. c 1544
2 CONT   	6. 	Isabel Collier b. c 1546
2 CONT   	7. 	Mary Collier b. c 1548
2 CONT   	8. 	Grace Collier b. c 1550
2 CONT   	9. 	Elizabeth Collier b. c 1550, d. 14 Oct 1594
2 CONT   	10. 	Cecilia Collier b. c 1552
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of Robert Collier 1515-1587 and Joyce Skrymsher 1516-1553 Marriage 1563 - Jane Needham
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT JAMES4 COLLYER (SIR ROBERT3 COLEIRE, JAMES2 COLIE'RE, ROBERT1) was born Abt. 1538 in London, England. He married JANE NEEDHAM. She was born 1542 in Shavington, Shropshire, England.
