1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sarah Pidge (Paige) Metcalf
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	1637  Roxbury, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT *'''Death: 	1677  Dedham, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT *'''Sarah Pidge (Paige), daughter of''' Thomas Pidge (Paige) and Mary Sothy, '''was probably born in Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts about 1637. On September 12, 1655, she married Thomas Metcalf in Dedham, Massachusetts. Thomas wa
2 CONC s 25 years old and Sarah was 17 or 18 when they were married. Thomas and Sarah had at least eight children, all born in Dedham. Sarah died in Dedham before 1679, possibly at the birth of her last child, a daughter born in 1677. Th
2 CONC ere is no reason to believe that Sarah was buried anywhere other than the Old Village Cemetery in Dedham.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT *''' Spouse:
2 CONT *'''  Thomas Metcalf (1629 - 1702)
2 CONT *''' Children:
2 CONT **  Mary Metcalf Fisher (1660 - 1727)*
2 CONT *'''Burial:  Old Village Cemetery, Dedham, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 160122609
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=160122609 __________________
2 CONT *'''A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England: Showing Three Generations of ... Vol. III.     by James Savage, ....
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/agenealogicaldi03dextgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicaldi03dextgoog#page/n212/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.202
2 CONT *   METCALF, frequently MEDCALF in early rec. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicaldi03dextgoog#page/n213/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.203
2 CONT * .... MICHAEL, Dedham, b. 1586, at Tatterford, in Co. Norfolk, was a dornock weaver at Norwich, and free of the city, where all his ch. were b. m. 13 Oct. 1616, Sarah, had Michael, b. 13 Nov. 1617, d. soon; Mary, 14 Oct. 1618, bu
2 CONC t the geneal. of the fam. in Reg. VI. 173, says 14 Feb. 1619 ; Michael, again, 29 Aug. 1620 ; John, 5 or 15 Sept. 1622, bef. ment ; Sarah, 10 Sept. 1624; Eliz. 4 Oct 1626; Martha, 27 Mar. or Oct. 1628; '''Thomas, 27 Dec 1629 or 30
2 CONC '''; Ann, 1 Mar. 1631 or 34, d. soon; Jane, 24 Mar. 1632; and Rebecca, 5 Apr. 1635; his w. was b. at a village near Norwich, he says, 17 June 1593, but possib. the figures have been mistaken, as in the examin. one week bef. the sa
2 CONC il, of the ship, call. I think, the Rose, of Yarmouth, from Yarmouth, Apr. 1637, he calls hims. 45 yrs. of age, and w. 39. "From the relig. tyranny" exercised by Wren, then Bp. of .Norwich, he felt forced to esc. even at the expen
2 CONC se of separ. from his fam. for a time, and emb. at London, 17 Sept. 1636, for N. E. but was sadly tormented by equal tempests on the water, and the ship at Christmas put back to Plymouth ; and so far was this a happiness that in A
2 CONC pr. foll, he had license for the whole fam. to come ; only 8 ch. are ment. in the custom-ho. docum. but I can hardly doubt that the name of John was casually overlook. At Boston he arr. "three days bef. mid. sum. with w. nine ch. 
2 CONC and a serv." wh. was Thomas Comberbach, aged 16, 1 presume in one of the three ships ment. by Winth. as coming in, from Ipswich, 20 June. He may have been br. of Joseph ; was freem. 13 May 1640, or 18 May 1642, and, perhaps, swore
2 CONC  on both days, tho. more prob. it is a fault of the Secr, as in the list appears. His w. d. 21 Feb. 1645, and he m. 13 Aug. foll. Martha, wid. of Thomas Pigg, or Pidge ; and he d. 27 Dec. 1664. A very, curious docum. his engagem. 
2 CONC aft. 70 yrs. of age to keep the town sch. in 1656, is giv. in Geneal. Reg. X. 282. His will, made six wks. bef. gives to eight ch. Michael being d. and ea. of the ds. m. Martha hav. then a sec. or third h. to gr.ch. Michael, s. of
2 CONC  Michael, and gr.ch. William Brignall, s. of d. Martha, wh. was a mem. of Roxbury ch. by her first h. and to Martha Bullard, d. of his w. Mary m. 24 Nov. 1642, Henry Wilson ; Sarah m. Robert Onion, as his sec. w. the first hav. d.
2 CONC  in Apr. 1643; Eliz. m. 15 Sept. 1648, Thomas Bancroft of Reading; Martha m. William Brignall, next, 2 Aug. 1654, Christopher Smith as the Geneal. Reg. VI. 173, says, tho. I doubt its correctness, for Christopher Smith in  668, is
2 CONC  nam. in his will by Jonathan Fairbanks as h. of his d. Mary, and third h . . . . .  Stow; Jane m. 1654, Samuel Walker, 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicaldi03dextgoog#page/n214/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.204
2 CONT *(tho. strong doubts of error in the name are felt) of Rehoboth ; and Rebecca m. 5 Apr. 1659, John Mackintosh. ....  '''THOMAS, Dedham, youngest s.''' of the first Michael, b. in Eng. '''m. 12 Sept 1656, Sarah Paige, had''' Sarah,
2 CONC  b. 3 Mar. 1658 ; Mary, bapt. 25 Nov. 1660 ; Samuel, b. 17 Oct 1661, d. soon ; Thomas ; 22 Sept 1665, d. soon; Samuel, again, 17 Sept 1668; Thomas, again, 7 or 21 May 1671 ; John, 20 Sept 1675 ; and Judith, 25 Nov. 1677, d. at 5 y
2 CONC rs. '''The w. d. and he m.''' 2 Dec. 1679, Ann Paine of Rehoboth, was freem. 1653, deac. and rep. 1691, d. 16 Nov. 1702. Sarah m.23 Nov. 1676, Samuel Whiting, and d. 1702. .... THOMAS, Dedham, '''s. of the first Thomas''', m. 24 N
2 CONC ov. 1696, Sarah, d. of William Avery, the sec of the name, had Sarah, b. 26 Apr. 1698, d. in few wks. ; Samuel, 9 Apr. 1699, d. at 14 yrs. ; Thomas, 30 Dec 1701 ; and Sarah, 1 Dec 1703; and he d. 12 Dec. 1704; and his wid. m. 6 Ap
2 CONC r. 1709, Joseph Wight, and d. 1748. Two of this name had, in 1829, been gr. at Harv. and seven at the other N. E. coll. It is oft. in old rec writ as no doubt it was sound. Medcalf.  ___________________
2 CONT *'''Herbert Clarence Burleigh fonds - Family files series - Metcalfe (ii)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/hcbmetcalfe_0
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/hcbmetcalfe_0#page/8/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.4
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Michael Metcalf, son of Rev. Leonard Metcalf, Rector of Tatterford, was born at Tatterford, co. Norfolk, Eng., June 17, 1587. 
2 CONT *Sarah Ellwyn, daughter of Thomas and Elisabeth Ellwyn, was born at Hingham, co. Norfolk, Eng., June 17, 1593. 
2 CONT *They were married at Hingham Oct. 13, 1616. They sailed for New England April 15, 1637. 
2 CONT *Their children were:
2 CONT **	1. .... etc.
2 CONT **'''	8. Thomas, born Dec. 27, 1629; married 1st, Sept. 12, 1655, Sarah Page''', 2nd, Dec. 2, 1679, —— .
2 CONT **	9.  .... etc. ________________
