2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT *'''Sir Robert Needham, Sheriff of Shropshire & Cheshire1
2 CONT *'''M, b. circa 1476, d. 4 June 1556
2 CONT *Father     Sir William Needham b. c 1450
2 CONT *Mother     Isabel Bromley b. c 1455
2 CONT *'''     Sir Robert Needham, Sheriff of Shropshire & Cheshire was born circa 1476 at Shavington, Shropshire, England.  He married Agnes Manwaring, daughter of John Manwaring, Esq. and Maud Legh, circa 1500.  Sir Robert Needham, Sh
2 CONC eriff of Shropshire & Cheshire died on 4 June 1556 at Shropshire; Buried at Adderley, Shropshire.
2 CONT *'''Family      Agnes Manwaring b. c 1478, d. 2 May 1560
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Thomas Needham, Esq.+1 b. 1510
2 CONT **Matilda Needham+ b. c 1515
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 707.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2324.htm#i69847 ____________
2 CONT
2 CONT *Anne TALBOT
2 CONT *Born: 1515, Grafton, Worcestershire, England
2 CONT *Father: John TALBOT (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret TROUTBECK
2 CONT *Married: Thomas NEEDHAM of Shavington (Sir) (b. ABT 1510 - d. 1560) (son of '''Sir Robert Needham and Agnes Mainwaring''') ABT 1534, Shavington, Shropshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Robert NEEDHAM (Sheriff of Shropshire)
2 CONT **2. Thomas NEEDHAM
2 CONT **3. John NEEDHAM
2 CONT **4. Margaret NEEDHAM
2 CONT **5. Margery NEEDHAM
2 CONT **6. Agnes NEEDHAM (b. 1546 - d. Jan 1623)  (m. Sir Richard Bulkeley)
2 CONT **7. Jane NEEDHAM
2 CONT **8. Anne NEEDHAM
2 CONT **9. Dorothy NEEDHAM
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/TALBOT.htm#Anne TALBOT2 _______________
2 CONT *VENABLES, Sir Thomas (by 1513-80), of Kinderton, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. by 1513, 1st s. of Sir William Venables of Kinderton by Eleanor, da. and coh. of Richard Cotton of Ridware, Staffs. m. Maud, da. of '''Sir Robert Needham of Shavington, Salop''', 3s. 3da. suc. fa. 31 July 1540. Kntd. 11 May 15
2 CONC 44.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/venables-sir-thomas-1513-80 ________________
2 CONT *VENABLES, Sir Thomas (by 1513-80), of Kinderton, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. by 1513, 1st s. of Sir William Venables by Eleanor, da. and coh. of Richard Cotton of Ridware, Staffs. m. Maud, da. of '''Sir Robert Needham of Shavington, Salop''', 3s. 3da. suc. fa. 31 July 1540. Kntd. 11 May 1544.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/venables-sir-thomas-1513-80 ______________
2 CONT *'''The Visitation of Shropshire; v.29 (1889) Part II.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/TheVisitationOfShropshireV.29
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/TheVisitationOfShropshireV.29/VisitationshrophshireTaken1623_treswellVol.28P2#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.371
2 CONT **	Needham of Shavington. Pg.371-372
2 CONT *John Needham of Needham co. Derb. 4 E. 3. = ; ch: Tho. Needham
2 CONT **	Tho. Needham of Needham in com. Derb. = ; ch: Will'm (m. Alice Cranage), Thomas Needham.
2 CONT ***		Thomas Needham of Needham 47 E. 3. = ; descendants Vide Derby.
2 CONT ***		Will'm Needham 49 E. 3. = Alice da. & heir to . . . .  Cranage of Cranage in Chester. ; ch: Rob't Needham
2 CONT ****			Rob't Needham of Cranage ob. 8 H. 4. = ch: Robert (m. Dorothy Savage) Needham.
2 CONT *****				Robert Needham ob. 27 H. 6. = Dorothy da. to Sr Jo. Savage Kt of ye Garter. ; ch: Hugh, William, Sr John (m. Margery Mannering), Agnes (m. John Starkey), Robert, Thomas (m. Mawde Brereton) Needham.
2 CONT ******					Sr John Needham Justice of the King's Bench & Chester 2 sonn of Robert ob. 1480 [Judge of Common Pleas 1457; Judge of King's Bench 1472]. = Margery da. to Randall Mannering widow to Will'm Bromley of Cheverton [Shraward
2 CONC ine ?].
2 CONT ******					Thomas Needha' of Shenton in co. Salop. = Mawde da. to Sr Wm Brereton of Brereton Kt. ; ch: Sr Wm (m. Isabell Bromley) Needham.
2 CONT *******						Sr Wm Needham Knight. = Isabell da. & cohae. to Sr John Bromley Kt. (Sr John Bromley Knight maried Jane dau. & heire to Wm Hartall Hexstall.) ; ch: (Pg.372 Margrett (m. Tho. Whittington), '''Sr Robt (m. Agnes Manwarin
2 CONC g)''' Needham)
2 CONT ********https://archive.org/stream/TheVisitationOfShropshireV.29/VisitationshrophshireTaken1623_treswellVol.28P2#page/n95/mode/1up
2 CONT ********Pg.372
2 CONT ********							Margrett vx. Tho. Whittington of Pountley who had 6 da.s
2 CONT ********'''							Sr Robt Needham of Shenton Kt ob. 20 H. 7 [bought Shavington 1506; Sheriff 1529]. = Agnes da. to John or Jenkin Manwaring of Pever in [com.] Chest'r. ; ch:''' Maude (m. Tho. Venables), Jane Anne (m. Sr Andrew Cor
2 CONC bett), Tho. (m. Agnes Hope & Ann Talbott), John, Robert Needham.
2 CONT *********								Tho. Needham of Shenton ob. in vita patris. = Agnes da. to . . . .  Hope. ; ch: Agnes Needham; = Ann da. to Sr John Talbott of Grafton Kt. ; ch: Robert (m. Francis Aston), John, Margrett (m. Richard Steventon), Ma
2 CONC rgery Mary (m. Geo. Conney) Agnes (m. Sr Richard Bulkley & . . . .  Cranage), Joane, Anne Needham.
2 CONT **********									Robert Needha' of Shenton [Sheriff 1565]. = Francis da. to Sr Edward Aston of Tixall Kt. ; ch: Elizab., Mawde (m. Jo. Aston), Margery Mary (m. Thomas Onslow & Sr Rob't Vernon), Ann (m. Rob't Powell), Jane (m. Ja
2 CONC mes Collyer), Thomas (m. Mary (wid. of Sr Robert Salisbury) Bagenhall), Sr Rob't (m. Ann Doyley & Joane Lacye) Needham.
2 CONT ***********										Sr Rob't Needham of Shenton Kt Viscount Kilmory in Ireland 1624 [Sheriff 1607]. = Ann da. to . . . .  Doyley widow to . . . .  Willmott. ; = Joane da. to John Lacye of Borseton in com Som'sett. ; ch: Francess 
2 CONC (m. Sr Rowland Cotton), Robert (m. Francess Andersonne & Elianor (wid. to Gilbert [Lord] Gerrard) Dutton), Elianor (m. Sr Wm Owen) Needham.
2 CONT ************										Robert Needham. = Francess da. to Sr Henry Andersonne of London Kt. ; ch: Robert, Frances (m. Tho. Cotton), Elianor Needham; = Lady Elianor da. & heire to Jo. Dutton wid. to Gilbert Lo. [Lord] Gerard. ; ch: C
2 CONC harles (2 sonn.) Needham _________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Internet sources show both Margaret and Isabel as Robert's parents. 
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Sheriff of Shropshire in 1528, 1535, and 1540, and he was Sheriff of Cheshire in 1538.  purchased the Lordship of Shavington, Salop, 1506 see pic of Shavington Hall Shropshire The Shavington estate, which had been in the Ne
2 CONC edham family from the 15th century,  consisted of some 1,500 acres, with a circumference of seven miles. It remained in the  Needham family until near the end of the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Needham's Will, dated May 24th, 1556, and probated July 30th, 1557, mentioned: his wife, Agnes: his daughter, Maud Venables, her husband, Sir Thomas Venables, and their daughter, Katheryn Venables: his son-in-law, Sir Andre
2 CONC w Corbett: his cousin and heir, Robert Needham, his brother, John, and his sisters, Jane Needham, Margery Needham, and Dorothy Needham: his son's daughter, Annes Needham, the daughter of Anne Hope: and his cousin, Edward Mainwarin
2 CONC g of Whitmore. The executors were Sir Andrew Corbett and Edward Mainwaring. The Estate of Shavington remained in the family, indicating that the testator's "cousin and heir" was actually his grandson, Thomas Needham's oldest son. 
2 CONC Also, the Will mentioned that Sir Edward Aston owed the testator twelve score marks for the marriage of Robert Needham, the testator's cousin and heir, and it was the testator's grandson, Robert Needham, who, in fact, did marry Fr
2 CONC ances Aston, Sir Edward Aston's daughter - another indication that the heir of the testator was actually his grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIED at St Peters Adderly Shropshire "Here lieth buryed under this stone the bodes of Sir Robart Nedeham knight and Dame Agnes his wife daughter of John Maynwaring of Pever ... which sayd Robart deceased the iiii daye of June An
2 CONC no domim. 1556, and the sayd Agnes deceased the ii daye of maye Anno domim 1560"
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that a Brass in Adderley Church says that Robert died on June 4th, 1556, and that his wife, Agnes, daughter of John Mainwaring of Peover, died on May 2nd 1560. Below the inscription are the smaller effigies of seven sons and 
2 CONC two daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Needham, Sheriff of Shropshire & Cheshire was born circa 1476 at of Shavington, Shropshire, England.1 He married Agnes Manwaring, daughter of John Manwaring, Esq. and Maud Legh, circa 1500.2 Sir Robert Needham, Sheriff 
2 CONC of Shropshire & Cheshire died on 4 June 1556 at Shropshire, England; Buried at Adderley, Shropshire.
