2 CONT *'''Ann Gargrave
2 CONT *'''F, #69842, b. circa 1573
2 CONT *Father      Sir Cotton Gargrave, Sheriff of Yorkshire, Burgess of Boroughbridge b. c 1540, d. 16 Jun 1588
2 CONT *Mother     Anne (Agnes) Waterton b. c 1551, d. a 16 Jun 1588
2 CONT *'''     Ann Gargrave was born circa 1573 at of Norsell, Yorkshire, England. She married Thomas Venables, Esq., son of Thomas Venables and Matilda Needham, on 15 July 1599.
2 CONT *'''Family      Thomas Venables, Esq. b. 1544, d. 8 Dec 1606
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Peter Venables b. c 1603, d. 1669
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2324.htm#i69842 _____________________________
2 CONT *Peter Venables (22 April 1604 – 13 February 1669 ) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1640 and 1669. He supported the Royalist cause in the English Civil War. [1]
2 CONT *'''Venables was the son of Thomas Venables, baron of Kinderton, and his wife Anne Gargreave''', daughter of Sir Cotton Gargreave of Nostoll, Yorkshire. He was High Sheriff of Cheshire in 1634.[2]
2 CONT *In November 1640, Venables was elected Member of Parliament for Cheshire in the Long Parliament.[3] He supported the King in the Civil War and was disabled from sitting on 22 January 1644.
2 CONT *In 1661, Venables was elected MP for Cheshire in the Cavalier Parliament and held the seat until his death.[4]
2 CONT *Venables died at the age of 64.
2 CONT *Venables married firstly Mary Wilbraham, daughter of Sir Richard Wilbraham of Woodhey and secondly Frances Cholmondeley sister of Sir Robert Cholmondeley.[2]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Venables_(MP) ______________________
2 CONT *VENABLES, Peter (1604-69), of Kinderton, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. 22 Apr. 1604, 3rd but o. surv. s. of '''Thomas Venables of Kinderton, being 1st s. by 2nd w. Anne, da. of Sir cotton Cotton Gargrave''' of Nostell, Yorks. educ. L. Inn 1620. m. (1) c.1622, Mary, da. of Sir Richard Wilbraham, 1
2 CONC st Bt., of Woodhey, Cheshire, 1s. d.v.p.; (2) settlement 11 Sept. 1628, Frances, da. of Sir Hugh Cholmondeley of Cholmondeley, Cheshire, 4s. (2 d.v.p.) 2da. suc. fa. 1605.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/venables-peter-1604-69 __________________________
