1 NAME Sarah /Clare/
2 GIVN Sarah
2 SURN Clare
2 _MARNM Griffin
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1640
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1675
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Col. Samuel Griffin was a merchant, high sheriff and land owner in Rappahannock County, Virginia, served as a colonel in the Virginia militia in 1642, and went to Northumberland County, VA about 1683 where he was a
2 CONC  Justice and Burgess in Northumberland County, VA, and a lieutenant colonel in the county militia.  His will was written 1702 and probated 1703. His wife, Sarah, nee ------, perhaps a Miss Clare, who was the widow of Thomas Griffi
2 CONC n of Rappahannock County, VA who died ca. 1659. Ambrose Clare gave Katherine Griffin 1,155 acres in 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Quit Rents of Virginia, Land Grants, Northern Neck of Virginia,
2 CONT     rents paid to Fairfax and Culpeper:
2 CONT     Ann Bushrod, 1700, 1704, Northumberland 39 acres and 26 acres;
2 CONT     John Bushrod, 1709, Westmoreland, 88 acres;
2 CONT     Lewis Griffen, 1694, Stafford, 154 acres;
2 CONT     Thomas Griffen, 1707, Richmond, 3,471 acres;
2 CONT     James Rogers, 1707, Northumberland, 100 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT     1704 Virginia Rent Roll:
2 CONT     Abner Gray, Essex, 100 acres
2 CONT     James Gray, Accomack, 900
2 CONT     John Gray, Accomack, 116
2 CONT     John Gray, Surry, 200
2 CONT     Joseph Gray, King & Queen, 200
2 CONT     Samuell Gray, King & Queen, 40
2 CONT     Capt. William Gray, Surry, 1,750
2 CONT     William Gray, Jr., Surry, 1,050
2 CONT     William Gray, Surry, 100
2 CONT     Charles Griffen, Princess Anne, 216
2 CONT     David Griffen, King & Queen, 100
2 CONT     Edward Griffen, King & Queen, 100
2 CONT     James  Griffen, Nansemond, 500
2 CONT     James Griffen, Prince George, 100
2 CONT     John Griffen, Surry, 200
2 CONT     John Griffen, Accomack, 150
2 CONT     Thomas Griffen, Essex, 200
2 CONT     Thomas Griffin, Princess Anne, 200
2 CONT     William Keene, Nansemond, 200.
2 CONT
2 CONT     HYPERLINK: http://www.combs-families.org/combs/assoc/u-fauntly.htm
2 CONT     20 Feb 1683 - 22 Sep 1684 (Old Rappa. DB7:129-131) Samuel GRIFFIN of Co of Northumberland in Virga., Mercht. out of naturall love and affection unto Moore and Griffin FAUNTLEROY, sons of William FAUNTLEROY, of Co of Rappa. Gen
2 CONC t. give and confirme 6 young cowes…mark… to be equally divided & delivered as they shall come to lawfull age… and … dye before they come to age then I give the Cattle as aforesaid unto the next Child the said William FAUNTLEROY ma
2 CONC y have by Katharine his now Wife… S/Samuell GRIFFIN, Wit: Jno: PARKER. Receipted by Will: FAUNTLEROY [sic] 21 Jul 1683. Recog. 3 Sep 1684 & Rec. 23 Sep 1684. (Deed Abstracts of Old Rappahannock County, Virginia, 1682-1686, Deed Bo
2 CONC ok No. 7, Ruth and Sam Sparacio, Antient Press, McLean, Virginia, 1990)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Oct 2016 Edited from Smart Matches, My Heritage: maiden name 'Clare'. Virginia Hopper Oldham Go
