3 CITY Dorchester
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 FEB 1669
2 ADDR
3 CITY Medfield
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU Landowner & Herdsman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/KN42-D5P/nicholas-wood-1595-1669
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Wood 6 June 1595–7 February 1669
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth   •   1 Sources 6 June 1595 Colchester, Essex, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT
2 CONT Age 73 Death   •   7 Sources 7 February 1669 Sherborn, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Wood in entry for Jonathan Wood, "Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915"
2 CONT
2 CONT SPOUSES AND CHILDREN
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Wood 1595-1669
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 10 July 1639 Medfield, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pidge 1624-1663
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (9)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Wood 1642-1678
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Wood 1642-1726
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Wood 1648-1682
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Wood 1651-1675
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable Wood 1655-1681
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Wood 1657-1669
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Wood 1659-
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah Wood 1660-1731
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleazer Wood 1662-1704
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Summary ==
2 CONT *  Born say 1620
2 CONT * Arrived 1638 Braintree later moved to Dorchester, Medfield and Natick
2 CONT * His origins and parents are unknown
2 CONT * Married first Mary Pidge and second Hannah (Unknown) See below. No other wives
2 CONT * Eight Children (see below)
2 CONT * Detailed Will (transcript below)
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Nicholas Wood born say 1620 arrived in 1638 in Braintree later moved to Dorchester, Medfield and Natick [Great Migration Directory 383]. His origins and parents are unknown. He married first [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Wood/
2 CONC 6000000006727986060 Mary Pidge] (or Pigg) (1622-1662) daughter of Thomas Pidge of Roxbury and his wife Mary Sothy [Great Migration Begins: Thomas Pidge 1465. Mary Pidge had been misidentified by earlier authors as [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Mary-Wood/6000000007606552071 Mary Williams] which is wrong. The evidence is laid out in The American Genealogist 36:112, 36:117 and NEHGR 40:324 both available on AmericanAncestors.org. After Mary Pidge in 1662/3 die
2 CONC d Nicholas Wood married second to Hannah (Unknown) widow of William Page who had died in 1664. She is thought to have married third to Edward Winn. Note I can't find any evidence for Hannah's maiden name. See NEHGR 48:457 for the 
2 CONC will of Nicholas Wood and sources in Torrey 3:1710. He's also in Sherborn Hist.:261 and GMB 1465. But the best treatment I could find of him is in Waldo Chamberlain Sprague, Genealogies Of the Families of Braintree, Mass. 1640-185
2 CONC 0s page 1943 published by NEHGR in 2001 which includes all the previously published updates to this family: 
2 CONT == The two wives of Nicholas Wood ==
2 CONT NICHOLAS1 WOOD married by 1642 or earlier Mary Pidge, daughter of Thomas Pidge of Roxbury as shown by the church records there. She died Feb. 19, 1662/3 at now Sherborn (Medfield V.R.) and he died there Feb. 7, 1669/70 (Medfield V
2 CONC .R.).  His will dated Jan. 16, 1669 "at my farm in Natick bounds" was proved Apr. 2, 1670. It mentions wife Anna "my now loving wife" and his children Jonathan, Eleazer, under age, daughters Abigail, Bethiah, Mehitable, now in the
2 CONC ir minority, daughter Mary Thurston, grand child Abraham Harding son of daughter Hannah
2 CONT
2 CONT Harding deceased. Residue to six daughters and two sons, wife Anna. and John Thurston Jr. and Thomas Bass, both my sons in law, executors with friend George Barber of Medfield supervisor, and signed on 18th of 4th mo. 1669. (Regis
2 CONC ter 48-457).
2 CONT
2 CONT For the location of his homestead in Sherborn see History of Sherborn and Holliston by Rev. Abner Morse (1856).
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife Anna or Hannah was the widow of William Page of Watertown who died Dec. 9, 1664. On Nov. 16, 1665 widow Hannah Page made a marriage contract with Nicholas Wood of Boggestow with John Coolidge Sr. and Henry Bright a
2 CONC s trustees of her property. After his death these trustees or feoffee? of the widow Annah Wood had a law suit with John Thurston of Medfield executor of Nicholas Wood's estate (See Bond's History of Watertown, etc.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Did she m. 3rd Edward Winn of Woburn who d. 1682??? - F.A. Bates says so.
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT Children of Nicholas & Mary (Pidge) Wood, born 1st two at Roxbury, others recorded at Medfield: 
2 CONT # Mary, twin, bapt. Dec. 25, 1642 at Roxbury, m. Oct. 4, 1660 at Medfield, John Thurston Jr of Medfield. 
2 CONT # Sarah, twin, bapt. Dec. 25, 1642 at Roxbury, m. Oct. 4, 1660 at Medfield, Dea. Thomas Bass of Medfield & Braintree. 
2 CONT # Hannah, m. Nov. 28, 1665 at Watertown (Medfield VR) Dea. John Harding of Medfield & Braintree. 
2 CONT # Jonathan, Jan. 3, 1651/2. Killed by Indians Feb. 21, 1675/6 at Medfield or Sherborn, m. May 26, 1674 at Dorchester, Mary Daniel of Milton. 
2 CONT # Mehitable, Jul. 22, 1655, m. Oct. 17, 1671 at Medfield, Capt. Joseph Morse. 
2 CONT # Abigail, Sep. 13, 1657 
2 CONT # Bethiah, Jul. 28, 1660, m. Ephraim (Cutler?) Feb. 8, 1678/9. 
2 CONT # Eleazer, Mar. 14, 1661/2. He was scalped by the Indians at the time his brother was slain, recovered, but was afterwards depressed and strange, left a family. He died May 20, 1704 at Sherborn.  Roxbury Records (Boston Returns) s
2 CONC ay Mary ye daughtr of ____ Wood of Braintree borne 1642 25 -(10), Sarah ye daughtr of - of Braintree borne 25 (10) 1642 (Reg. 6:377-8). He married Dorothy (_____). Her maiden name is unknown and was not Babcock. Morse just made th
2 CONC at up. See NEHGR 40:104, 41:24, 41:32. and after he died Dorothy married second to Capt John Ware 1646-1718. Eleazer Wood and Dorothy had only two children Abigail and Hannah. Hannah married Joseph Ware son of John Ware above - he
2 CONC r step-brother. They had no daughter Dorothy as Morse assumed. The Dorothy who married John Ware was the widow of Eleazer Wood and not their daughter.
2 CONT == Will and Probate ==
2 CONT NEHGR. 48:457. 
2 CONT S. P. #521: Will of Nicholas Wood Jan. 16, 1669 (70) "living at my farm in Natick bounds", To wife Anna my now loving wife one third of real estate bought of Richard Parker and £17 a year till son Jonathan is 21 for the bringing u
2 CONC p of my two younger children. To son Jonathan all lands bought of Richard Parker, being the farm I now live on, and 4 acres of English pasture lying on the N. side of the brook that runneth by my house excepted. Also to son Jonath
2 CONC an 10 a. of meadow of the parcel bought of Lt. Fisher of Dedham, beginning at the S. line of the meadow next to John Hall's farm, also cattle, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Eleazer all lands bought of Lt. Fisher of Dedham except the 10 a. above mentioned joining to my other farm above said and the 4 acres excepted. To dau. Mehitable Wood all salt marsh in Milton except if it is over £60 in val
2 CONC ue the surplus to go to my executors. To dau. Abigail Wood lands and meadow at Roxbury and what it falls short of £60 to be made up by my executors. To dau. Bethya all houses & lands in Watertown which I had with my last wife at h
2 CONC er decease and all above £60 value to go to my executors. If son Jonathan die before age 21 and single Eleazer to be sole heir of his estate and to pay £10 to his sister Mary Thurston within one year and so annually till he have p
2 CONC aid to each of them £10. If son Eleazer die before age 21 Jonathan to be sole heir paying £6 apiece to all his sisters then living beginning with £6 to Mary Thurston within one year and so annually.
2 CONT
2 CONT If my three daughters now in their minority die before age, being single, then their portions to be divided equally among brothers and sisters. To grand child Abraham Harding son of my daughter Hannah Harding deceased £5 at age pa
2 CONC id by son Jonathan. Residue to six daughters and two sons when Jonathan is 21. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Anna & John Thurston Jr. & Thomas Bass both my sons in law executors & friend George Barbour of Medfield supervisor, signed 18th of 4th mo. 1669. Witnesses: Henry Layland, Hopestill Layland. Proved Jun. 2, 1670.
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT # Sprague, Waldo Chamberlain, Genealogies of the families of Braintree, Massachusetts, 1640-1850: including the modern towns of Randolph and Holbrook and the city of Quincy (Boston, Massachusetts: NEHGS, 2001) p 1943+
2 CONT # Fourth Report of the Record Commissioners of the City of Boston. 1880. Dorchester Town Records (Boston 1883) 1:38; 
2 CONT # John S. Fipphen and Richard C. Fipphen, Phippen Genealogy: Ancestors and Descendants of David Phippen (c. 1585-1650) of Melcombe Regis, Dorset, and Hingham and Boston, Massachusetts (Boston, MA: Newbury Street Press, 2017) [http
2 CONC s://shop.americanancestors.org/products/phippen-genealogy-ancestors-and-descendants-of-david-phippen-c-1585-1650-of-melcombe-regis-dorset-and-hingham-and-boston-massachusetts link]
2 CONT #  Records of the Governor and Company of the Massachusetts Bay in New England , 1628–1686, Nathaniel B. Shurtleff, ed., 5 volumes in 6 (Boston 1853–1854) 1:378; 
2 CONT # Suffolk County, Massachusetts, Probate Records Case #521; 
2 CONT # The New England Historical & Genealogical Register, Volume 1 through present (1847+) 40:324; [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?volumeId=11664&pageName=324&rId=24
2 CONC 1582119 link] 
2 CONT # The New England Historical & Genealogical Register, Volume 1 through present (1847+) 48:457 [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?pageName=457&volumeId=11582 link]
2 CONT # The American Genealogist 36:117; [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/american-genealogist-the/image/?pageName=112&volumeId=11877 link] See also 36:112
2 CONT # Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England, 1620-1633 , 3 volumes (Boston 1995) [https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/2496/42521_b158320-00153?pid=64135  1465 Thomas Pidge]
2 CONT # Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migration Directory p 383: Wood, Nicholas
2 CONT # Torrey 3:1710 WOOD, Nicholas1 (-1670) & 1/wf Mary PIGG/PIDGE/ WILLIAMS? (-1663), ?dau Thomas; by 1642; Roxbury/Braintree/ Dorchester/Medfield {Reg. 34:69, 40:324, 48:457; Stevens-Miller 2:23; Williams (,4) 12; Holman Ms: Pidge 2
2 CONC , 4; Wood 1; TAG 22:210, 36:112, 117; Lexington 154; Hill (#1)) 37; Paul Anc 137; TIngley-Meyers 248, 249; Savage}
