2 CONT Thomas Metcalf (1629 - 1702)
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon Thomas Metcalf aka Metcalfe
2 CONT Born 27 Dec 1629 in St. Edmonsbury, Norwich, Norfolk, Englandmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Michael Metcalf and Sarah (Ellwyn) Metcalf
2 CONT Brother of Michael Metcalf, Mary (Metcalf) Wilson, Michael Metcalf, John Metcalf, Sarah (Metcalf) Onion, Elizabeth (Metcalf) Bancroft, Martha (Metcalf) Stowe, Ann Metcalf, Jane (Metcalf) Polley, Joanne (Metcalf) Walker and Rebecca
2 CONC  (Metcalf) MacIntosh
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Pidge) Metcalf — married 12 Sep 1655 in Dedham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT Husband of Anne (Chickering) Metcalf — married 2 Dec 1679 in Rehoboth, Massachusettsmap
2 CONT Husband of Mehitable (Hand) Chapin — married about 22 Jan 1688 in Braintree, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Sarah (Metcalf) Whiting and Mary (Metcalf) Fisher
2 CONT Died 16 Nov 1702 at age 72 in Dedham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Richard Draper private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 28 Feb 2024 | Created 3 Apr 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 1,467 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Metcalf immigrated to New England as a child during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT Thomas Metcalfe, son of Micheal and Sara Metcalfe, was baptized on January 11, 1629/30 at St. Edmund, Norwich, Norfolk, England. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Metcalf was born December 27, 1629, to Michael and Sarah (Elwyn) Metcalf. [2] He was likely born in Hingham, Norfolk England where his parents were married.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 8, 1637, Micheal Metcalfe of Norwich, aged 45, his wife Sarah, aged 39, and their eight children, including Thomas, were enrolled as a passengers bound for Boston in New England, on the ship the "Rose". [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Metcalf married first Sarah Paige September 12, 1655 or 1656 at Dedham, Massachusetts.[2][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married second Ann (Chickering) Paine, December2, 1679 at Rehoboth/Dedham, Massachusetts. He married third Mehitable (Hand) Savil January 22, 1689 at Braintree, Massachusetts.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Thomas were:[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, born March 3, 1658
2 CONT Mary, baptized November 25, 1660
2 CONT Samuel, born October 17, 1661; died soon
2 CONT Thomas, September 22, 1665; died soon
2 CONT Samuel, September 17, 1668
2 CONT Thomas, May 7 or 21, 1671
2 CONT John, September 20, 1675
2 CONT Judith, November 25, 1677; died at 5 years
2 CONT Thomas Metcalf of Dedham wrote his will on April 14, 1702 and it was proved on November 30, 1702. In it he left bequests to: [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT my wife Mehitable
2 CONT my son in law Samuel Whiting
2 CONT Samuel Whiting, son of my eldest daughter Sarah
2 CONT Sarah's three son, Samuel, Jeremiah and Josiah Whiting
2 CONT daughter Mary Fisher
2 CONT daughter Mary Fisher's children as they come of age
2 CONT Mehitable Metcalf, daughter of my wife Mehitable
2 CONT son in law John Fisher
2 CONT son Thomas Metcalf, sole executor [7]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
