1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WIKITREE
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Newcomb-191 Elizabeth (Newcomb) Emery (1658 - abt. 1757)]
2 CONT Born 26 Aug 1658 in Braintree, Norfolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
2 CONT Died about 1757 [uncertain] at about age 98 in Berwick, York, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
2 CONT Elizabeth Emery formerly Newcomb aka Pidge 
2 CONT Daughter of Francis Newcomb and Rachel (Brackett) Newcomb 
2 CONT Sister of Rachel (Newcome) Adams, John Newcomb, Hannah (Newcomb) Thorp, Mary (Newcomb) Spear, Sarah Newcomb, Judith (Newcomb) Jennison, Peter Newcomb, Abigail Newcomb and Leah (Newcomb) Price 
2 CONT Wife of John Pidge — married 1677 in Dedham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony map icon at age 18
2 CONT Wife of James Emery — married 28 Dec 1695 in Dedham, Norfolk, Province of Massachusetts Bay   at age 37
2 CONT Mother of Jonathan Pidge , Elizabeth Pidge , Josiah Pidge , Hannah (Pidge) Tingley and Rachel (Pidge) Freeman
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Elizabeth Newcomb, daughter of Francis and Rachel (Brackett) Newcomb was born at Braintree, MA on Aug. 26, 1658. [1] (p. 244) [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married first at Dedham, MA on May [3] or July 3, 1677, John Pidge, [2] son of Thomas and Mary/Mercy (Sothy) Pidge, as his second wife. John was born about 1640, near Roxbury, MA. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT John died at Dedham in May, 1691, and administration of his estate was given to his widow Elizabeth on May 12. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT A division of his estate was made June 10, 1701. Named in the division were his widow Elizabeth, daughter Mary Kenney by his first wife, and children Jonathan, Josiah, Elizabeth, Hannah, and Rachel. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT The above division was presented to the court on June 14, 1709, by James Emery, Elizabeth's second husband.[Suffolk Probate: 17:55] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT After John's death she married second at Dedham, James Emery on Dec. 28, 1695, as his ?second wife. [3] [2] James was baptized at Romsey, Hampshire on Sept. 18, 1631, son of Anthony and Frances (___) Emery. James was of Kittery, Y
2 CONC ork, ME, where he held land that he received from his father. [5] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (the widow of John Emery and Executrix of John Emery Jr's estate) is noted in York Deed Record, Folio 272, in Book XII 8/18/1727 as being the wife of Thomas Abbott Jr. In this document Elizabeth is presently the wife of 
2 CONC Thomas Abbott Jr. and is selling land previously owned by her son James Emery Jr to Richard Shacklerley. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is presumed that she married Thomas Abbott Jr. between 1720 and 1726 in Berwick. Together Elizabeth and Thomas are listed in the church records eight times, twice for their granddaughter's baptism in 1757/1758 and six times for
2 CONC  their children's baptism.[7].
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT 1 Jonathan born at Dedham on April 4, 1678. [3] [4]
2 CONT 2 Elizabeth born March 12, 1681; [3] died in July 1730; married Jeremiah Ingraham on Oct. 3, 1709. [4]
2 CONT 3 Josiah born Dec. 11, 1683; [3] died Feb. 18, 1729/30; married Hannah Freeman about 1708. [4]
2 CONT 4 Hannah born Nov. 22, 1686 [3]; died at Attleborough April 17, 1763; married Samuel Tingley on Dec. 15, 1713 at Attleborough. [4]
2 CONT 5 Rachel born about 1689; died at Attleborough Jan. 11, 1733/4; married first Noah Fuller on Feb. 21, 1711/12; married second Jeremiah Freeman on Jan. 29, 1716/17. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT Braintree Births
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Nucome, the daughter of Ffrancis Nucome and Rachell his wiffe was borne the (26) (6) 1658. (p. 641) [1]
2 CONT Dedham Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT 1677: John Pidg and Elizabeth Newcomb married the 3rd of the 5th. (p. 17)
2 CONT James Emary of Barwick, in Kittery, and Elizabeth Pidge of Dedham was married Desember 28, 1695. (p. 27)
2 CONT Dedham Births
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan, ye Son of John & Elizabeth Pidge, born ye 4th 2d, 78. (p. 16)
2 CONT Elizabeth, Daughter of John & Eliza. Pidg, borne 12:1:1681. (p. 18)
2 CONT Josiah, ye son of Jno. & Elizabeth Pidg, was borne the 11:10: 83. (p. 19)
2 CONT 1686: Hannah, ye daughter of Jno. & Elizabeth Pidge, was borne November 22. (p. 22) [3]
2 CONT Elizabeth was born before 1768. Elizabeth Newcomb ... [8]
2 CONT
