1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Bullard, first son of Benjamin, was born in 1670, in what was then Medfield, Massachusetts but would become Sherborn.[1]
2 CONT He married Tabitha, possibly the widowed Tabitha Edwards Pond, between 1690 and 1701.[2]
2 CONT Benjamin and Tabitha had children in Sherborn: [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin (b. Mar 4, 1702-3),
2 CONT Jonathan (b. Oct 24, 1706),
2 CONT Seth (b. Feb 17, 1708-9),
2 CONT and reportedly another son, name unknown, and perhaps a daughter or two, no birth records yet found.
2 CONT Benjamin died at 96 years of age, it is said. No death record yet found.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bullard-501
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Bullard (1670 - abt. 1760) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Bullard
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1 Mar 1670 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Benjamin Bullard and Martha (Pidge) Bullard
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Maria Bullard, Elizabeth Bullard, Sarah (Bullard) Tomblin, Samuel Bullard, Hannah (Bullard) Sheffield, Eleazer Bullard, John Bullard [half], Elizabeth (Bullard) Jones [half], Mary (Bullard) Leland [half], Malachi Bullar
2 CONC d [half] and Isaac Bullard [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Tabitha (Edwards) Bullard — married about 1700 in Massachusetts Bay Province
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of John Robert Bullard, Benjamin Bullard, Jonathan Bullard, Seth Bullard and Mary (Bullard) Haven
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1760 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bullard-501 created 29 Nov 2013 | Last modified 1 Jul 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Vital Records of Medfield through 1850, p. 25, 'Benjamin, s. Benjamin and Martha, May 1, 1670'
2 CONT ↑ no vital record of their wedding yet found.
2 CONT ↑ [http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Middlesex/Sherborn/Images/Sherborn_B019.gif Middlesex, Massachusetts, "Vital Records of Sherborn,", pp. 19-21, Mother recorded as Tabitha, Tabatha, & Tabatha
2 CONT "Other Bullards." See also History of Worcester County, Masachusetts.
2 CONT Vital records of Sherborn, Massachusetts, page 20.
2 CONT Other Bullards, a genealogy : supplementary to Bullard and allied families; page 9
2 CONT Morse, Rev. Abner. A Genealogical Register of the Descendants of Several Ancient Puritans. (H.W. Dutton & Son, Boston, 1857-1864).; Vol. 1, p. 13
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT More sources needed for marriage date, wife's surname, and their deaths.
