1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ann Batt''', daughter of Nicholas & Lucy Batt born circa 1630 in England, emigrated 5 Apr 1635 on the "James" of London from Southampton England, with her father, a linen weaver, arrived 3 Jun 1635 at Boston, Ma
2 CONC ssachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Webster was given in a legacy in her father's will dated 18 June 1674. On 28 Feb 1677/78 "John Emery, Jr, aged about 50 years, "deposed " that in the year 1653 on the day that John Webster was contracted to Ann Batt, eldest da
2 CONC ughter of Nicolas Batt of Newbury ... said whilst I live I cannot do much for her but I will weave her cloth ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Batt married on 13 June 1653 to John Webster, a blacksmith, at Newbury, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann (Batt) Webster died 18 Oct 1716 Newbury, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT "WEBSTER, Anne, w. Sergt. John, "when she had lived in a marriage state with her sd husband about sixty three years," Oct. 18, 1716."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ "The Planters of the Commonwealth: A Study of the Emigrants and Emigration in Colonial times 1620-1640" by Charles Edward Banks, Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc, Copyright 1930, 2006., p 137 ↑ Robert Charles Anderson, Great
2 CONC  Migration 1634-1635, A-B. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2008.) Originally published as: The Great Migration, Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635, Volume 1, A-B, by Robert Cha
2 CONC rles Anderson, George F. Sanborn, Jr., and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1999. , p 202 ↑ 3.0 3.1 "Vital Records of Newbury, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849", The Essex Institut
2 CONC e, 1911, Vol. 2, p 503, 747 https://archive.org/details/vitalrecordsofne02esse See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ancestry of Charles Stinson Pillsbury and John Sargent Pillsbury: compiled for Helen Pendleton (Winston) Pillsbury" by Mary Lovering Holman, publ, 1938
2 CONT
2 CONT "Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s", edited by P. William Filby, Gale Research Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network, Inc., 2006.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Essex/Newbury/aMarriagesB.shtml "(Batt) Anne, and John Webster, June 13, 1653."
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Essex/Newbury/aDeathsW.shtml "(Webster) Anne, w. Sergt. John, "when she had lived in a marriage state with her sd husband about sixty three years," Oct. 18, 1716."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39655501/anne-newburg-webster
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Newburg Batt Webster
2 CONT BIRTH	23 Oct 1630
2 CONT Wiltshire, England
2 CONT DEATH	18 Oct 1716 (aged 85)
2 CONT Newburyport, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	39655501 · View Source
2 CONT MEMORIAL
2 CONT PHOTOS 0
2 CONT FLOWERS 16
2 CONT Anne married John Webster II on June 13, 1653 in Newbury, Essex County, Massachusetts. To this union, 9 children were born:
2 CONT
2 CONT John
2 CONT Mary
2 CONT Sarah
2 CONT Abigail
2 CONT Lucy
2 CONT Stephen
2 CONT Anna
2 CONT Nicholas
2 CONT Jonathan
2 CONT
2 CONT John & Anne moved to Newbury from Ipswich after his father's death, later to Haverhill where he was the second blacksmith in the town. He moved back to Newbury later, which is where he probably died. He and his wife were married f
2 CONC or 63 years.
2 CONT
