2 CONT *'''Collections for a history of Staffordshire, Volume 2 By William Salt Archaeological Society, Staffordshire Record Society Pg.107
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=dKVCAAAAYAAJ&pg=RA1-PA108&lpg=RA1-PA108&dq=Joane+Hextall&source=bl&ots=ukytRg-ioE&sig=NlDTiLS5B4M0Gv45skw77D0kVrU&hl=en&ei=fCANTIzWN4yONaTmhbYE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=10&ved=0CDQQ6AE
2 CONC wCQ#v=onepage&q=Joane%20Hextall&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.107
2 CONT * .... John Bromley, the grandson and heir of Thomas Bromley, proved his age in 4 Hen. Vi.; and in 7 Hen Vi. he died seized of a third part of Ashley, &c. He died without issue, and his sister Margaret, wife of William Hextall, wa
2 CONC s his next heir.
2 CONT *   William Hextall, the husband of Margaret, was lord of Millwich and of Hextall, a township in the parish of Seighford, and living in 10 and 22 Hen. VI.
2 CONT *   According to Erdeswick and Huntbache he had issue by the said Margaret a son Humfrey, who died without issue, and two daughters, Joan, who was married to Sir John de Bromley, of Badington, and Margaret, who was married to Rich
2 CONC ard Petit. .... etc.  Sir John de Bromley, of Badington, Knight (who was also Lord of 
2 CONT *Pg.108
2 CONT *Bromley in right of his wife and living in 22 Hen. VI. and 20 Edw. IV., but dead before 1 Hen. VII.), had issue by Joan his wife the daughter and co-heiress of William Hextall, three daughters and coheirs, namely, Margery (or Mor
2 CONC fe), who was the first wife of Sir William Stanley, of Hooton, Knight, by whom she had an only daughter and heiress, Margaret, wife of Peter Gerard, son and heir apparent of Sir Thomas Gerard, of Kingsley and Bryn, co. Lancaster, 
2 CONC Knight; Margaret, wife of Sir John Harpur of Rushall, co. Stafford, Knight; and '''Elizabeth (or Isabel, wife of Sir William Needham''', between whom their lands were divided.
2 CONT * .... Sir John Bromley died September 4th, 1419 (7Hen. V.), and was buried at Acton in Cheshire. The inquisition states that he held in demesne, of of fee, the manors of Badington and Bromhall from James Lord Audelegh by military
2 CONC  service, val. 40 merks. He held also the manor of Cholmston, and half the manor of Alvaston, and lands in Alstanton, Wolstanwood, Monks Copenhall, and Church Copenhall. By his wife Margery, daughter of Sir John Massey, of Tatton,
2 CONC  Knight, he had several sons, of whom the survivor, William Bromley, of Badington, Esq., was father of Sir John Bromley, who married Joan Hextall.
2 CONT _____________
2 CONT 'Needham2'
2 CONT Families covered: Needham of Cranach (Cranage, Cravach or Crevach), Needham of Kilmorey, Needham of Shavington, Needham of Shenton
2 CONT [This page was initially named Needham1. It was renamed following a review in which earlier generations and a senior line of the family were found.]
2 CONT William de Nedeham of Chester (a 1375, judge)
2 CONT m. Alice de Cranach (dau/heir of William de Cranach or Cranage)
2 CONT *1.	Robert Nedeham of Cranach (d 1407) this generation reported by Visitation but not mentioned by either BP1934 or Lodge
2 CONT ** 	A.	Robert Nedeham of Cranach or Cranage 'of Sherington' (Shavington) (d 1448-9)
2 CONT ** 	Lodge identifies Robert's wife Dorothy as a dau of Sir John Savage of Clifton by Catharine, dau of Thomas Stanley. The Savage records suggest that she was 3 generations earlier, which is supported by the dates.
2 CONT ** 	m. Dorothy Savage (d 1430, dau of Sir John Savage of Clifton)
2 CONT *** 	i.	Thomas Needham of Cranach or Cranage or Crevach (d 1463)
2 CONT *** 	Lodge identifies Thomas's wife Maud as a dau of Sir William Brereton of Brereton by Maud, dau of John Dutton of Dutton & widow of Sir William Booth of Dunham. We do not see such a wife for a Sir William Brereton.
2 CONT *** 	m. Maud Brereton (dau of Sir William Brereton of Brereton)
2 CONT **** 	a.	'''Sir William Needham of Cranach & Shavington''' (d 1487?)
2 CONT **** 	'''m. Isabel Bromley''' (dau of Sir John Bromley by Joan Hexstall)
2 CONT *****(1)	Sir Robert Needham of Shavington & Shenton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 1556)
2 CONT ***** 	BP1934 does not name Robert's wife. Visitation (Shropshire) identifies her as Agnes, dau of John/Jenkin Manwaring of Pever. Visitation (Cheshire, 1580, 'Needham of Shevinton & of Cranage'), which provides some support for a
2 CONC  few generations, identifies her as Anne, dau of _ Manwaring of Baddeley. Lodge identifies her as Agnes, dau of John Manwaring of Baddeley.
2 CONT ***** 	m. Agnes Manwaring (dau of John or Jenkin Manwaring)
2 CONT ****** 	(A)	Thomas Needham of Shenton
2 CONT Whilst BP1934 & Lodge show only Thomas's marriage to Anne Talbot, Visitation (Shropshire) shows him as having also married ...
2 CONT ****** 	m1/2. Agnes Hope
2 CONT ******* 	(i)	Agnes Needham
2 CONT ****** 	m2/1. Anne Talbot (dau of Sir John Talbot of Grafton and Albrighton)
2 CONT ******* 	(ii)	Robert Needham of Shenton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 18.12.1603)
2 CONT ******* 	m. Frances Aston (dau of Sir Edward Aston of Tixhall)
2 CONT ******** 	(a)	Sir Robert Needham, 1st Viscount Kilmorey (d 26.11.1631) - continued below
