2 CONT *Pg.108
2 CONT *Bromley in right of his wife and living in 22 Hen. VI. and 20 Edw. IV., but dead before 1 Hen. VII.), had issue by Joan his wife the daughter and co-heiress of William Hextall, three daughters and coheirs, namely, Margery (or Mor
2 CONC fe), who was the first wife of Sir William Stanley, of Hooton, Knight, by whom she had an only daughter and heiress, Margaret, wife of Peter Gerard, son and heir apparent of Sir Thomas Gerard, of Kingsley and Bryn, co. Lancaster, 
2 CONC Knight; Margaret, wife of Sir John Harpur of Rushall, co. Stafford, Knight; and '''Elizabeth (or Isabel, wife of Sir William Needham''', between whom their lands were divided.
