2 CONT 'Needham2'
2 CONT Families covered: Needham of Cranach (Cranage, Cravach or Crevach), Needham of Kilmorey, Needham of Shavington, Needham of Shenton
2 CONT [This page was initially named Needham1. It was renamed following a review in which earlier generations and a senior line of the family were found.]
2 CONT William de Nedeham of Chester (a 1375, judge)
2 CONT m. Alice de Cranach (dau/heir of William de Cranach or Cranage)
2 CONT *1.	Robert Nedeham of Cranach (d 1407) this generation reported by Visitation but not mentioned by either BP1934 or Lodge
2 CONT ** 	A.	Robert Nedeham of Cranach or Cranage 'of Sherington' (Shavington) (d 1448-9)
2 CONT ** 	Lodge identifies Robert's wife Dorothy as a dau of Sir John Savage of Clifton by Catharine, dau of Thomas Stanley. The Savage records suggest that she was 3 generations earlier, which is supported by the dates.
2 CONT ** 	m. Dorothy Savage (d 1430, dau of Sir John Savage of Clifton)
2 CONT *** 	i.	Thomas Needham of Cranach or Cranage or Crevach (d 1463)
2 CONT *** 	Lodge identifies Thomas's wife Maud as a dau of Sir William Brereton of Brereton by Maud, dau of John Dutton of Dutton & widow of Sir William Booth of Dunham. We do not see such a wife for a Sir William Brereton.
2 CONT *** 	m. Maud Brereton (dau of Sir William Brereton of Brereton)
2 CONT **** 	a.	Sir William Needham of Cranach & Shavington (d 1487?)
2 CONT **** 	m. Isabel Bromley (dau of Sir John Bromley by Joan Hexstall)
2 CONT *****(1)	Sir Robert Needham of Shavington & Shenton, Sheriff of Shropshire (d 1556)
2 CONT ***** 	BP1934 does not name Robert's wife. Visitation (Shropshire) identifies her as Agnes, dau of John/Jenkin Manwaring of Pever. Visitation (Cheshire, 1580, 'Needham of Shevinton & of Cranage'), which provides some support for a
2 CONC  few generations, identifies her as Anne, dau of _ Manwaring of Baddeley. Lodge identifies her as Agnes, dau of John Manwaring of Baddeley.
2 CONT ***** 	m. Agnes Manwaring (dau of John or Jenkin Manwaring)
2 CONT ****** 	etc.
2 CONT ***** 	(2)	'''Margaret or Mary Needham mentioned by Visitation, not by Lodge ## duplication here? ##'''
2 CONT ***** 	'''m. Thomas Whittington of Pountley''' (d 1546)
2 CONT **** 	b.	etc.
