2 CONC hn Delves. They hd one son, '''John Esq'''. WILLIAM MAINWARING, Esq. died before 1476. ....
2 CONT *'''10. JOHN MAINWARING, Esq., of Over Peover, Cheshire, son and heir. He married MAUD LEGH, daughter of Robert Legh, Esq., of Adlington, Cheshire, by Isabel, daughter of William Stanley, Knt. They had two sons, John, Knt., and Ro
2 CONC bert, and three daughters, Maud (wife of Thomas Starkey, Esq.), Joan (wife of Thomas Ashton), and Agnes. By an unknown mistress, he also had an illegitimate son, Charles. JOHN MAINWARING, Esq., died 8 July 1495. ...
2 CONT *'''Children of John Mainwaring, Esq., by Maud Legh:
2 CONT **	i. JOHN MAINWARING, Knt. [see next].
