2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 278.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 282.
2 CONT * 4.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 557.
2 CONT * 5.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 707.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 206.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p386.htm#i11589 _________________________
2 CONT *'''Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...    By Douglas Richardson
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&printsec=frontcover&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&hl=en&sa=X&ei=kshLUY2yHM_SigKTqYHwAg&ved=0CDwQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=mainwarinG&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.278
2 CONT *   JOHN BOTELER, Knt., of Warrington, Lancashire, married ISABEL HARINGTON [see BOTELER 8].
2 CONT *9. ELLEN BOTELER, born about 1423. She married 21 Jan. 1443/4 WILLIAM MAINWARING, Esq., of Over Peover, Cheshire, son and heir apparent of John Mainwaring, Knt., of Over Peover, Cheshire, by his 1st wife, Margaret, daughter of Jo
2 CONC hn Delves. They had one son, '''John Esq'''. WILLIAM MAINWARING, Esq. died before 1476. ....
2 CONT *'''10. JOHN MAINWARING, Esq., of Over Peover, Cheshire, son and heir. He married MAUD LEGH, daughter of Robert Legh, Esq., of Adlington, Cheshire, by Isabel, daughter of William Stanley, Knt. They had two sons, John, Knt., and Ro
2 CONC bert, and three daughters, Maud (wife of Thomas Starkey, Esq.), Joan (wife of Thomas Ashton), and Agnes. By an unknown mistress, he also had an illegitimate son, Charles. JOHN MAINWARING, Esq., died 8 July 1495. ...
2 CONT *'''Children of John Mainwaring, Esq., by Maud Legh:
2 CONT **	i. JOHN MAINWARING, Knt. [see next].
2 CONT **	ii. AGNES MAINWARING, married ROBERT NEEDHAM, Esq., of Shavington (in Adderley), Shroshire [see NEEDHAM 11].
2 CONT *11. JOHN MAINWARING, Knt., of Over Peover, Cheshire, Sheriff of Flintshire, son and heir, born about 1471. He married KATHERINE HONFORD, daughter of John Honford, Esq., of Honford, Cheshire, by Margaret, daughter of John Savage, 
2 CONC K.G. [see TRAFFORD 12 for her ancestry]. They had thirteen sons, Randall, Knt., Edmund, John, Peter, Philip, Edward, Robert, Thomas, George, Henry, Nicholas, William, and William (2nd of name), and two daughters, Margaret and Kath
2 CONC erine (wife of William Newton). He was knighted in France in 1513. SIR JOHN MAINWARING left a will dated 4 March 1515/6, proved 18 Nov. 1516 (P.C.C. 1 Maynwaryng). He was buried at Over Peover, Cheshire, His widow, Katherine, was 
2 CONC mentioned in the 1527 will of John Stanley, Knt. She died in 1529. .... ______________________________
2 CONT *'''The visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580 (1882)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/visitationchesh00fellgoog
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/visitationchesh00fellgoog#page/n167/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.151
2 CONT **Leigh of Adlington. - CHART
2 CONT *Robinett Leigh of Adlington. = Maud.; ch: Rob't (m. Isabel Savage & Isabell Stanley), James (a Preist.), William, Peter, Ellin (m. Roger Leigh) Leigh.
2 CONT *Rob't Leigh of Adlington. = 1. Isabel d. to Jno Savage s.p.; = 2. Isabel d. to Sr Wm Stanley married by consent of the Pope because shee was of the blood of his first wife.; ch: Rob't (m. Ellin Booth), '''Maud (m. Jno Manwaring)'
2 CONC '', Agnes (m. Sr Andrew Brereton), .... (m. _ Picott), Margaret (m. Thos Mere), Isabel (m. Sr Lawrence Warren & Sr George Holford), Margrett (m. Wm Damport) Leigh
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/visitationchesh00fellgoog#page/n181/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.165
2 CONT **Meinilwarin. Manwaringe of Peever. - CHART
2 CONT *Sr John Manwaring of Peever. = Margrett d. to . . . .  Tuchett Lord Audley.; ch: Wm (m. Mary Delves & Ellin Butler) Mainwaring.
2 CONT *Wm Mainwaring of Peever 22 H. 6 Maried = 1. Mary d. to Sr Jno Delves.; = 2. Ellin d. to Sr Jno Butler of Bewsy.; ch: '''John (m. Maud Leigh)''' Manwaring.
2 CONT *'''John Manwaring of Peever.  = Maud d. to Rob't Leigh of Adlington.; ch: Sr John (m. Katherin Hanford) Manwaring.
2 CONT *Sr John Manwaring of Peever. = Katherin d. to Wm Hanford of Hanford.; ch: Edmund, John, Piers, Wm, Richard, (Pg.166 Randoll, (m. Elizab. Brereton), Phillip (m. Anne Lecester), Edward (m. Alice Boghey), Rob't (m. _ Glegg), Thomas,
2 CONC  George, Richard, Henry) Mainwaring. ___________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 3 By John Burke Pg.453-457
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=yshsAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA454&lpg=PA454&dq=Robert+Legh+stanley&source=bl&ots=rdUuPvqvS0&sig=TTmd3ucv2Ompo9S-jzDWz0SDEEc&hl=en&ei=gVT9S-TrL4nONLOh0N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CB8Q6AEwBD
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=Robert%20Legh%20stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 454
2 CONT *   ROBERT LEGH, esq. of Adlington, wedded, first, Isabella, daughter of John Savage, of Clifton, by whom he had no issue; and, secondly, Isabella, daughter of Sir William Stanley, knt. of Hooton; by whom he had,
2 CONT **	I. ROBERT, his heir.
2 CONT **	I. Margaret, m. first to Thomas Mere, of Mere; and secondly to Robert Reddish, of Catteral.
2 CONT **	II. Margery, m. to William Davenport, esq. of Bramall.
2 CONT **	III. Isabel, m. first, to Laurence Warren, esq. of Poynton; and, secondly, to Sir George Holford, of Holford.
2 CONT **'''	IV. Matilda, m. to John Mainwaring, esq. of Peover.
2 CONT **	V. Agnes, m. to Sir Andrew Brereton, of Brereton.
2 CONT **	VI. ___ m. to ___ Pigott, esq. of Chetwynd, Salop.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PP1&lpg=PP1&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&source=bl&ots=RRsM2STbba&sig=n4fyHWGDQZODK9D1BzNoVJisVpE&hl=en&ei=KRvKTeTDBISisAOaj9SeAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CCQQ6AEwAjg
2 CONC K#v=snippet&q=legh&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.331
2 CONT *   16. ANNE TALBOT, married (as his 1st wife THOMAS NEEDHAM, Esq., of Cranage, Cheshire, and Shavington (in Adderley), Shropshire, son and heir of Robert Needham, Knt., of Cranage, Cheshire and Shavington (in Adderley), Shropshir
2 CONC e, Sheriff of Shropshire, 1528-9, 1535-6, 1540=1, Sheriff of Cheshire, 1538-9, by Agnes, daughter of '''John Manwaring, Esq., of Over Peover, Cheshire''', He was born in 1510. ....
2 CONT *Pg. 557
2 CONT *   14. KATHERINE HONFORD, married JOHN MAINWARING, Knt., of Over Peover, Cheshire, Sheriff of Flintshire, son and heir of '''John Mainwaring, Esq., of Over Peover, Cheshire, by Maud, daughter of Robert Legh''', Esq., of Adlington
2 CONC , Cheshire. He was born about 1471. They had thirteen sons, Randall, Knt., Edmund, John Peter Phlip, Edward, Robert, Thomas, George, and Henry, Nicholas, William, William (again), and two daughters, Margaret and Katherine (wife of
2 CONC  William Newton). He was knighted in France in 1513. SIR JOHN MAINWARING left a will dated 4 March 1515/6, proved 18 Nov. 1516 (P.C.C. 1 Maynwaryng). He was buried at Over Peover, Cheshire. His widow, Katherine, was mentioned in t
2 CONC he 1527 will of John Stanley, Knt. She died in 1529. ____________________________
