1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Peter Daniels, Esq.1
2 CONT *'''M, #33096, b. 1561, d. 3 August 1590
2 CONT *Father	Thomas Daniels, Esq. b. 1531, d. 9 Aug 1574
2 CONT *Mother	Alice Dutton b. 1530, d. 4 Sep 1594
2 CONT *'''     Peter Daniels, Esq. was born in 1561 at Over Tabley, Cheshire, England. He married Anna Manwaring''', daughter of Henry Manwaring and Mary Ellen Venables, '''in 1574. Peter Daniels, Esq. died on 3 August 1590; Age 29.
2 CONT *'''Family     Anna Manwaring''' b. c 1559, d. 29 Jul 1633
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Mary Daniel b. c 1578
2 CONT **Jane Daniel b. c 1580
2 CONT **Anne Daniel b. c 1582
2 CONT **Peter Daniel, Esq.+ b. 1584, d. 18 Apr 1652
2 CONT **Richard Daniel b. c 1586
2 CONT **Frances Daniel b. c 1588
2 CONT **Robert Daniels+ b. c 1589, d. 6 Jul 1655
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S10229] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 366; Burke's Commoners, Vol. I, p. 45; Burke's Landed Gentry, 1936, p. 2453.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1102.htm#i33096 _______________
2 CONT *OUTDATED, Unity Daniels(Croshaw) IS NO LONGER LISTED AS A DAU. OF ANNA MANWARING & PETER DANIELS
2 CONT *'''Peter Daniels, Esq.1
2 CONT *'''M, #33096, b. 1561, d. 3 August 1590
2 CONT *Father      Thomas Daniels, Esq. b. 1531, d. 9 Aug 1574
2 CONT *Mother     Alice Dutton b. 1530, d. 4 Sep 1594
2 CONT *'''     Peter Daniels, Esq. was born in 1561 at Over Tabley, Cheshire, England. He married Anna Manwaring, daughter of Henry Manwaring and Mary Ellen Venables, in 1574. Peter Daniels, Esq. died on 3 August 1590; Age 29.
2 CONT *'''Family      Anna Manwaring b. c 1559, d. 29 Jul 1633
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Mary Daniel b. c 1578
2 CONT **Jane Daniel b. c 1580
2 CONT **Anne Daniel b. c 1582
2 CONT **Peter Daniel, Esq.+ b. 1584, d. 18 Apr 1652
2 CONT **Richard Daniel b. c 1586
2 CONT **Frances Daniel b. c 1588
2 CONT ** Unity Daniels(Croshaw) b. 1576                                                                                                                                                                          
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S10229] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 366; Burke's Commoners, Vol. I, p. 45; Burke's Landed Gentry, 1936, p. 2453.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1102.htm#i33096 _____________________
2 CONT *'''The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester: Comp. from ..., Volume 1     By George Ormerod
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=DYY1AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA475#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.475
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   IX. Thomas Daniel of Over Tabley, esquire, brother and heir male to the last Peter, married Alice, daughter of Fouk Dutton of the city of Chester, and had issue '''Peter, son and heir'''; Thomas, second son; Richard, third son
2 CONC ; William, fourth son, died 20 die Maii, 33 Eliz. 1591; John, fifth son, and Margaret, a daughter, living 1575, 17 Eliz. Lib. C. fol. 240. x.
2 CONT *   This Thomas Daniell, esquire, died 1575, 17 Eliz. aged 41 years. Alice survived, and was living 1590, Lib. C. fol. 239. m. and 238. l.
2 CONT *'''   X. Peter Daniell of Over Tabley, esquire, son and heir''' of Thomas and Alice, '''married Anne, daughter of''' Henry Manwaring of Carinsham in Chester, esquire, '''1574, and had issue''' Peter, son and heir, six years old w
2 CONC hen his father died; Richard Daniell, second son, died without issue; Frances, married Edward Littleton, younger son of Litleton of Pillaton in Staffordshire, near Pancridge; Anne, second daughter, died without issue; Mary, third 
2 CONC daughter, married John Woodnot of Shenton in Cheshire; after to John King of Salmondley in Lincolnshire; Jane, fourth daughter, died without issue.
2 CONT *'''   This Peter died 3 die Augusti, 1590, 32 Eliz. aged 29 years. Anne his widow afterwards married''' Thomas Ashold parson of Swetenham in Cheshire; and she died 29 Julii, 1633, and had the wardship of her son: Lib. c. fol. 239
2 CONC . n. o.
2 CONT *   XI. Peter Daniell of Over Tabley, esq. '''son and heir of Peter and Anne''', married Christian, daughter of Richard Grosvenour of Eaton-boat, in Cheshire, esquire, and had issue Peter, eldest son, Henry, second son, married An
2 CONC ne daughter of Sir John Dorell of Westwoody, in Berkshire, but had no issue; John Daniell, third son, was an apprentice in London, and married, but died also without issue; William, fourth son, married Dorothy Forth of Wigan in La
2 CONC ncashire; Thomas, fifth son, slain at the battel of Brainford, near London, 1642. Margaret, eldest daughter, married Richard Green of Congleton in Cheshire, gentleman; Christian, second daughter, married George Davenport of Calvel
2 CONC ey, esq., Mary, third daughter, married one Colonel Finch, 1651, an officer for the parliament-party against the king, and are both now living in Ireland, 1666. Elizabeth, fourth daughter, died unmarried; Anne, the youngest daught
2 CONC er, married Robert Sanford of Sanford, in Shropshire, esquire, 1648.
2 CONT *   This Peter Daniell was one of the knights of this county for the parliament 1625, and died 18th day of April 1652, aged 68 years, and was buried at Great Budworth. Christian his wife survived, and died 1663.
2 CONT *   XII. Peter Daniell of Over Tabley, the younger, esquire, son and heir of Peter and Christian, married .... etc. ________________________
2 CONT *'''A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great ..., Volume 1     By John Burke
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=U_CvyAF3ko4C&pg=PA45#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.45
2 CONT *   THOMAS DE ANYERS, esq. of Over Tabley, who m. Alice, daughter of Foulk Dutton, esq. of Chester, and had, with other issue, a son,
2 CONT *'''   PETER DE ANYERS, esq. of Over Tabley, his successor in 1575. This gentleman wedded, in 1574, Anne, daughter of''' Henry Mainwaring, esq. of Carinckam, in Cheshire, '''by whom (who subsequently married''' Thomas Ashold, esq.
2 CONC  of Swetenham, in Cheshire, and d. in 1633) '''he had issue,
2 CONT **	PETER, his successor.
2 CONT **	Richard, d. s. p.
2 CONT **	Frances, m. to Edward Littleton, esq. son of Littleton of Pillaton.
2 CONT **	Anne, d. unmarried.
2 CONT **	Mary, m. first, to John Woodroot, esq. and, secondly, to John King, esq.
2 CONT **	Jane, d. without issue.
2 CONT *The elder son and successor,
2 CONT *   PETER DE ANYERS, esq. of Over Tabley, was but six years of age when his father died. In 1625, he represented the county of Chester in parliament, and marrying Christian, daughter of Richard Grosvenor, esq. of Eaton, in Cheshir
2 CONC e, had issue,
2 CONT **	I. PETER, of Over Tabley, a captain of a foot company in the regiment of John, Earl of Rivers, raised for the king's service. He d. at Oxford of a shot received at the siege of Gloucester, leaving (with a daughter, Margaret, wh
2 CONC o probably married into the Minchull family, a gentleman of that name being mentioned as the uncle of Sir Samuel Daniell) a son,
2 CONT ***	THOMAS, of Over Tabley, who m. Alice, niece of Henry Neville, esq. .... etc. ________________________
2 CONT *DANIELL, Peter (1584-1652), of Over Tabley, Cheshire
2 CONT *b. 1584,1 1st s. of '''Peter Daniell of Over Tabley and Anna, da. of Henry Mainwaring''' of Carincham, Cheshire.2 educ. Queen’s, Oxf. 1601; G. Inn 1604.3 m. 1620, Christian (d.1663),4 da. of Sir Richard Grosvenor* of Eaton Hall, 
2 CONC Cheshire, 7s. (2 d.v.p.) 6da. suc. fa. 1590.5 d. 18 Apr. 1652.6
2 CONT *The Daniells had been established at Over Tabley since the end of the thirteenth century and had long been active in county affairs.11 '''Daniell’s father died in 1590 and his wardship was purchased by his mother''', who ensured 
2 CONC that he received a traditional gentleman’s education at Oxford and Gray’s Inn. On marrying the daughter of Sir Richard Grosvenor in 1620, Daniell became a close friend of his father-in-law and his most trusted adviser. Daniell sto
2 CONC od alongside  .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/daniell-peter-1584-1652 ______________________
2 CONT *Sir Richard Grosvenor, 1st Baronet (9 January 1585 – 14 September 1645) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1621 and 1629. He is an ancestor of the modern day Dukes of Westminster.
2 CONT *Grosvenor was born at Eaton Hall, Cheshire, the only surviving son of 17 children.[1] His father was Richard Grosvenor of Eaton, and his mother was Christian, the daughter of Sir Richard Brooke of Norton Priory, Cheshire.[2] His 
2 CONC early education was by John Bruen, a local puritan and at the age of 13 he went to Queen's College, Oxford.[1] He matriculated in 1599 and graduated BA on 30 June 1602.[3]
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Grosvenor stood surety for the debts of his '''brother-in-law, Peter Daniell, but in 1629 Daniell defaulted on his debts''', and for almost ten years Grosvenor was incarcerated in the Fleet Prison.[1]
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Richard_Grosvenor,_1st_Baronet ________________________
