1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Peter Daniel, Esq.1
2 CONT *'''M, #33094, b. 1584, d. 18 April 1652
2 CONT *Father      Peter Daniels, Esq. b. 1561, d. 3 Aug 1590
2 CONT *Mother     Anna Manwaring b. c 1559, d. 29 Jul 1633
2 CONT *'''     Peter Daniel, Esq. was born in 1584 at Kibley, Cheshire, England. He married Christian Grosvenor, daughter of Richard Grosvenor and Christiana Brooke, circa 1610. Peter Daniel, Esq. died on 18 April 1652 at of Over Tabley
2 CONC , Cheshire, England.
2 CONT *'''Family      Christian Grosvenor b. 4 Nov 1587, d. 1663
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Peter Daniel, Esq. b. c 1611, d. 1643
2 CONT **Henry Daniel b. c 1613
2 CONT **Ursula Daniels+ b. c 1615, d. b 1635
2 CONT **John Daniel b. c 1617
2 CONT **Mary Daniels+ b. c 1619, d. 26 Jan 1679
2 CONT **Margaret Daniel b. c 1621
2 CONT **Christian Daniel b. c 1623
2 CONT **William Daniel b. c 1625
2 CONT **Thomas Daniel b. c 1627, d. 1642
2 CONT **Elizabeth Daniel b. c 1629
2 CONT **Anne Daniel b. c 1631
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S10227] Unknown author, Burke's Commoners, Vol. I, p. 45; Burke's Landed Gentry, 1936, p. 2453.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1102.htm#i33094 _________________________
2 CONT *'''DANIELL, Peter (1584-1652), of Over Tabley, Cheshire
2 CONT *'''b. 1584,1 1st s. of Peter Daniell of Over Tabley and Anna, da. of Henry Mainwaring of Carincham, Cheshire.2 educ. Queen’s, Oxf. 1601; G. Inn 1604.3 m. 1620, Christian (d.1663),4 da. of Sir Richard Grosvenor* of Eaton Hall, Che
2 CONC shire, 7s. (2 d.v.p.) 6da. suc. fa. 1590.5 d. 18 Apr. 1652.6
2 CONT *'''The Daniells had been established at Over Tabley since the end of the thirteenth century and had long been active in county affairs.11 Daniell’s father died in 1590 and his wardship was purchased by his mother, who ensured tha
2 CONC t he received a traditional gentleman’s education at Oxford and Gray’s Inn. On marrying the daughter of Sir Richard Grosvenor in 1620, Daniell became a close friend of his father-in-law and his most trusted adviser. Daniell stood 
2 CONC alongside Grosvenor in the county election of 1626, but whereas Grosvenor was unanimously supported for the first place, Daniell was opposed by (Sir) William Brereton (1st bt.)* and Peter Minshull. Grosvenor persuaded Brereton and
2 CONC  Daniell to draw lots beforehand to see who would go forward to face Minshull. Brereton was thereby eliminated, but at the election, held in the shire hall, the sheriff was unable to determine which man had the greater number of v
2 CONC oices and so ordered a poll to be taken outside on Flookersbrook Heath. This also proved indecisive, and only after two days of wrangling did Minshull yield.12 Daniell is not known to have spoken in the Commons, and was named to o
2 CONC nly one bill committee, concerning citations in ecclesiastical courts (9 March).13 Following the dissolution, Daniell was removed from the Bench and deprived of his office as feodary, probably because of Grosvenor’s role in the at
2 CONC tempted impeachment of Buckingham.14
2 CONT *'''By the late 1620s Daniell was heavily indebted and unable to pay his creditors, having tied up his lands in various trusts. Grosvenor, being his suretor, was consequently confined to the Fleet, where he remained until December
2 CONC  1638, when Daniell agreed to pay his debts from his son’s marriage settlement.15 Daniell played no recorded role during the Civil War but was named as a delinquent in 1648, possibly because three of his sons had served as royalis
2 CONC t officers.16 The eldest, Peter, was killed during the siege of Gloucester in 1643, while Thomas was slain at Brentford the year before.17 Daniell himself died at Great Budworth, in Cheshire, on 18 Apr. 1652. No will or administra
2 CONC tion has been found and no further member of his immediate family sat in Parliament.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/daniell-peter-1584-1652 ______________________
2 CONT *'''Peter Daniell (1584–1652) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons in 1626.
2 CONT *'''Daniell was of Over Tabley, Cheshire. He matriculated at Queen's College, Oxford on 16 October 1601 aged 17. He was a student of Gray's Inn in 1604. In 1626, he was elected Member of Parliament for Cheshire.[1]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Daniell ___________________
2 CONT *'''Peter Danyel1
2 CONT *M, #530204
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Apr 2012
2 CONT *'''     Peter Danyel married Christian Grosvenor''', daughter of Richard Grosvenor and Christian Brooke.1
2 CONT *'''     He lived at Tabley, Cheshire, England.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 4132. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p53021.htm#i530204 ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Sir Peter Daniell of Over Tabley
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of marriage has been listed as 1625 but this date is inconsistent with the dates of birth for the children. Peter Daniell has been listed as the father of Captain William Daniel of Middlesex, Va., or the father of William
2 CONC  Daniel of Wigan Co., Over Tabley, England. The assignment of William Daniel of Middlesex has been unproven.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Peter Daniell was one of the knights of this county for the parliament 1625, and died 18th day of April 1652, aged 68 years, and was buried at Great Budworth. Christian his wife survived, and died 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following references are considered the more reliable: Source : the original manuscripts of Sir Peter Leicester of Nether Tabley. The Leicester family were the neighbours of the Daniell's of Over Tabley for a few hundred years
2 CONC . These particular notes were dated 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Peter Daniels:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Duveen McDonald, listed sources on family sheet include: Will of James Daniel D. 8/18/1747 probated 10/4/1748, Middlesex, Virginia will Book 3 page 220.
2 CONT
2 CONT "A Generation of the Glassell Family" by Reverend Horace Hayden, 1891m /g929.264 h (DPL)
2 CONT
2 CONT "VA Historical Magazine"," Middlesex, VA, Daniel Descendants", 929.273D221m (SLC)
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Margaret Daniel8/27/1750 p 1750, Middlesex, VA will book 1745-1760 pg 138
2 CONT
2 CONT Jackie Burton of Hamilton, Ohio, Wurts Magna Carta Vol 6 page 1783
2 CONT
2 CONT 		Peter Daniels (Anna Mainwaring3, Henry Mainwaring2, Randall Mainwaring1) was born 1584 in Tabley, Cheshire, England, and died 18 APR 1652 in Cheshire, England. He was buried AFT 18 APR 1652 in Cheshire, England - Great Budworth.
2 CONC  He married Christina Grosvenor BET 1601 AND 1610 in England, daughter of Richard Grosvenor and Christina Brooke. She was born 04 NOV 1587 in Eaton, Cheshire, England, and died 1663 in England. 
2 CONT
