1 NAME Isabel /Harper/
2 GIVN Isabel
2 SURN Harper
2 _MARNM Pabodie
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 NOV 1594
2 PLAC St. Albans, Hertfordshire, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 27 APR 1667
2 ADDR
3 STAE Plymouth Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Isabel (Harper) Pabodie migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isabel Harper''' was born circa 1594 at St. Albans, Hertfordshire, England and died after 1658.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: 	  	Thomas Harper
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # John Pabodie (b ca 1585-d. 1667), son of John Pabodie and Agnes (?), in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Children: 	
2 CONT # Thomas Pabodie b. c 1612
2 CONT # Francis Pabodie b. c 1614, d. 19 Feb 1698
2 CONT # William Pabodie+ b. c 1620, d. 13 Dec 1707
2 CONT # Annis Pabodie b. c 1622
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Harper-190
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel Harper was born about 1594, probably in England. She is probably the daughter of Thomas Harper. She seems to have married John Pabodie. An abstract of John's will shows that in 1649 his wife was Isabel, his children were Th
2 CONC omas, Francis, William, and Annis Rouse, and two grandsons named John. Documented evidence for Isabel Harper is not easy to find. It is possible that she married first a Brittaine and married John Pabodie as a second husband. At t
2 CONC his point it is unclear if John pabodie had two wives named Isabel - and which order he married the wives, or if he married a widow, Isabel Harper Brittaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT A record of a marriage bond between John Paybodie of Noseley and Isabella Brittaine of Noseley in 1608 is found in Leicestershire marriage licences, being abstracts of the bonds and allegations for marriage licences, preserved in 
2 CONC the Leicester Archdeaconry Registry, 1570-1729 by Leicester (England). Archdeaconry; Hartopp, Henry, Originally published by the British Record Society, 1910 [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT At least four children born to the family. Thomas, Francis, William, and Annis (Anice) were listed in his will of 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1635, the family immigrated to New England. They seem to have traveled on the "Planter". John Pabodie has been called "of Duxbury", Massachusetts. He died there and was buried at the Myles Standish Burial Ground about April 
2 CONC 27, 1667. His wife survived him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~havens5/p23700.htm
2 CONT # [S9880] "GedCom AH 13 from Emcee on Internet. Jeanne Beauvais of Warren, MI. On a Tape as "Mayflower GedCom". AH 13 GedCom by Jeanne Beauvais , 29280 Gloede D-8, Warren, Michigan. This file is a merged file from GEDCOMS prepared
2 CONC  by: Jerry Wayne Tompkins; John A. Hansen; Jeanne Beauvais; Robert Shore; Gary Shedd. Reference used were: Susan Rosser's MAYFLOWER INCREASINGS, MAYFLOWER MARRIAGES and MAYFLOWER BIRTHS AND DEATHS vol. 1 and 2. On HD as F:gedcoms\
2 CONC AH 13", Jeanne Beauvais of Warren, MI. 
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Isabel (Harper) Pabodie (abt.1594-abt.1664)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Harper-190 : accessed 13 September 2024). cites
