1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Surname was Hewish, seen as Hussey.  No known relationship to the Hussey family of Sleaford in Lincolnshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT THE FAMILIES OF DODINGTON AND COLLIER.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his first wife he had John de Dodington, his son and heir, living 8 Hen. V., who married Mary, daughter of---Payne of Hutton, and had a son John Dodington, living 2 Rich. III,, who married Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of '''
2 CONC Oliver Hussey of Donyford''', in Wiltshire, and hod issue:-
2 CONT * 1. Richard Doddington, of whom hereafter. 
2 CONT * 2. Sir John Dodington, Knt., whose daughter and heiress Isabella married Robert Collier.  
2 CONT * 3. Thomas. 
2 CONT * 4. William . 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Father: Oliver HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Birth: ABT 1430
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Partnership with: John DODDINGTON
2 CONT
2 CONT       Marriage: ABT 1453, Of Stafford,England
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Child: Isabella DODDINGTON Birth: ABT 1457
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors of Elizabeth HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT         /-Oliver HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Elizabeth HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Elizabeth HUSSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT   =John DODDINGTON  Marriage: ABT 1453, Of Stafford,England
2 CONT
2 CONT       2 Isabella DODDINGTON
2 CONT
2 CONT         =Robert COLIERE  Marriage: ABT 1489
2 CONT
2 CONT             3 James COLIERE
2 CONT
2 CONT               =Isabella LEVESON
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Oliver Hewish, of Doniford 
2 CONT '''
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188771470822&size=large}}
2 CONT A ''Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great'' ..., Volume 4.  By John Burke.  “Huyshe, of Sand and Clysthyon.”  Page 409-416  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=6AtBAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA410&dq=pedigree%20of%20huysh
2 CONC &pg=PA410#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Doddington-3
2 CONT ##This is an interesting source of information about the Dodington/Doddington famiy: http://fmg.ac/phocadownload/userupload/scanned-sources/tpg3/pp568-575.pdf
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hussey-101 comments 
2 CONT ##A ''Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great'' ..., Volume 4.  By John Burke.  “Huyshe, of Sand and Clysthyon.”  Page 409-416  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=6AtBAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA410&dq=pedigree%20of%20huy
2 CONC sh&pg=PA410#v=onepage&q&f=false] >  “Her father Oliver is listed on page 410 as having married Johanna Avenall; Elizabeth married to John Doddington is in the paragraph about her father Oliver.”
2 CONT ##The Visitations of the County of Somerset in the Years 1531 & 1575, https://books.google.com/books?id=dyw6AQAAMAAJ by Frederick Weaver (1885) says at p569, John Dodington married "Eliz d and h of Oliver Hewish of Donniford Som"
2 CONT ##The Topographer and Genealogist, Volume 3, John Nichols (1858), https://books.google.com/books?id=Nh0IAAAAQAAJ at p21 says John Dodington married "Elizabeth Hussey, daughter and heiress of Oliver Hussey, of Donyford, in Wiltshir
2 CONC e."
2 CONT ##Archaeological papers relating to the counties of Somerset, Wilts, Hants, and Devon by William Henry Rogers (1902) https://archive.org/details/archaeologicalpa00roge addresses the Huysh/Hewish/Huyshe/Huyish family of Doniford at
2 CONC  p241/1, Oliver at p249/8, and his daughter Elizabeth who married "John Dodington of Dodington" at p251/10.
2 CONT ##In The Heraldic Visitations of Staffordshire, Elizabeth is show as the "da. and h." (daughter and heiress) of Oliver Hussey: at page 88. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=gfwcAAAAYAAJ&vq=Doddington&pg=PA88#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONC  GoogleBooks] >
