1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was Lord of the manor of Mancenden, Essex.  He also acquired the manor of Catmere Hall in Littlebury and was buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Succeeded his uncle Sir Thomas as Lord Of The Manor of Catmere Hall in Littlebury in 1443.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #''Bradbury memorial. Records of some of the descendants of Thomas Bradbury, of Agamenticus (York) in 1634, and of Salisbury, Mass. in 1638, with a brief sketch of the Bradburys of England''. Comp. chiefly from the collections of 
2 CONC the late John Merrill Bradbury, of Ipswich, Mass by Lapham, William Berry, 1828-1894, comp; Bradbury, John Merrill, 1818-1876 pg 8 , [https://archive.org/details/bradburymemorial00laph/page/8/mode/2up?view=theater&q=braughing Arch
2 CONC ive.Org] > pg 28 < [https://archive.org/details/bradburymemorial00laph/page/28/mode/2up?view=theater&q=braughing Archive.Org] >
2 CONT # At Ancestry - Historical Information - no image  William Bradbury, son of Robert Bradbury, named in an inquisition post mortem on the estate of his uncle, Sir Thomas Bradbury in 1510, then aged thirty years; named in this will h
2 CONC eir of his uncle's estate, Lord of Manor Mancendon; acquired the manor of Catmere Hall in Littlebury, Essex, in 1543, and was buried at Littlebury, June 15, 1546. Children: 1. William. 2. Phillippa, married (first) Michael Welbore
2 CONC , of Pondes in Clavering, Essex; and (second) John Barlee, of Stapleford Abbots, Essex. 3. Matthew, married Margaret Rowse, of the city of Cambridge, England.
