1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Bradbury was born about 1439 in Braughing, Hertfordshire, a younger son of William Bradbury and his wife, Elizabeth (or Margaret) Rokell.   His first and only known marriage was to the widow Joan (Leche) Bod
2 CONC ley when she was in her 40's and he was aged between 50 and 56 years.  They had no children together.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bradbury, Mercer
2 CONT
2 CONT Textile Mercer,Lord Mayor City of London
2 CONT
2 CONT Sheriff 1498-9. Mayor 1509-10. M.P. London 1495; Auditor 1509-10; Master Mercers 1508. Died 11 Jan 1510; Will (PCC 26 Bennett) 9 Jan; proved 27 Feb 1510.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Documents/aldermen_of_london.htm The Aldermen of the City of London]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A number of wealthy individuals lived locally and contributed generously to the building but a large part of the money was raised by the efforts of John Leche, who was Vicar of Walden from 1489 to 1521, and his sister Jane (Johane
2 CONC ) who married '''Thomas Bradbury, the Master of the Mercers Company in the City of London and Lord Mayor of London from 1509''' until his death early the following year.Her name lives on in Saffron Walden, of course, in the title 
2 CONC of Dame Bradbury's School in Ashdon Road These two, together with four other notable citizens of the town, created the Guild of the Holy Trinity whose history and purposes are set out in Appendix 7. it was chiefly through the work
2 CONC  of this Guild that the building of the church was carried through to its successful conclusion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.stmaryssaffronwalden.org/Publisher/File.aspx?ID=219855
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # https://archive.org/details/visitationscoun01banngoog/page/n160/mode/2up?view=theater
2 CONT #  For the will of Sir Thomas Bradbury, see TNA PROB 11/16/90. 
2 CONT # For Joan (nee Leche) Bodley Bradbury, see her will, TNA PROB 11/23/272, and the Wikipedia article edited by the author of this website.
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joan_Leche
2 CONT #The National Archives; Kew, Surrey, England; Records of the Prerogative Court of Canterbury, Series PROB 11; Class: PROB 11; Piece: 16. Ancestry.com. England & Wales, Prerogative Court of Canterbury Wills, 1384-1858 [database on-
2 CONC line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2013.
2 CONT #''Bradbury memorial. Records of some of the descendants of Thomas Bradbury, of Agamenticus (York) in 1634, and of Salisbury, Mass. in 1638, with a brief sketch of the Bradburys of England''. Comp. chiefly from the collections of 
2 CONC the late John Merrill Bradbury, of Ipswich, Mass by Lapham, William Berry, 1828-1894, comp; Bradbury, John Merrill, 1818-1876 pg 8 , [https://archive.org/details/bradburymemorial00laph/page/8/mode/2up?view=theater&q=braughing Arch
2 CONC ive.Org] > pg 28 < [https://archive.org/details/bradburymemorial00laph/page/28/mode/2up?view=theater&q=braughing Archive.Org] >
