2 DATE 1580
2 PLAC Wolverhampton, Staffordshire, , England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth was the widow of Thomas Creswell before her marriage to Leonard Ashton.(to whom????)
2 CONT
2 CONT notes
2 CONT
2 CONT * Pedigree of Aston of Tixall, in "The Heraldic Visitations of Staffordshire Made by Sir Richard St. Geoerge, Norroy, in 1614, and by Sir William Dugdale, Norroy, in the Years 1663 and 1664," ed. H. Sydney Grazebrook, in Collectio
2 CONC ns for a History of Staffordshire, vol. 5, pt. 2, publ. 1885 (London: Mitchell and Hughes), p. 18, gives: Elizabeth, da. to James Leveson of Lilleshull, co. Salop, Merchant of the Staple. 2nd wife.
2 CONT * From reference in will of James Leveson dated 8 Apr 1545, marriage ceremony had apparently taken place but marriage had not yet been consummated at that date, presumably because at least one of the couple was still a child. The 
2 CONC will stipulated that the bequests to "my sonne in Lawe Water Aston" and "my Daughter his wyffe" not be given to them "except the marriage betwixt them take effect and til they have lyne to geather" and that if the marriage was not
2 CONC  consummated, various provisions of the marriage settlement agreed between Sir Edward Aston and James Leveson would be undone.
2 CONT * inherited 27 Oct 1547 Cup of 5 pounds, gold ring and black gown, from will of father James Leveson dated 8 Apr 1545 Bequest conditional on consummation of Elizabeth's marriage to Sir Walter Aston. If the marriage did not "take e
2 CONC ffect", Elizabeth would inherit money and property that had been part of her marriage settlement, as long as she married with the consent of her mother Margery.
2 CONT
