1 NAME Jane /Clare/
2 GIVN Jane
2 SURN Clare
2 _MARNM Moore Newby
2 NICK Jane (Clare) [Bogue] [Moore] [Loadman] [Byers] Newby
2 NICK no proof of marriage to James ? Loadman.
2 NICK Jeane
2 NICK Jean Newby
2 NICK Jeane
2 NICK Jean Clare Aka Bogue Moore Loadman Byer
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1640
2 PLAC Aucheneraw, Scotland [uncertain]
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 6 AUG 1701
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT Jane Clare is often seen as the daughter of William Clare and Mary Corey, born c.1640 in Scotland however there is no documentation of this at this time. Various records have led to speculation that she is the sister of Timothy Cl
2 CONC eare. However, the frequently seen origins of Timothy Cleare are questionable as it can now be documented he came to Carolina from Maryland and prior to that possibly Nevis, West Indies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Virgil T. Bogue has speculated that she is the daughter of a Calvin Clark but does not give his reasoning.[1] Jane is also written as Jeane and Jean in numerous Perquimans records of the period.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane is believed to have had five husbands. Some have speculated about the conflation of two women (see Research Notes) but most are of the opinion that various records and circumstantial evidence point to one woman named Jane hav
2 CONC ing had five husbands over the course of her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husbands
2 CONT
2 CONT Bogue researchers Virgil T Bogue, Flora Deming Bogue, and Jean Leeper appear to be in basic agreement on the husbands:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William Bogue - only Leeper speculates on the origins of William Bogue and this is speculation absent documentation.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. William or John or __________ Moore m about 1675 according to some
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. James or ______________ Loadman - Note: the marriage to Loadman appears to have little documentation other than his name recorded in the marriage record of Jane and Richard Byer. According to Virgil T. Bogue, Jane and James wer
2 CONC e married at the time they came to North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Richard Byer m ____ of January 1682/83[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. William Newby m 6 Aug 1701[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT It should be noted that Virgil T. Bogue's writing appears to become very confused when he discusses the marriage to John Moore as at one point he writes he marries Jane Edwards, daughter of Peter Edwards of Isle of Wight whose wil
2 CONC l proved 8 Oct 1638 names her (highly unlikely a will proved 1638 names someone probably not yet born).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT With William Bogue
2 CONT
2 CONT William born say 1665
2 CONT Robert born say 1667
2 CONT Margaret born say 1669
2 CONT With ________ Moore
2 CONT
2 CONT William Moore is documented by a deed 12 Aug 1701, "Jeane Bier, widow, do give my son, Wm. Moore, a Patent of Land from me and my now husband, William Newby, after the death of both of us."[5]
2 CONT With James Loadman
2 CONT
2 CONT James who died 1694, William Bogue (his half-brother) the administrator of his estate.[6] Birth record not yet located, perhaps born in Virginia. James is also noted in a 1687 deed, "I, Jean Loadman, do give my son James, one cow 
2 CONC and calf."[7] It appears James is meant to be represented by this profile for a James Loadman however the profile may be conflating father and son of the same name (see dates).
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Conflation of two Janes? Virgil T Bogue makes note of research (1944) of Leslie R Zoellner who is said to have had records showing that Richard Byer (Baird) had two wives bearing the name of Jane: 1st, Jane Loadman, who probably m
2 CONC . 1st William Bogue, by whom she had ch., William, Robert and Margaret, and whom he m 1 Jan 1682/83 and who probably died between 1682-88; 2nd Jane Wogell (Nogell), widow of Lawrence Nogell, who d 16 Dec 1685 whom he m 8 Oct 1686,
2 CONC  and who, after the death of Richard Byer m William Newby. Virgil Bogue generally discredits this interpretation of documents with a discussion and citations in his work (see Sources) in Book II, Page 194-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawrence NOGGELL m. [ ? ] BOGUE who had 3 ch: Robert, William & Margaret, or [ ? ] MOORE m. [ ? ] BOGUE who had the 3 ch b. ca. 1665-70. Jane [ ? ] m. [ ? ] MOORE and had son William b. ca. 1670-1677. MOORE died and Jane m. Lawren
2 CONC ce NOGGELL and moved to Carolina with him and the three BOGUE children and her son William MOORE proving headrights for the same in 1694. NOGGELL died and Jane m. Richard BYER in 1686. The Bogue children were grown by then [betwee
2 CONC n ages 16 and 24], but Richard BYER still names them as Sons in law in his will written between 1686 and 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gwenbj&id=I1605
