1 NAME Timothy /Clare/
2 GIVN Timothy
2 _MARNM Clare
2 NICK Clere
2 NICK Cleare
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1660
2 PLAC Auchencrow, Berwickshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE ABT 1724
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 NOV 1724
2 PLAC Perquimans, North Carolina, British Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Timothy Clare, son of William Clare, was born in Auchencraw, Scotland, probably in the 1650’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a book entitled “Bristol and America Servants to Foreign Plantations,” Vol II, 1663-1679, (page 136), he is listed. He sailed in the middle 1660’s or early 1670’s from Bristol, England, and was bound for the Island of Nevis in 
2 CONC the West Indies, 200 miles southeast of Puerto Rico, just west of Antigua.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1674, Timothy had been transported into Maryland. Maryland Hall of Records, Annapolis, Maryland-Land Office, Liber 18, folio 105:- “23th of November 1674-Came Thomas Hassald of Cecil County, and proved his Right to 150 acres of
2 CONC  Land it being due him for Transporting himself, Thomas Davis, and Timothy Clare, into this province to Inhabit.” By 1681, Timothy Clare, with others, had removed to Albemarle, Berkeley precinct, later Perquimans County, North Car
2 CONC olina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy was married/1 about 1663 to Elizabeth ____, who was born about 1640, and died before 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married/2 on 7 June 1685, to Mary Bundy, born about 1660, daughter of William Bundy and his first wife, Elizabeth. (See: Bundy Family, Part IV)
2 CONT
2 CONT In May of 1693, in Perquimans County, North Carolina, he sat on Grand Jury, which meant he had at least 300 acres of land at this tune to qualify for Grand Jury duty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died 30 December 1694, in Perquimans County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Clare was Keeper of the Tolles Books for west Perquimans in 1698. He was Burgess for Perquimans in October 11, 1709; Justice of the Peace. He was a Quaker and wielded a strong influence in the county (Perquimans County, No
2 CONC rth Carolina) for the betterment of settlers, and the usefulness of its citizens. He owned large bodies of land in Perquimans County, North Carolina. Numerous deed transfers, and his will indicate that he was probably quite wealth
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married/3, on 1 March 1702 to Hannah Lawrence (Larance), who was born 1 December 1669, in Berkeley Precinct, North Carolina, daughter of William Lawrence and Rachel Welsh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Lawrence was born between 1614 & 1619, in Henrico County, Virginia. He was married in 1633, in Berkeley Precinct North Carolina (later Perquians Precinct, North Carolina.
2 CONT William Lawrence, son of Charles Lawrence, was born about 1629, in Berkeley Pct., North Carolina, and married in 1653, to Rachel Welch, who was born about 1633, in Berkeley Pct. Willliam died 13 Auguat 1694
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Lawrence, daughter of William Lawrence, was the widow of Israel Snelling who was born about 1669 & died 31 8mo 1700, by whom she had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Snelling, born 1690/l married to Peter Jones;
2 CONT Hester Snelling, born 17 August 1690, who married 1716 to John Winslow.
2 CONT In 1717, week-day Meetings were directed to be held at the houses of Timothy Clare and Samuel Nicholson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Clare is known to have had at least eight children: six by his first wife, including twins; one by his second wife; and one by his third wife. Dates of birth for all eight are given by the Perquimans Monthly Meeting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy died 10 of 9mo (November) 1724, the day he made his will, in Perquimans Precinct., North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT A brief abstract of the will of Timothy Clare (“Cleare”) (Archives, Raleigh, North Carolina, File No. SS844-original wills) is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Hannah
2 CONT (estate that was hers before he married her, etc.); daughter Hannah, daughter Mary Mayo (land whereon J. Pereylives, adj. Jno. Winsloe); grandson Joseph Winsloe (land whereon his father and mother now live) son-in-law Thomas Winsl
2 CONC oe (landadj. Jno. Hudson) (See Winslow Fam) said Thomas Winsloe’s two sons Timothy and Jessee Winsloe; daughter Elizabeth Winslowe (land adj. Jno. Winsloe); dau. Jane and son-in-law Thomas Jessop (land bought of brother-in-law Wil
2 CONC liam Bundey); dau. Sarah White; dau. Hepzibah Perery (Perry) (land formerly belonging to “ye Sampsones”); dau. Hannah (land bought of Jas. Perishoe and Thos. Harvey) (also land at Sanders Dock adj. John Hudson); daughter Jane and 
2 CONC son-in-law Thomas Jessop (land adj. Stephen Gibons); daus Elizabeth Winsloe and Sarah White; their sister Hannah; grandson John Robinson (his father Joseph Robinson) (land adj. Thomas Winsloe); daus. Mary Mayo, Elizabeth Winsloe, 
2 CONC Jane Jesso, Sarah, Hannah Cleare; Grandson and granddaughter John and Sarah Robinson; friend Mary Rattlife; grandson John Robinson; grandson Thomas Winsloe, Jr., and his brother Timothy Winsloe; five daughters, Mary, Elizabeth, Ja
2 CONC ne, Sarah, and Hannah. Executors: sons-in-law Thomas Jessop and Thomas Winsloe. Will signed: Timothy Cleare. Witnesses: Thomas Bagley, Smith Calla, J. Jessop. Will dated 10 November 1724; probated l7 November 1724.
2 CONT The Inventory of the Estate of Timothy Clare was taken 23 of 9mo, (November) 1724, by Gabriel Newby, William Moor, and Francis Toms, and in additional to much personal property, included five Negroes. Numerous entries in Hinshaw, 
2 CONC attest to the fact that he was a trusted and loyal Quaker, quite wealthy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Clare, twin, born 21da 12mo 1685; married/1, to Edward Mayo (2) (See Mayo Family, Part VIII, below) insert link married/2 on 3d 6mo 1726 Joseph Newby, born 27 September 1693, son of Gabriel Newby and Mary Toms. (See Newby Fam
2 CONC ily, Part II)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Clare, twin, born 21da 12mo 1685; She was of Royal descent according to the History of Perquimans County, North Carolina and Brown's Genisis to America;; married 1704, 1st/wife of Thomas Winslow, son of Timothy Winslow (
2 CONC See: Winslow Family, Part VIII )
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Clare, born 10 9mo 1687. Probably died young, unmarried
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Clare, born 14 7mo 1689; died young, unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Clare, born 22 January 1691/2; married/1 1711 Joseph Robinson of Nancemond County, Virginia; occupation cordwainer; married/2 in 1721/3 (2/wife of 3) to Thomas Jessop, who was born 14 March 1687/8 in England, son of Timothy J
2 CONC essop & Mary Jessop.
2 CONT Grandchildren:
2 CONT Sarah Robinson, born 8 November 1711, Perqumans County, North Carolina
2 CONT John Robinson, born 12 January 1713/4, Perquimans County, North Carolina
2 CONT Mary Jessop, born 16 November 1723, Perquimans County, North Crolina
2 CONT Elizabeth Jessop, born 24 August 1725, Perquimans County, North Carolina
2 CONT Jonathan Jessop, born 27 August 1733, Perquimans County, North Carolina
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Clare, born 24 December 1693; married/1 1717 John White, son of John White & first/wife Rachel, Isle of Wight County, Virginia; married/2 Jacob Elliott, son of Thomas Elliott (See Elliott Family and White Family, Part II)
2 CONT
2 CONT m/2
2 CONT Hepsabeth Clare, born 14 2mo 1702; married by 1724, 1st wife of Jacob Perry Sr. (See: Perry Family, Part VIII)
2 CONT
2 CONT m/3
2 CONT Hannah Clare, born 15 12mo 1708; married/1 1725 Benjamin Bundy, son of Caleb Bundy and Jane Maners; married/2 about 1730 Moses Elliott, son of Thomas Elliott (See Bundy Family, Part IV and Elliott Family, Part III)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT One Ladd’s Family by Ruth Kline Ladd
2 CONT
2 CONT Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy Vol.1
2 CONT
2 CONT NC Historical and Genealogical Register, 3-201
2 CONT
2 CONT Journal of North Carolina Genealogy Summer 1965 issue, p 1480-2
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "William and son Caleb and son-in-law Timothy Cleare have records established with the Nat. Soc. of Colonial Dames of America, XVII Century and Daughters of the American Colonists. All desc. of Wm. & Elizabeth Bundy are eligible t
2 CONC o join these organizations." Source: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~sharprm/bundy.htm
