1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~marshall/esmd176.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Col. Samuel Griffin; b. circa 1638 at Rappahannock Co, VA; m. Sarah at Virginia; 2nd husband; d. circa 1703.  Sarah married his brother Thomas Griffin; 1st husband
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a merchant. He resided at Rappahannock Co., VA. He resided at Northumberland Co., VA. He left a will on 2 Feb 1702 at Northumberland Co., VA; proved 15 Sep 1703.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Col. Samuel Griffin and Sarah were:
2 CONT *     2.          i. Katherine Griffin, b. 16 Mar 1664; m. Col. William                  Fauntleroy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT Griffin,Lieut Coll Saml. Will. 2 Feb 1702/3. 5 Sept 1703. of N. Co. Gentleman.
2 CONT * To Gr'son Griffin Fauntleroy the son of Wm Fauntleroy decd all land in Cherry Point Neck.
2 CONT * To Gr'son Wm Fauntleroy another son of Wm Fauntleroy decd land called Quitenneko in Richmond Co.
2 CONT * To Gr-son Morre Fauntleroy.
2 CONT * To Gr-daus Elizabeth Gwyn and Sarah Gwyn, daus of "my Son in Law" Leroy Griffin decd.
2 CONT * To dau Kath: Gwyn now wife of David Gwyn.
2 CONT * To my dau in law Winnifred Griffin widow, late wife of Leroy Griffin decd.
2 CONT * To bro in law John Hobbs of London and my dear sister Elizabeth his wife.
2 CONT * To my cozen Tho: Hewett son of my sister Mrs Eliz Hobbs. Also to Mrs Hobbs' son Jno Hewett.
2 CONT * To Kath: dau of my sister Kath: Sprigg decd. Ref to Mrs S having other children but does not name them.
2 CONT * To kinsman Coll Wm Tayloe.
2 CONT * To Hugh Campbell and Mary Thompson who were my servants.
2 CONT * To my kinsman Saml Godwin.
2 CONT * Overseers: Col Wm Tayloe and Mr Saml Godwin in VA and my coz Tho Hewett in England.
2 CONT * Witt: Wm Cornish, Wm Medcalfe, Hen Medcalfe, who y oath prove the will 5 Sept 1703.
2 CONT * Re-recorded 15 Sept 1714 by Mr Griffin Fauntleroy. 17. pp 213-215
2 CONT
2 CONT * Source:
2 CONT * Fleet, Beverley,
2 CONT * Northumbria collectanea, 1645-1720
2 CONT * Baltimore: Genealogical Pub. County, 1961, 254 pgs
2 CONT ===
2 CONT * 1713-1749 Wills-Admin Northumberland Co Va, (Lewis & Booker): Page 73
2 CONT * Griffin, Col. Samuel,(burned will)-W. W. 2 February 1702,
2 CONT * Original probate 15 September 1703, and presented to Court 15 September 1714, by Griffin Fantleroy.
2 CONT  ===
2 CONT * James Hughes 2005-06-15 09:20:39
2 CONT * Early Settlers Mass, Pa, Virginia
2 CONT * Name: .Samuel GRIFFIN
2 CONT * Given Name: .Samuel
2 CONT * Surname: Griffin
2 CONT * Sex: M
2 CONT * Birth: 1633 in Northcumbeland,Va
2 CONT * Death: 1703 in Northcumberland,Va
2 CONT * Note: Colonel in Army.Samuel married Sarah,the widow of his brother Thomas.
2 CONT * In 1662, he and George Marsh were ordered to make a treaty with Tappyoniunoun, king of the Mattapony indians,to leave their town and surrounding lands. They also had to order the English settlers in the area that settled there i
2 CONC llegally, to pay the king for their lands.
2 CONT * In 1692 he was appointed Justice of Northcumberland County.
2 CONT * In 1702, he was appointed Justice of the Peace.
2 CONT * In 1683 he was a Burgess from Northcumberland. Granted 1153 Acres in Northcumberland and 1046 Acres in Rappahannock County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage 1 Sarah GURDOU b: 1640 in Northcumberland,Va
2 CONT * Children
2 CONT * Katherine GRIFFIN b: March 16,1664 in Richmond,Va
2 CONT ===
