1 OCCU weaver, Lt. Col. of New Kent Co.
1 TITL Lt. Col
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lt. Colonel of New Kent County The first of the King and Queen County Collier family was William Collier, "Citizen and Weaver of London," who came to York County, Va.,in 1670, and later settled in New Kent County, 
2 CONC where in 1675 he appears as. lieutenant-colonel of the county militia. He is said to have been the ancestor of a numerous progeny in the counties of New Kent, King William, King and Queen and Charles City. Among his sons was Charl
2 CONC es Collier of King and Queen, born in 1660, probably in England, and died in King and Queen in 1735. He had a son John Collier (shown by will of John Collier, Jr., probated in Hanover in 1749), who was born in 1685 and died in 176
2 CONC 5.--Dates from "Colonial Families of the Southern States."
2 CONT
2 CONT William took his family and went to Virgnia where his uncle Isaac Collier was in York Co. Wm. is mentioned in York co. records in 1670. He later moved to New Kent Co. where he joined the militia as an officer. In 1675 he was named
2 CONC  Lt. Colonel of that county. Wm. and Sarah had one son born in England just before they made the trip to Va. and three more born in America. They were the ancestors of the Colliers of New Kent, Hanover, and King William Counties, 
2 CONC Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Charles (born in London 1660/married Mary Eyers, 
2 CONT *Sarah,
2 CONT *John and 
2 CONT *William Collier Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gochapman&id=I12296
2 CONT * http://www.curtisit.com/curtis/colyer/wgo3.html#I275
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William Collier was born in Hert Fort Shire, England, in 1620.  His wife, Sallie, was born in Kent in 1636 and cam to America with her husband.  Sallie died in the Virginia Colonies in 1692.
2 CONT --------------------
