2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth and Christening
2 CONT
2 CONT Christening:
2 CONT Date: 13 Sep 1635
2 CONT Place: Wrentham, , England
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT John Thurston married Mary Wood in Medfield on Oct. 4, 1660.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary had, in Medfield:[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, b. Aug. 15, 1665, died unmarried in 1744
2 CONT Mehitable, b. Sept. 9, 1667, married Eleazar Ellis in Dedham
2 CONT Hannah, b. Nov. 18, 1669
2 CONT Bethia, b. Apr. 30, 1672
2 CONT Esther, b. Jan. 23, 1674-5, married Jonathan Boyden, then John Turner
2 CONT John, b. Sept. 27, 1677, married Sarah Pierce
2 CONT Benjamin, b. June 26, 1680, died 1704
2 CONT Service to the Town
2 CONT
2 CONT John was Medfield's representative to the General Court in 1697 and 1702. He was chosen Deacon in 1699.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon John Thurston died in Medfield on Mar. 3, 1711-12. His widow Mary lived on until Nov. 23, 1726[5]
2 CONT
