2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=nfhSZxL8bTEC&lpg=RA11-PA491&ots=WuEURynuFk&dq=samuel%20morse%201639&pg=RA11-PA491#v=onepage&q=samuel%20morse%201639&f=false Historic Homes and Institutions and Genealogical and Personal .]..,
2 CONC  Volume 1 edited by Ellery Bicknell Crane
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Morse, eldest child of Joseph Morse (2), was born in Dedham, Massachusetts. 1639. He inherited part of his father's and grandfather's estate. His house built in 1663 on the knoll east of Main and Pound streets junction was 
2 CONC burned by the Indians in 1676. and was not rebuilt on that site, where the old cellar hole is or was lately visible. He built his second house near that lately of John Ord. Jr., and the old well is still in use. In 1705 he was a l
2 CONC ieutenant of militia and teacher of the school at Medfield. In 1706 he obtained leave to flow the land "near the cowpens" for a fulling mill, which was built on the site of the stone mill lately owned by Crehore. Samuel Morse was 
2 CONC selectman six years and deputy to the general court in 1707. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married:
2 CONT # 1665. Elizabeth Wood, who died in 1682.
2 CONT # 1684. Sarah Thurston, who died in 1688. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1718. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Samuel and Elizabeth (Wood) Morse were:
2 CONT # Samuel, born 1665; 
2 CONT # Elizabeth, March 21, 1668; 
2 CONT #  Hannah, August 31. 1669. died young; 
2 CONT # Ruth, March 21, 1672; 
2 CONT # Joseph, 1674; 
2 CONT # Joshua, April 2. 1677, mentioned below; 
2 CONT # Eleazer. August 10, 1680; 
2 CONT # Benoni, June 19, 1682, died 1704. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel and Sarah (Thurston) Morse were:
2 CONT #  Solomon, born 1684. died 1704; 
2 CONT # Sarah, 1686, married Isaac Bullard, of Sherborn.
