1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Medfield births: MORSE, Joshua, s. Samuell and Elizabet[torn], Apr. 2, 1677. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Elizabeth Penniman, Nov. 8, 1699 Braintree (U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900 and online family record)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Mary Paine, 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT Medfield deaths: MORSE, Joshua, Apr. 26, 1749. 
2 CONT == Summary ==
2 CONT Joshua Morse m/1  Elizabeth Penniman m/2 Mary Paine. He did not marry Mary Kingsbury!
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Joshua Morse married first Elizabeth Penniman and second Mary Paine daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Paine/6000000006719779514 Samuel Paine of Braintree] (not Mary Kingsbury), How do we know? [https://www.familysear
2 CONC ch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-1942-36089-14186-27?cc=2106411 Suffolk Deeds, Vol. 42, folio 158: 23 Mar 1723/4]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Samuel Pain of Braintrey... "in Consideration of the Love and Affection that I have to my son Joshua Morse & my daughter Mary Morse" conveys 6 acres of land "out of my homestead ... as hereafter it may be divided by my Children 
2 CONC after mine & my wifes decease".
2 CONT
2 CONT Crane states Joshua's second marriage was to the Widow Mary Paine of Braintree, who died in 1747. Morse Gen. states she was Mary Paine, dau of Samuel and Mary (Penniman) Paign. "Legislators of the Massachusetts General, 1691-1790"
2 CONC  p. 291, states he married second "Mary Paine (1680-1747) in c1709, 3/8ch;" citing Morse Gen, Braintree VR & the History of Medfield. In the Vinton Memorial (p 353), we find a Mary born in 1680 to Samuel and Mary (Pennniman) Paine
2 CONC , however, it provides no further information. Mary Paine is a cousin to Elizabeth Penniman, Joshua's first wife. The Braintree VRs do not have the marriage, and appear to have been cited because they were the source of the birthd
2 CONC ate. Source:Tilden, William S. History of the Town of Medfield, Massachusetts, 1650-1886, p. 441, appears to be older than Crane and says widow Mary Paine of Braintree. This is the stance taken in the latest sketch of this family 
2 CONC in Sprague, Waldo Chamberlain Title Genealogies of the families of Braintree, Mass., 1640-1850 : including the modern towns of Randolph & Holbrook and the city of Quincy, after the separation from Braintree in 1792-3. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tingley, p. 447 (which is wrong), says she is "Mary, widow of --- Paige and daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Eleazer-Kingsbury/6000000007454303611 Ebenezer and Esther Kingsbury], b. May 6, 1680" (presumably he means Eleaze
2 CONC r?, the birth in Dedham on 6 May 1680 is to Eleazer, who m. Esther Judson 1676 according to Dedham records). And while Abner Morse says Mary, d/o Samuel Pain and Mary Penniman, a newer Morse genealogy which is also wrong by Howard
2 CONC  Morse, says Mary Kingsbury, d/o Eleazer and Esther. But Dedham records give the death of Mary, "daughter of Eleazar & Ester Kingsbury" on 6 Jun 1717, so apparently the newer sources are wrong here. The above deed proves conclusiv
2 CONC ely that Joshua married Mary Paine and not Mary Kingsbury. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources ==
2 CONT # Sprague, Waldo Chamberlain Title Genealogies of the families of Braintree, Mass., 1640-1850 : including the modern towns of Randolph & Holbrook and the city of Quincy, after the separation from Braintree in 1792-3
2 CONT # Hon. Joshua Morse, in Morse, Abner. Memorial of the Morses: containing the history of seven persons of the name, who settled in America in the seventeenth century : with a catalogue of ten thousand of their descendants : to whic
2 CONC h are added biographical sketches of many of their number. (Boston: William Veazie, 1850), 40, 41, Questionable quality. Joshua4 Hn. wife Elizabeth married November 15, 1699: 2. Mary, born October 27, 1680, m. prior to 1707, and d
2 CONC ied March 17, 1746-7, r. Medfield. Children born after 1705: Mary 1707, Jemima 1709, Joshua 1710, Eliakim 1712, Ruth 1716, Ebenezar 1717/8, Lydia 1719, and Joseph 1721.
2 CONT #Crane, Ellery B. Historic Homes and Institutions and Genealogical and Personal Memoirs of Worcester County, Massachusetts: With a History of Worcester Society of Antiquity. (New York: Lewis Publishing Co., 1907), v 1 p 492. He (J
2 CONC oshua Morse) married (second) Widow Mary Paine, of Braintree, who died in 1747. Children born after 1705: Mary 1707, Jemima 1709, Joshua 1710, Eliakim 1712, Lydia 1714, Ruth 1716, Ebenezer 1717/8, and Joseph 1721.
2 CONT # Hon. Joshua Morse, in Cutter, William Richard, and William Frederick Adams. Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the state of Massachusetts. (New York: Lewis Historical Publishing Co., 1910), v 4 p 2275.
2 CONC  [He married] second Mary Page, widow, of Braintree, born October 27, 1680, died March 1746-47.
