1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography == 
2 CONT John Fisher (1661-1755) was born 2 Apr 1661 in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts the son of John Fisher and Elizabeth Boylston (Fisher "John s. John and Elizabeth, APR. 2 1661." Medfield Births p 51).[1][2][3][4]  He married Mary M
2 CONC etcalf daughter of Deacon Thomas Metcalf on June 8, 1683 in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts.[2] Mary Metcalf was baptized on 25 Nov 1660 in Dedham, and died in Medfield on Dec. 16, 1727.[2] She was the sister of Samuel Metcalf bo
2 CONC rn in Dedham on Sept. 17, 1668 who died in Canada in 1690.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1690 during the expedition to Canada under Captain Andrew Gardner 60 men were lost. On 4 Jun 1736 the House of Representatives of Massachusetts constructed a list of heirs of these fallen soldiers to receive land grants in cons
2 CONC ideration of the loss to their families. The Grant known as Gardner's Canada would become incorporated later as Warwick. In the third list of grantees/heirs in the proprietors records we find "Samuel Fisher of Wrentham, eldest mal
2 CONC e heir to Samuel Metcalf." Samuel Metcalf was Samuel Fisher's brother-in-law. In other words Samuel Metcalf was the brother of Samuel Fisher's wife Mary (Metcalf) Fisher and son of Deacon Thomas Metcalf 1629 - 1702. (See Roster of
2 CONC  the Expedition of 1690 to Canada, NEHGR Vol 99 1945 p 307 - 314)[2]  This information is extremely interesting in terms of the identity of Samuel Fisher's mother Mary (Metcalf) Fisher, wife of John Fisher. Mary Metcalf daughter o
2 CONC f Deacon Thomas Metcalf was baptized in Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts in 25 NOV 1660.("Mary ye daughter of of brother Thomas Metchalf was baptized 25 9 1660." p 35}[5] She was the only Mary Metcalf to have a brother Samuel Metcal
2 CONC f. Samuel Metcalf was the second of the name. He was born on 17 Sep 1668 in Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts, and died in the expedition to Canada under Captain Andrew Gardner in 1690.[2] He had no children and hence his only heir w
2 CONC as his brother-in-law Samuel Fisher who received the land grant described above.[2] This brings up two errors frequently encountered: 1) This Samuel died in 1690 not in 30 JUN 1713. The Samuel who died on 30 JUN 1713 in Dedham the
2 CONC refore had to be the young son of Thomas 1671 - 1704 and Sarah Avery i.e. his nephew. 2) The wife of John Fisher was not the Mary Metcalf daughter of John Metcalf 1622 - 1675 who was born 2 Jun 1668 in Medfiled. ("Medcalfe, Mary, 
2 CONC d. John and Mary, June 2, 1668." p 71)[1] That Mary is therefore most certainly the Mary Metcalf who married Eleazar Ellis on on 26 Oct. 1687 in Medfield[1] because she had no brother Samuel so she could not have been the wife of 
2 CONC John Fisher. These two errors are ubiquitous in the literature and on the Internet so I encourage the reader to look at these sources themselves. 
2 CONT == Children == 
2 CONT * 1.	Samuel Fisher b. 29 Sep 1685 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, Samuel, s. John Jr. and Mary, Sept. 29, 1685." Medfield Births p 52)[1][4] d.19 Jan 1769 Wrentham, Norfolk, Massachusetts,("Fisher, Samuel, Jan. 19, 1769
2 CONC ." Vol 2 p 445 Wrentham Deaths)[6] 
2 CONT * 2.	John Fisher b. 9 Sep 1687 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, John, s. John and Marie, [born] Sept. 9, 1677." Medfield Births p 51)[1][4] d. 2 Feb 1712/13 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, John, h. Rebekah, [d
2 CONC ied] Feb. 2, 1712-13." Medfield Deaths p 211.)[1] 
2 CONT * 3.	Mary Fisher b. 9 Oct 1689 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Marie, d. John and Marie, Oct. 9, 1689." Medfield Births p 51)[1][4] d. 16 Apr 1719 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Turner, Mary, w. John, [died] Apr. 
2 CONC 16, 1719." Medfield Deaths p 239).[1] 
2 CONT * 4.	Judith Fisher b. 29 Dec 1691 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Judieth, d. John and Marie, Dec. 29, 1691." Medfield Births p 51)[1][4] d. 11 May 1727 Wrentham, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Turner, Judith, w. of Stephen
2 CONC , [died] May 11, 1727" Medfield Deaths p 504). [6] 
2 CONT * 5.	Simon Fisher b. 4 Jun 1695 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Simon, s. John and Marie, June 4, 1695" Medfield Births p 52)[1][4] d. 22 Feb 1724/25 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, Simon, s. John and Mary, 
2 CONC Feb. 22, 1724-5" Medfield Deaths p 212)[1] 
2 CONT * 6.	Elizabeth Fisher b. 29 May 1697 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Elizabeth, d. John and Marie, [born] May 29 [1697]." Medfield Births p 51)[1][4] d. 27 Jan 1718/19 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, Elisabe
2 CONC th, d. John and Mary, [died] Jan. 27, 1718-19." Medfield Deaths p 211).[1] 
2 CONT * 7.	Sarah Fisher b.4 Jun 1700 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Sarah, d. John and Mary, [born] June 4, 1700." Medfield Births p 52)[1][4] 
2 CONT * 8.	Hannah Fisher b. 26 Jul 1703 Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts ("Fisher, Hannah, d. John and Mary, [born] July 26, 1703" Medfield Births p 51)[1][4]  Biography and sources by https://www.geni.com/people/Roland-Henry-Baker-III/
2 CONC 6000000028772339285
2 CONT == Sources == 
2 CONT
