2 CONT * 2. Theodore F Jones, The New England Historical & Genealogical Register: Roster of the Expedition of 1690 to Canada (Boston, MA: NEHGS, Jan 1945), Volume 99 p 312 (" 44. "Samuel Fisher of Wrentham, eldest male heir to Samuel Met
2 CONC calf." Samuel5 Fisher: b. Medfield, Sept. 29, 1685, d. Wrentham, Jan. 19, 1769, was the son of John4 Fisher, 1661-1755, and his wife Marys Metcalf (Thomas1), bpt. Dedham, Nov. 25, 1660, d. Medfield, Dec. 16, 1727, m. Medfield, Jun
2 CONC e 8, 1683. Mary2 Metcalf was the sister of Samuel2 Metcalf, b. Dedham, Sept. 17, 1668, d. in Canada."). . link
2 CONT * 3. Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, United States. Vital Records of Medfield, Massachusetts, to the Year 1850. (Boston, Massachusetts: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1903) p 52. ("Fisher, Samuel, s. John Jr. and Mar
2 CONC y, Sept. 29, 1685.")
2 CONT * 4. Philip A Fisher, The Fisher Genealogy: Record of the Descendants of Joshua, Anthony, and Cornelius Fisher, of Dedham, Mass., 1630-1640. (Everett, Mass.: Massachusetts Pub. Co., 1898) p 31. John Fisher, s/o John Fisher and Eli
2 CONC zabeth Boylston, b. Medfield 2 Apr 1661, d. 7 Nov 1755, m. (1) 8 Jun 1683 Mary Metcalf, m. (2) 1 Jul 1731 Sarah, widow of Ichabod Harding, and "probably" before that widow of Joseph Ellis of Dedham (and if so, maiden name Hemenway
2 CONC ). p 50. ("Samuel Fisher, s/o John Fisher and Mary Metcalf, b. Medfield 29 Sep 1685, d. Wrentham 19 Jan 1769, m. 16 Dec 1707 Mary Rockwood. Will dated 17 Jun 1761, probated 24 Feb 1769, son John executor, his father's widow, four 
2 CONC daughters, son Samuel, son Nathan.")
2 CONT * 5. Don Hill Gleason, A memorial volume. The record of baptisms, marriages and deaths, and admissions to the church and dismissals therefrom, transcribed from the church records in the town of Dedham, Massachusetts. 1638-1845 Als
2 CONC o all the epitaphs in the ancient burial place in Dedham, together with the other inscriptions before 1845 in the three parish cemeteries (Dedham, Mass.: Dedham Transcript Press, 1886) Vol. 2 (Also referred to as Volume to of the 
2 CONC Early Record of the town of Dedham in some genealogies) p 35 link
2 CONT * 6.  Baldwin, Thomas W. Vital records of Wrentham, Massachusetts, to the year 1850. (Boston: Stanhope Press, 1910)
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________
2 CONT *'''John Fisher
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	Apr. 2, 1661  Medfield, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT *'''Death: 	Nov. 7, 1755  Medfield, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT *'''John Fisher was born in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts on April 2, 1661. He was the son of''' John Fisher and Elizabeth Boylston. '''He wed Mary Metcalf in Medfield on June 8, 1683, in Medfield. John was a selectman six time
2 CONC s between 1699 and 1719. He also served as Coroner. In 1716 he was a delegate to the General court. John and Mary had six children''' and Mary died on December 16, 1727. '''John then married Mrs. Sarah Hemenway Harding on July 1, 
2 CONC 1731. John owned houses and land in Medway and Dedham. He owned one slave. John died in Medfield on November 7, 1755, although there is no record of his death in the town records. The only cemetery being used in Midfield at the ti
2 CONC me of John's death was Vine Lake Cemetery. That is most likely where he is buried. There are many unmarked graves in the cemetery.
2 CONT *Family links: 
