2 CONT Judith (Fisher) Turner (1691 - 1727)
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Turner formerly Fisher
2 CONT Born 29 Dec 1691 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Daughter of John Fisher and Mary (Metcalf) Fisher
2 CONT Sister of Samuel Fisher, John Fisher, Mary (Fisher) Turner and Hannah (Fisher) Morse
2 CONT Wife of Stephen Turner — married 22 Nov 1712 in Medfield, Suffolk, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Mother of Judith (Turner) Adams, Elizabeth (Turner) Morse, Stephen Turner and Ichabod Turner
2 CONT Died 11 May 1727 at age 35 in Wrentham, Suffolk, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Halsey Bullen private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 24 Aug 2023 | Created 13 Feb 2021
2 CONT This page has been accessed 65 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Fisher was born to John and Mary Metcalf Fisher on 29 Dec 1691 in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts, ("Fisher, Judieth, d. John and Marie, Dec. 29, 1691." Medfield Births p 51)[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen and Judith Turner settled in the part of Wrentham that later became Norfolk.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith died on 11 May 1727,[4] likely the consequence of an unsuccessful pregnancy. Stephen lived on, dying in Wrentham on 8 Feb 1775. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen and Judith/Judah Turner had, in Wrentham:[5] [6][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Judeth, b. 7 Nov 1714, m. Ebenezer Adams, 17 Jan 1743-4
2 CONT Hannah, b. 16 Nov 1716, died 9 Nov 1736
2 CONT Elizabeth, b. 27 Nov 1718
2 CONT Stephen, b. 1 Feb, 1720-1, m. Deborah Pond, 30 Apr 1747, died 16 Aug 1794 "in his 74th y."
2 CONT Keziah, b. 1 July 1723
2 CONT Ichabod, b. 3 Dec 1725, m. Susanna Fisher 28 Mar 1751
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
