1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/201647416/hannah-lane
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Tingley was born 16 Jun 1721 in Attleborough (as it was spelled at the time), Bristol Co., MA, the daughter of Samuel Tingley and his wife, Hannah (Pidge) Tingley (Attleborough, MA Vital Records, p. 266).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Tingley, of Attleborough, married Elkanah Lane, of Norton, MA on 10 Jun 1742 (Attleborough, MA Vital Records, p. 581).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah (Tingley) Lane died in Norton, MA on 15 Sep 1772, in her 52nd year (Norton, MA Vital Records, p. 380).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Lane is said to have been buried in the Norton Common Cemetery in Norton, Bristol Co., MA. Unfortunately, no grave marker for her remains. A historical marker at the cemetery notes, "Using this land for public use, a militi
2 CONC a training field, and burying place caused many problems, for in 1802, it was noted "The four-footed beasts that were turned loose upon the common trampled upon the green sod that covered the loved of earth , (un)till the exact re
2 CONC sting place of many was obliterated."
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT No discernable inscribed gravestone for Hannah (Tingley) Lane remains at the cemetery.
