1 NOTE {geni:about_me} April 7, 1748;  "To the Honorable Samuel Danforth Esq Judge of Probate  This may certifie that the subscribed Martha Phips widow and relict of John Phips late of Sherborn deceased am satisfied and content with the 
2 CONC sum of 200 pounds old tenor in stead of my dower in this estate and stand ready to discharge said estate on payment of said sum aforesaid  as witness my hand 
2 CONT
2 CONT                                                                                   Martha                                                                Her mark         M                                                            
2 CONC                          Phips
2 CONT
2 CONT Sherborn April seven seventeen hundred and forty eight. "In the 1916 map of Central Burying Ground there is a Fairbanks grouping of stones:  Capt. Eleazer Fairbanks, Mrs. Martha Phipps, daughter Abigail Fairbanks, and daughter Deb
2 CONC orah and her husband, plus some unnamed stones.  (Martha and the unnamed stones have unfortunately disappeared.)  Copies of that graveyard by historian Frank Bardwell in 1883 include:  "Martha Fairbanks Phipps, wife of John Phipps
2 CONC  (formerly wife of Eleazer Fairbanks)" (but no death date)"  provided by Sherborn Town historian Betsey Johnson, 1997.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Aft. 1743, moved to Brookfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT She does not appear as widow of John Phips of Sherborn in any of the published genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~walkersj/Marthabullard.htm
