1 TITL Sgt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Webster, son of John Webster of Ipswich and Mary, after his father's death moved with the family to Newbury, where he married Anna Batt.  
2 CONT 8 Children :  
2 CONT # John, 3 b. February 11, 1656
2 CONT # Mary, 3 b. March 29, 1658, d May 4, 1658
2 CONT # Sarah, 3 b. July 1, 1659. 
2 CONT #Abigail, 3 b. March 16, 1662. 
2 CONT # Lucy, 3 b. December 19, 1664.
2 CONT # Mary,3b.May24,1667.
2 CONT #Anna,3 b. September 7, 1671 
2 CONT # Nicholas, b. October 9, 1673. He graduated at Harvard College in 1695, and was a minister in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sgt. John Webster: Alternative birth year: 1632 Alternative death year: 1714 Alternative Death location: Ipswich, Essex, MA  
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation:  Blacksmith.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39655386/john-webster John Webster II]
2 CONT BIRTH	1632 Suffolk, England
2 CONT DEATH	18 Oct 1716 (aged 83–84) Newburyport, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	39655386 · View Source 
2 CONT 3em>This death date is the same as his wife's, and cannot be confirmed as yet. Is it possible they died the same day from illness?  
2 CONT 3em>John was the son of John Webster I & Mary Shatswell. John Webster immigrated to New England in 1633/1634 with his parents and one older sister, Mary. After first residing in Boston, they soon moved to Newbury (port) and by the
2 CONC  time young John was about 10, the family had settled at Ipswich, Massachusetts. John was about 14 years old when his father died and being the oldest son of eight children presumably assumed some family responsibilities. Except f
2 CONC or a period of about 4 years between 1653 and 1657, John and his family lived in Newburyport, Massachusetts.  
2 CONT 3em>He married Anne Newburg Batt on June 13, 1653 in Newbury, Essex County, Massachusetts. She was daughter of Nicholas Batt. To this union, 9 children were born:  
2 CONT 1 John
2 CONT 2 Mary
2 CONT 3 Sarah
2 CONT 4 Abigail
2 CONT 5 Lucy
2 CONT 6 Stephen
2 CONT 7 Anna
2 CONT 8 Nicholas
2 CONT 9 Jonathan  
2 CONT 3em>John Webster was a Sargeant in Captain Thomas Noyes Co., Newbury in King Philip's War. Savage mentions that Col. Rec.IV 362 and related in Coffin that he was in military trouble at some time. 
2 CONT 3em>John moved to Newbury from Ipswich after his father's death, later to Haverhill where he was the second blacksmith in the town. He moved back to Newbury later, which is where he probably died. He and his wife were married for 
2 CONC 63 years.
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT John Webster 1605–1646 
2 CONT Mary Shatswell Webster Emery 1606–1694 
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Anne Newburg Batt Webster 1630–1716 (m. 1653) 
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT Hannah Webster Emerson 1635–1707 
2 CONT Elizabeth Webster Simmons 1640–1694 
2 CONT Abigail Webster Merrill 1642–1712 
2 CONT Israel Webster 1643–1683 
2 CONT Half Siblings
2 CONT Nathan Webster 1646–1694 
2 CONT Jonathan Emery 1652–1723 
2 CONT Hannah Emery Bartlett 1654–1705 
2 CONT John Emery 1656–1730
2 CONT
