1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mighill-17
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mighill, son of Thomas Mighill and Ellen Ward, was born ca. 1634 at Rowley and married 6 June 1659 at Newbury, MA Sarah, b. 12 June 1640 at Newbury, dau. of Nicholas and Lucy (__) Batt. He lived for a while at Oyster River in
2 CONC  town of Dover, NH, later at Newbury and died 1702 at Suffield, Hartford Co., CT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Mighill & Sarah Batt:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John, b. ca. 1660; m. Elizabeth Ferrman
2 CONT # Thomas, b. ca. 1662; m. 1st Abigail McLaflin, 2nd Joanna__.
2 CONT # Sarah, b. ca. 1664; living 1674.
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b. ca. 1666; m. John Warner.
2 CONT # Mary, b. 2 June 1668.
2 CONT # Samuel, b. ca. 1670; m. Sarah Rawlings.
2 CONT # Nathaniel, b. ca. 1672; m. Sarah Bliss.
2 CONT # Nicholas, b. ca. 1674; m. Dorothy Ferman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Dutchess County, NY: The Settlers of the Beekman Patent (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2016), (Orig. Pub. by Frank J. Doherty, Pleasant Valley, NY. Frank J. Doherty, The Settl
2 CONC ers of the Beekman Patent, Dutchess County, New York: An Historical and Genealogical Study of All the 18th Century Settlers in the Patent, ten volumes. 1990–2003).  Page 805-806.  [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB409/rd/13283/
2 CONC 805/236150717 AmericanAncestors]
