1 NAME John /Stanley/ Esq.
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Stanley
2 NSFX Esq.
2 _MARNM Stanley
2 NICK John Stanley of Weever and Over Alderley jure uxoris; John Stanley of Hooton
1 NAME Sir John Stanley of Weever & Over Alderly
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Clifton, Cheshire, England
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1440
2 ADDR
3 CITY Over Alderley
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1476 AND 1485
2 PLAC Tower Of London
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU Bro. of Thomas, Earl of Derby, descent from Edward I, and Henry I
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stanley''' 
2 CONT * Birth:  circa 1425 in Over Alderley, Cheshire, England
2 CONT * Death: between 1476 and 1485
2 CONT * Parents: Sir Thomas Stanley, Joan Goushill
2 CONT * Wife: Elizabeth Weaver (her 1st husband 
2 CONT * Children: 3 sons (John; Thomas, Esq; & George) and 5 daughters (Cecily, wife of Thomas Venables, Esq; Margery, wife of Sir William Torbock; Anne, wife of Ralph Ravenscroft, Esq; Jane, wife of Thomas Hawarden, Esq; & Cecily, wife
2 CONC  of Hugh Davenport, Esq.)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cheshirenow.co.uk/stanley_family.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/visitationofches00glov#page/216/mode/2up
2 CONT ===============================================================
2 CONT *5.  John Stanley, of Weever and Over Alderley, co. Chester jure uxoris, living 29 March 1470 but d. before 1485, third son of Thomas Stanley, Knt., Lord Stanley, by Joan, daughter of Robert Goushill, Knt., of Hoveringham.[10] He 
2 CONC m. (as her first husband) after 1445, Elizabeth de Weever, heiress of Weever, in the parish of Middlewich, co. Chester, d. 17 Feb. 1512/3.[11] She m. (2) John Done, Knt., of Utkinton.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Jure uxoris is a Latin term that means "by right of his wife" or "in right of a wife".[1] It is commonly used to refer to a title held by a man whose wife holds it in her own right. Similarly, the husband of an heiress could beco
2 CONC me the possessor of her lands jure uxoris, "by right of [his] wife". Jure uxoris monarchs are not to be confused with kings consort, who were merely consorts of their wives, not co-rulers.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Ormerod's [http://books.google.com/books?id=7kEjAQAAMAAJ&vq=Weever&pg=PA113#v=onepage&q&f=false The history of the county palatine and city of Chester:] page 113:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Thomas de Weever married Elizabeth, daughter of .... By her he had issue Elizabeth, daughter and heiress, wife of '''sir John Stanley''', a younger son of Thomas, the first lord Stanley, to whom king Henry VI. a° 24, gave the dis
2 CONC posal of her in marriage as his ward; she remarried sir John Done of Utkinton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ========================================================
2 CONT *'''John Stanley, Esq.1,2,3,4,5
2 CONT *'''M, #44557, b. circa 1425, d. between 1476 and 1485
2 CONT *Father     Sir Thomas Stanley, Lord Lieutenant of Ireland, Lord of Latham and Knowsley, 1st Lord Stanley, Constable & Justice of Chester1,2,3,6,5 b. c 1405, d. 11 Feb 1459
2 CONT *Mother     Joan Goushill1,2,3,6,5 b. c 1401, d. c 27 Apr 1466
2 CONT *'''     John Stanley, Esq. was born circa 1425 at of Over Alderley, Cheshire, England; 3rd son.1 He married Elizabeth Weaver, daughter of Thomas Weaver, Esq. and Elizabeth, after 1446; They had 3 sons (John; Thomas, Esq; & George
2 CONC ) and 5 daughters (Cecily, wife of Thomas Venables, Esq; Margery, wife of Sir William Torbock; Anne, wife of Ralph Ravenscroft, Esq; Jane, wife of Thomas Hawarden, Esq; & Cecily, wife of Hugh Davenport, Esq.).1,2,3,4,5 John Stanle
2 CONC y, Esq. died between 1476 and 1485.1,3,5
2 CONT *'''Family      Elizabeth Weaver b. c 1440, d. 17 Feb 1513
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Cecily Stanley+1 b. c 1460, d. 1514
2 CONT **Margery Stanley+1,3,5 b. c 1466
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 490.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 679.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 126.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 91.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 25.
2 CONT * 6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 90.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1483.htm#i44557
2 CONT *______________
2 CONT *'''Sir John Stanley1
2 CONT *M, #14628
2 CONT *Last Edited=6 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT *'''     Sir John Stanley was the son of Sir Thomas Stanley, 1st Lord Stanley and Joan Goushill.1 He married Elizabeth Weever, daughter of Sir Thomas Weever.1
2 CONT *'''      He was an ancestor of the Barons Stanley of Alderley.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Stanley_of_Alderley
2 CONT
2 CONT The Stanley Baronetcy, of Alderley Hall in the County of Chester, was created in the Baronetage of England in 1660 for the barrister Thomas Stanley. He was a descendant of the '''Hon. Sir John Stanley, third son of Thomas Stanley'
2 CONC '', 1st Baron Stanley (whose eldest son was created Earl of Derby in 1485). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1101. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1463.htm#i14628
2 CONT *____________
2 CONT *'''John STANLEY (Sir)
2 CONT *'''Born: 1436, Weever, Alderley, Chester, England 
2 CONT *'''Died: ABT 1485
2 CONT *Father: Thomas STANLEY (Knight Lord of Lathom)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan GOUSHILL
2 CONT *'''Married: Elizabeth WEEVER (b. ABT 1438 - d. 1515) (dau. of Sir Thomas Weever and Elizabeth Fitton) (w. of Sir John Done)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John STANLEY of Melling
2 CONT **2. Thomas STANLEY (Esq.)
2 CONT **3. Ralph STANLEY
2 CONT **4. William STANLEY
2 CONT **5. Ellen STANLEY
2 CONT **6. Anne STANLEY
2 CONT **7. George STANLEY
2 CONT **8. Cecily STANLEY
2 CONT **9. Margery STANLEY
2 CONT **10. Jane STANLEY
2 CONT **¿11. Thomas STANLEY?
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY5.htm#John STANLEY (Sir)1
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT
