2 CONT JOHN STANLEY John Stanley, Esq., son of Sir Thomas Stanley, Lord Lieutenant of Ireland, Lord of Latham and Knowsley, 1st Lord Stanley, Constable & Justice of Chester and Joan Goushill.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The manor of Over Alderley came into the Stanley family when heiress Elizabeth Weever married John Stanley, a brother of the Earl of Derby." 
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alderley_Park
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stanley "became the founder of the Alderley line of Stanley family. He married Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of Thomas de Weever of Weever and Alderley." 
2 CONT http://www.cheshirenow.co.uk/stanley_family.html
2 CONT
2 CONT By his daughter Anne and Ralph Ravenscroft, 16th Great-grandfather to Diana, Princess of Wales (Lady Diana Spencer), and 17th Great-grandfather to Prince William 
2 CONT https://famouskin.com/famous-kin-chart.php?name=52600+john+stanley&...
2 CONT
2 CONT Elder brother of 82201765 Thomas Stanley, 1st Earl of Derby; and 150289118 William Stanley. Birth order as per Cheshire Now - Stanley family pages online (link above in biography). An oft-seen birthdate 1425 fits with this informa
2 CONC tion. Other sites position John as the third son. Research required.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stanley of Weever 
2 CONT Visitations of Cheshire, 1580 
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/visitationofches00glov/page/215/mode/1u...
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Weever 
2 CONT Weever of Middlewich 
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyp02orme/page/112/mode/1u...
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Weever, daughter of Thomas Weever. 
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Weever-2
2 CONT
2 CONT After John Stanley died, his widow Elizabeth Weever married John Done, Kt.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stanley, Esquire, in right of his wife, of Weever and Over Alderly, Cheshire 
2 CONT Son of Sir Thomas Stanley, 1st Baron Stanley, and Joan Goushill, daughter of Robert Goushill, Knight of Hoveringham. 
2 CONT Married Elizabeth Weever after 1445/6. 
2 CONT Daughters: 
2 CONT • Cecily (Stanley) Venables 
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Venables 
2 CONT • Margery (Stanley) Torbock 
2 CONT married William Torbock 
2 CONT • Anne (Stanley) Ravenscroft (died 1579) 
2 CONT Wife of Ralph Ravenscroft 
2 CONT "Anne 3d d. to John Stanley brother to Thos Earle of Darby." Anne and Ralph Ravenscroft are direct ancestors of Diana, Princess of Wales. 
2 CONT • Jane (Stanley) Hawarden 
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Hawarden
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Weever) Stanley married second, John Done, Kt. 
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Done-6
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Stanley, 1st Baron Stanley 
2 CONT Thomas Stanley, 1st Baron Stanley, son of Sir John Stanley and Elizabeth Harrington, served as Lord Lieutenant of Ireland from 1431 to 1436 and was appointed comptroller of the royal household by Henry VI in 1432. Married Joan Gou
2 CONC shill, daughter and coheiress of Sir Robert Goushill and Elizabeth FitzAlan, daughter of Richard Fitzalan, 11th Earl of Arundel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Stanley (Wikipedia) 
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Stanley,_2nd_Earl_of_Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT STANLEY 
2 CONT Thomas Stanley, son of Sir John Stanley and Joan Goushill, born circa 1435, inherited his father's titles, including that of King of Mann and Baron Stanley. Stanley owned what is now Tatton Park in Cheshire. He married, firstly El
2 CONC eanor, sister of Richard Neville, Earl of Warwick and secondly to Lady Margaret Beaufort, the mother of Henry VII, as his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created Earl of Derby after playing a decisive part in the Battle of Bosworth field, which placed his step-son and the Tudor dynasty on the throne of England and is reputed to have retrieved the crown of England from the ba
2 CONC ttlefield and placed it on the head of his own stepson. His brother William Stanley was later convicted of treason and executed by Henry VII for his support of the pretender Perkin Warbeck. Thomas and William's elder brother, Sir 
2 CONC John Stanley, became the founder of the Alderley line of Stanley family. He married Elizabeth, daughter and heiress of Thomas de Weever of Weever and Alderley.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family resided at Weever for several generations, but Sir John's great-grandson Thomas Stanley, High Sheriff of Cheshire in 1572, made Alderley the main family seat. He re-built the old halls both of Weever and Alderley. The h
2 CONC all was situated in the village of Nether Alderley close to the mill. It was surrounded by a moat, which was crossed by a stone bridge. He was the first member of the family to be buried at Alderley. An alabaster monument in Nethe
2 CONC r Alderley Church, depicts him in armour, with his four children at his feet. 
2 CONT http://www.cheshirenow.co.uk/stanley_family.html
2 CONT
2 CONT MARGERY (STANLEY) TORBOCK 
2 CONT • Second daughter of John Stanley and Elizabeth Weever. 
2 CONT • As widow of John Stanley, Margery's mother Elizabeth Weever married John Done, Knight. 
2 CONT • Margery Stanley (daughter of John Stanley and Elizabeth Weever) was the wife of Sir William Torbock, Knight. 
2 CONT • Margery Stanley and William Torbock are my ancestors, in the line to Durien "Duren" Tinker. 
2 CONT SOURCES - Sir William Torbok, Knight and Margery Stanley: 
2 CONT 1) Ormerod, George; Peter Leycester; William Smith; William Webb; and Thomas Helsby. The history of the county palatine and city of Chester: compiled from original evidences in public offices, the Harleian and Cottonian mss., paro
2 CONC chial registers, private muniments, unpublished ms. collections of successive Cheshire antiquaries, and a personal survey of every township in the county, incorporated with a republication of King's Vale Royal and Leycester's Ches
2 CONC hire antiquities. (London: G. Routledge, 1882) 
2 CONT Volume 3 page 577.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Faris, David. Plantagenet ancestry of Seventeenth-Century colonists: the descent from the later Plantagenet Kings of England, Henry III, Edward I, Edward II, and Edward III, of emigrants from England and Wales to the North Amer
2 CONC ican colonies before 1701. (Baltimore [Maryland]: Genealogical Pub. Co., c1996) page 236.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Earwaker, J. P. (John Parsons). East Cheshire, past and present, or, A history of the hundred of Macclesfield in the county Palatine of Chester - from original records. (London: Printed for the Author, 1878-1880)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery Stanley, second daughter of John Stanley and Elizabeth Weever. Margery Stanley married Sir William Torbock, Knight. William Torbock (son-in-law of John Stanley and Elizabeth Weever) in Book of Knights: "Other Knightes made
2 CONC  in Scotlande by George, Lord Strange, beinge there with Thomas, Erle of Surrey, Anno 13 of the Kinge's reigne: Sir William Terbuke" 
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/bookofknightsban00metcuoft/page/31/mode...
2 CONT
2 CONT William Torbock, Knight of Tarbock, Lancashire, was born about 1464, the second son of Sir Richard de Torbock and Elizabeth Daniell, daughter of Thomas Daniell, of Wigan. His older brother, Sir Henry Torbock, died in 1489, leaving
2 CONC  William to inherit. William Torbock married Margery Stanley, daughter of Elizabeth Weever and John Stanley, Esquire of Weever and Over Alderley, Cheshire, about January of 1489/90. 
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT Thomas Torbock 
2 CONT Henry Torbock 
2 CONT Richard Torbock 
2 CONT Mary / Maud Torbock (married name Dutton)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Torbock was knighted by George Stanley, Lord Strange, in 1497.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Torbock, Knight died 5 May 1505.
2 CONT
2 CONT ——————
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stanley's widow Elizabeth Weever married John Done, Kt. 
2 CONT Land lease by Elizabeth Weever and John Done, Kt. 
2 CONT Reference: 
2 CONT DVE/1/M IV/31 
2 CONT Description: 
2 CONT Lease by "John Donne Knight and Dame Elizabeth his wife daughter and heir to Thoms Wevr Lord of Wever" to "Wylliam Wev son of Edwarde Wevre Knight" of a messuage (bounded). Witness (int. al.) Wyllia Venables Baron of Kynderton Tho
2 CONC mas Venables son & heir apparent of the said Wylliam and Hary Vernon. 
2 CONT Date: 
2 CONT 28. June. 2. Hen.VII 
2 CONT Held by: 
2 CONT Cheshire Archives and Local Studies, not available at The National Archives 
2 CONT https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/fb5df84a-1796-4...
2 CONT
2 CONT • Sometimes called knight, but this confuses him with a later John Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Elder brother, according to the Stanley website. Other sites say he was a third son. This John inherited the Weever estates of his wife Elizabeth. Possibly this John Stanley was in fact his own father's elder son; and because th
2 CONC is John took the Weever estates, John's younger brother was the father's heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Ancestorium website 
2 CONT https://ancestorium.com/tng/getperson.php?personID=I012126&amp;tree=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Weaver, born circa 1440 at Wever, Cheshire, England. Married John Stanley, Esq., son of Sir Thomas Stanley, Lord Lieutenant of Ireland, Lord of Latham and Knowsley, 1st Lord Stanley, Constable & Justice of Chester and Jo
2 CONC an Goushill, (married "after 1446"); Three sons (John; Thomas, Esq; & George) and five daughters (Cecily, wife of Thomas Venables, Esq; Margery, wife of Sir William Torbock; Anne, wife of Ralph Ravenscroft, Esq; Jane, wife of Thom
2 CONC as Hawarden, Esq; & Cecily, wife of Hugh Davenport, Esq.). Elizabeth Weaver married Sir John Done, son of Sir John Done and Elizabeth Dutton, before 28 June 1487; Two sons (Richard, Esq; & William) and three daughters (Ellen, wife
2 CONC  of David Middleton, of Piers Holland, & of Urian Brereton; Mary, wife of Richard Bruen, Esq; & Joan, wife of Tochet Beeston, Esq.). Elizabeth Weaver died on 17 February 1513 at of Utkinton, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stanley 
2 CONT Living in 1476. 
2 CONT Died by 1485, the year his wife Elizabeth Weever remarried.
2 CONT
