1 NAME William de Venables of Goldborne and Kinderton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1439
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kinderton, Cheshire Golborne Moston
3 STAE England
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1493
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1. William de Venables of Goldborne and Kinderton, son and heir of Thomas, had the barony and lands of Kinderton settled on him by Henry Venables, 3 Edw IV, see emboldened above. He was a prisoner in Chester Castle
2 CONC  1-2 Edw IV, died 8 Hen VII.   He married twice but there was no issue from his second wife, Katherine, dau and coheiress of Robert Grosvernor of Hulme and widow of Richard Wynynton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/venables.html
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/G3BG-R2L
2 CONT Brief Life History of William'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Sir William Venables was born in 1439, in Kinderton, Cheshire, England, his father, Thomas de Venables, was 36 and his mother, Margaretha Stanley, was 32. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Petronelle Caverswall in 1458, in Over Alderley, Cheshire, England. They were the parents of at least 2 daughters and 3 sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the birth of his last child with Petronelle, he remarried Catherine Grosvenor, with whom he had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1493, in the Battle of Braxton at Lancashire, England, United Kingdom, at the age of 54, and was buried in Lancashire, England.
