1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stanley-49
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel was the daughter of Sir William Stanley[1] [2] of Hooton. "The Sequestration Papers of Thomas Pigott of Chetwynd" record Isabel's given name as Mabel.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT >On 7th day before the Kalends of September, 1424, which was 26 August, at Frascati, Pope Martin V issued a mandate to the bishop of Lichfield, to dispense Robert de Legh, donsel, and Isabel Stanley, daughter of William Stanley, k
2 CONC night, of his diocese, to contract and solemnize marriage notwithstanding an impediment of quasi-affinity (impedimentum publice honestatis justicie) arising from the fact that Robert, when in or about his fifth year, and the late 
2 CONC Isabel Savage (related to the above Isabel Stanley in the second degree of kindred), when in her seventh year, contracted espousals, Isabel Savage dying after cohabiting for eight years with Robert.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel was the second wife of Robert de Legh of Adlington, and they married sometime after 26 August, 1424.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Legh, esq. of Adlington, wedded, first, Isabella, daughter of John Savage, of Clifton, by whom he had no issue; and, secondly, '''Isabella, daughter of Sir William Stanley, knt. of Hooton'''; by whom he had,
2 CONT
2 CONT *  i. Robert, his heir. Robert Leigh, married Ellin, daughter of Sir Robert Booth of Dunham, he died 8 January, 2 Henry VI,[2] which was 1424;
2 CONT * I. Margaret, m. first, to Thomas Mere, of Mere; and, secondly, to Robert Reddish, of Catteral. 
2 CONT * II. '''Margery, m. to William Davenport, esq. of Bramall'''. 
2 CONT * ill. Isabel, m. first, to Laurence Warren, esq. of Poynton ; and, secondly, to Sir George Holford, of Holford. 
2 CONT * iv. Matilda, in. to John Mainwaring, esq. of Peover. 
2 CONT * v. Agnes, m. to Sir Andrew Brerelou, of Brereton. 
2 CONT * VI. Ellen, was married to John Pigot of Chetwynd, Shropshire,[3] (— wife of — Picott of Chetwind[2]); to Pigott, esq. of Chetwynd, Salop. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Legh was I. at his decease (inq. p. m. 18 Edward IV.) by his son, Robert Legh, esq. of Adlington
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Pedigree
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stanley03.php Stirnet: ‘Stanley03’] 
2 CONT * Sir William de Stanley of Stourton, Stanley and Hooton (b 1368, d 1428) m. (1386) Margery de Hooton (dau/heir of William de Hooton of Hooton (by Margaret, dau/heir of John Leftwich of Leftwich), son of Sir William of Hooton)
2 CONT **1.	Sir William Stanley (b 1387, dvp 1417) 	m. (1402) Blanche (or Margaret) Arderne (dau of Sir John Alderne of Aldford and/or Hardin)
2 CONT *** 	E.	Isabel Stanley	m. Robert Legh of Adlington (b 1409, d 1478)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ll/leigh01.php#link5 Stirnet: Leigh01’]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * i.	Robert Legh of Adlington (b 1386)	m. Maud
2 CONT **	a.	Robert Legh of Adlington (b 1409, d 1478) 	m1. (sp) Isabella Savage (dau of Sir John Savage of Clifton)	m2. '''Isabella Stanley''' (dau of Sir William Stanley of Hooton)
2 CONT *** 	(1)	Robert Legh of Adlington m. Ellen Booth (dau of Sir Robert Booth of Dunham Massey)
2 CONT *** 	(2)	Maud Legh 	m. (John) Mainwaring of Over Peover (d 08.07.1495)
2 CONT *** 	(3)	Agnes Legh 	m. Sir Andrew Brereton of Brereton
2 CONT ***(4)	(Ellen?) Legh 	m. (Thomas?) Picott of Chetwind
2 CONT *** 	(5)	Margaret Legh 	m. Thomas Mere of Mere
2 CONT *** 	(6)	Isabel Legh	m1. Sir Lawrence Warren of Pointon (d 1474)  	m2. Sir George Holford
2 CONT *** 	(7)	Margery (probably not Margaret) Legh 	m. William Damport of Bromhall
2 CONT
