1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Agnes Legh 
2 CONT *'''F, #44398, b. circa 1445
2 CONT *Father      Robert Legh, Esq. b. 3 May 1410, d. 29 Jan 1479
2 CONT *Mother     Isabella Stanley
2 CONT *'''     Agnes Legh was born circa 1445 at of Adlington, Cheshire, England. She married Sir Andrew Brereton, son of Sir William Brereton and Philippa Hulse, circa 1459.
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Andrew Brereton b. c 1440
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Elizabeth Brereton+ b. c 1470
2 CONT **Sir William Brereton+ b. 1473
2 CONT **Ellen Brereton+ b. c 1477, d. 22 Sep 1541 
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1477.htm#i44398 ____________________
2 CONT *'''Agnes Leigh was born in 1456 at Adlington, Cheshire, England.1 She was the daughter of Robert Leigh and Isabel Stanley.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Agnes Leigh and Andrew Brereton
2 CONT **1.Ellen Brereton+1 b. 1477, d. 22 Sep 1541
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p20870.htm#i208696 _____________________
2 CONT *Isabel STANLEY 
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1435, Hooton, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Father: William STANLEY
2 CONT *Mother: Alicia HOUGHTON 
2 CONT *Married: Robert LEIGH 
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **'''1. Agnes LEIGH 
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY4.htm ________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 3 By John Burke Pg.453-457
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=yshsAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA454&lpg=PA454&dq=Robert+Legh+stanley&source=bl&ots=rdUuPvqvS0&sig=TTmd3ucv2Ompo9S-jzDWz0SDEEc&hl=en&ei=gVT9S-TrL4nONLOh0N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CB8Q6AEwBD
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=Robert%20Legh%20stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 454
2 CONT *   ROGERT LEGH, esq. of Adlington, wedded, first, Isabella, daughter of John Savage, of Clifton, by whom he had no issue; and, secondly, Isabella, daughter of Sir William Stanley, knt. of Hooton; by whom he had,
2 CONT **	I. ROBERT, his heir.
2 CONT **	I. Margaret, m. first to Thomas Mere, of Mere; and secondly to Robert Reddish, of Catteral.
2 CONT **	II. Margery, m. to William Davenport, esq. of Bramall.
2 CONT **	III. Isabel, m. first, to Laurence Warren, esq. of Poynton; and, secondly, to Sir George Holford, of Holford.
2 CONT **	IV. Matilda, m. to John Mainwaring, esq. of Peover.
2 CONT **'''	V. Agnes, m. to Sir Andrew Brereton, of Brereton.
2 CONT **	VI. ___ m. to ___ Pigott, esq. of Chetwynd, Salop.
2 CONT *Robert Legh was s. at his decease (inq. p. m. 18 Edward IV.) by his son,
2 CONT **   ROBERT LEGH, esq. of Adlington, who m. Ellen dau. of Sir Robert Booth, of Dunham-Massey, and had six sons and five daughters, namely, ______________________
2 CONT *Alice SAVAGE
2 CONT *Father: John SAVAGE (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Dorothy VERNON
2 CONT *Married: William BRERETON (son of '''Andrew Brereton and Agnes Leigh''') ABT 1488, Clifton, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. William BRERETON (b. 1506) (m. Anne Booth)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SAVAGE.htm#Alice SAVAGE5 ________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * John Paul Rylands, ed., The visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580 etc, (London: Harleian Society, 1882), pp.147-8. https://archive.org/stream/visitationofches00glov#page/148/mode/2up
2 CONT * “Hand-list of the Legh of Booths Charters in the John Rylands Library”. By F. Taylor, M.A., PhD, Keeper of Manuscripts and Assistant Librarian in the John Rylands Library. Page 247.  < [https://www.keele.ac.uk/media/k-web/k-cent
2 CONC ral-services/libraries/specialcollections/pdfs/keeleleghofboothshandlist.pdf PDF] > 
