1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sir Randall Mainwaring1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9
2 CONT *'''M, #10995, b. circa 1495, d. 6 September 1557
2 CONT *Father      Sir John Manwaring, Sheriff of Flintshire2,10,9 b. c 1470
2 CONT *Mother     Katherine Honford2,10,9 b. c 1472, d. 1529
2 CONT *'''     Sir Randall Mainwaring was born circa 1495 at of Over Peover, Cheshire, England.2,5,9 He married Elizabeth Brereton, daughter of Sir Randle Brereton, Chamberlain of Chester and Eleanor Dutton, circa 1518; They had 3 daugh
2 CONC ters (Margaret, wife of Sir Arthur Mainwaring; Elizabeth, wife of Peter Shakerley, Esq., & of Christopher Holford, Esq; & Katherine, wife of John Davenport, Esq.).2,3,4,5,7,8,9 Sir Randall Mainwaring left a will on 30 November 154
2 CONC 5.2,5,9 He married Elizabeth Leycester, daughter of Ralph Leycester and Ellen Legh, in 1551; They had no issue.2,5,9 Sir Randall Mainwaring died on 6 September 1557 at Over Peover, Cheshire, England.2,5,9
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Elizabeth Brereton d. bt 30 Nov 1545 - 1551
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Katharine Mainwaring2
2 CONT **Margaret Mainwaring+11,2,4,5,6,8,9 b. c 1521, d. b 2 Sep 1590
2 CONT **Elizabeth Manwaring+2 b. c 1535, d. a 1601
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Elizabeth Leycester 
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S2802] Unknown author, Plantagenet Ancestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 1, 208; Burke's Dormant and Extinct Baronetcies, p. 335.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 557.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 309.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 94.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 279.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 106-107.
2 CONT * 7.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 522.
2 CONT * 8.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 2.
2 CONT * 9.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 283.
2 CONT * 10.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 278.
2 CONT * 11.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 486.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p366.htm#i10995 _____________________
2 CONT *Elizabeth Mainwaring1
2 CONT *F, #574680
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Jan 2013
2 CONT *     Elizabeth Mainwaring married Peter Shakerley, son of Geoffrey Shakerley and unknown daughter Holland.1
2 CONT *      Cheshire.1 She lived Over Peover.1 Her married name became Shakerley. Daughter and coheir of '''Sir Randal Mainwaring'''.1
2 CONT *Child of Elizabeth Mainwaring and Peter Shakerley
2 CONT ** 1.Geoffrey Shakerley+2 d. 1618
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 3, page 3576. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p57468.htm#i574680 _____________________
2 CONT *MAINWARING, Sir Arthur (c.1525-90), of Ightfield, Salop.
2 CONT *b. c.1525, 1st. s. of Sir Richard Mainwaring by Dorothy, da. of Robert Corbet of Moreton Corbet, Salop. educ. G. Inn 1542. m. by 1557, Margaret, da. and coh. of '''Sir Randolph Mainwaring of Peover, Cheshire''', 1s. George 3da. K
2 CONC ntd. Oct. 1547. suc. fa. 1558.1
2 CONT *   Mainwaring was a considerable landowner, much of whose property lay outside Shropshire. '''The death of his father-in-law in September 1557 brought him extensive estates, from the Cheshire branch of his family, in Bradley, Str
2 CONC etton and elsewhere in that county, together with houses in the city of Chester.''' .... etc. 
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/mainwaring-sir-arthur-1525-90 __________________________
2 CONT *MAINWARING, George (bef.1551-1628), of Ightfield, Salop.
2 CONT *b. bef. 1551, o.s. of Sir Arthur Mainwaring by Margaret, da. and coh. of '''Sir Randolph Mainwaring of Peover, Cheshire'''. educ. Shrewsbury 1562; I. Temple 1565. m. Anne, da. of William More I of Loseley, Surr., 4s. 1da. suc. fa
2 CONC . 1590. Kntd. c.1593.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/mainwaring-george-1551-1628 ________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir Randall Mainwaring[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
2 CONT *'''Born Abt 1495   of, Over Peover, Cheshire, England   [3, 10]
2 CONT *'''Died 6 Sep 1577  [3, 10] 
2 CONT *Father   Sir John Mainwaring,   b. 1471, of, Over Peover, Cheshire, England ,   d. 1515 
2 CONT *Mother   Katherine Honford,   b. 1471, Honford, Cheshire, England ,   d. 1529 
2 CONT *'''Family 1   Elizabeth Brereton,   d. Aft 30 Nov 1545 
2 CONT *'''Married  Abt 1518  [10] 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **1. Margaret Mainwaring,   b. Abt 1521,   d. Bef 1590
2 CONT **2. Elizabeth Mainwaring,   b. Abt 1524
2 CONT **3. Catherine Mainwaring,   b. Abt 1526
2 CONT *'''Family 2   Elizabeth Leycester,   b. Abt 1525, of, Toft, Cheshire, England ,   d. 1579 
2 CONT *Married   1551  [10]  ◦CONDITION: This couple had no children. 
2 CONT *Sources 
2 CONT *1.[S25] #798 The Wallop Family and Their Ancestry, Watney, Vernon James, (4 volumes. Oxford: John Johnson, 1928), FHL book Q 929.242 W159w; FHL microfilm 1696491 it., vol. 3 p. 771.
2 CONT * 2.[S415] #7319 The Mainwaring Family, Finley, R. Mainwaring, (London, Griffith, Farran, Okeden & Welsh, Newberry House, Charing Cross Road and Sydney. Facsimile reprint 1976 The Research Publication Company, 52 Lincoln's Inn Fie
2 CONC lds, London), FHL Book 929.242 M285f., p. 33, 34.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] #11232 The Genealogist (1980-), Association for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, (New York: Organization for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, 1980-), FHL book 929.105 G286n., vol. 5 no. 1 p. 164.
2 CONT * 4.[S884] The visitation of the county palatine of Lancaster, made in the year 1567, by William Flower, esq., Norroy king of arms, Flower, William, ([Manchester] : Chetham Society, 1870), 942.7 B4c v. 81., p. 3.
2 CONT * 5.[S131] #560 [1819] The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester (1819), Ormerod, George, (3 volumes. London: Lackington, Hughes, Mavor & Jones, 1819), FHL microfilms 924,226-924,227., vol. 1 p. 495.
2 CONT * 6.[S2083] #2142 The visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580 ..., Rylands, John Paul, (London : [s.n.], 1882. xii, 298 p. : coats of arms, facsims., geneal. tables ; 26 cm.), FHL microfilm 162051 Item 2., vol. 18 p. 125.
2 CONT * 7.[S131] #560 [1819] The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester (1819), Ormerod, George, (3 volumes. London: Lackington, Hughes, Mavor & Jones, 1819), FHL microfilms 924,226-924,227., vol. 2 p. 96.
2 CONT * 8.[S2088] #710 Collections for a History of Staffordshire (1880-), Staffordshire Record Society, (Annual periodical. Birmingham: William Salt Archaeological Society, 1880-), FHL book 942.46 B4sc., vol. 1 n.s. pedigree chart faci
2 CONC ng p. 304.
2 CONT * 9.[S20] Magna Carta Ancestry: A study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Richardson, Douglas, (Kimball G. Everingham, editor. 2nd edition, 2011), vol. 3 p. 94, 279.
2 CONT * 10.[S20] Magna Carta Ancestry: A study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Richardson, Douglas, (Kimball G. Everingham, editor. 2nd edition, 2011), vol. 3 p. 279.
2 CONT * 11.[S2159] #1843 The Visitation of Shropshire, Taken in the Year 1623 (1889), Treswell, Robert (main author), (Publications of the Harleian Society: Visitations, volumes 28, 29. London: [Harleian Society], 1889), FHL book 942 B4
2 CONC h volumes 28-29; FHL microfilm 162,., vol. 29 pt. 2 p. 349. 
2 CONT *From: https://histfam.familysearch.org//getperson.php?personID=I41614&tree=EuropeRoyalNobleHous __________________________
2 CONT *a. Sir John Mainwaring of Over Peover, Sheriff of Flintshire (b 1470, d 03.1515)
2 CONT *  m. Catherine Honford (sister of William Honford of Honford or Hanford)
2 CONT **'''	(1) Sir Randall Mainwaring of Over Peover (b c1495, d 06.09.1557)
2 CONT **'''	  m1. Elizabeth Brereton (dau of Sir Randoll Brereton)
2 CONT **'''	  m2. Elizabeth Leycester (dau of Sir Ralph Leycester of Toft)
2 CONT **'''	Visitation (1580) shows Sir Randall's sole wife and mother of his children as Elizabeth Brereton. Visitation (1613) reports one source that identifies Elizabeth Leister (Leycester), second wife, as mother of his children but
2 CONC  another source that says the mother was Elizabeth Brereton. There is obviously some doubt here.
2 CONT ***		(A) Margaret Mainwaring
2 CONT ***		  m. Sir Arthur Mainwaring of Ightfield, Sheriff of Shropshire (a 1563) @@ below
2 CONT ***		(B) Katherine Mainwaring
2 CONT **		  m. John Davenport of Henbury
2 CONT ***		(C) Elizabeth Mainwaring
2 CONT ***		  m1. Peter Shakerley of Hulme (d 06.01.1553)
2 CONT ***		  m2. Christopher Holford of Holdford (d 1581) 
2 CONT *From: Stirnet.com __________________________
