2 CONT Full list of Names: http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=24093
2 CONT
2 CONT With the loss of all three of their Manors, the Lathom's of Parbold, though many of them still continued to live in the district, disappeared into a mediocre obscurity, the last of whom there is record being that William Lathom (2
2 CONC 5) who died in 1730, nearly thirty years after the death of Peter Lathom of the Charity.  Assuming for the moment that Peter, was himself a Lathom of Parbold, then William and Peter are indeed the last of the breed. Whilst I can f
2 CONC ind no positive evidence in favour of such an assumption, all the few ascertainable data seem to suggest it and to leave no other reasonable alternative. For these data we have to look to the latter half of the seventeenth century
2 CONC ."
