1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "John Jackson, of Hickleton, co York, Esq., 1st son and heir of Sir John Jackson of Edderthorpe in that county (died 2 July 1637) by his 2nd wife, Fiennes, daughter of Sir Thomas Waller, Governor of Dover Castle, was born about 16
2 CONC 31, and was created Baronet, 31 December 1660. He was aged 34 at the Visit. of Yorkshire in 1665. He married firstly, in or before 1653, <strong>Katherine, sister of George,1st Baron Delamere, daughter of William Booth, of Dunham<
2 CONC /strong>, co Chester, by Vere, daughter and coheir of Thomas (Egerton), 1st Viscount Brackley. She, who was born 11 May 1624, died 1667. He married secondly, Lucy, widow of Sir William Jopson, 2nd Baronet [S 1635], of Cudworth in 
2 CONC Royston, co York, daughter of Henry Tindall of Brotherton in that county. He died in or before 1670."
2 CONT
