2 CONT
2 CONT This four volume set was written from 1860-1862 and reprinted in 1873 and 1884. This book "shows the three generations of those who came before May 1692, on the basis of Farmers Register. It also includes "Genealogical notes and e
2 CONC rrata" by Mrs. D. H. Dall and a "Genealogical Cross Index of the Four Volumes" by O. P. Dexter Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1998 (reprint)Page: 221.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.8: Ramon Meyers Tingley, Some Ancestral Lines; Being a Record of Some of the Ancestors of Guilford: Solon Tingley and His Wife, Martha Pamelia Meyers, Collected by Their Son, Raymon Meyers Tingley (Rutland, VT: The Tuttle Publ
2 CONC ishing Co., 1935)Page: 274.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.9; The Mayflower Descendant
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy CD-ROM contains 48 volumes of Pilgrim records. The first 37 volumes, compiled by George Ernest Bowman in "The Mayflower Descendant Magazine" from 1899 to 1937, are rich sources of information about the first 250 years of Am
2 CONC erican history. Also included are all five volumes of Bowman’s Pilgrim Notes and Queries and three volumes of Bowman’s Vital Records of Brewster, Halifax, and Truro, and Bowman’s post-publication corrections taken from his persona
2 CONC l copy of the magazine. New are B. N. Derick’s volume on Dennis cemeteries and a volume on Wellfleet cemeteries. (Boston, MA: Massachusetts Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1899 to 1937]
2 CONT
2 CONT [republished on CD by Search & Research Publishing, Wheat Ridge, CO 1996],Vol. 13, p. 86 and Vol. 17, p. 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.10: Eugene Willard Montgomery, Willard-Peabody Genealogy (Galena, IL: 1915), Vol. 2, p. 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN PAYBODY was born about 1590 in England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He probably arrived in the Plymouth Colony in 1635 or 1636, for his name appears on the list of freemen of the colony dated March 7, 1636/37, and he was admitted and sworn with others whose names were on that list on Jan. 2, 1637/
2 CONC 8. 
