1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/De_Hutton-2
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Dorrington had issue William, who had a son Roger, father of William, whose son and heir was Philip Doryngton, who had Thomas de Dodington (8 Hen. V.), in the county of Somerset. William, father of Philip, by deed confirme
2 CONC d to Nicholas Fitz Roger de Cantoe, for his homage and service, all that land lying in Barnardsworth, in the manor of Doddeton, which William his grandfather held, to have and to hold to him and his heirs, of William de Doddeton a
2 CONC nd his heirs, with all rights, liberties, and customs, as his grandfather William had and held those lands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas, as above, (living in the reign of Richard II. and 8 Henry V.) married two wives; 1, Beatrix, daughter of _______ Bachelor; 2, Joan, of whom presently. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By the first he had issue John, his son and heir (8 Henry V.), who, by Mary, daughter of Payn de Hutton, had issue = John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He, by Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Oliver Hussey, had, 
2 CONT * 1. Richard, 
2 CONT * 2. John, 
2 CONT * 3. Thomas, 
2 CONT * 4. William, which two last died issueless.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/De_Doddington-1
2 CONT * MISCELLANEOUS ANTIQUITIES, (IN CONTINUATION OF BIBLIOTHECA TOPOGRAPHICA BRITANNICA,) N° IV. * * * CONTAINING THE HISTORY AND ANTIQUITIES OF SHENSTONE. The Pedigrees of all the Families and Gentry, both ancient and modern, of tha
2 CONC t Parish. By the late Rev. HENRY SANDERS, B.A. of Oriel College, Oxford, and Thirteen Years Curate of Shenstone. LONDON, Printed by and for J. NICHOLS, PRINTED BY AND FOR THE SOCIETY OF ANTIQUARIES, 1794.
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/phocadownload/userupload/scanned-sources/tpg3/pp568-575.pdf
