2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hussey-101 comments 
2 CONT ##A ''Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great'' ..., Volume 4.  By John Burke.  “Huyshe, of Sand and Clysthyon.”  Page 409-416  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=6AtBAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA410&dq=pedigree%20of%20huy
2 CONC sh&pg=PA410#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] >  “Her father Oliver is listed on page 410 as having married Johanna Avenall; Elizabeth married to John Doddington is in the paragraph about her father Oliver.”
2 CONT ##The Visitations of the County of Somerset in the Years 1531 & 1575, https://books.google.com/books?id=dyw6AQAAMAAJ by Frederick Weaver (1885) says at p569, John Dodington married "Eliz d and h of Oliver Hewish of Donniford Som".
2 CONC   Page 31.  “Hewish of Donniford, in St. Decuman’s.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=dyw6AQAAMAAJ&vq=Huyish&pg=PA31#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT ##The Topographer and Genealogist, Volume 3, John Nichols (1858), https://books.google.com/books?id=Nh0IAAAAQAAJ at p21 says John Dodington married "Elizabeth Hussey, daughter and heiress of Oliver Hussey, of Donyford, in Wiltshir
2 CONC e."
2 CONT ##Archaeological papers relating to the counties of Somerset, Wilts, Hants, and Devon by William Henry Rogers (1902) https://archive.org/details/archaeologicalpa00roge addresses the Huysh/Hewish/Huyshe/Huyish family of Doniford at
2 CONC  p241/1, < [https://archive.org/details/archaeologicalpa00roge/page/n236/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >); Oliver at p249/8, < [https://archive.org/details/archaeologicalpa00roge/page/n247/mode/2up?view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONC ; and his daughter Elizabeth who married "John Dodington of Dodington" at p251/10.
2 CONT ##In The Heraldic Visitations of Staffordshire, Elizabeth is show as the "da. and h." (daughter and heiress) of Oliver Hussey: at page 88. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=gfwcAAAAYAAJ&vq=Doddington&pg=PA88#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONC  GoogleBooks] >
