1 NAME Anne /Wyant/
2 GIVN Anne
2 SURN Wyant
2 _MARNM Bradbury
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1454
2 PLAC Catmiere Hall, Littlebury, Essex, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1490
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE Greater London
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne WYANT 1 was born 1454 in Littlebury, Essex, England. She married Robert BRADBURY on 1475 in Littlebury, Essex, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  		M	i	 William BRADBURY was born 1476 and died Jun 1546.  Married Joan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/r/a/Charles-E-Bradbury/GENE10-0005.html Bradbury Memorial, p. 29]
2 CONT
2 CONT ">"The Herald's Visitation do not give the name of the wife of Robert Bradbury, and unfortunately he left no will, and there was no inquisition post mortem to solve the mystery. In some of the pedigrees he is said to have married 
2 CONC Anne Wyant, and we have followed it, but with this explanation. His son having been assigned a wife that belonged to the generation of the father, it is quite probable that the Visitation has made a mistake of one generation, and 
2 CONC that Jane (Fitzwilliam) Bendish was the mother and not the wife of William Bradbury."
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/r/a/Charles-E-Bradbury/GENE10-0004.html Bradbury Memorial #: E-339]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Wife's name also reported incorrectly as Anne Wyant (482) Robert Bradbury is named in the inquistion of his brother, Sir Thomas, then dead (supposed Justice of the Assize, Isle of Ely, Feb 4, 1486, witness to will of George Nich
2 CONC oll of Littlebury, Dec 2, 1484, died 1489, and buried in church of Grey Friars, London), is said to have married Anne, daughter of Infans Wyant (see note on son William). "
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT # Lapham, William Berry, Bradbury Memorial (Portland, Maine: Brown, Thurston & Company, 1890.), p. 29, Los Angeles Public Library, 929.2 B798.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [http://dunhamwilcox.net/me/me_bio_bradbury.htm Genealogical and Family History of the STATE OF MAINE.]  Compiled under the editorial supervision of George Thomas Little, A. M., Litt. D. LEWIS HISTORICAL PUBLISHING COMPANY New Y
2 CONC ork 1909. [Transcribed by Coralynn Brown] "Bradbury."  "(III) Robert (2), eldest child of William and Martha (Rockhill) Bradbury, named in in inquisition of his brother, Sir Thomas, then dead, supposed justice of the assize, Isle 
2 CONC of Ely, Feb. 4, 1486, witness to the will of George Nichall, of Littlebury, Dec. 2, 1484, died 1489, and was buried in the church of Grey Friars, London), is said to have married '''Anne, dau. of Infans Wyant'''. They had a son Wi
2 CONC lliam, next mentioned."
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg2504.htm
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/r/a/Charles-E-Bradbury/GENE10-0005.html
