1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/FITZWILLIAM.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane FITZWILLIAM
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1440
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Thomas FITZWILLIAM of Marblethorpe
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Margaret DYMOKE
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Robert BRADBURY (d. ABT 1489) ABT 1478
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William BRADBURY (b. ABT 1480 - d. 15 Jun 1546)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Bradbury Memorial:  A Note pertaining to William Bradbury, b. 1480, m. Joan (Fitzwilliams) Bendish also The Ancestry of Thomas Bradbury ... p. 37,63 
2 CONT
2 CONT > "We have followed the Herald's Visitation here, but there is evidently a serious mistake in their reckoning. Thomas Bendish died about 1477, and his wife Joan or Jane had deceased prior to May 4, 1490, at which date her inquisit
2 CONC ion post mortem was held, when it was found that Richard Bendish, grandson of Thomas, aged five years, was heir to her estate. She evidently belonged to a generation back of William Bradbury, and if she married a Bradbury, as she 
2 CONC is reported, it must have been his father Robert. (Robert is consistent with the Genealogy of Ralph Waldo Emerson). When Symonds made his collection of epitaphs in Essex in 1639, there was in the church at Clavering a stone bearin
2 CONC g the inscription in Latin: "Pray for the souls of William Bradbury, Esq. and Wife Elisabeth," which Elisabeth died August 13, 1536. William Bradbury died later, after his removal to Littlebury, and was buried there. This would sh
2 CONC ow that his wife's name was Elisabeth. The Herald's Visitation do not give the name of the wife of Robert Bradbury, and unfortunately he left no will, and there was no inquisition post mortem to solve the mystery. In some of the p
2 CONC edigrees he is said to have married Anne Wyant, and we have followed it, but with this explanation. His son having been assigned a wife that belonged to the generation of the father, it is quite probable that the Visitation has ma
2 CONC de a mistake of one generation, and that Jane (Fitzwilliam) Bendish was the mother and not the wife of William Bradbury."
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/r/a/Charles-E-Bradbury/GENE10-0005.html
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg2504.htm#52402
