3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 JUL 1525
2 PLAC Newell Jocelyn
2 ADDR
3 CITY High Roding
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''The New England historical and genealogical register, Volume 71     By Henry Fitz-Gilbert Waters, New England Historic Genealogical Society
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=f0plVwLW5zQC&pg=PA238&lpg=PA238&dq=Maude+Sutton+1312&source=bl&ots=lh0yOyUmUy&sig=BSnsLrHC_vkN8ZpaRgOqjy_vjUM&hl=en&ei=sWbmTtWKOaavsQLjx9D5BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CD8Q6AEwBQ
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Maude%20Sutton%201312&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 239
2 CONT *   14. JEFFREY14 JOCELYN, of Hide Hall in Sawbridgewoth, co. Herts, died in 1425. Perhaps he married first KATHERINE ___, daughter of Thomas, Lord Bray; and he married, perhaps secondly, JOAN ___, who is said to have been daughte
2 CONC r of Thomas Berrie. On 17 Oct. 1394 he is recorded as about to go into Ireland in the King's service, with Thomas de Percy, stewared of the King's housebhold. By his will of 1424, which in now missing, he left Hide Hall to his son
2 CONC  and heir Thomas, subject to the dower of his wife Joan.
2 CONT *   Children by first wife:
2 CONT **Pg. 240
2 CONT **   15. THOMAS15 JOSCELYN (Jeffrey14), of Hide Hall in Sawbridgeworth, co. Herts, died before 1478. He married about 1426, ALICE DUKE, daughter of Lewis of Dukes, co. Essex, by his wife Anne, daughter and heiress of John Cotton, 
2 CONC Esq.
2 CONT **   Child:
2 CONT ***Pg. 241
2 CONT ***   17. GEORGE16 JOSSELYN (Thomas15, Jeffrey14), of Hide Hall in Sawgridgeworth, co. Herts, and of Sheering, co Essex, born in 1428, died after 1480, the year in which he settled Hide Hall on his son Ralph. He married MAUD BARDO
2 CONC LPH, daugher and heir of Edmund. He is said to have been called "Jocelyn the Courtier." He was heir of his uncle, Sir Ralph (14, vi), and at the death of the latter in 1478 was said to be fifty years and more of age.
2 CONT ***   Children:
2 CONT ****	i. RALPH,17 b. abt. 1455; d. in 1504; m. abt. 1480 KATHERINE MARTIN, living 1513, dau. and coheiress of Richard of Faversham, co. Kent. Ralph Josselyn was collector of the alien subsidy for co. Herts in 1488/9, commissioner o
2 CONC f gaol deliveries in 1499, 1503, and 1504, and justice of the pearce from 1486 until his death. Children: 1. George,18 a priest, b. abt. 1490; d. s.p. after 1524 ..... 2. Gabriel, b. abt. 1492; d. s.p. after 1524 .... 3. John, b. 
2 CONC abt. 1494; d. in 1553; m. Anne ___ ; Margaret, his dau. and heiress, m. John Foxley.
2 CONT ****''''''	19. ii. JOHN, b. abt. 1460. 
2 CONT ****	iii. PHILIP, a priest, b. abt. 1452; d. abt. 1509. He was inducted as vicar of Sawbridgeworth, co. Herts, 22 Dec. 1487, and later was vicar of High Roding, co. Essex, holding this living until his death. his successor was ind
2 CONC ucted there 23 June 1509.
2 CONT ****	iv. ELIZABETH, d. before 1524; m. ROBERT FITZHERBERT, who d. before 1524. Child: 1. Anne, m. John Bettenham.
2 CONT *____________
2 CONT *''''''The Journal of American history, Volume 6    By Mabel Thacher Rosemary Washburn, National Historical Society
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=NmgKAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA527&lpg=PA527&dq=Maude+Sutton+1312&source=bl&ots=7j4IO6jmht&sig=K1mwcggloWGyK7_5FHnIBk7E_HI&hl=en&ei=sWbmTtWKOaavsQLjx9D5BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CDsQ6AEwBA
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Maude%20Sutton%201312&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 527
2 CONT *   Thomas, eldest son and heir, in 1428 married Alice Duke, daughter of Lewis Duke of Essex. To them was born a son, 
2 CONT **George, known as George Joslyn, the Courtier, on account of his accomplishments and courtly grace. he married Maude Bardolph, daughter of Edmund Bardolph.
2 CONT ***   The son of George and Maude Joslyn, ''''''John Joslyn, in 1509 married Philippa, daughter of Sir William Bradbury of Littlebury near Walden, Essex.'''''' 
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *Nicholas WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Born: 1482 / ABT 1500, Lillingstone Lovell, Oxfordshire, England
2 CONT *Died: ABT 1553 / 24 Jun 1557
2 CONT *Notes: held the office of chief porter of Calais. He is variously styled chief porter, master porter, or knight porter. He was knighted by Henry VIII at the siege of Boulogne, 1544, and died in 1557. He married the sister of Sir 
2 CONC Thomas Josselyn, K.B., and lived at Lillingstone Lovell, then a detached bit of Oxfordshire surrounded by Buckinghamshire. Lady Wentworth survived to live with her younger son, Paul Wentworth, at Burnham Abbey, and was burled in B
2 CONC urnham church. 
2 CONT *Father: Henry WENTWORTH of Codham (Esq.)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan FITZSIMON
2 CONT *Married: Jane JOSSELYN (b. ABT 1482) (dau. of ''''''John Josselyn of Hyde Hall'''''') 1525, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **2. Henry WENTWORTH
2 CONT **3. Joan WENTWORTH
2 CONT **4. Paul WENTWORTH
2 CONT **5. Francis WENTWORTH
2 CONT **6. Clara WENTWORTH
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/WENTWORTH.htm#Nicholas WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)1
2 CONT *________________
