2 CONT >A number of wealthy individuals lived locally and contributed generously to the building but a large part of the money was raised by the efforts of John Leche, who was Vicar of Walden from 1489 to 1521, and his '''sister Jane (Jo
2 CONC hane) who married Thomas Bradbury, the Master of the Mercers Company in the City of London and Lord Mayor of London from 1509 until his death early the following year. Her name lives on in Saffron Walden, of course, in the title o
2 CONC f Dame Bradbury's School in Ashdon Road''' These two, together with four other notable citizens of the town, created the Guild of the Holy Trinity whose history and purposes are set out in Appendix 7. it was chiefly through the wo
2 CONC rk of this Guild that the building of the church was carried through to its successful conclusion. 
