2 CONT '''Notes''': [https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-St-John/6000000000214072236?through=6000000006164557155 Jane [Ingleton]]] was nine months old on the death of her father Robert [Ingleton] in 1503 (when he himself was still a minor);
2 CONC  her mother Ann was the daughter of Sir Richard Empson, who was Robert's guardian; after Robert's death Ann and her new husband John Hugford attempted to sue the Ingleton estate in Chancery, whereupon Jane was removed from her cus
2 CONC tody and placed under the wardship of Dame Joan Bradbury, widow. She married Humphrey Tyrrell in 1517 (being then aged 14) and after his death in 1549 married Alexander St John. The palimpsests were recovered in 1984 and 1997 by B
2 CONC .S.H.E.
