2 CONT Children 	Robert Aston (Born Aston)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Walter Aston (c.1529-1589) another prominent Staffordshire protestant, built Tixall Gatehouse around 1580. In August 1586 the Hall was the temporary prison of Mary Queen of Scots while her quarters at Chartley were being searc
2 CONC hed for incriminating evidence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Walter's grandson became Walter, First Lord Aston at the coronation of James 1st. He was sent to Spain as Ambassador from 1620-1625 to try and arrange a marriage between the Infanta daughter of Philip III, and Charles, Prince 
2 CONC of Wales.On his second visit from 1635-1638 he became a Roman Catholic. His successors were then subject to increased taxation and political and social isolation as recusants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT * J.P. for Staffs., 1553. Knighted 18 July 1560. Sheriff of Staffs., 1570-1 & 1580-1. From: http://archiver.rootsweb.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/1999-10/0938908183
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedigree of Aston of Tixall, in "The Heraldic Visitations of Staffordshire Made by Sir Richard St. Geoerge, Norroy, in 1614, and by Sir William Dugdale, Norroy, in the Years 1663 and 1664," ed. H. Sydney Grazebrook, in Collections
2 CONC  for a History of Staffordshire, vol. 5, pt. 2, publ. 1885 (London: Mitchell and Hughes), p. 18, gives: Sir Walter Aston of Tixall, co. Staff. Died (sic) in ao 1583.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.halhed.com/t4r/getperson.php?personID=I10424&tree=tree1
2 CONT
