1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes:  Elinor may have been from the Aston family of Tixall, Staffordshire, England.  If she married Thomas Bouldinge in Stratford-upon-Avon at near 18 years of age and had a young child at the death of Thomas and
2 CONC  lived in Barford, she could have then went to live with her brother Edward Aston in Charlecote and met William Peyto from Chesterton being that these communities were a mere 5 +/- miles apart.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.halhed.com/tng/getperson.php?personID=I5777&tree=halhed
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Aston and Peyto families having influence may have given young Thomas the advantage needed in starting a better life in America for both Thomas Bouldinge and his wife Mary Boulding obtaining land grants and title of Ancient P
2 CONC lanter status in Early America.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps with the passing of William Peyto in 1609 is an event which leads to Thomas' search for a better life in America by sailing on the Swan in 1610.  The first name William is then introduced into the family tree and still com
2 CONC mon today.
