1 NAME Hepsabeth Ann /Clare/
2 GIVN Hepsabeth Ann
2 SURN Clare
2 _MARNM Perry
2 NICK Hepzibeth
2 NICK Cleare
2 NICK Hepzibeth Ann Clare
2 NICK Hepsabeth Perry
2 NICK Hepsabeth Clare
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1702
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE 1753
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 JAN 1753
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Parents?:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Clare-698 speculates "Clare is thought to be the step-daughter of Timothy Clare and was raised by him. Her father may be Israel Snelling."
2 CONT She is referred to as his daughter Hepzibah Perry in his will of November 10, 1724 where he leaves her 200 acres of land. 
2 CONT Timothy Clare’s wife was Hannah “Anna” Snelling Lawrence
2 CONT 2. The Findagrave memorial for Hannah says she is her daughter.
2 CONT 3. The FAG memorial for Timothy's wife Elizabeth says she is her daughter...
2 CONT 4. https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~myfriendsthelambs2/genealogy/part8/other/clare.html
2 CONT calls her the daughter of 2nd wife
2 CONT "m/2 Hepsabeth Clare, born 14 2mo 1702; married by 1724, 1st wife of Jacob Perry Sr. (See: Perry Family, Part VIII)"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=64202831-15-203&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-4bc037c3152c28d8a2e6190603bbf969&mrid=661cc58c83370eae0893085c5b8423e4 MyHeri
2 CONC tage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 23 2016, 23:06:42 UTC''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=108223660&pid=364 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edit 2/15/25: Note that Elizabeth Perry (last name unknown) cannot be Hepsabeth's mother, as some sources on MyHeritage indicate. This is because Elizabeth died in 1702 PRIOR to the birth of Hepsabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/M237-QX3 biography:
2 CONT Married 12/25/1722 in Perquimans Co., NC to Jacob Lawrence Perry.
2 CONT
2 CONT ************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Suppliment to the Welch Journal, she is called Hephzibah Cleare. Info comes from that source and Sally's Family Place (sallysfamilyplace.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT From Perquimans County. The Perry's, Lawrence's & Cleare's all lived very close to each other.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cleare's came to Virginia & Massachusetts from England in the middle & late 1600's. It appears that Timothy Cleare, father of Hephzibah, was a relative of the Cleare's that migrated from Massachusetts to Virginia around 1680. 
2 CONC The Cleare's were Quakers and the monthly meetings were held at the house of Timothy Cleare.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maiden signature "Hepsibah Clare" appears on the wedding certificate for Stephen Scott and Hannah Nicholson April 1, 1721. By 1724 she is referred to in her father's will as Hepzibah Perry. Hepsabeth Clare was born 14 Feb 1702
2 CONC , the daughter of Timothy Clare and his wife Hannah Larence [widow of Israel Snelling].
2 CONT
2 CONT p.150 Deed Book E no. 167 "We Jacob, & Hepsibeth Perry of Perq. for the love we bear our son Israel Perry of same, have given 150a bounded on ye North by ye River, & on ye east by line of John Winslow." October 16, 1749. Test' Jac
2 CONC ob Perry Jr., Reuben Perry.
2 CONT
