2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Major Moore Fauntleroy [Parents &lt;pafg104.htm&gt;]&lt;pafc110.htm&gt; was born on 9 Jan 1679 in of,,Richmond,Virginia. He died in 1739 in , Richmond, Virginia. He married Margaret Micou in 1704 in of, Crondall, Richmond, Virgini
2 CONC a.
2 CONT Margaret Micou was born about 1683 in Port Micou,Essex,Virginia. She died in 1742 in ,Richmond,Virginia. She married Major Moore Fauntleroy in 1704 in of,Crondall,Richmond,Virginia.
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT M i Moore Fauntleroy Jr. &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F ii Elizabeth Fauntleroy &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F iii Margaret Fauntleroy &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F iv Sarah Griffin Fauntleroy &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F v Mary Fauntleroy &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F vi Judith Fauntleroy &lt;pafg132.htm&gt;
2 CONT F vii Katherine Fauntleroy was born about 1717 in of,Crondall,Richmond,Virginia. She died after 1742.
2 CONT http://www.tmason1.com/pafg110.htm#1972
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 10 Apr 1739.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert H. Fauntleroy, Fauntleroy Family, The, Microfilm published: Washington, 1952, P 19, Family History Library, 35 N. West Temple Street, Salt Lake City, UT 84150 USA, FHL 1318331 Item 3."He was a Justice in Richmond County fro
2 CONC m 1711 to 1715, commissioned captain in Virginia Militia in 1727, and major in 1734. He as the oldest son, inherited Crondall and the Island, 1200 acres in all, and lived at Crondall, and by his will in 1739 left it to his son Moo
2 CONC re."
