1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Maj. David Gwynn resided at Richmond Co., VA. He left a will; proved 22 Feb 1702/3. Death date also seen as Bef 8 Mar 1704/05.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT #Elizabeth Gwynn
2 CONT #Sarah Smith (born Gwynn)
2 CONT #Katherine Brockenbrough (born Gwyn)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonial Families of the Southern States p.250 has David Gwynn, Major, of Essex Co., Va., who served with distinction in the British Army; a supporter of the Established Church; m. Katherine Griffin, dau. of Hon. Samuel Griffin, o
2 CONC f Northumberland Co., Va. . . .  The author of this article was Stella Pickett Hardy.  She claims that David Gwynn was the son of Capt. Owen Gwynn, Knight, son of Sir John Wynne and his wife, Lady Sarah Gerrard. The name Wynn was 
2 CONC apparently used interchangeably with Gwynn, perhaps because of the family's connection to Gwydir.  It appears to have been a contraction of Gwydir and Wynne.
2 CONT
