1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Collier Barksdale ''' was born in 1715 and died in October, 1774, in Tidewater, Richmond, Virginia. He was married to Sarah Randolph who was born in 1714 in Charlotte County, Virginia. They married in 1739 in Ch
2 CONC arlotte County, Virginia. Sarah Randolph was the daughter of Henry Randolph III (298) and his wife, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Collier Barksdale cultivated tobacco on his plantation. He had taken a load of tobacco to Petersburg, Virginia, when on the return trip home he became seriously ill and died before reaching home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Collier's family is not well-researched. His wife Sarah's is. Henry Randolph III was the son of Henry Randolph II and his wife, Sarah Swann.  Henry Randolph II was the son of Henry Randolph I. Henry Randolph I was the son of Willi
2 CONC am Randolph and his wife, Dorothy Lane. Elizabeth Randolph was the daughter of Colonel Frances Eppes and his wife, Anne Isham Eppes  of Henrico Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Collier Barksdale's brother, Henry, had several children who fought in the Revolutionary War. They included Claiborne (1738-1821) who married Sarah Goode (born 1745) and then Mrs. Jane Morton Carter. Claiborne served as a soldier 
2 CONC from Virginia. Beverly (1756-1822) married Anna Terry and Judith Womack. Beverly served as a PS from Virginia. Henry Hickerson (1758-1831) married Molly Bayne and served WGN from Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I27795 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Collier BARKSDALE 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 1715 in Richmond,Tidewater,Virginia or Charlotte Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: OCT 1774 in Charlotte, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate: 3 OCT 1774 Charlotte Co, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 1 JUL 1766 Charlotte Co, VA 
2 CONT
