2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Seth was born August 4,1668 in Braintree, Massachusetts the son of Josiah Chapin Mary King.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seth Chapin married Mary Hill White November 8, 1742 in Mendon, Massachusetts. Seth, Capt., and Mary Hill of Holliston, Nov. 8, 1742.* Marriage Record
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away April 1, 1746 1746 in Mendon, Massachusetts. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAP1N, Capt. Seth 3 (Josiah,- Samuel 1 ), b. Braintree, Aug. 4, 1068; m., 1st, Mary Read, May 23, 1680. She survived less than four months, and d. without issue, Sept. 12, 1689. He m., 2d, Bethiah Thurston, March 25, 1691. Their 
2 CONC chn. were, —
2 CONT
2 CONT Seth, jun , b. Medfield, July 2, 1692; one of our most conspicuous early citizens.
2 CONT Betiiiah, b., place not given, Feb. 16, 1693; rn. Jonathan Thayer, jun., Oct. 1, 1714.
2 CONT Josiah, b., place not given, March 1, 1695-96; untraced.
2 CONT John, b., place not given, May 13, 1698; always res. here; dea. of the ch., etc.
2 CONT Mary, b. hereabouts April 30, 1700; m. Robert Taft.
2 CONT Samuel, b. hereabouts June 2, 1702; not well traced.
2 CONT Deborah, b. hereabouts June 14, 1704; m. Nathaniel Nelson, April 15, 1725.
2 CONT Hopestill, b. hereabouts Nov. 27, 1715; m. the 2d Dr. John Corbett, Bell.
2 CONT Joseph, b. hereabouts March 6, 1707; m. Mary Nelson, Feb. 5, 1729.
2 CONT Abigail, b. hereabouts June 10, 1710; untraced.
2 CONT Lydia, b. hereabouts Feb. 2, 1712; m. Taft.
2 CONT Benjamin, b. hereabouts April 6, 1713; m. Sarah French, Feb. 23, 1732-33.
2 CONT Ebenezer, b. hereabouts Dec. 23, 1714; lived and d. in old Mendon.
2 CONT Japheth, b. hereabouts Feb. 24, 1716; d. April 15, 1717. The mr. d. March 2, 1744; the fr. in April, 1746.
2 CONT It appears from the old proprietary records that Capt. Seth Chapin had acquired a family homestead and domicile near the " Post Lane " bridge on Mill River some time previous to May 26, 1700; for at that date he had the following-
2 CONC described parcel of land laid out to him: "Forty-five acres of the 4th division laid out to Seth Chapin, and in possession of said Chapin, encompassing the said Chapin's homestead and meadow upon the Mill River," etc. (See Part I.
2 CONC  of this work, Chap. III. p. 38.) He went on adding parcel after parcel to his real estate, till he became the owner of several hundred acres on our territory. In 1713 he and his wf. made a gift-deed of 60 acres to their son Seth,
2 CONC  jun., situated in what we now call So. Hopedale. Aug. 31, 1715, they sold and deeded to Josiah Wood, formerly of Concord, their homestead, consisting of 150 acres, with the buildings thereon. They then removed to Mendon Town, to 
2 CONC live thenceforth with or near his venerable fr., Josiah Chapin, Esq. There, while fulfilling his filial duties with exemplary fidelity, he was welcomed to the front rank of official dignity, and finally closed a life of 78 yrs. wi
2 CONC th very similar manifestations of public confidence and respect to those enjoyed by his honored father.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Milford, Massachusetts, Part 2. by Ballou, Adin, 1803-1890. Publication date 1882
2 CONT
2 CONT Title
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Capt.
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1746, an estate distribution agreement was signed by the heirs, viz., John Chapin, of Mendon, Samuel Chapin of Uxbridge, Joseph Chapin of Mendon, Benjamin Chapin of Grafton, Ebenezer Chapin of Mendon, Bethiah, wife of Jonathan 
2 CONC Thayer, Mary, wife of Robert Taft of Mendon, Deborah, wife of Nathaniel Nelson of Mendon, Hopestill, wife of John Corbit of Bellingham, Josiah Taft of Uxbridge, Elizabeth Chapin, widow of Seth Chapin, Jr and guardian to Rachel, Ly
2 CONC dia, Seth, and Moses Chapin (all children of Seth Jr.), and Nathaniel Nelson guardian of David Chapin and Daniel Chapin (also children of Seth Jr.), the children of Sarah Rawson, decd, the children of Abigail Wheelock, wife of Pau
2 CONC l Wheelock of Country Gore.[2]
2 CONT
