2 CONT Samuel Chapin (1702 - 1753)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Chapin
2 CONT Born 2 Jun 1702 in Mendon, Suffolk, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Seth Chapin and Bethiah (Thurston) Chapin
2 CONT Brother of Seth Chapin, Bethiah (Chapin) Thayer, Josiah Chapin, John Chapin, Mary (Chapin) Taft, Deborah (Chapin) Nelson, Hopestill Chapin, Joseph Chapin, Abigail Chapin, Lydia (Chapin) Taft, Benjamin Chapin, Ebenezer Chapin and J
2 CONC aphet Chapin
2 CONT Husband of Anna (Craggin) Chapin — married 19 May 1729 in Mendon, MAmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Anna (Chapin) Wood and Deborah (Chapin) Wood
2 CONT Died 27 Apr 1753 at age 50 in Uxbridge, Worcester, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Kathryn Martin, private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 16 Apr 2024 | Created 22 Feb 2017
2 CONT This page has been accessed 387 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Chapin was born June 2, 1702;[1]the son of Seth Chapin and his wife Bethiah[1] (Thurston) Chapin.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Uxbridge and was known as Deacon Samuel Chapin.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT At Uxbridge he married Anna Graggin[2] on May 19, 1729.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Deacon Samuel Chapin and his wife Anna:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was born May 12, 1731.
2 CONT Samuel was born March 12, 1732-3
2 CONT Ephraim was born May 24, 1735.
2 CONT Deborah was born Jan. or June 17, 1737; she married Dexter Wood on March 3, 1757. She was the great grandmother of Henry W. Taft, Esq. of Lenox, Massachusetts.
2 CONT Samuel Chapin died April 27, 1753[3] at Uxbridge[3]and was buried at Uxbridge Center. [3] His remains were later reburied at Prospect Hill Cemetery. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Chapin of Uxbridge, yeoman died intestate and on 10 May 1753, his widow Anna was granted the administration of his estate.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT His inventory was taken on 7 May 1753 in Uxbridge.[5]
2 CONT
