1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph was the son of Capt. Seth Chapin and Bethia Thurston Chapin.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPIN", Joseph 4 (Seth, 3 Josiah, 2 Samuel 1 ), b. March 6, 1707; and m. Mary 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson, Feb. 5, 1729; cer. by Josiah Chapin, Esq. She was a dr. of Gershom 
2 CONT
2 CONT and Abigail (Ellithorpe) Nelson, b. April 16, 1713; and a sr. of Eld. Na- 
2 CONT
2 CONT thaniel Nelson. Their chn. were, — 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b. 1731 ; untraced. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail, b. 1732; m. Silas Rawson, Jan. 5, 1762. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom, b. 1734; m., 1st, Betty Johnson, 1758; 2d, Deborah Torrey, 1762. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel, b. 1736; m. Beulah . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ephraim, b. May 5, 1745; m., let, Hannah Rider, Holl. ; 2d, Wid. Anna Tidd. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether there were any other chn., I am uninformed, but presume not. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The parents were reed, into the Cong. ch. here from the First Ch. in Men- 
2 CONT
2 CONT don, March 26, 1769. I infer from this transfer of relationship that they had 
2 CONT
2 CONT then recently become res. here, but had aforetime dwelt elsewhere, prob. in old 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mendon. Their son Ephraim seems to have preceded them in the Easterly 
2 CONT
2 CONT Precinct, and soon became a conspicuous citizen here. Under his filial auspices, 
2 CONT
2 CONT as may be presumed, they spent the last yrs. of their lives at a small homestead 
2 CONT
2 CONT on Main St., not far from the Luther Claflin place. He d. July 1, 17S8; and 
2 CONT
2 CONT his son Ephraim, as execr., set. his est. His wid., Mary (Nelson) Chapin, d. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb. 16, 1798
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and his siblings are listed as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Seth, jun , b. Medfield, July 2, 1692; one of our most conspicuous early citi- 
2 CONT
2 CONT zens. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah, b., place not given, Feb. 16, 1693; m. Jonathan Thayer, jun., Oct. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1, 1714. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah, b., place not given, March 1, 1695-96; untraced. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John, b., place not given, May 13, 169S; always res. here; dea. of the ch., etc. 
2 CONT
