2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Thayer II
2 CONT 4 June 1694–11 August 1736
2 CONT •
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Josiah Joseph
2 CONT
2 CONT When Josiah Joseph Thayer II was born on 4 June 1694, in Mendon, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Captain Josiah Thayer Sr., was 24 and his mother, Sarah Bass, was 20. He married Elizabeth I
2 CONC ngalls on 1 January 1715, in Providence, Rhode Island, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 5 daughters. He died on 11 August 1736, in Sherborn, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Coloni
2 CONC al America, at the age of 42, and was buried in Sherborn, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America.
