2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Document 793: History of Providence County, Volume I; Ed. by Richard M. Bayles: WW Preston & Co., NY 1891
2 CONT http://www.rootsweb.com/~rgenweb/article34.html
2 CONT p. 106-108 ...They had several Children, one of whom, John Darling, born in 1664, settled in the southern part of Bellingham, Mass., where he was known as &quot;Captain John. &quot;He was the father of thirteen children.  From &qu
2 CONC ot;Captain John&quot; spang the branch of the Darling family to which the subject of this sketch belongs. (Lucius B. Darling)  Samuel seems to have been a vavorite name with the darlings, the great-grandfather, grandfather and the
2 CONC  father of Lucius all bearing that name, as well as a brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Document 793: The Darling Family in America: Early settlers prior to 1800.  New York. MW Clemens, 1913 (birth information)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Dennis Darling and Hannah Francis Darling.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, first, about 1686, Elizabeth Thompson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, second, on Jan 2,1687/8, Anna Rockwood.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, third, about 1691, Elizabeth Morse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by first marriage): John Darling Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by second marriage): Anna Darling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by third marriage): Elizabeth Darling Brown, Samuel Darling, Ruth Darling Thayer, Hannah Darling Thompson, Margaret Darling French, Ebenezer Darling, Mary Darling Draper, Martha Darling Thompson, Abigail Darling Chickerin
2 CONC g Thayer, Rachel Darling, and Deborah Darling Bosworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attained the rank of Captain in the King Philip's War. Petitioned the King for land to become the Town of Bellingham and became the first President of the Selectmen for that area.
2 CONT A large farmer and weaver, he and his sons also had control of the water power from the Blackstone River.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/52568475/john-darling Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projec
