1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Samuel Darling was born on March 18, 1694, in Mendon, Worcester County, Massachusetts, and died on February 17, 1774, in Bellingham, Norfolk County, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, thirdly, Tamerson Adams, the widow of Joseph Ellis, on February 7, 1760, in Medway, Norfolk County, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Darling and Mary Thompson had eight children as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Darling Jr (1720-1814)
2 CONT Michael Darling (abt.1723-1817)
2 CONT Elizabeth Darling (1725)
2 CONT Abigail (Darling) Draper (1731-1826)
2 CONT John Darling (1733-1800)
2 CONT Rachel Darling (1735)
2 CONT Joshua Darling (1737-1815)
2 CONT Ruth (Darling) Pits
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Darling and Penelope Brown had one child as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope (Darling) Wilson (1742-
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Darling and Tamerson Adams had no children together.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Darling Sr. (1694 - 1774)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Capt. Samuel Darling Sr.===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 18 Mar 1694 in Mendon, Suffolk County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Darling and Elizabeth (Morse) Darling
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Darling [half], Ruth (Darling) Thayer, Hannah (Darling) Thomson, Margaret (Darling) French, Ebenezer Darling, Mary (Darling) Draper, Martha (Darling) Thompson and Deborah (Darling) Bosworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Thompson) Darling — married 5 Dec 1716 (to 7 Jun 1740) in Mendon, Suffolk, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Penelope (Brown) Darling — married 12 Sep 1741 (to 10 Jul 1759) in Bellingham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Tamerson (Adams) Darling — married 7 Feb 1760 in Medway, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Samuel Darling Jr, Michael Darling, Abigail (Darling) Draper, John Darling, Joshua Darling and Penelope (Darling) Wilson
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 17 Feb 1774 at age 79 in Bellingham, Suffolk County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Samuel's tombstone is on findagrave.com
2 CONT ↑ http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Norfolk/Medway/Images/Medway_M186.gif
2 CONT Find A Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com : accessed 16 March 2018), memorial page for Samuel Darling (18 Mar 1694–17 Feb 1774), Find A Grave Memorial no. 31700976, citing Scott Cemetery, Bellingham, Norfolk Co
2 CONC unty, Massachusetts, USA; Maintained by Kevin Avery (contributor 47024642) Find A Grave memorial #31700976. URL: [1]
2 CONT Suffolk County, MA: Probate File Papers.Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2017-2019. (From records supplied by the Massachusetts Supreme Judicial Court Archives. Digitized mages pro
2 CONC vided by FamilySearch.org) Case 15616: Will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife was Mary Thompson Darling, married Dec 5,1716 at Mendon,MA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Penelope (Brown) Butterworth Darling, intentions at Bellingham,MA Sep 12,1741. She was the widow of Noah Butterworth. Penelope Darling was the daughter of Nathaniel Brown and Sarah Jencks Brown, and she died Ju
2 CONC l 10,1759 at Bellingham,MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife, married at Medway,MA on Feb 7,1760, was Tamesin Adams Ellis Darling, widow of Joseph Ellis Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by first marriage): an infant daughter, Samuel Darling Jr, Michael Darling, Elizabeth Darling Darling, Ruth Darling Pitts, Abigail Darling Draper, John Darling, Rachel Darling Darling, and Joshua Darling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by second marriage): Penelope Darling Wilson.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31700976/samuel-darling Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 30 2023, 7:0
2 CONC 7:15 UTC''
