1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HENRY5 BOSWORTH, son of Ichabod4 (Jonathan, Jr.3, Jonathan2 Edward1) and 1st wife Sarah (Stacy), born probably in Rehoboth about 1710, or very early in 1711;(*) place and date of death unknown; married at Smithfiel
2 CONC d, R. I., Apr. 25, 1732, DEBORAH DARLING, youngest daughter of Capt. John2 (Dennis1) and 3rd wife Elizabeth (Morse) Darling, born in Mendon, Mass. (later set off as Bellingham) Jan. 8, 1713_14; died before Mar. 17, 1750, on which 
2 CONC date she is mentioned in her father's will, as "daughter Deborah Bosworth deceased."
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarke, Mrs. Mary Bosworth. Bosworth Genealogy vol. 4. San Francisco: n.p., 1928. page 453
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of death unknown, but before Mar 17, 1750 when referred to in her father's will as deceased.
