1 TITL Rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rev Ebenezer Morse, Sr
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the 65 original "grantees" of Newfane, Windham County, Vermont in 1753, by Benning Wentworth, governor of New Hampshire. He was also the first minister of the Boylston, Massachusetts, Congregational Church. His grave
2 CONC  is an above-ground sarcophagus. A further biography is at: http://www.boylstonhistory.org/morse.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:  Joshua Morse (1679 - 1748)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Mary Paine Morse (1680 - 1746)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:   Persis Bush Morse (1727 - 1788)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * John Morse (1746 - 1822)
2 CONT * Mary Morse Rice (1747 - 1767)
2 CONT * Eliakim Morse (1750 - 1758)
2 CONT * Joshua Morse (1752 - 1828)
2 CONT * Ebenezer Morse (1754 - 1754)
2 CONT * Ebenezer Morse (1755 - 1813)
2 CONT * Joseph Morse (1757 - 1779)
2 CONT * Eliakim Morse (1759 - 1858)
2 CONT * Annis Morse Andrews (1764 - 1845)
2 CONT * Mary Morse Abbott (1767 - 1843)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Burial Ground,  Boylston,  Worcester County,  Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: Beneath this stone rests the remains of Reverend Ebenezer Morse, A.M., who upwards of fifty years exercized the functions of a Christian minister in this place. Endowed by the Father of Lights with a strong and capaci
2 CONC ous mind, he richly stored it by seeking and intermeddling with all wisdom. As a advisor, he was learned; as a physician, eminent; as a philosopher, deep, extensive and correct in his views. As a politician, of piercing insight of
2 CONC  individual character. Shrewd in reply, able in controversy, abounding with narrative, the passion of helpless merit, and fulfulling with exactness the duties of husband, teacher and friend, he died Janurary 3, 1802, aged 84. The 
2 CONC stone also preserves the memory of Mrs. Persis Morse, the amiable and virtuous consort of the Rev. E. Morse. She died May 6, 1788, aged 61 years, having been united in marriage 33 years. From this union descended eleven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=8029748 Note: Age: 84 Spouse: Persis (Bush) Morse (d. 1788)
2 CONT
