3 CITY Medfield
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1823
2 ADDR
3 CITY Amherst
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canada
1 TITL Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was proprietor of Georege's tavern in Roxbury and frunished supplies for General Amherst's expedition to Oswego. He was taken by the French and shipped for Bordeaux, but on the passage they were seized by a Brit
2 CONC ish Man-of-war and sailed for London. The horror's of this passage were such tha King George sent for him, and, to compensate him, gave him a commision as Commissary General for America and a large tract of land at Amherst, N.S.
2 CONT
2 CONT Founder of Amherst, N.S.
2 CONT
2 CONT  "It was named Amherst by Colonel Joseph Morse, the first settler, in honour of Lord Jeffery Amherst, the commander-in-chief of the British Army in North America during the Seven Years' War."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph and Olive (MASON) MORSE;
2 CONT
2 CONT i.    SIMEON MORSE, b. 21 Oct, 1746, at Rutland, mass., m. MARY FREEMAN, and died in New York childless.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.   ALPHEUS MORSE, b. 30 Jun 1750, in Amherst, N.S, m. in Horton, THEODA CRANE; remained there. Had 8 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.  THADDEUS MORSE, b. 30 Mar 1752, at Woodstock, Conn., died unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.   OLIVE MORSE, b. 13 Jan 1754, in Boston, m. (1) 17 May 1769 Lt. WILLIAM EDDY, b. 16 Aug 1752. d. 3 May 1778. m. (2) Lt HEZEKIAH KING, d. 16 May 1829. Still living in May 1848. Had 3 children EDDY, 5 children KING
2 CONT
2 CONT v.    CAROLINE MORSE, b. 13 Jul 1763, in Cumberland, Nova Scotia. m. in 1785, DAVID ONION. He served in Rev. War. She died 29 May 1848 in Medfield. Had 3 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT REFERENCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT MORSE GENEALOGY, Comprising The Decendants of SAMUEL, ANTHONY, WILLIAM, AND JOSEPH MORSE AND JOHN MOSS, being a revision of The MEMORIAL OF THE MORSES, Published by Rev Abner Morse in 1850, Compiled by J. HOWARD MORSE and MISS EMI
