2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Holbrook is related to US President William Howard Taft. Here is the trail.
2 CONT John was the son of Thomas Holbrook,[1] one of the first settlers of Sherborn, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John served as constable of Sherborn in 1697. He was a "sealer of leather" from 1705 to 1732. He was commissioner of assessments in Sherborn in 1715. He served as selectman of Sherborn for six years, and was representative in 1772
2 CONC .[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Silence Wood in about 1694. In circa that year, they built their house in Sherborn, Massachusetts, on land given to them by his father-in-law. The house was located on 69 Forest street; it was still standing in 1999.[3]
2 CONC [4][2] Descendants of John and Silence continued to live in this house in 1981.[2] Their son, Jonathan, was known to have resided in the house.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of John and Silence Holbrook include:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT John, born March 22, 1694-5; married Ruth Hill; died 1756
2 CONT Elizabeth, born July 22, 1696; married Joseph Twitchell; died 1782
2 CONT Jonathan, born December 21, 1699; married Abigail Breck; died 1754
2 CONT Joseph, born May 1, 1702; unmarried; died March 13, 1725-6;
2 CONT Ezra, born May 16, 1709; married Grace Cooledge; died November 10, 1786
2 CONT Joshua, born August 22, 1714; unmarried; died November 1, 1740
2 CONT John died on February 28, 1740/1.[6] His wife died on May 11, 1756.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Entry from Torrey NE Marriages HOLBROOK, John (?1667-1740) & Silence [WOOD] (1676-1756); 6 Mar 1692/3; Sherborn {Court Rec. 1:193; TAG 22:208; Stevens-Miller 2:25; Twitchell 18; Holman Ms: Holbrook 4; Wood 9; Sherborn Hist. 141, 2
2 CONC 04}
