2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Holbrook Jr. is related to US President William Howard Taft. Here is the trail.
2 CONT John Hobrook was born 22 March 1694/5 in Sherborn, Massachusetts. He was the son of John Holbrook and Silence Wood.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Ruth Hill on 13 March 1718/9 at Sherborn, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Ruth Holbrook settled initially in Sherborn, then removed west to Grafton about 1734, judging from the births of their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Holbrook died in Grafton on 12 May 1747.[3]
2 CONT On 19 Dec 1747, John Holbrook married as his second wife Elizabeth Edgar in her town, Hopkinton.[4][5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Edgar Holbrook died in Grafton on 16 July 1750,[7] perhaps as a consequence of an unsuccessful pregnancy.
2 CONT In 1752, John married as his third wife Mrs. Joanna (Newmarch) Upton of Reading, widow of Ezekiel Upton.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Holbrook died in Grafton on 6 May 1756.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Ruth Holbrook had at least seven children, first five in Sherborn[10] and last two in Grafton:[11]:
2 CONT
2 CONT William, b. 24 May 1719, m. Sarah Batchellor, 25 May 1753, d. 27 May 1792, in 74th year
2 CONT Silence, b. 23 Mar 1723-4, m. Samuel Goodale of Sutton, 20 Oct 1743
2 CONT Ruth, b. 28 Dec 1726, m. Jonathan Eames of Holliston, 12 June 1744
2 CONT Elizabeth, 6 June 1730
2 CONT John, b. 28 Aug 1733, m. (Mrs) Abigail Warrin, 16 Jan 1758
2 CONT Sarah, b. 18 Jan 1734-5, m. Robert Mellen, in Holliston 19 Nov 1761
2 CONT Moses, b. 14 Sep 1738, m. Mary Whipple 15 Jan 1767, d. 20 or 26 Mar 1802, in his 63rd year
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
