1 NAME John /Cutter/ Jr
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Cutter
2 NSFX Jr
2 _MARNM Cutter
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Hill Cemetery 
2 ADDR
3 CITY New Ipswich
3 STAE NH
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 JAN 1725
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woburn
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts Bay
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 SEP 1771
2 ADDR
3 CITY New Ipswich
3 STAE Province of New Hampshire
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=62806685&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT He followed the family occupation, plying the glazier's trade at Waltham, Lexington, and Shrewsbury. About 1767 he came to New Ipswich, settled near the Temple line, (32, N. D.,) and became a farmer, although frequently absent wor
2 CONC king as a glazier in the neighboring towns. His mother and stepfather made their home with him for several years.  
2 CONT .
2 CONT Buried on the east side of New Ipswich about two rods from the walk next to the road. His tombstone is described:
2 CONT Near the top is a human face with wings, below this are the words: "Momento Mori" Under this is inscribed the epitaph:
2 CONT Erected
2 CONT in Memory of
2 CONT Mr. John Cutter
2 CONT Who departed this
2 CONT life Sept. 27, 1771
2 CONT in his 46th year of
2 CONT his age
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: John Cutter and Rachel Powers John' (Ephraim', Richard', Elizabeth'), b. Watertown, July 23, 1700;d. Nov. 20, 1747 ; m. Rachel Poulter, who survived him and married Barnabas Davis of Littleton, Mass. John followed his fat
2 CONC her's trade of a glazier, living at Lexington and Woburn. Four of his nine children settled in New Ipswich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Susanna Hastings Nov 16, 1749
2 CONT *She survived him and married Simeon Gould (2), and died at Jaffrey, Aug. 5, 1827
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: John, Joseph, Moses, Benjamin, Susanna, Moses, David, Rachel, Sarah, Rachel, Benoni.
