2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was born in 1693. He is the son of Isaac Williams and Elizabeth Hyde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Williams and Abigail Goddard, daughter of William and Leah (Fisher) Goddard of Sherborn, were married May 14, 1716 in Sherborn, Middlesex Co., Massachusetts.[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Goddard Williams, wife of Samuel Williams, died March 6, 1716-17 in Sherborn, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Williams and Abigail Wood were married February 4, 1719-20 in Sherborn, Middlesex Co., Massachusetts.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorrity Williams, daughter of Samuell and Abigail, was born July 8, 1722. Eliezer Wood Williams, son of Sam[ue]ll and Abigail, was born Jan. 5, 1720-1.[6]
2 CONT
