2 CONT CALEB WHITING married (1) HANNAH FAIRBANKS December 18, 1753 in Douglas, daughter of JONATHAN FAIRBANKS and HANNAH COOLIDGE. She was born July 3, 1731, and died August 21, 1759. He married (2) HANNAH SIBLEY-SOUTHWORTH March 20, 17
2 CONC 60 in Douglas, daughter of JOHN SIBLEY and HANNAH MARSH. She was born June 13, 1732 in Sutton, and died July 2, 1819, Douglas. Hannah Sibley married, first, September 17, 1753, Stephen Southworth, b. January 12, 1731, Freetown, Ma
2 CONC ssachusetts, and d. bef. 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will dated January 24, 1816, probated at Douglas November 23, 1819, calls himself "yeoman" and names son-in-law Joshua Fairbanks executor, and names his wife, his children and/or their heirs as recipients of his estate (case #
2 CONC 64568). 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Massachusetts Soldiers and Sailors in the War of the Revolution: Captain of a company which marched on the alarm of April 19, 1775, to Roxbury; service, 10 days; also, 2d Major, Col. Ezra Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt. of Ma
2 CONC ss. militia; list of field officers proposed by Legislature Jan. 12, 1776; regiment made up of men belonging to Mendon, Uxbridge, Northbridge, Upton, and Douglas; also, 2d Major, Col. Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt.; list of field
2 CONC  officers of Mass. militia; commissioned Feb. 15, 1776; also, Captain, 8th co., Col. Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt. of Mass. militia; list of officers; commissioned April 10, 1778; also, return dated Douglas, May 28, 1778, made t
2 CONC o the Superintendent of Worcester Co., by said Whiting, Captain, of men enlisted into the Continental Army for the term of 9 months; also, Captain, Col. Benjamin Hawes's regt.; entered service July 28, 1778; discharged Sept. 12, 1
2 CONC 778; service on expedition to Rhode Island; also, resignation dated May 17, 1780, signed by said Whiting, resigning his commission as Captain of 8th co., 3d Worcester Co. regt., which position he had held a number of years, on acc
2 CONC ount of his advanced age and because his superior officers were younger men than himself; resignation approved by Col. Nathan Tyler; ordered in Council June 6, 1780, that the resignation be accepted. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 60579675
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=60579675
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. CALEB WHITING was born August 19, 1729 in Weston, Massachusetts, and died September 6, 1819 in Douglas, Massachusetts; bur. Douglas Center Cemetery, Douglas. He married (1) HANNAH FAIRBANKS December 18, 1753 in Douglas, Massach
2 CONC usetts, daughter of JONATHAN FAIRBANKS and HANNAH COOLIDGE. She was born July 3, 1731, and died August 21, 1759. He married (2) HANNAH SIBLEY-SOUTHWORTH March 20, 1760 in Douglas, Massachusetts, daughter of JOHN SIBLEY and HANNAH 
2 CONC MARSH. She was born June 13, 1732 in Sutton, Massachusetts, and died July 2, 1819, Douglas, Massachusetts. Hannah Sibley married, first, September 17, 1753, Stephen Southworth, b. January 12, 1731, Freetown, Massachusetts, and d. 
2 CONC bef. 1760. They had two sons, Stephen and Solomon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb's will dated January 24, 1816, probated at Douglas November 23, 1819, calls himself "yeoman" and names son-in-law Joshua Fairbanks executor, and names his wife, his children and/or their heirs as recipients of his estate (ca
2 CONC se #64568). In a document, dated June 1, 1852, to appoint an administrator of the remaining estate of Caleb Whiting "The said executor [Joshua Fairbanks] died about the year 1825 and the said David is now living and has a family c
2 CONC onsisting of himself & wife who are now in precipitous circumstances & have become chargeable to the town of Douglas." Abner Whiting was made trustee of the estate. On December 31, 1852, the real estate was appraised at $1,430.00 
2 CONC and was "sold at public auction April 9, 1853 and struck off to Horace L. Whiting, he being the highest bidder." See Vital Records of Douglas, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also of interest is the case of Whiting v. Whiting in Reports of Cases Argued and Determined in the Supreme Judicial Court of Massachusetts (pages. 236-242) to determine the validity of claims  by Frederick Whiting, eldest son of 
2 CONC David, pertaining to Caleb's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Stephen Southworth was one of three witnesses listed when Caleb made his Last Will and Testament in 1816. This is likely Hannah's son from her first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb Whiting attained the rank of Major in the Revolutionary War. From Massachusetts Soldiers and Sailors in the War of the Revolution: Captain of a company which marched on the alarm of April 19, 1775, to Roxbury; service, 10 da
2 CONC ys; also, 2d Major, Col. Ezra Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt. of Mass. militia; list of field officers proposed by Legislature Jan. 12, 1776; regiment made up of men belonging to Mendon, Uxbridge, Northbridge, Upton, and Douglas; 
2 CONC also, 2d Major, Col. Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt.; list of field officers of Mass. militia; commissioned Feb. 15, 1776; also, Captain, 8th co., Col. Wood's (3d Worcester Co.) regt. of Mass. militia; list of officers; commission
2 CONC ed April 10, 1778; also, return dated Douglas, May 28, 1778, made to the Superintendent of Worcester Co., by said Whiting, Captain, of men enlisted into the Continental Army for the term of 9 months; also, Captain, Col. Benjamin H
2 CONC awes's regt.; entered service July 28, 1778; discharged Sept. 12, 1778; service on expedition to Rhode Island; also, resignation dated May 17, 1780, signed by said Whiting, resigning his commission as Captain of 8th co., 3d Worces
2 CONC ter Co. regt., which position he had held a number of years, on account of his advanced age and because his superior officers were younger men than himself; resignation approved by Col. Nathan Tyler; ordered in Council June 6, 178
2 CONC 0, that the resignation be accepted. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of CALEB WHITING and HANNAH FAIRBANKS are: 
2 CONT * i. SARAH WHITING, b. January 26, 1755; m. DAVID ALEXANDER, October 13, 1774, Douglas, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT * ii. CALEB WHITING, b. November 7, 1756; d. April 12, 1809; m. LUCY ROSS, April 6, 1780, Douglas, Massachusetts. This may be the father of Daniel Whiting. See the Daniel Whiting Research page for details on the possible connectio
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of CALEB WHITING and HANNAH SIBLEY-SOUTHWORTH are: 
2 CONT * iii. JOHN WHITING, b. April 4, 1761, Douglas, Massachusetts; d. February 29, 1808, Douglas, Massachusetts; m. HANNAH FAIRBANKS, May 31, 1780; b. October 5, 1761; d. July 12, 1819. 
2 CONT * iv. HANNAH WHITING (2), b. March 21, 1763; d. January 1855. 
2 CONT * v. ABNER WHITING (3), b. June 20, 1765, Douglas, Massachusetts; d. February 15, 1837, Douglas, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT * vi. TIMOTHY WHITING (4), b. April 1, 1768, Douglas, Massachusetts; d. August 6, 1847, Boston, New York. 
2 CONT * vii. DAVID WHITING (5), b. May 23, 1771, Douglas, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Retrieved from http://myplace.frontier.com/~wandadc/whiting.htm)
2 CONT
