1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Fisher-9427
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah Fisher was born to John and Rebekah Fisher October 9, 1713 in Medfield, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah married John Baxter, October 13, 1732, in Medfield, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah and John had the following known children:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b 1734
2 CONT Nathan, b and d in 1735
2 CONT Mary, 1737; m Thomas Mason in 1763
2 CONT Richard, 1740; settled in Princeton
2 CONT Moses, 1742; settled in Rutland
2 CONT John, 1746
2 CONT Sarah, 1750-1780; m in 1778 Silas Bullard
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah (Fisher) Baxter, widow of Captain John Baxter, died July 30, 1796, in Medfield, Massachusetts.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah (Fisher) Baxter (1713 - 1796)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rebekah Baxter formerly Fisher===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 9 Oct 1713 in Medfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John Fisher and Rebecca (Wheelock) Adams
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Abigail (Adams) Swift [half] and Elisha Adams [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Baxter — married 12 Oct 1732 in Medfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Joseph Baxter, Nathan Baxter, Mary (Baxter) Mason, Richard Baxter, Moses Baxter and John Baxter
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 30 Jul 1796 at age 82 in Medfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 17 Aug 2021 | Created 3 Mar 2016
2 CONT
