1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW HAMPSHIRE (Soldier).  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A068590  DAR Ancestor # A068590]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkanah Lane was born 1 Apr 1719 in Norton, Massachusetts the son of Ephraim Lane and his wife, Ruth (Shepardson) Lane (Norton MA Vital Records, p. 90).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married in Norton, on 10 Jun 1742, to Hannah Tingley (died 15 Sep 1772), the daughter of Samuel Tingley and Hannah (Pidge) Tingley, of Attleboro, Massachusetts (Norton MA Vital Records, p. 267).
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved prior to the American Revolution to Swanzey, Cheshire Co., NH with some members of his family. Elkanah Lane was a veteran of the Revolutionary War. (SAR P-232850) (DAR Ancestor # A068590). Minute Man marched Apr 25, 1775 
2 CONC to Lexington and Concord, MA. Paid 15 days at Cambridge for 5 days in the Militia at another time, 1 £, 9s, 3d. His son Elkanah Jr. served in 1776 at Ft. Ticonderoga.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/201618610/elkanah-lane
