1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GRAVE LOCATION - David Foster died in Winthrop.  He was buried in Winthrop at either Metcalf Cemetery or Lakeview Cemetery.   No gravestone has been located. REVOLUTIONARY WAR SERVICE:  David served for 16 months a
2 CONC s a private in the Massachusetts and Rhode Island Militia. He served under Captain McCobb, Col. Enos, and Captain Olney, and participated in the Seige of Boston, the Battle of Bunker Hill; went to Quebec by the way of the Kennebec
2 CONC  River, and the Battle of Princeton---  He received a pension for his service, and is recognized as a Patriot by the DAR - Daughters of the American Revolution.   His father, several of his brothers, and his father-in-law were als
2 CONC o Revolutionary War Patriots. MARRIAGE:  In 1783, David married Melicent How, the daughter of Ichabod and Sarah How. CHILDREN:  David and Melicent had ten children.
2 CONT
2 CONT David and family were included in Stackpole's History of Winthrop, and in FOSTER GENEALOGY published in 1899 by F. C. Pierce.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/228288941/david-foster Find A Grave Memorial] - [https:
