1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Twitchell married Deborah Fairbanks, 2 June 1739, daughter of Eleazer Fairbanks, of Sherborn, and with her was recieved in the church, 27 July 1740. Deborah Fairbanks was descended from Jonathan Fairbanks wh
2 CONC o came from Sowerby, in the West Riding of Yorkshire, England, to Boston, Massachusetts., in the year 1633, and settled in Dedham, Massachusetts, where he built the noted "Old Fiarbanks House",the oldest dwelling which is still st
2 CONC anding in New England for that same period of time and has been continuously owned and occupied by the builder's lineal decendents. It was claimed that the house was built in 1636. George Fairbanks second son of Jonathan, resided 
2 CONC in Dedham until 1657, when he moved to Medfield, now Medway, Massachusetts. His dwelling in Medfield was the famous stonehouse near the Northern order of Bogestow Pond, in the eastern part of town, which is now in the place called
2 CONC  Millis, incorporated in 1885. It originally was a garrison-house. George Fairbanks was drowned in 1682, and his son, Jonathan inherited the stone house. He also was drowned in 1719, while attempting to cross the river from Medfie
2 CONC ld. The farm then fell to his two sons, Samuel and Jonathan, a part of which was sold to their uncle, George, who occupied the S.W. portion of the original homestead, in recent years occupied by Frank E. Coo.
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://reocities.com/Heartland/Ranch/8457/Twitch.html
