1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The existence of Mary's four daughters is contained in her mother's Will.[7] Mary Albee's mother, Mary Thayer, made her Will on 12 Aug 1740. She made a codicil to her Will on 14 Oct 1743. In her original Will, she made a bequest 
2 CONC to her daughter, Mary Albee. In the Codicil, she stated that Mary Albee was deceased, so she gave Mary's share of the estate to Mary's daughters: Mary Wood, Martha Sheffield, Elizabeth Albee, Margaret Albee.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Property
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed: "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986," images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-99ZH-K639?cc=2106411&wc=MCBL-3WR%3A361612201%2C361677201 : 22 May 2014), Worcester > Deeds 1751-1754 vol 33-34 > ima
2 CONC ge 94 of 623; county courthouses and offices, Massachusetts. (21 Oct 1748: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >James Albee and Mary his wife, Samuel Albee, Seth Albee, Margaret Albee all of Mendon, with Samuel Wood of Upton with Mary his wife and Isaac Sheffeild of Holliston and Martha his wife for £25 convey to Josiah Ward of Mendon five
2 CONC  eighth parts of a tract in Menond on a plain common called Mill Plain on the South side of the country Road about 7 acres bounded by hiers of Samuel Daniels [and others]. 16 Apr 1751 acknowledged by Margaret Albee now Margrett Ha
2 CONC yward plus the others.)
