1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac moved from Massachusetts to Gray (formerly New Boston), Maine between 1765 and 1770 and was killed when a tree accidentally fell on him. He was the first Foster in Gray. "He was well educated, and came of goo
2 CONC d family. Some of the old people have told that he had two brothers come to see him and they were very nicely dressed and stopped at the hotel, claimed that he married beneath him."
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # Patience YOUNG b: ABT 1746 in Falmouth, York County, Maine
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # John Foster b: October 1, 1786
2 CONT # Isaac Foster b: January 24, 1770
2 CONT # Jacob Foster b: September 3, 1771
2 CONT # Joseph Foster b: March 23, 1773
2 CONT # Samuel Foster b: July 6, 1774
2 CONT # Rachel Foster b: April 28, 1776
2 CONT # William Foster b: April 28, 1776 d: young
2 CONT # Hepsibeth Foster b: July 21, 1777
2 CONT # Moses Twichell Foster b: December 23, 1778
2 CONT # William Foster b: October 7, 1781 d: September 2, 1857
2 CONT # Rebecca Foster b: February 24, 1784
