1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anne Tompson''', the second daughter of Edward Tompson, was born in Simsbury, Connecticut, on December 31, 1689.[1]. Anne Thomas died in Pembroke, Massachusetts, on March 1, 1722-3, aged 33 years, 3 months (Pembroke Center Ceme
2 CONC tery records). She is buried in Pembroke Center Cemetery, although it appears that her gravestone is no longer extant.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr12/rr12_131.html#P16158
2 CONT
2 CONT 27265. Lieut. Isaac Thomas. Born on 19 Oct 1682 in Marshfield, MA.42 Isaac died in Pembroke, MA 16 Mar 1731/2.395 Buried in Pembroke Centre Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac first married Anna Thompson, second Abigail Cushing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac lived in Pembroke (now Hanson) on the lands purchased by his father from the Indians Jeremiah and Matthias.42
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 Oct 1711 when Isaac was 28, he first married Anna Thompson, daughter of Rev. Edward Thompson (20 Apr 1665-16 Mar 1704/5) & Sarah Webster (31 Jul 1659-aft 1704), in Newbury, MA.60 Born on 31 Dec 1689 in Newbury, MA. Anna died
2 CONC  in Pembroke, MA 1 Mar 1722/3.42 Buried in Pembroke Cemetery.42
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna died in childbirth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Capt. Edward Thomas (14 Oct 1713-26 Dec 1802).  Married Rachel Cushing. 
2 CONT # Anne Thomas (Died soon) (22 May 1715-28 Aug 1715)
2 CONT # Mary Thomas (Died soon) (27 Jul 1716-13 Oct 1716)
2 CONT # Mary Thomas (6 May 1718-14 Oct 1796).  Married Benjamin Jacob. 
2 CONT # Ruth Thomas (12 Apr 1721-14 Sep 1806). Married Josiah Cushing. 
2 CONT # (infant child) Thomas (Died soon) (Mar 1722/3-1 Mar 1722/3). This unnamed child was buried with her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 Jan 1723/4 Isaac second married Abigail Cushing (35267)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
