1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001, Essex, Ipswich, Parish baptisms, marriages, deaths 1665-1838 vol. 3, p. 25
2 CONT
2 CONT 1694, Line 5: Mr. Thomson of Newbury, Daughter Abigail Sept. 23
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail's birthplace is listed in the Record of Births, Publishments, Marriages and Deaths In the Town of Ipswich.  Collected from the Essex County Records from 1635 to 1687, And also from the Parish Records of the several Parishe
2 CONC s of said Town and not hertofore entered in the  Town Records.
2 CONT Per this record, Abigail was christened on 23 September 1694 in Rowley, Essex, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The town of Rowley was originally colonized as a plantation by Reverend Ezekiel Rogers who arrived on The John of London with about twenty families.  In 1639, the grant for Rowley, Massachusetts was from Ipswich on the south to Ne
2 CONC wbury on the north, and from the ocean on the east to the Merrimack River on the west.  
2 CONT On September 4, 1639, the town was incorporated, and included portions of modern-day Byfield, Groveland, Georgetown, and Haverhill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Byfield is a Village in the town of Newbury, Newbury in Essex County, Massachusetts. Rowley borders Byfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial ID: 60396845
