2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Batt was born 4 July 1688, in Newbury, Massachusetts. He was the son of William Moulton Jr. (1664-1732) and Abigail (Webster) Moulton (1662-1723).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 4 December 1712, Batt married Hannah (Sibley) Moulton (1696-1729) in Newbury, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Batt's wife Hannah died on 8 September 1729, in Amesbury, Massachusetts.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 29 May 1730, Batt married Jemima George (abt.1701-1752) in Newbury, Massachusetts.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Batt Moulton passed away in 1750. There is no record of his death. Find A Grave states it is 1750, but there is no tombstone.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
