2 CONT 50. JOHN9 MERRILL (JOHN8, NATHANIEL7 +MERRILL, NATHANIEL6 *MERRILL, NATHANIEL5, JOHN4 *MERRELL, THE YOUNGER, JOHN3 *MERYELL, JOHN2, THOMAS1) was born April 3, 1696 in Newbury, Essex, Mass, and died 1773 in Concord, NH. He married 
2 CONC LYDIA HAINES January 15, 1722/23 in Haverhill, Essex, Mass, daughter of THOMAS HAINES and HANNAH HERRIMAN. She was born August 7, 1705 in Newbury, Essex, Mass, and died Unknown in Concord, NH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOHN MERRILL: From "A Merrill Memorial" by Samuel Merrill, Cambridge, MA 1917-1928
2 CONT
2 CONT John(4) Merrill (John(3), Nathaniel(2)) was born 3 Apr 1696 in Newbury, MA, and died in 1773 in Concord, NH. He lived in 1718 in York, ME and from there removed to Haverhill, MA, where he married. About 1730 he was one of the firs
2 CONC t settlers in Concord, NH, and established the first ferry there across the Merrimack River. His home was "on the Hill at the lower end of Main St. at the junction of the roads." Dec 17 1730, he was chosed deacon of the Congregati
2 CONC onal Church. In many ways he was a prominent citizen of Concord. He married , 15 Jan 1722/23, Lydia Hayes, daughter of Thomas and Hanna (Harriman) Hayes of Haverhill. She was born 7 Aug 1705 and died in Concord. Children, the firs
2 CONC t four were born in Haverhill, the rest in Concord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of JOHN MERRILL and LYDIA HAINES are: 
2 CONT * i. THOMAS10 MERRILL, b. February 5, 1723/24, Haverhill, Essex, Mass; d. July 2, 1788, Conway, N.H.; m. (1) PHEBE ABBOT, 1747, Concord, N.H.; b. November 22, 1727, Concord, N.H.; d. 1755, Concord, N.H.; m. (2) MEHITABLE HARRIMAN,
2 CONC  Aft. 1756; b. January 14, 1725/26, Plaistow, N.H.; d. Abt. 1764; m. (3) ABIGAIL GOODHUE, April 2, 1765, Stratham, N.H.; b. Abt. 1730, Stratham, N.H.; d. Abt. 1779; m. (4) ELIZABETH ABBOT, October 9, 1780; b. November 8, 1738, Hol
2 CONC lis, N.H.; d. October 12, 1789, Conway, N.Y.. 
2 CONT * ii. JOHN MERRILL, b. November 25, 1725, Haverhill, Essex, Mass; d. 1760, Bow, N.H.; m. REBECCA ABBOT, Abt. 1750, Concord, N.H.; b. May 27, 1731, Concord, N.H.; d. Aft. 1760. 
2 CONT * iii. MOSES MERRILL, b. September 27, 1727, Haverhill, Essex, Mass; d. 1767; m. DORCUS ABBOT, March 1747/48, Pembroke, N.H.; b. November 11, 1728, Andover, Mass; d. Unknown. 
2 CONT * iv. LYDIA MERRILL, b. November 30, 1729, Haverhill, Essex, Mass; d. Unknown; m. AMOS FOSTER, Abt. 1750; b. Bef. 1729; d. Unknown. 
