1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (IV) Daniel, son of Thomas Mighill Miles & Abigail Maccaflin, was born about 1710; died in 1777. He was known in some records as '''Daniel Mighill.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # (first) Susanna , who died before 1762. 
2 CONT # (second) (intention dated November 6, 1762) Abigail Kingsley, of Pomfret, Connecticut. His widow Abigail married, May 16, 1786, David Sanderson at Petersham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by first wife, born at Petersham: 
2 CONT * 1. Susannah, December 20, 1740; married, April 5, 1767, Samuel Curtis. 
2 CONT * 2. Joab, March 13, 1741; soldier in revolution; father of Daniel Miles, grandfather of Daniel C. Miles, of Westminster, and of General Nelson A. Miles, United States army. 
2 CONT * 3. Joanna, September 12, 1742. 
2 CONT * 4. Daniel, mentioned below. 
2 CONT * 5. Benjamin, August 9, 175—. 
2 CONT * 6. Abigail, July 18, 175—. 
2 CONT * 7. Patience, April 3, 175—. 
2 CONT * 8. Freedom, May 20, 175—. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of second wife: 
2 CONT * 9. Dana, January 22, 1764. 
2 CONT * 10. Benjamin, November 1, 1768.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?lpg=PA639&dq=daniel+miles+1762+abigail+kingsley&pg=PA638&id=ofcsAAAAYAAJ&ots=0zyU-d5sAN#v=onepage&q=daniel%20miles%201762%20abigail%20kingsley&f=false New England Families, Genealogical and Mem
2 CONC orial:] A Record of the ..., Volume 2 edited by William Richard Cutter.  "Miles."  Pages 638-639
2 CONT
2 CONT >He was an early settler at Nichewaug, afterward Petersham, Worcester county, Massachusetts. He was there as early as 1740, when the birth of a daughter is recorded. Daniel Miles and Nehemiah Coy, of Nichewaug, deeded to Aaron Whi
2 CONC tney a lot originally drawn by Edward Houghton in Nichewaug, October 2, 1745. Daniel Miles, of Nichewaug, John Williams, of Pomfret, and Thomas Miles, of Canterbury, Connecticut, deeded to Joseph Hinds and Silas Bennett, of Shrews
2 CONC bury, land at Nichewaug, being the whole of the right of Ephraim Houghton, except a house lot and two divisions laid out previously, by deed dated April 2, 1751. The mother of Daniel may have been a Houghton. Daniel Miles bought l
2 CONC and in Petersham, March 19, 1762, of Dennis Lockley, of Templeton, Massachusetts. Daniel Miles deeded land at Petersham to his son Daniel in 1771. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >His will was dated June 10, 1771, bequeathing to children, Daniel, Joab, Dana, Benjamin, Joanna, Susanna, Patience and Freedom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
