1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Mary Bruen, wife of John Baldwin of Milford, CT=
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald Lines Jacobus (see citation below) demonstrated conclusively that Mary Bruen was the daughter of Obadiah Bruen and Sara(h) ____ (? Seeley).    There has been a controversy as to whether Mary Bruen was the '''sister''' of Ob
2 CONC adiah or the daughter of Obadiah.  Obadiah's father, John Bruen of Stapleford did have a daughter, Mary, baptized 14 July 1622, who died young.  The date of the baptisim was supplied by the Vicar of Tarvin.  Obadiah's brother, Joh
2 CONC n Bruen, states definitely that of his his father's children from his third marriage, two died young and only Joseph survived.  This statement according to Jacobus  "...effectively disbars the claim that the wife of John Baldwin, 
2 CONC Sr., was this Mary [child of John Bruen and his third wife]..."  In addition, he notes that  Mary Bruen named her children Obadiah and Sarah after her parents.  And finally, Mary Bruen is said in her marriage record to be of Pequo
2 CONC t [New London], which fits with her being the daughter of Obadiah Bruen and Sarah ___ of New London!
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruen, baptized at St. Julians, Shrewsbury, Shropshire, England, 12 June 1634, died at Milford, 2 Sept. 1670, daughter of Obadiah and Sarah ( ) Bruen.  See Donald Lines Jacobs and also Ancestry and descendants of Frederick Tr
2 CONC acy Camp & his wife Marion Fee
2 CONT John F. Camp, Nathan Grier Parke.  J.F. Camp, 1961. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruen was the second wife of John Baldwin who was much older.  She was the mother of
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary, born Sept 7, 1654
2 CONT # Sarah, born Dec 25, 1655
2 CONT # Abigail, born Nov 15, 1658
2 CONT # Obadiah, born Oct 29, 1660
2 CONT # Hannah, born Nov 20, 1663
2 CONT # George, born June 13, 1665
2 CONT # Richard, born June 1665
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT # Families of Early Milford, Connecticut by Suzanne Emma Woodruff Abbott  p. 14 - 15.
2 CONT # "Ancestry of Obadiah and Mary Bruen," by Donal Lines Jacobus, in The American Genealogist (1949), Vol 26, pp 12 - 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Mary Bruen's Royal Ancestry=
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruen was a descendant of a number of the Anglo-Norman noble families, including de Bohun, de Warrenne, de Montfort, de Say, etc. as follows (Note - as of 3/13/2011 taken from a family history so will be corrected as the Angl
2 CONC o-Norman lines on Geni are verified):
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary Bruen's father was [http://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruen/6000000006979363766?through=6000000000689076874 John Bruen, Esquire] of Bruen Stapleford.
2 CONT # John Bruen's mother was [http://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Dorothy-Holford/6000000006979633753?through=6000000006979363766 Dorothy Holford], daughter of Thomas Holford
2 CONT # Thomas Holford's wife was [http://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Jane-Holford/6000000006979988031?through=6000000006979633753 Lady Jane Booth], daughter of Sir William Booth and Ellen Montgomery
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-William-Booth/6000000008640674342?through=6000000006979988031 Sir William Booth] was the son of George Booth, Esq and Katharine de Montfort
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-de-Montfort/6000000006100960457?through=6000000008640674342 Katharine de Montfort] was the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Montfort/6000000002106169658?through=600000000610096
2 CONC 0457 Robert de Montfort], son of Sir Baldwin de Montfort
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Baldwin-De-Montfort/6000000006444072721?through=6000000002106169658 Baldwin de Montfort] was the son of Sir William de Montfort of Colshill, Warwickshire, Knight
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/William-de-Montfort/6000000002101237251?through=6000000006444072721 Sir William de Montfort of Colshill] married Margaret, daughter and heir of Sir John Peche of Hampton in Arden
2 CONT # The father of Sir William de Montfort, [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Baldwin-de-Montfort/6000000003615689655?through=6000000002101237251 Sir Baldwin de Montfort], married [http://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-de-Clinton/6000000
2 CONC 003615689661?through=6000000003615689655 Margaret de Clinton], daughter of Sir John Clinton of Maxstoke.  Sir Baldwin de Montfort was the son of Sir John and grandson of Peter de Montfort of Beldesert in Warwickshire.
2 CONT # Margaret de Clinton's parents were [http://www.geni.com/people/Idonea-de-Say/6000000003827339725?through=6000000003615689661 Idonea de Say] (daughter of Geoffrey de Say) and Sir John de Clinton.  Sir John (born 1323) was the son
2 CONC  of Sir John de Clinton.
2 CONT # Idonea de Say was the daughter of Maud de Beauchamp (daughter of Guy de Beauchamp) and Geoffrey de Say, Knight (born 1305), son of Geoffrey
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Maud-de-Beauchamp/6000000010679171212?through=6000000003827339725 Maud de Beauchamp] was the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Guy-de-Beauchamp-Earl-of-Warwick/6000000005858685119 Guy de Beaucha
2 CONC mp] who was the second husband of Alice de Tony (de Toeni), daughter of Ralph.  Guy de Beauchamp was the sixth in descent from Walter de Beauchamp, steward to King Henry I. '''[NOTE: Weis' Ancestral Roots--citing CP XI: 477, CP XI
2 CONC I(1): 774 note 1 and XII (2): 370-72--says that Maud (who married Geoffrey de Say) is the daughter of Guy de Beauchamp and Alice de Toeni (widow of Thomas Leybourne, daughter of Ralph VII de Toeni; later married William la Zouche)
2 CONC . CP is Complete Peerage or Cokayne's Peerage.]'''
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Alice-de-Toeni/6000000008508704002?through=6000000005858685119 Alice de Toeni] was the daughter of  Ralph de Toeni (the son of Roger de Toeni and the seventh in descent from Roger de Toeni, standard b
2 CONC earer to William the Conqueror)
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Ralph-de-Toeni/6000000002166198144?through=6000000008508704002 Ralph de Toeni] was the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Alice-de-Bohun/6000000000276143606?through=6000000002166198144 Alice de Bohun]
2 CONC  (daughter of Humphrey the Good) and Roger de Toeni
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Humphrey-IV-de-Bohun-2nd-Earl-of-Hereford-1st-Earl-of-Essex/6000000001744825938?through=6000000000276143606 Humphrey de Bohun], Earl of Hereford and High Constable of England, born 1176, married Maud,
2 CONC   daughter of Ralph de Issodun, Earl of En
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Humphrey-IV-de-Bohun-2nd-Earl-of-Hereford-1st-Earl-of-Essex/6000000001744825938?through=6000000000276143606 Humphrey de Bohun's] parents were Henry de Bohun, Earl of Hereford and High Constable of Eng
2 CONC land and Maud, the only daughter of Geoffrey Fitz-Piers, Justice of England and Earl of Essex.
2 CONT # Henry de Bohun's parents were Margaret, daughter of Prince Henry and Adela de Warrenne and Humphrey de Bohun, the fourth of that name
2 CONT # Adela de Warrenne was daughter of William the second Earl.  Her husband was Henry, Earl of Huntington, brother of Malcolm IV and William the Lion, both of who were in turn kings of Scotland
2 CONT # William de Warrenne, Second Earl of Surrey, married Elizabeth, daughter of Hugh the Great, Count of Vermandois, brother of Phillip I, King of France and son of Henry I of France and Anne of Russia, who was the grand-daughter of 
2 CONC Romanus II, Emperor of Constantinople.
2 CONT #
