2 CONT == Biography == This Mary Bruen, daughter of [[Bruen-24|Obediah Bruen]] and [[Seeley-1014|Sarah Seeley]], was baptized 12 June 1634 at Julians, Shrewsbury, England.<ref name=Jacobus>D. L. Jacobus, "The Ancestry of Obadiah Bruen" i
2 CONC n ''The American Genealogist''. (New Haven, CT). Online with subscription at AmericanAncestors.org, [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB283/i/11819/13/23572582 vol. 26 (1950) pages 12-17].</ref>
2 CONT NOT THIS MARY: [[Bruen-41|Mary Bruen]], daughter of [[Bruen-32|John Bruen Esq.]] and his third wife, bap. 14 Jul 1622 at Tarvin, Cheshire, England<ref>"England, Cheshire Parish Registers, 1538-2000," index, FamilySearch (https://f
2 CONC amilysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/F7YY-2J4 : accessed 08 Feb 2014), Mary Bruen, 1622.</ref> is NOT the second wife of John Baldwin, Sr.<ref>"Additions and Corrections for 'Families of Early Milford Connecticut by Susan Woodruff Abbott'
2 CONC " in ''The Connecticut Nutmegger''. (Glastonbury, CT: Connecticut Society of Genealogists). Online at AmericanAncestors.org (w/subscr.), [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB59/i/11798/214/134602750 vol. 13 (1980) page 214].</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth :: 1634 Shrewsbury, Shropshire, England<ref name=Ball/> :: Arrival New England<ref name=Immigration>U.S. and Canada, Passengerand Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s Author: Ancestry.com  Page: Place: New England; Year: 164
2 CONC 0; Page Number: 163</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes (previously on [[Bruen-41]] )==<i>Mary Bruen BIRTH</i>: 1634, Shrewsbury, Salop, England <u>[Ref#83,#113]</u>:: <i>DEATH</i>: 2 Sep 1670, Milford, Connecticut, America <u>[Ref#113]</u>
2 CONT :: <i>NOTE </i>: Second wife. <u>[Ref#83]</u> :: <i>NOTE </i>: 1639, emig. to America.:: 10923.<b> Mary Bruen.</b> Born ca Jun 1634 at Shrewsbury, Shropshire. Baptized on 12 Jun 1634 at St. Julians, Shrewsbury. Mary died at Milfor
2 CONC d, CT, on 2 Sep 1670.71 :: :: On 13 Oct 1653 Mary married <u>John Baldwin (2620)</u>, son of <u>John Baldwin (702)</u> (ca 1565-bef 14 Oct 1637) & Hannah [Baldwin] (-aft 14 Oct 1637), at Milford, CT.<u>79</u> Born in 1593 at Wendo
2 CONC ver, Buckinghamshire. John died at Milford, CT, in Jun 1681. Buried on 21 Jun1681 in Milford, CT.<u>79 :: </u> ::  :: From Abbott's <i>Families of Early Milford</i>:<u>71 :: </u>:: "John Balwin will dated 24 May 1681. ... Admitted
2 CONC  to the church 1652. ... He was not a freeplanter because he was not a member of the church but later joined on 19 March 1648. His home lot was #113 on the map of 1646, containing 2 acres 1 rod and 10 poles." :: :: Charles Candee 
2 CONC Baldwin, author of <i>The Baldwin Genealogy,</i><u>10</u> was not convinced that John Baldwin of Wendover, son of John & Hannah Baldwin, was the John Baldwin who settled at Milford. ::  :: Children: :: 9427	i. 	<u>Mary</u> (1654-1
2 CONC 676) :: 9428	ii. 	<u>Sarah</u> (ca1655-1729) :: 9429	iii. 	<u>Abigail</u> (1658-1739) :: 9430	iv. 	<u>Obadiah</u> (1660-1738) :: 9431	v. 	<u>Hannah</u> (1663-1691) :: 9432	vi. 	<u>George</u> (1665-1728) :: 9433	vii. 	<u>Richard</u
2 CONC > (1665-1726) :: :: 10.<b> </b>Charles Candee Baldwin, <i>The Baldwin Genealogy from 1500 to 1881</i>, Cleveland, Ohio, 1881. :: :: 71.<b> </b>Susan Woodruff Abbott, <i>Families of Early Milford, Connecticut</i>, Genealogical Publ
2 CONC . Co., Baltimore, 1979. ::  :: 79.<b> </b>"Milford Vital Records." ::  :: http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr05/rr05_151.html#
2 CONT
2 CONT :: 1634 Shrewsbury, Shropshire, England<ref name=Ball/>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===
2 CONT : Child: [[Baldwin-3787|Abigail Baldwin]]:: 13 Oct 1653 Milford, New Haven, Connecticut, USA<ref name=Marriage>Connecticut, Town Marriage Records, pre-1870 (Barbour Collection) Author: Ancestry.com P</ref><ref name=Marriage24>Amer
2 CONC ican Marriages Before 1699 </ref> Second wife of John Baldwin: Mary Bruen b: 14 Jun 1622 in Shrewsbury, Shropshire, England. Married: 15 Aug 1653 in Milford, New Haven, CT. Mary Bruen Baldwin died Sept. 2, 1670, in Milford, CT, wh
2 CONC ere husband John Baldwin was buried June 21, 1681.  John and Mary's children: <ref>Geni: John Baldwin, Sr.(c.1620 - 1681)</ref><ref>Source 15; Will of John Baldiwn dated 24 May 1681</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT :1.Mary Baldwin c: 17 Sep 1654 in Milford, New Haven, CT :2.Sarah Baldwin b: 25 Dec 1655 in Milford, New Haven, CT c: 1655:3.Abigail Baldwin b: 15 Nov 1658 in Milford, New Haven, CT c: Apr 1659 :4.Obadiah Baldwin b: 29 Oct 1660 in
2 CONC  Milford, New Haven, CT:5.George Baldwin b: 13 Jun 1662 in Milford, New Haven, CT c: 28 Oct 1666 in Milford, New Haven, CT. :6.Hannah Baldwin b: 20 Nov 1663 in Milford, New Haven, CT :7.Richard Baldwin b: 27 Sep 1666 in Milford, N
2 CONC ew Haven, CT Notes about Mary Bruen:<ref>Geni: John Baldwin, Sr.(c.1620 - 1681)</ref>The Milford Conn. vital records read: "John Baldwin, Sr.' married (no date) Marie (Mary) Brewen, dau. of John, of Pequot. " Another copy of the M
2 CONC ilford records reads: " Aug15-----. " As "Mary wife of John Baldwin, Sr." was admitted to the Milford church on April 30, 1653, the blank date must be 1652. John Bruen was a well-known English Puritan, which accounts for his menti
2 CONC on in the marriage record, although he died in England. Pequot was the early name for New London, CT, where Mary lived with her distinguished brother Obadiah Bruen.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===:: 2 Sep 1670 Died early in England not Connecticut<ref name=Marriage/><ref name=Death>Connecticut Town Death Records, pre-1870 (Barbour Collection) Author: Ancestry.com </ref><ref name=SAR>U.S., Sons of the American 
2 CONC Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970 Author: Ancestry.com  Page: SAR Membership Number: 97893</ref>:: 2 SEP 1670 Milford, New Haven, Connecticut, United States <ref name=Ball>Descendants of Edward Ball of New Jersey</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==<references />* https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/111054658/obadiah-bruen
2 CONT * Source 15; Will of John Baldiwn dated 24 May 1681: gives to sons John (eldest), Josiah, Nathaniel and Joseph; Dau. Elizabeth Porter; Dau. Abigail Baldwin, two daughters Sarah and Hannah; Sons George, Obediah (no doubt named afte
2 CONC r the father of his (2) wife Mary Bruen) and Richard. In February of 1639, Milford was purchased of the Indians and the Conn. settlement was made during the year. His name does not appear onthe list of Free Planters drawn up on 29
2 CONC  Nov. 1639, as he was not a church member. His name is appended as among the settlers, but not a voting member in the colony.* <span id='GCF'></span>[[Space:Genealogies of Connecticut Families|Genealogies of Connecticut Families]]
2 CONC  (Genealogical Pub. Co., 1983) Vol.1, [https://books.google.com/books?id=k6fDl9gE45IC&pg=PA79 Page 79]
2 CONT * David Baldwin of Summit (1795 -1878), Schoharie County , N.Y. His Ancestors & Decendants, compiled by Frank Boyd Baldwin, Peoria, Illinois, 1964
