2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: New Haven Colony]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Hannah Bruen was born on 9 Jan 1642/3 in Gloucester in the Massachusetts Bay Colony. Hannah died in Newark, NJ, ca. 1685.
2 CONT On 30 Oct 1663 Hannah was married to [[Baldwin-3383| John Baldwin]] son of [[Baldwin-1576|John Baldwin]], by Robert Treat in Milford in the New Haven Colony.<ref>''Connecticut: Vital Records (The Barbour Collection), 1630-1870'', 
2 CONC [http://archive.org/details/vitalrecordsofmi00milfMilford, p. 11] (accessed 11 Sep 2017).</ref> John's wife Hannah Bruen was niece of his stepmother Mary Bruen<ref> [https://archive.org/details/baldwingenealogy00bald Charles Cande
2 CONC e Baldwin, The Baldwin Genealogy from 1500 to 1881, Cleveland, Ohio, 1881]</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT *[http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~marshall/esmd125.htm Bruen Family Genealogy]
2 CONT * http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr05/rr05_151.html#P93652
2 CONT *Charles Candee Baldwin, <i>The Baldwin Genealogy from 1500 to 1881</i>, Cleveland, Ohio, 1881.
2 CONT * Susan Woodruff Abbott, <i>Families of Early Milford, Connecticut</i>, Genealogical Publ. Co., Baltimore, 1979*''Connecticut: Vital Records (The Barbour Collection), 1630-1870'' (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New Englan
2 CONC d Historic Genealogical Society, 2011.) From original typescripts, Lucius Barnes Barbour Collection, 1928. (subscription required)* <span id='GCF'></span>[[Space:Genealogies of Connecticut Families|Genealogies of Connecticut Famil
2 CONC ies]] (Genealogical Pub. Co., 1983) Vol.1, [https://books.google.com/books?id=k6fDl9gE45IC&pg=PA78 Page 78]* <span id='Jacobus'></span>Jacobus, Donald Lines. ''Ancestry of Obadiah and Mary Bruen'', [[Space:TAG|The American Genealo
2 CONC gist]] (1950) Vol. 26, Page 12.
