1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Seeley-93
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Seeley (abt. 1653 - bef. 1690)
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Seeley
2 CONT Born about 1653 in New Haven, Connecticutmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Nathaniel Seeley and Mary (Turney) Seeley
2 CONT Brother of Nathaniel (Seeley) Seelye, Benjamin Seeley, Joseph Seeley, John Seeley, Mary (Seeley) Squire, Sarah (Seeley) Squire, Phebe Seeley and Rebecca Seeley
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Olmstead) Seeley — married before 16 Mar 1675 [location unknown]
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Sarah (Seeley) Gregory, Elizabeth Seeley, Nathaniel Seeley, Robert Seeley Jr. and Nehemiah Seeley
2 CONT Died before 30 Jun 1690 before about age 37 in Fairfield, Connecticut Colonymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Kyle Gillett private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 6 May 2024 | Created 12 Jul 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 1,403 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Seeley was born about 1653 in New Haven, Connecticut, son of Nathaniel Seeley (<1627–~1675) and Mary Turney (1631–1675).
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (21) married Sarah Olmstead (19) (born in 1655 in Fairfield, Connecticut; daughter of Nehemiah Olmstead and Elizabeth (Burr) Seeley) on March 16, 1675.[1] Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Seeley (~1675– )
2 CONT Elizabeth Seeley (1675–>1705)
2 CONT Nathaniel Seeley (~1680– )
2 CONT Robert Seeley (1683–1753)
2 CONT Nehemiah Seeley (~1685–~1779)
2 CONT Robert died before June 30, 1690 in Fairfield, Connecticut Colony, aged about 36. Robert was mentioned on a memorial in Old Stratfield Cemetery, Bridgeport, Fairfield County, Connecticut, United States with a death date of 30 June
2 CONC  1690.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Marriage: "U.S., New England Marriages Prior to 1700"
