2 CONT *'''Sir William Stanley1
2 CONT *'''M, #14627, b. 1437, d. 16 February 1494/95
2 CONT *Last Edited=6 Mar 2011
2 CONT *'''     Sir William Stanley was born in 1437 at Lytham, Lancashire, England.2 He was the son of Sir Thomas Stanley, 1st Lord Stanley and Joan Goushill.3 He married, firstly, Joan Beaumont, daughter of John de Beaumont, 1st Viscou
2 CONC nt Beaumont and Elizabeth Phelip, in 1465.4 He married, secondly, Elizabeth Hopton, daughter of Thomas Hopton and Eleanor Lucy, before 7 December 1471.1 He died on 16 February 1494/95 at Tower Hill, The City, London, England, behe
2 CONC aded.1
2 CONT *'''     He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.).1 He fought in the Battle of Bosworth on 22 August 1485, where he played a decisive role in King Henry VII's victory.3 He lived at Holt, Norfolk, England.3 In 1494 H
2 CONC e was found guilty of treason for his support of Perkin Warbeck.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir William Stanley
2 CONT ** 1.Jane Stanley+2 b. c 1463, d. 1525
2 CONT *Citations
