2 CONT
2 CONT EARLY YEAR OF THE WARS OF THE ROSES
2 CONT In the early years of the Wars of the Roses, William gave his support
2 CONT to the Yorkists., fighting in the Battle of Blore in September 1459, When the
2 CONT Yorkists were victorious  The following year he fled England as did other 
2 CONT Yorkists leaders.  On 11 June 1460 he was Declaared a traitor, with his 
2 CONT given as "squier" 
2 CONT
2 CONT His adherence to the Yorkists cause was rewarded in 1461, when 
2 CONT Edward IV gained the throne. William was made Chamberlain of Cheter,
2 CONT Constable of the Castle of Flint, and Sheriff of Flintshire.  He was Knighted
2 CONT
