2 CONT ______________
2 CONT
2 CONT in July 1461.  He helped secure Nort Wales and the North of England , and
2 CONT took part in the 1462 siege of Ainwick, Northumberland, suppling 400 
2 CONT archers.  In 1464 he fought in the Battle of Hexham,  Afterward he was
2 CONT granted the lordship of Skipton, Yorkshire, which had previously been held
2 CONT by John Clifford, along with other Clifford lands.
