2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Sir John Done1,2,3 
2 CONT *'''M, #44357, b. circa 1443, d. circa 1498
2 CONT *Father     Sir John Done d. 1460
2 CONT *'''     Sir John Done was born circa 1443 at of Utkinton, Cheshire, England. He married Elizabeth Weaver, daughter of Thomas Weaver, Esq. and Elizabeth, before 28 June 1487; They had 2 sons (Richard, Esq; & William) and 3 daughte
2 CONC rs (Ellen, wife of David Middleton, of Piers Holland, & of Urian Brereton; Mary, wife of Richard Bruen, Esq; & Joan, wife of Tochet Beeston, Esq.).1,2,3 Sir John Done died circa 1498.1,3
2 CONT *'''Family      Elizabeth Weaver b. c 1440, d. 17 Feb 1513
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Joanna Done+ b. c 1468, d. c 1542
2 CONT **Ellen Done+4 b. c 1470
2 CONT **Richard Done, Esq.+ b. c 1487, d. a 1517
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 490.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 126.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 25.
2 CONT * 4.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1476.htm#i44357
2 CONT *______________
2 CONT *John STANLEY (Sir)
2 CONT *Born: 1436, Weever, Alderley, Chester, England 
2 CONT *Died: ABT 1485
2 CONT *Father: Thomas STANLEY (Knight Lord of Lathom)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan GOUSHILL
2 CONT *'''Married: Elizabeth WEEVER (b. ABT 1438 - d. 1515) (dau. of Sir Thomas Weever and Elizabeth Fitton) (w. of Sir John Done)
2 CONT *Children: .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY5.htm#John STANLEY (Sir)1
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Wever-83307 about 1464 in Wever, Cheshire, Eng. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *” The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester: Comp. from ..., Volume 2”  By George Ormerod.  Page 248.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=dIY1AQAAMAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA843-IA106&dq=William%20Wyrrall%201435%20jane%20done&pg=
2 CONC RA1-PA248#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00689583&tree=LEO
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The Heroines of Welsh History: Comprising Memoirs and Biographical Notices of the Celebrated Women of Wales ... Thomas Jeffery Llewelyn Prichard W. and F. G. Cash, 1854 - Wales - 586 pages. Page 187. [https://books.google.com/book
2 CONC s?id=_lgJAAAAIAAJ&vq=Sir%20John%20Done&dq=the%20Heroines%20of%20Welsh%20History%3A%20Compromising%20Memoirs…%22&pg=PA187#v=onepage&q&f=false  GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elyn Done, the lady of this memoir, was the daughter of Sir John Done, and resided with her parents at Utkinton, in the county of Chester. Her affections had been won by a Welsh gentleman named David Myddelton, but her parents wer
2 CONC e strongly opposed to their union, and determined on ha»ing her married to her cousin Richard Done, of Croten, in their own immediate neighbourhood. ....
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
