1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Torbock-3
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Torbock Born about 1497 in Huyton, Lancashire, Englandmap ANCESTORS  Son of William Torbock and Margery (Stanley) Torbock Brother of Margaret (Torbock) Dalton [half] Husband of Elizabeth Moore — married [date unknown] [loca
2 CONC tion unknown] DESCENDANTS  Father of William Torbock Died 20 Sep 1554 in Lancashire, England Profile managers: Frances Doyle  and Magna Carta Project WikiTree Profile last modified 3 Nov 2020  Created 15 Jun 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Magna Carta Surety Baron Descendant (see text). Thomas Torbock is in trails badged by the Magna Carta Project to several surety barons (see text below).
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Thomas Torbock, Esquire of Tarbock, Lancashire, son and heir of William Torbock was born about 1497 to Margery Stanley, daughter of John Stanley, Esquire of Weever and Over Alderley, Cheshire.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Moore, daughter of William Moore, Esquire of Bank-house at Kirkdale, Lancasahire. The couple had three sons, Willliam, Edward and Richard, and two daughters, Margaret (m. William Ireland) and Alice (m. John Ha
2 CONC rington).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas passed away 20 Sep 1554, leaving an undated will, proved in 1554, requesting burial at Huyton, Lancashire.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, (2011), Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Royal Ancestry series, 2nd edition, 4 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham, (Salt Lake City, Utah: 
2 CONC the author, 2011), volume III, page 127 Richardson, Royal Ancestry (2013) Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham, (Salt Lake City, Utah: the author, 2013),
2 CONC  volume IV, page 26. Dobson, John B. "The Ancestry of Oliver Mainwaring: Torbock." Genealogy Page of John Blythe Dobson. University of Winnipeg, 3 Apr. 2010. Web. 21 Feb. 2015. uwinnipeg.ca. Langton, William, ed. The Visitation of
2 CONC  Lancashire and a Part of Cheshire. Vol. II. Manchester: Chetham Society, 1882. Print. archive.org Acknowledgements Magna Carta Project Thomas Torbock appears in Magna Carta Ancestry in a Richardson-documented trail from the Manwa
2 CONC ring Gateway Ancestors, Oliver Manwaring and Mary (Mainwaring) Gill, to Magna Carta Surety Baron Saher de Quincy (vol. III, pages 126-129 MANWARING) that was badged in February 2015 by the Magna Carta Project. The Project later id
2 CONC entified this profile in other badged trails between the Manwaring Gateways and surety barons Roger le Bigod, Hugh le Bigod, Henry de Bohun, Gilbert de Clare, Richard de Clare, John de Lacy, Saher de Quincy (2nd trail) and Robert 
2 CONC de Vere. A trail to surety William Malet was also identified and is not yet badged. All the trails need re-review to ensure they meet current project standards. The trails are set out in the Magna Carta Trails section of the Gatew
2 CONC ay's profile. Needs Re-review: This profile needs re-review against the project's checklist to bring it up to current project standards. ~ Thiessen-117 09:31, 3 September 2020 (UTC) See Base Camp for more information about identif
2 CONC ied Magna Carta trails and their status. See the project's glossary for project-specific terms, such as a "badged trail".
2 CONT
