2 CONT **	Dalton.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/visitationsyork00britgoog#page/n98/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.86
2 CONT *Roger Dalton of Dalton Hall in Yorkshyre & after of Croston had no issue by his 2 and 3 wyffe. = . . . .  doughter of Sir John Ratclyf of Lancashyre fyrst wyff. ; ch: '''1. William (m. Margaret Terboke''' & Jane Towneley), 2. Rog
2 CONC er (sine prole.), Sybell (m. William Wolberd Draper) Dalton ; = 2. . . . .  doughter of Standyche. ; = 3. . . . .  doughter of Faryngton. ; = 4. See next page (Pg.87 Jane Jakes)
2 CONT **'''1. William Dalton of Bispam''' son & heyre to Roger '''= Margaret doughter of Sir William Terboke of Terboke Hall fyrst wyf to William. ; ch:''' Robert (sine prole), Roger (sine prole), Jane (sine prole), Margery (m. . . . . 
2 CONC  Wenloke & Gylbert Moreton), 3 others  (sine prole) Dalton. ; = 2nd to Jane bass doughter to Sir John Towneley of Lancashyre. ; ch: Robert (m. Anne Kechyn), Thomas (2 son.), Roger (3 son.), Rychard 4 son.), Anne (m. . . . .  Westm
2 CONC er) Dalton
2 CONT ***Margery fyrst wyff to . . . .  Wenloke & after to Gylbert Moreton & had issue by nether of them but dyed sans issu.
2 CONT ***Robert dalton of Thurnam weded Anne doughter of John Kechyn. _________________
2 CONT *'''The John Dalton book of genealogy     by Dalton, Mark Ardath
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/johndaltonbookof00dalt
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/johndaltonbookof00dalt#page/25/mode/1up
2 CONT **PEDIGREE OF DALTON FAMILY
2 CONT **compiled by JOHN LUCHER DALTON 1889
2 CONT *   A copy was obtained from Voyla Dalton Smith, the daughter of John Luther Dalton and a copy of the Dalton pedigree chart sent to Sarah Cedenia Dalton of Parowan, Utah, by John Luther Dalton. 
2 CONT *   In a letter sent to me, dated March 19, 1960, Mrs. Voyla Dalton Smith has this to say, "Father left on a mission to England the 28th of April 1863 and re- turned 1866. He also made a subsequent trip to England for genealogical
2 CONC  research in 1888 and compiled his findings in 1889. Father never put down the source of his information as I have indicated but Mother said that he searched histories, deeds, wills, cemetery records and etc." 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/johndaltonbookof00dalt#page/26/mode/1up
2 CONT *   .... etc.
2 CONT *— 12 — 
2 CONT *   Roger Dalton married twice, first Miss Radcliff of Wymerly 
2 CONT *— 13 — 
2 CONT * '''  Their son William''', 1513, Byspham, Lancashire, '''also married twice. He had no children by his first wife''', and his second wife was Jane Townley or Towerly. By her he had three sons. 
2 CONT *— 14 — 
2 CONT *   1 -Robert Dalton, married Ann Kitchin and he died without male issue. 
2 CONT *   2-Thomas Dalton, married Ann Molyneux. Thomas inherited Thurnham and other properties and his descendants in the female line have lived at Thurnham Hall up till about thirty years ago. 
2 CONT *   3 -Roger Dalton (Our Line) married Mary Ward or Warer of Lancashire. 
2 CONT *— 15 — 
2 CONT *   .... etc. ______________
2 CONT *'Dalton01'
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *                              (A) Roger Dalton of Dalton Hall
2 CONT *                                m1. _ Ratclyff (dau of Sir John Ratclyff of Lancashire)
2 CONT **'''                                   (i) William Dalton of Bispam
2 CONT **'''                                     m1. Margaret Terboke''' (dau of Sir William Terboke of Terboke Hall)
2 CONT ***                                        (a) Margery Dalton (dsp)
2 CONT ***                                          m1. _ Wenloke
2 CONT ***                                          m2. Gylbert Moreton
2 CONT ***                                        (b)+ other issue (dsp) - Robert, Roger, Jane, 8 others
2 CONT **                                     m2. Jane (natural daughter of Sir John Towneley of Lancashire)
2 CONT ***                                        (m) Robert Dalton of Bispham, Pillin and Thurnham (dsp 1580)
2 CONT ***                                          m. Anne Kechyn (dau of John Kechyn)
2 CONT ***                                        Visitation ends with this generation, identifying Robert as "of Thurnham". This is presumed to be the Robert who is the first mentioned by Commoners, being described therein as "of Bishpa
2 CONC m and Pilling, who acquired by purchase, in 1556, the manor and estate of Thurnham" and who was succeeeded by his nephew.
2 CONT ***                                        (n) Thomas Dalton
2 CONT ***                                          m. Anne Molyneux (dau of Sir Richard Molyneux of Sefton)
2 CONT ****                                             ((1)) .... etc.
2 CONT ***                                        (o) Anne Dalton
2 CONT ***                                          m. _ Westmer
2 CONT ***                                        (p)+ other issue - Roger, Richard
2 CONT **                                   (ii)  .... etc.
