1 NAME Margaret /Stanley/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN Stanley
2 _MARNM Grimshaw
2 NICK Margaret Stanley AKA Harrington
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1490
2 PLAC Hornby Castle
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hornby
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1549
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Margaret Stanley
2 CONT * AKA “daughter and heir of Sir John Harrington” on Visitations (should be grand daughter) 
2 CONT * Died: 1549 
2 CONT *Father: John STANLEY of Melling
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth HARRINGTON Married: Thomas GRIMSHAW
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Grimshaw, {died 1539} and married Margaret, daughter and co-heiress of Elizabeth, daughter of Sir John Harrington, of Hornby, by John Stanley, of Melling, esq. Illegitimate son of James Stanley, Bishop of Ely. They had seve
2 CONC n children: -
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Richard Grimshaw, {died 1575} (cont.)
2 CONT * 2. Henry Grimshaw
2 CONT * 3. Nicholas Grimshaw
2 CONT * 4. Ralph Grimshaw
2 CONT * 5. Anne Grimshaw
2 CONT * 6. Alice Grimshaw
2 CONT * 7. Isabel Grimshaw, {living 1513}
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Comment''' from Stirnet:
2 CONT
2 CONT > Dugdale identifies Thomas's wife as Margaret, dau/heir of Sir John Harrington of Horrneby Castle, but (noting that she was the coheir of her mother) Whitaker identifies her as ...  Margaret Stanley (dau of John Stanley of Mellin
2 CONC g, natural son of James Stanley, Bishop of Ely, by Elizabeth, dau of Sir John Harrington of Hornby.  
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From 'Townships: Melling', in A History of the County of Lancaster: Volume 3, ed. William Farrer and J Brownbill (London, 1907), pp. 208-215. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/lancs/vol3/pp208-215 [access
2 CONC ed 27 August 2016].
2 CONT
2 CONT * 32. Duchy of Lanc. Inq. p.m. xiii, n. 34; xiv, n. 81. Dame Jane's sisters were Anne, who married John Swift, and Margaret, who married Thomas Grimshaw. For the latter's claim see Add. MS. 32105, n. 813. Margaret Grimshaw, widow,
2 CONC  died in 1549, holding the third part of 34 messuages, 1,000 acres of land, &c., 8 'oppells' of a horse-mill and a watermill in Melling, Aintree, and Liverpool. All was held of the king by the third part of a knight's fee, and 4s.
2 CONC  5¼d. rent. The heir was her son Richard, forty-six years of age; Duchy of Lanc. Inq. p. m. ix, n. 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000193809926822&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *< [https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00638546&tree=LEO Genealogics.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT * < [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/grimshaw01.php Stirnet: ‘Grimshaw01’] > cites 
2 CONT ** (1) the pedigree on 'Clayton-les-Moores' within vol II of 'An History of the Original Parish of Whalley and Honor of Clitheroe', originally by Thomas Dunham Whitaker (1818), continued & completed by Rev. Ponsonby A. Lyons (1876
2 CONC )
2 CONT ** (2)  < [https://s3.amazonaws.com/photos.geni.com/p13/b2/c3/d6/fd/53444840bc5bad67/grimshaw_of_clayton_in_the_moors_pedigree_original.jpg "Grimshaw of Clayton in the Moors"] > Dugdale's Visitation of Lancashire in 1664-5 mixes u
2 CONC p Margaret Stanley with her mother Elizabeth Harrington 
2 CONT **< [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stanley02.php#linklo2 Stirnet: ‘Stanley02’] > 
2 CONT * < [http://grimshaworigin.org/miscellaneous-grimshaw-individuals/early-grimshaw-family-history/ Early Grimshaw Family History] > mixes up Alice Grimshaw (who married John Holden) with an earlier Alice Grimshaw (who married Robert
2 CONC  Waddington) - corrected at < [https://faysampson.co.uk/family-history/jack-priestleys-family-history/19-waddington-grimshaw/ “Jack Priestley’s Family History”] > 
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00638547&tree=LEO
2 CONT * Source: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY5.htm#Margaret STANLEY1 Added by; HRH Prince Kieren de Muire Von Drakenberg
