1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Massey b. c.1515, 1st s. of Sir John Massey by Katherine, da. of Thomas Venables, Baron of Kinderton, and aunt of Sir Thomas Venables. m. (1) Anne (d.1568), da. of George Booth of Dunham, 6s. 2da.; (2) Marg
2 CONC aret, wid. of Richard Forsett and of Roger Amyce. suc. fa. 1551.
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/genealogyofbooth00boot/page/10
2 CONT
2 CONT George, born about 1515, died 35 Henry VII. (see his history), 
2 CONT * i. Elizabeth, who married Richard Sutton. 
2 CONT * ii. Dorothy, who married Robert Tatton. 
2 CONT * v. Anne, who married William Massey ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1477.htm#i44383
2 CONT
2 CONT George Booth, Esq. was born circa 1490 at of Dunham-Massey, Cheshire, England; Age 29 in 1519.1,2,4 He married Elizabeth Boteler, daughter of Sir Thomas Boteler, Seneschal of Liverpool and Margaret Delves, circa 1514; They had 3 s
2 CONC ons (George, Esq; John; & Robert) and 7 daughters (Ellen, wife of John Carington; Anne, wife of William Massy, Esq; Margaret, wife of Sir William Davenport; Elizabeth, wife of Richard Sutton, Esq; Dorothy, wife of Robert Tatton, E
2 CONC sq; Alice, wife of Peter Daniell, Esq; & Cecily).
