1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Ravenscroft1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #19579, d. 1588
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=7 Apr 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT      Elizabeth Ravenscroft was the daughter of Thomas Ravenscroft and Catharine Grosvenor.1 She married Thomas Egerton, 1st Viscount Brackley, son of Sir Richard Egerton and Alice Sparke, before 1576.2 She died in 1588.1 She was b
2 CONC uried at Doddleston, Chester, England.1
2 CONT       Her married name became Egerton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Ravenscroft and Thomas Egerton, 1st Viscount Brackley
2 CONT  1.Hon. Mary Egerton+3
2 CONT  2.Sir Thomas Egerton+1 b. b 1579, d. Aug 1599
2 CONT  3.John Egerton, 1st Earl of Bridgwater+1 b. 1579, d. 4 Dec 1649
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT  1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 272. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT  2.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 271.
2 CONT  3.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 1673. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1958.htm#i19579
2 CONT *_____________________________
2 CONT *'''Thomas Egerton, 1st Viscount Brackley, PC (1540 – 15 March 1617) was an English nobleman, judge and statesman who served as Lord Keeper and Lord Chancellor for twenty-one years.
2 CONT *Thomas Egerton was born in 1540 in the parish of Dodleston, Cheshire, England. He was the illegitimate son of Sir Richard Egerton and an unmarried woman named Alice Sparks. He was acknowledged by his father’s family, who paid for
2 CONC  his education. He studied Liberal Arts at Brasenose College, Oxford, and received a Bachelor’s Degree in 1559. He then studied law at Lincoln's Inn and became a barrister.[1] He was a Roman Catholic, until a point in 1570 when hi
2 CONC s lack of conformity with the Church of England became an issue when his Inn passed on a complaint from the Privy Council.[2]
2 CONT *He built a respectable legal practice pleading cases in the Courts of Queen’s Bench, Chancery and Exchequer. After Queen Elizabeth I saw him plead a case against the crown he was made Queen's Counsel. In 1579 he was made a Master
2 CONC  of the Bench of Lincoln’s Inn. On 28 June 1581 he was appointed Solicitor General.
2 CONT *'''He married Elizabeth Ravenscroft and by her fathered:
2 CONT ** Thomas, who married Elizabeth Venables; their daughter, Mary, was married to Thomas Leigh, 1st Baron Leigh
2 CONT ** John (his heir),
2 CONT ** Mary, who married Sir Francis Leigh.
2 CONT *As Solicitor General, Egerton became .... etc.
2 CONT *'''During this time his first wife died''', and he married Elizabeth Wolley, the widow of Sir John Wolley, and daughter of Sir William More of Loseley, Surrey. He bought Tatton Park, in 1598. It would stay in the family for more 
2 CONC than three centuries.[3] Also at this time - 1597 or 1598 - he hired John Donne as secretary. This arrangement ended in some embarrassment, since Donne secretly married Ann More, Elizabeth's niece, in 1601.
2 CONT *Elizabeth died around the beginning of 1600, and then Egerton married Alice Spencer, whose first husband had been Ferdinando Stanley, 5th Earl of Derby.[4][5] She survived him by two decades, and was an important patron of the ar
2 CONC ts, usually known as the Dowager Countess of Derby.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Egerton,_1st_Viscount_Brackley
2 CONT *_________________________ '''EGERTON, Thomas I (1540-1617), of Lincoln's Inn, Islington, York House and Harefield, Mdx. and of Chester.
2 CONT *b. 23 Jan. 1540, illegit. s. of Sir Richard Egerton of Ridley, Cheshire by Alice Sparke. educ. Brasenose, Oxf. 1556; L. Inn 1560, called 1572. '''m. (1) bef. 1576, Elizabeth (d.1588), da. of Thomas Ravenscroft of Bretton, Flints.
2 CONC , 2s. John and Thomas II 1da.'''; (2) privately 1597, Elizabeth (d.1600), da. of William More I, sis. of Sir George More of Loseley, wid. of Richard Polsted and John Wolley, s.p.; (3) 1600, Alice, da. of Sir John Spencer†, of Alth
2 CONC orp, Northants., wid. of Ferdinando, 5th Earl of Derby, s.p. Kntd. 1594; cr. Baron Ellesmere 1603, Visct. Brackley 1616.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/egerton-thomas-i-1540-1617 __________________
