1 OCCU Squire of Ollerton Hall
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the father of https://www.geni.com/people/Hughe-Baguley/6000000175888977113
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Please site ORIGINAL DOCUMENTS and SOURCES, i.e. photos of gravesites, wills, land deeds, baptismal certificates, marriage records from parishes, etc. as scholarly research is needed on this family! Thank you! Otherwise this shoul
2 CONC d not be a master profile. Much of what is on the internet on family websites contain errors.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Bigelow Society website (drawn from Somersby's research, Robert Baguley of Ollerton Hall who was who died November 4, 1582, HAD ONLY 2 SONS:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Randell de Baguley married Jane had seven children and died in 1626
2 CONT * 2. John de Baguley died in 1597 WIFE UNKNOWN
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://josfamilyhistory.com/htm/hopkins/butler/butler-bigelow.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT BAGULEY, spouse unknown. The Bigelow Genealogy cites the descent to the American John Bigelow through Robert. He had three sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Randall Baguley (died 1636)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.John Baguley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT i.   Randall Baguley, died May 1626 in Wrentham, Suffolk, England; married Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.  John Baguley.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.  Hugh, b ca 1580; d ca 1629.  Subject: Bigelow/Baguley/Bagley/Begley [NO]
2 CONT
2 CONT I only recently discovered that your surname and mine are derivatives of the same root.  I am descended from Robert Baguley (1550-1590) through his son  [sic - unproven] Hugh (1580-1629) down to the immigrant Peter born in 1608 in
2 CONC  Siddington, Cheshire and landing in Nansemond County, Virginia in 1635.  The name changed to Bagley during the 17th century and to Begley during the 18th.  Family legend has it that our earliest ancestor was transported to Americ
2 CONC a for stealing a goose - and that the village was named for the family.  For years I have been trying to locate a village in England called Begley.  If you would like more information on your southern cousins, write me back and I'
2 CONC 'll provide you with what I have.  Regards   David Begley 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Lineage 
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188680855855&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments: Somerby is known to have produced tampered pedigrees.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT ''Research note: I don't think there is an Ollerton or a Knutsford in Suffolk, but both these places exist in Cheshire??'' Name:  Robert of Ollerton Bigelow (Baguley)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Taking Bigelow as the last name from Bigelow (Baguley).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Death''': 4 NOV 1582 in Knutsford, Suffolk, England, Age:  25-26
2 CONT
