1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Margarey Mainwaring''' was born 1396 in Baddiley, Nantwich, Cheshire, England. She married William Bromley on 1408 in Baddington, Cheshire, England. She was the daughter of Sir Randle (of Over Peover) Mainwaring
2 CONC  and Margery de Venables. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Bromley on 1408 in Baddington, Cheshire, England, son of John /Bromley/ and Margery (of Tatton) /Massey/. He was born 1392 in Baddington, Nantwich, Cheshire, England, and died 1430. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margarey /Mainwaring/ and William /Bromley/ are:
2 CONT #Sir (Knight) John Bromley was born 1409 in Baddington, Nantwich, Cheshire, England, and died 1488
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sr John Needham Justice of the King's Bench & Chester 2 sonn of Robert ob. 1480 [Judge of Common Pleas 1457; Judge of King's Bench 1472]. = '''Margery da. to Randall Mannering widow to Will'm Bromley of Cheverton [Shrawardine ?].'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Randle_Mainwaring_(1367-1456)
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester: Comp. from Original Evidences in Public Offices, the Harleian and Cottonian Mss., Parochial Registers, Private Muniments, Unpublished Ms. Collections of Successive Cheshire A
2 CONC ntiquaries, and a Personal Survey of Every Township in the County; Incorporated with a Republication of King's Vale Royal and Leycester's Cheshire Antiquities, Volume 1 by George Ormerod, Daniel King, William Smith, William Webb (
2 CONC sheriff.), Sir Peter Leycester, 1882
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > … Agnes, another daughter, was affianced to William Bromley of Badington in Cheshire, son of sir John Bromley, but she died before marriage; whereupon he married Margaret, sister to Agnes. This Margaret was a widoe 15 Hen. VI. 1
2 CONC 436. After she married sir John Nedham of Crannich, justicarius de banco, and judge of Chester 1 Edw. IV. But sir John Nedham had no issue by her.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT I have my doubts about  Margery Mainwaring being married to Sir Lawrence (De Warenne) Warren (1394 - c.1443).
2 CONT
2 CONT Here are a couple of references 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Ancestral roots of certain American colonists who came to America before ... By Frederick Lewis Weis, Walter Lee Sheppard, Kaleen E.  <[http://books.google.com/books?id=3F9nG8aFJ7MC&pg=PA206&lpg=PA206&dq=Lawrence+De+Warenne&sour
2 CONC ce=bl&ots=9jB9kFFpxp&sig=gxsV_6tK39RG9pXkUcBw-RfKc8U&hl=en&ei=b-3BS_PYOcyknwe74JmHCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CBcQ6AEwBg#v=onepage&q=Lawrence%20De%20Warenne&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT * Representative men and old families of southeastern Massachusetts ..., Volume 3 < [ http://books.google.com/books?id=GHIWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1676&lpg=PA1676&dq=Nicholas+Of+Headboro+Warren&source=bl&ots=1n-xacuIYk&sig=_B0O2VBN7ABYc4Xsy
2 CONC hR-9dktf1I&hl=en&ei=MvHBS8DONojlnQesnbG6Cg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CBYQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT * https://wc.rootsweb.com/trees/143095/I10406/margarey-mainwaring/registry
2 CONT * https://archive.org/details/TheVisitationOfShropshireV.29/page/n94/mode/1up?view=theater
