1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173426903969 Stanley 1 (May 10, 2024; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham  Published 2005
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA1099&lpg=PA1099&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&source=bl&ots=2Ewbuw0F3N&sig=amyJUT1pP9FfbnhwRw0p_-APrSM&hl=en&ei=AybKTe2VLYm6sAOVxpGMAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=resul
2 CONC t&resnum=2&ved=0CB4Q6AEwATg8#v=onepage&q=Stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 303
2 CONT *  10. MARY SAVAGE, married (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral) and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, Sheriff of Cheshire, son and heir of William Stanley, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral) and S
2 CONC toreton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire by his 2nd wife, Blanche, daughter of John Arderne, Knt. He was born about 1405 (aged 23 in 1428). They had four sons, William, Esq., John, Richard, and Thomas. In 1424 his widowed mot
2 CONC her, Blanche, released her rights to the manor of Stanley, Staffordshire and lands in Chorlton and Le Moels (both in Wirral), Cheshire to him.  He was heir in 1428 to his grandfather, William Stanley, Knt. In 1432 he granted lands
2 CONC  in Pulton Launcelyn, Bromburgh and le Spitall to Edward de Hoghton and others. In 1434 Richard Coly of Chester granted him lands in Pennesby and Thingwall. In 1437 king ordered the constable of Windsor Castle to take William Stan
2 CONC ley, his brother-in-law, John Savage, Knt., Randolph Brereton, and Urian Brereton into custody for an unspecified offence. In 1439 Richard Bolde was appointed the marriage of Richard Donne, the king's ward, by mainprise of William
2 CONC  Stanley, of Hooton, Cheshire, Esq., and another. He was granted a pardon by the king in 1446. 
2 CONT **Pg. 304
2 CONT **  11. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral), and Storeton, Cheshire, Stanley, Staffordshire, etc., son and heir, born say 1425. He married ALICE HOGHTON (or HOUGHTON), daughter of Richard Hoghton, Knt., of Hoghton (in Ley
2 CONC land), Lancashire, by his wife, Margaret. They had one son William, Knt., and one daughter Isabel (wife of John Marchumley). In 1450 he fought for the king against the traitor, Jack Cade, of Kent. In 1454 John Hertcombe granted au
2 CONC thority to John Savage the younger, William Stanley esquires, and Thomas Kendale to cause a deed to be made in his name regarding the castle, lordship and manor of Mold, Flintshire. In 1460 he was pardoned L166 in arrears as late 
2 CONC receiver of Richard, Duke of York, of the lordship of Denbigh in Wales. In 1462 he and others were appointed to take muster of Roland Fitz Eustace, Knt., and 300 archers at some convenient place near Chester. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq.
2 CONC , died 17 FEb 1466. His wife, Alice, was living 11 March 1465/6.
2 CONT ***''''''  12. WILLIAM STANLEY, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral), Roveacre, and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, son and heir, born about 1445. He married (1st) MARGARET BROMLEY, daughter and co-heiress of John Bromley, 
2 CONC Knt., of Badington (in Acton), Cheshire, by Joan, daughter and co-heiress of William Hexstall, Knt. They had one daughter, Margery. His wife, Margaret, died in 1469. He married (2nd) in 1470 AGNES GROSVENOR, daughter and co-heires
2 CONC s of Robert Grosvenor, Esq., of Holme, Cheshire, by Joan, daughter of Lawrence Fitton, Knt. They had a son, William, Knt. William was knighted about 1484. He was an executor c.1492 of the will of Mr. Henry Medwall, master of St. G
2 CONC iles. SIR WILLIAM STANLEY died in 1512. His widow, Agnes, died in 1520-1.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY4.htm#William STANLEY2
2 CONT *''''''William STANLEY
2 CONT *Born: 1433, Lathom, Lancashire, England 
2 CONT *Died: 3 Mar 1511/2, Hooton, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Notes: Became Sheriff of Chester in 1462 and one of the King's Carvers. In 1465, he was made Sheriff for life and continued in that office until 1494. He built the Old Stone Tower of Hooton.
2 CONT *Father: William STANLEY
2 CONT *Mother: Alicia HOUGHTON
2 CONT *''''''Married: Anne (Agnes) GROSVENOR 1439, Hulme, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **1. William STANLEY (Sir)
2 CONT **2. Agnes STANLEY
2 CONT **3. Alice STANLEY 
2 CONT **4. Catherine STANLEY 
2 CONT **5. Isabel STANLEY (Prioress of Derby) 
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------</nowiki> WRONG PARENTS FOR WM. WHO M. ALICIA HOGHTON
2 CONT *''''''Stanley Descendancy
