2 CONT *http://www.isle-of-man.com/manxnotebook/fulltext/hs173x/p1s01.htm 
2 CONT *Sir William, the son of the above William by Mrs. Houghton, succeeded his father Sir William, and was the eleventh male heir in a direct line ; he married to one of the daughters of John Savage of Clifton, Esq. and by her had iss
2 CONC ue two sons, John and William. I cannot discover that John the elder was ever married, but rather that he died young and without issue : But, 
2 CONT *''''''Sir William'''''', the second son of the above Sir William by Mrs. Savage, succeeded his father as twelfth heir male of his family. He was stiled senior, and ''''''married to his first; wife, Margaret the daughter of John B
2 CONC romley, Esq. by whom he had a daughter, who married to Gerrard of Brinn, in the county of Lancaster ; and Margaret his wife dying, he married to his second wife Agnes, the daughter of Robert Grosvenor of Hulme, Esq. by whom he had
2 CONC  a son named William. 
