2 CONT '''Phillipa Hulse'''1 
2 CONT F, #208700, '''b. 1416'''
2 CONT Last Edited=5 Apr 2023
2 CONT '''     Phillipa Hulse was born in 1416 at Brereton, Cheshire, EnglandG.1 She married William Brereton''', son of Sir William de Brereton and Alice Corbet.2
2 CONT '''     Her married name became Brereton.'''2
2 CONT '''Children of Phillipa Hulse and William Brereton'''
2 CONT 1. Jane Brereton+2 d. 1517
2 CONT 2. Roger Brereton3
2 CONT 3. Andrew Brereton+1 b. 1448, d. 1527
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT 2.[S3268] Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT 3.[S5792] Robin Dening, "re: Rochfort Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 2 January 2012. Hereinafter cited as "re: Rochfort Family."
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p20870.htm#i208700
2 CONT ___
2 CONT '''William BRERETON (Sir)'''
2 CONT Born: 8 Sep 1414, Brereton, Cheshire, England
2 CONT Died: 1485, Chester, Cheshire, England
2 CONT Notes: In 1435, King Henry VI, presented John Browne, clerk, to Malpas Church by reason of the minority of the son and heir of Sir William Brereton, Kt.
2 CONT In Jun 1474, William, jointly with Robert Brereton, rector of Brereton, made over to the bishop and dean of Winchester, and to their heirs and assigns for ever, all his possessions in Lincolnshire; William was the cousin of Willia
2 CONC m Wainflete, bishop of Winchester, who was the son of father's sister, Margery.[4]
2 CONT In 1484, at Chester, Thomas Fyton of Pownall, William Davenport of Broomhall, and Edward Fyton, esquires, gave to William Brereton, knight, and Dame Maud his wife, a bond for observance of covenants on the marriage of the said Tho
2 CONC mas with Elizabeth daughter of the said Dame Maud.
2 CONT Father: William BRERETON (Sir)
2 CONT Mother: Alice CORBETT
2 CONT '''Married 1: Philippa HULSE''' (dau. of Sir Hugh Hulse) 1436, Chester, Cheshire, England
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT 1. William BRERETON of Brereton (Esq.)
2 CONT 2. Roger BRERETON (b. 1442 - d. 1513)
2 CONT 3. Hugh BRERETON of Wimbersley
2 CONT 4. Matthew BRERETON
2 CONT 5. Maud BRERETON
2 CONT 6. Andrew BRERETON of Brereton (Sir)
2 CONT 7. Jane BRERETON
2 CONT 8. Elizabeth BRERETON
2 CONT 9. John BRERETON (Sir)
2 CONT 10. Eleanor BRERETON
2 CONT 11. Henry BRERETON
2 CONT 12. Robert BRERETON
2 CONT Married 2: Maud DUTTON (dau. of Sir John Dutton and Margaret Savage) (w. of William Booth)
2 CONT From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/BRERETON1.htm#William_BRERETON_(Sir)6
2 CONT _____
2 CONT Breretons of Cheshire, 1100 to 1904 A. D (1904)
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/breretonsofchesh00brer
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/71/mode/1up
2 CONT Pg.71
2 CONT '''Sir William de Brerton VIII., tenth Lord of Brereton''', succeeded his grandfather ; died in 1485. His first wife was Matilda, daughter of John Dutton, of Button, widow of Sir William Booth, of Dunham; married in 1478. By her h
2 CONC e had six sons: 1, William, died issueless ; 2, Andrew ; 3, Robert ; 4, Roger ; 5, Henry ; 6, Matthew. William married Katherine, daughter of Sir John Byron, of Horestan Castle, Derbyshire ; his second brother. Sir Andrew, succeed
2 CONC ed his father as eleventh Lord of Brereton. '''His second wife was a daughter of Sir Hugh Hulse, of Elwood Hall, Cheshire. By her he had two sons and four daughters:''' 1. Sir John Brereton, of Lea Hall, whose first wife was Kathe
2 CONC rine, daughter of Maurice Berkeley, of Beverstone, Gloucester, widow of John, Lord Stourton. By her he had one daughter, Wyburgha, heir of her mother ; she married Sir William Compton, knight. His second wife was Joan, daughter an
2 CONC d heiress of Sir Geoffrey Masey, of Hatton, widow of Sir William Stanley. By her he had one son, Philip, who died without issue ; 2, Hugh of Wimbersley, second son, married Anne, daughter of Robert Done, of Utkington ; 3, Elizabet
2 CONC h, wife of John Ratclyffe, of Ordeshall, Lancashire; 4, Jane, wife of Cotton, of Rudware;
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/72/mode/1up
2 CONT Pg.72
2 CONT 5, Eleanor, wife of Hugh Cholmondeley ; 6, Matilda, wife of Thomas Needham, of Shavington.
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire (1978)
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT Pg.74
2 CONT *BRERETON--BARON BRERETON.
2 CONT RALPH DE BRERETON (son of William de Brereton, and grandson of William de Brereton,) was father (besides a 2nd son, Gilbert, and a dau., Isolda, wife of Gilbert de Stoke,) of an elder son and heir.
2 CONT SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, living temp. JOHN and HENRY III., who m. Margery, dau. of Randle de Thornton, and had a son, RALPH, and a dau., wife of Thurstan de Smethwick. The former
2 CONT SIR RALPH BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, had two sons, WILLIAM (SIR), and Gilbert, father of Henry and Sibella, wife of William de Bouths. The elder son,
2 CONT SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. the dau. of his guardian. Sir Richard de Sandbach, Knt., and was father of
2 CONT SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Roesia, dau. of Ralph de Vernon, and had issue,
2 CONT *I. WILLIAM, m. Margery, dau. of Richard de Bosley, and d. in his father's lifetime, leaving issue,
2 CONT **1 WILLIAM (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT **2. etc.
2 CONT *II. John. .... etc.
2 CONT Sir William was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, living 49th EDWARD III., who m. 1st Ellen, dau. of Philip, and sister and finally heiress of David Egerton, of Egerton, and by her had a son and successor,
2 CONT WILLIAM.
2 CONT He m. 2ndly, Margaret, dau. of -- Done, of Utkinton, and widow of John Davenport, and by her had a son and two dau., ..... etc.
2 CONT The eldest son,
2 CONT SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, m. 1st, in 1386, Angella, dau. of Hugh Venables, and by her had issue,
2 CONT *I. WILLIAM, d. before his father, having m. Alice, sister and heiress of Richard Corbett, of Leighton, and by her (who m. 2ndly, John Stretley, Esq.,) had issue,
2 CONT **1 WILLIAM (SIR), successor to his grandfather.
2 CONT **2 Ralph.
2 CONT **1 Alice, wife of Peter Corbett, of Leighton.
2 CONT **2 Johanna, wife of Robert Aston, of Parkhall, co. Stafford.
2 CONT *II. .... etc.
2 CONT Sir William m. 2ndly, Elena, dau. of Sir William Massy, of Tatton, Knt., and by her, who m. 2ndly, Sir Gilbert Halsall, Knt., had a son,
2 CONT *Thomas, in holy orders, rector of Brereton, 1433.
2 CONT Sir William d. 4th HENRY VI., and was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT '''SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Philippa, dau. of Sir Hugh, and sister of Thomas Hulse, and had issue,'''
2 CONT *I. WILLIAM, m. Katherine, dau. of Sir John Byron, and d. s. p.
2 CONT *II. ANDREW (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT *III. John (Sir), m. 1st Katherine, dau. of Maurice Berkeley, of Beverston, and relict of John, Lord Stouron, and by her had a dau. and heiress, .... etc.
2 CONT Sir John m. 2ndly, Jane, dau. and heiress of Geoffrey Massy, of Tatton, and relict of Sir William Stanley, and by her had a son, .... etc.
2 CONT *IV. Robert.
2 CONT *V. Roger.
2 CONT *VI. Henry.
2 CONT *VII. Matthew.
2 CONT *VIII. Hugh, of Wimbersley, m. Anne, dau. of Robert Done.
2 CONT *I. Elizabeth, wife of John Radcliffe of Ordeshall.
2 CONT *II. Jane, wie of Cotton, of Rudware.
2 CONT *III. Eleanor, m. 1st, Thomas Bulkeley, of Eyton, and 2ndly to Hugh Cholmondeley.
2 CONT *IV. Matilda, wife of Thomas Needham, of Shavington.
2 CONT The eldest surviving son,
2 CONT SIR ANDREW BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. Agnes, dau. of Robert Legh, of Adlington, and had issue, .... etc.
2 CONT ______________________________
2 CONT Sybil MILBOURNE
2 CONT Born: ABT 1471, Burghill, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT Died: 26 Nov 1537
2 CONT Notes: some sources says that her husband was John Brereton, Esq., '''son of William Brereton and Phillippa Hulse.'''
