2 CONT *'''Sir William Brereton1
2 CONT *M, #341836
2 CONT *Last Edited=12 Mar 2009
2 CONT *'''     Sir William Brereton lived at Brereton, Cheshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Sir William Brereton
2 CONT ** 1.Maud Brereton+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2158. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p34184.htm#i341836 
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT '''William BRERETON (Sir)'''
2 CONT '''Born: 8 Sep 1414, Brereton, Cheshire, England'''
2 CONT '''Died: 1485, Chester, Cheshire, England'''
2 CONT Notes: In 1435, King Henry VI, presented John Browne, clerk, to Malpas Church by reason of the minority of the son and heir of Sir William Brereton, Kt.
2 CONT In Jun 1474, William, jointly with Robert Brereton, rector of Brereton, made over to the bishop and dean of Winchester, and to their heirs and assigns for ever, all his possessions in Lincolnshire; William was the cousin of Willia
2 CONC m Wainflete, bishop of Winchester, who was the son of father's sister, Margery.[4]
2 CONT In 1484, at Chester, Thomas Fyton of Pownall, William Davenport of Broomhall, and Edward Fyton, esquires, gave to William Brereton, knight, and Dame Maud his wife''', a bond for observance of covenants on the marriage of the said 
2 CONC Thomas with Elizabeth '''daughter of the said Dame Maud'''.
2 CONT Father: William BRERETON (Sir)
2 CONT Mother: Alice CORBETT
2 CONT '''Married 1: Philippa HULSE''' (dau. of Sir Hugh Hulse) '''1436, Chester, Cheshire, England'''
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT 1. William BRERETON of Brereton (Esq.)
2 CONT 2. Roger BRERETON (b. 1442 - d. 1513)
2 CONT 3. Hugh BRERETON of Wimbersley
2 CONT 4. Matthew BRERETON
2 CONT 5. Maud BRERETON
2 CONT 6. Andrew BRERETON of Brereton (Sir)
2 CONT 7. Jane BRERETON
2 CONT 8. Elizabeth BRERETON
2 CONT 9. John BRERETON (Sir)
2 CONT 10. Eleanor BRERETON
2 CONT 11. Henry BRERETON
2 CONT 12. Robert BRERETON
2 CONT Married 2: Maud DUTTON (dau. of Sir John Dutton and Margaret Savage) (w. of William Booth)
2 CONT From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/BRERETON1.htm#William_BRERETON_(Sir)6
2 CONT _____
2 CONT *John RADCLIFFE
2 CONT *Died: 14 Apr 1497
2 CONT *Notes: married Elizabeth, daughter of '''Sir William Brereton of Brereton, co. Chester, a kinsman of the Venables and descended from the same stock'''. John died on the 12 Apr 1497 leaving a family of two sons, Alexander, who suc
2 CONC ceeded his grandfather, William, and three daughters, Christina, Anna, and Elizabeth 
2 CONT *Father: William RADCLIFFE of Ordsall (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Jane TRAFFORD
2 CONT *Married: Elizabeth BRERETON
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Alexander RADCLIFFE of Ordsall (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **2. Margaret RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **3. William RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **4. Christina RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **5. Anne RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **6. Elizabeth RADCLIFFE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/RADCLIFFE3.htm#John RADCLIFFE1 
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 4
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera04burk
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera04burk#page/401/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.401
2 CONT * Alexander Radclyffe, esq. of Ordshall, who m. Agnes, daughter of Sir William Harrington, knt. of Hornby Castle, in Lancashire, and by her, who died in 1490, liad issue, 
2 CONT ** I. William, his heir. 
2 CONT ** II. Robert ... etc.
2 CONT * Alexander Radclyffe d. in 1476, and was s by his eldest son, 
2 CONT * William Radclyffe, esq. of Ordshall, who m. Jane, daughter of Sir Edmund Trafford, knt. of Trafl'ord, and by her, who wedded, secondly, James Byron.of Clayton, and, thirdly, Talbot, of Salesbury, had issue, 
2 CONT **	I. John, who m. Elizabeth, daughter of '''Sir William Brereton, knt. of Brereton, in Cheshire''', and dying, v. p. 12th April, 1497, left issue, 
2 CONT *** Alexander (Sir), successor to his grandfather. 
2 CONT *** William. 
2 CONT *** Christian, m. to William Hulton, esq. 
2 CONT *** Margery, wife of Thurstan Parr.
2 CONT *** ____ , m. to Sir Richard Aston, knt. of Middleton. 
2 CONT * William Radclylffe. d. 15th May, 13 Henry VII. and was s. by his grandson. 
2 CONT * Sir Alexander Radclyffe, of Ordshall, knt. high sheriff of Lancashire in 1547, who m. Alice, daughter of Sir John Booth, knt. of Barton, in Lancashire, and had issue, .... etc. 
2 CONT ____________________________________
2 CONT *'''Breretons of Cheshire, 1100 to 1904 A. D (1904)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/breretonsofchesh00brer
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/71/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.71
2 CONT *'''   Sir William de Brerton VIII., tenth Lord of Brereton, succeeded his grandfather ; died in 1485. His first wife was Matilda, daughter of John Dutton, of Button, widow of Sir William Booth, of Dunham; married in 1478. By her 
2 CONC he had six sons''': 1, William, died issueless ; 2, Andrew ; 3, Robert ; 4, Roger ; 5, Henry ; 6, Matthew. William married Katherine, daughter of Sir John Byron, of Horestan Castle, Derbyshire ; his second brother. Sir Andrew, suc
2 CONC ceeded his father as eleventh Lord of Brereton. '''His second wife was a daughter of Sir Hugh Hulse, of Elwood Hall, Cheshire. By her he had two sons and four daughters''': 1. Sir John Brereton, of Lea Hall, whose first wife was K
2 CONC atherine, daughter of Maurice Berkeley, of Beverstone, Gloucester, widow of John, Lord Stourton. By her he had one daughter, Wyburgha, heir of her mother ; she married Sir William Compton, knight. His second wife was Joan, daughte
2 CONC r and heiress of Sir Geoffrey Masey, of Hatton, widow of Sir William Stanley. By her he had one son, Philip, who died without issue ; 2, Hugh of Wimbersley, second son, married Anne, daughter of Robert Done, of Utkington ; 3, Eliz
2 CONC abeth, wife of John Ratclyffe, of Ordeshall, Lancashire; 4, Jane, wife of Cotton, of Rudware; 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/72/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.72
2 CONT * 5, Eleanor, wife of Hugh Cholmondeley ; 6, Matilda, wife of Thomas Needham, of Shavington.  
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT *'''Brereton; a family history (1919)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/9/mode/1up
2 CONT *   About 1176, Ralph de Brereton, a grand-son of the first Ralph, is witness in a grant of Marton to Richard de Davenport. 
2 CONT *   About 1194, William de Brereton, son of this last Ralph, received a deed at the time of his marriage to Margery, daughter of Randle de Torhaunt, eight witnesses signing the contract. This William was knighted by Henry III in 1
2 CONC 208, the beginning of honors held in the Brereton family for over five hundred years. 
2 CONT *   In 1216, Sir Ralph de Brereton, son of William, granted land to "Brereton" church, as shown by parish records still in existence. 
2 CONT *   About 1232, this Sir Ralph received payment of "half a salt works" for some public services done in Cheshire. 
2 CONT *   During the year 1250, Sir William Brere-
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/10/mode/1up
2 CONT *ton was witness to legal documents in Chester. In 1307, another William Brereton was witness to four deeds still on file there. The same year, William le Brereton, Kt, was witness to deeds of sale in Chester. 
2 CONT *   Sir William Brereton, Kt., son and heir of Ralph, married a daughter of Sir Richard de Sandbach, in fulfillment of a contract made with William de Venables. 
2 CONT *   About 1275, Sir William Brereton married Roesia, daughter of Ralph de Vernon. This wedding united the Breretons with the Vernons of "Haddon Hall," so well described by Majors in the novel "Dorothy Vernon." This Sir William lat
2 CONC er gave one hundred marks for the marriage of their daughter Margery to Thomas de Davenport in 1301. He was knighted by Edward III in 1321. 
2 CONT *   In 1342, Sir William and his wife, Roesia, united in a deed of lands in Brereton parish. Roesia must have believed in "woman's rights" and had her name put in the deeds. This Sir William received indulgences from the Pope for 
2 CONC services rendered in 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/11/mode/1up
2 CONT *the Crusades to the Holy Sepulchre, about 1350. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/13/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Returning to the records, we find that William de Brereton, son of the previous Sir William, died before his father, leaving a son of the same name. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/14/mode/1up
2 CONT *   In 1354, Sir William Brereton, heir to his grandfather, married Ellena, daughter of David de Egerton, a descendant of the Norman barons; by this alliance the Brereton estates were greatly extended, placing their social standin
2 CONC g among the best in England. 
2 CONT *   In 1386, Sir William Brereton, son of the above, married Anylla, daughter of Sir William Venables, a descendant of Gilbert de Venables, first baron of Cheshire, and grantee of the first Brereton estate, three hundred years bef
2 CONC ore. By a second marriage, to Elena, daughter of Sir William Massey of Tatton Hall, in 1426, the Brereton holdings were among the great estates of England, including the manors of Malpas and Picton, with lands in Woodhull, Crouton
2 CONC , Charlton, and Norwich. 
2 CONT *   William de Brereton, son of the above, married Alice, sister and heiress of Sir Richard Corbett of Leighton ; this William died during the life of his father. About this time the "de" was dropped from English names, as it was 
2 CONC simply a descriptive 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/15/mode/1up
2 CONT *term and never a title, nor represented any special honor. 
2 CONT *   In 1409, a record says that King Henry removed the Mayor of Chester and placed Sir William Brereton in charge as military governor. 
2 CONT *'''   William Brereton, on the death of his grandfather, in 1435, was found heir to the vast estates of Brereton, and also the estates of his step-mother, in Tilston and Herthull, as recorded in 1438. He was knighted in 1485. His
2 CONC  son''', William Brereton, died issueless, breaking the line of descent, the succession passing to his nephew, son of Sir Andrew Brereton, in 1507.  
2 CONT ______________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire (1978)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.74
2 CONT **	BRERETON--BARON BRERETON.
2 CONT *   RALPH DE BRERETON (son of William de Brereton, and grandson of William de Brereton,) was father (besides a 2nd son, Gilbert, and a dau., Isolda, wife of Gilbert de Stoke,) of an elder son and heir. 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, living temp. JOHN and HENRY III., who m. Margery, dau. of Randle de Thornton, and had a son, RALPH, and a dau., wife of Thurstan de Smethwick. The former 
2 CONT *   SIR RALPH BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, had two sons, WILLIAM (SIR), and Gilbert, father of Henry and Sibella, wife of William de Bouths. The elder son, 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. the dau. of his guardian. Sir Richard de Sandbach, Knt., and was father of 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Roesia, dau. of Ralph de Vernon, and had issue, 
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, m. Margery, dau. of Richard de Bosley, and d. in his father's lifetime, leaving issue,
2 CONT ***		1 WILLIAM (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT ***		2. etc.
2 CONT **	II. John. .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir William was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, living 49th EDWARD III., who m. 1st Ellen, dau. of Philip, and sister and finally heiress of David Egerton, of Egerton, and by her had a son and successor,
2 CONT **	WILLIAM.
2 CONT *He m. 2ndly, Margaret, dau. of -- Done, of Utkinton, and widow of John Davenport, and by her had a son and two dau., ..... etc.
2 CONT *The eldest son,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, m. 1st, in 1386, Angella, dau. of Hugh Venables, and by her had issue,
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, d. before his father, having m. Alice, sister and heiress of Richard Corbett, of Leighton, and by her (who m. 2ndly, John Stretley, Esq.,) had issue,
2 CONT ***'''		1 WILLIAM (SIR), successor to his grandfather.
2 CONT ***		2 Ralph.
2 CONT ***		1 Alice, wife of Peter Corbett, of Leighton.
2 CONT ***		2 Johanna, wife of Robert Aston, of Parkhall, co. Stafford.
2 CONT **	II. .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir William m. 2ndly, Elena, dau. of Sir William Massy, of Tatton, Knt., and by her, who m. 2ndly, Sir Gilbert Halsall, Knt., had a son,
2 CONT **	Thomas, in holy orders, rector of Brereton, 1433.
2 CONT *Sir William d. 4th HENRY VI., and was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT *'''   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Philippa, dau. of Sir Hugh, and sister of Thomas Hulse, and had issue,
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, m. Katherine, dau. of Sir John Byron, and d. s. p.
2 CONT **	II. ANDREW (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT **	III. John (Sir), m. 1st Katherine, dau. of Maurice Berkeley, of Beverston, and relict of John, Lord Stouron, and by her had a dau. and heiress, .... etc.
2 CONT **	Sir John m. 2ndly, Jane, dau. and heiress of Geoffrey Massy, of Tatton, and relict of Sir William Stanley, and by her had a son, .... etc.
2 CONT **	IV. Robert.
2 CONT **	V. Roger.
2 CONT **	VI. Henry.
2 CONT **	VII. Matthew.
2 CONT **	VIII. Hugh, of Wimbersley, m. Anne, dau. of Robert Done.
2 CONT **	I. Elizabeth, wife of John Radcliffe of Ordeshall.
2 CONT **	II. Jane, wie of Cotton, of Rudware.
2 CONT **	III. Eleanor, m. 1st, Thomas Bulkeley, of Eyton, and 2ndly to Hugh Cholmondeley.
2 CONT **	IV. Matilda, wife of Thomas Needham, of Shavington.
2 CONT *The eldest surviving son,
2 CONT *   SIR ANDREW BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. Agnes, dau. of Robert Legh, of Adlington, and had issue, .... etc. 
2 CONT ______________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 3 By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=yshsAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA454&lpg=PA454&dq=Robert+Legh+stanley&source=bl&ots=rdUuPvqvS0&sig=TTmd3ucv2Ompo9S-jzDWz0SDEEc&hl=en&ei=gVT9S-TrL4nONLOh0N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CB8Q6AEwBD
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=brereton&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.337
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BULKELEY, knt. of Eaton, chief justice of Chester in the reign of HENRY IV. who married Margaret, daughter of Sir Richard Molyneux, of Sephton, and grandaughter (maternally) of Thomas Earl of Derby, by whom he had 
2 CONC issue,
2 CONT **	I. THOMAS, of Eaton, who married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Geoffry Warburton, of Warburton. (See Vol. II. page 2,) and had three sons, and two daughters, namely,
2 CONT ***		1. THOMAS, m. Eleanor, daughter of '''Sir William Brereton''', and had a son, THOMAS, who d. s. p.
2 CONT ***		2. Robert, whose son .... etc. 
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 4 Pg.407
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=KikAAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA401&lpg=PA401&dq=Margaret+Radclyffe+1476&source=bl&ots=OUpvVzw1r0&sig=a4jI1o8sv5hn8ZjyoIg7pQ-eJ0M&hl=en&ei=bLkGTJOmKZTWNunSqcAJ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CDAQ6A
2 CONC EwCA#v=onepage&q=Brereton&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.401
2 CONT *   WILLIAM RADCLYFFE, esq. of Ordshall, who m. Jane, daughter of Sir Edmund Trafford, knt. of Trafford, and by her, who wedded secondly, James Byron of Clayton, and, thirdly,  Talbot, of Salesbury, had issue,
2 CONT **	I. JOHN, who m. Elizabeth, daughter of '''Sir William Brereton, knt. of Brereton, in Cheshire''', and dying, v. p. 12th April. 1497, left issue,
2 CONT ***		ALEXANDER (Sir), successor to his grandfather.
2 CONT ***		William.
2 CONT ***		Christian, m. to William Hulton, esq.
2 CONT ***		Margery, wife of Thurstan Parr.
2 CONT ***		---, m. to Sir Richard Aston, knt. of Middleton.
2 CONT **	I. Elizabeth, .... etc.
2 CONT *William Radclyffe, d. 15th May, 13 HENRY VII. and was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT *   SIR ALEXANDER RADCLYFFE, of Ordshall, knt. high sheriff of Lancashire in 1547, who m. Alice, daughter of Sir John Booth, knt. of Barton, in Lancashire, and had issue, .... etc. 
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT *Sybil MILBOURNE 
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1471, Burghill, Herefordshire, England 
2 CONT *Died: 26 Nov 1537 
2 CONT *Notes: some sources says that her husband was John Brereton, Esq., son of '''William Brereton and Phillippa Hulse'''.
2 CONT *Father: Simon MILBOURNE (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Jane BASKERVILLE
2 CONT *Married 1: Richard HACKLUYT
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **1. Thomas HACKLUYT (b. ABT 1485) (m.1 Margaret Augmondsham - m.2 Mary Lochard) 
2 CONT **2. Francis HACKLUYT (b. ABT 1486)
2 CONT *Married 2: John BREYNTON (d. 11 Apr 1527) (son of Thomas Breynton and Dau. Harper) ABT 1487
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **1. Elizabeth BREYNTON (b. ABT 1488) (m. Sir James Baskerville) 
2 CONT **2. Simon BREYNTON (b. ABT 1491) (m. Alice Bytton)
2 CONT **3. Isabel BREYNTON (b. ABT 1494) (m. John Lingen) 
2 CONT **4. John BREYNTON (b. ABT 1497) (m. Elizabeth Higgins)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/MILBOURNE.htm#Sybil MILBOURNE1 
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT William Brereton
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1176, Brereton, Cheshire, England Marriage: Unknown Died: After 1208, England
2 CONT    General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Ormerod's History of Chester, Vol. III, p.88, "Brereton and Holt of Brereton" Predigree, William is shown as the son of Wiiliam de Brerton, and the father of Sir Ralph de Brerton, Knight. 713
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Background Information. 696  About 1194, William de Brereton, son of Ralph II, received a deed at the time of his marriage to Margery, daughter of Randle de Torhaunt, eight witnesses signing the contract. this William was kingit
2 CONC hed by Henry III in 1208, the beginning of honors held in the Brereton family for over five hundred years.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Brereton, a Family History, pg. 9
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM12 BRERETON VIII, 10TH LORD OF BRERETON (William11, William10, William9, William8, William7, William6, Ralph5, William4, Ralph3, William2, William1), son of William and Alice (CORBET) BRERETON, was born between 1375 and 142
2 CONC 1, and died in 1485. He married (1st) (OO-2) MATILDA DUTTON, daughter of (OO-1) John DUTTON. He married (2nd) (VG-2) PHILLIPPA HULSE, daughter of (VG-1) Sir Hugh. [19, 13, 22]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of: William12 BRERETON VIII, 10th Lord of Brereton and Matilda DUTTON:
2 CONT
2 CONT 25	i.	WILLIAM13 BRERETON of Brereton, d. in 1507; m. KATHERINE BYRON of Horestan Castle, Derbyshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	26	ii.	ANDREW BRERETON, 11TH LORD OF BRERETON of Brereton, m. (APW-16) AGNES LEGH of Adlington, Cheshire, daughter of (APW-13) Robert and (AMA-25) Isabel (de STANLEY) LEGH.
2 CONT
2 CONT 27	iii.	ROBERT BRERETON of Brereton, b. about 1440.
2 CONT
2 CONT 28	iv.	ROGER BRERETON of Brereton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 29	v.	HENRY BRERETON of Brereton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 30	vi.	MATTHEW BRERETON of Brereton.
2 CONT
