2 CONT **	Leigh, of Boothes.
2 CONT *John Leigh 7 H. 6. mar. Maude da. to Sr William Boothe of Dunham, Knight.
2 CONT **	Sr John Leigh of Bouthes knight slayne at Blore heathe 2 R. 3. mar. Joane, da. & coe heire to Sr Tho. Ashton de Asheton knight in co. Lanc.
2 CONT **	ch of John Leigh & Joane Ashton
2 CONT ***		http://www.archive.org/stream/recordsociety58recouoft#page/152/mode/1up
2 CONT ***		1. John Leighe of Boothes 5 H. 7. mar. Eme da. & coe heire to Sr Robart Grosvenor of Holme, knight, 2ndly to Peter Shakerley. 2. Philip Leigh of the bouthis coossen & heire male 18 H. 8. mar. Elizabeth daughter of '''Sr Andre
2 CONC w Brereton'''. 3. Geffery Leighe.
2 CONT ***		ch of Philip Leigh & Elizabeth Brereton
2 CONT ****			1. Sr John Leigh of Bouthis knight ob. 5-6 P. & Ma., 13 Aug't [1558]. mar. Jane sister of William Snede knight, da. to Richard Snead of Bradwall. 2. Roger. 3. Edward. 4. William. 5. Ellin maried to Sr Ralf Lester of Tofte. 
2 CONC 6. Amy ob. s. p'le. 7. Jane maried to Richard Starky of Streeton & after to Stanly. _____________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 3 By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=yshsAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA454&lpg=PA454&dq=Robert+Legh+stanley&source=bl&ots=rdUuPvqvS0&sig=TTmd3ucv2Ompo9S-jzDWz0SDEEc&hl=en&ei=gVT9S-TrL4nONLOh0N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CB8Q6AEwBD
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=brereton&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.45
2 CONT *   WILLIAM MASSIE, esq. purchased, .... He wedded Alice, daughter and heiress of Adam Woton, of Edgerley and Chester, and by her, who m. secondly, Hugh Ball, of Coddington, had two sons, namely,
2 CONT **	I. MORGAN, of Eggerley, on whom his mother's lands were entailed. He m. Margery, daughter of John Davenport, esq. of Davenport, by Maud his wife, daughter of '''Sir Andrew Brereton, knt. of Brereton''', and had an only son and 
2 CONC heir,
2 CONT ***		ROBERT, ancestor of the MASSIES, of Eggerley, in whom that manor remained .... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.454
2 CONT *   ROBERT LEGH, esq. of Adlington, wedded, first, Isabella, daughter of John Savage, of Clifton, by whom he had no issue; and, secondly Isabella, daughter of Sir William Stanley, knt. of Hooton; by whom he had,
2 CONT **	I. ROBERT, his heir. .... etc.
2 CONT **'''	V. Agnes, m. to Sir Andrew Brereton, of Brereton. _________________________
2 CONT *'''A history and genealogy of the Davenport family, in England and America, from A. D. 1086 to 1850 .. (1851)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/historygenealogy51dave
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historygenealogy51dave#page/26/mode/1up
2 CONT *   John Davenport, of Davenport, Esq., son of John, held the office of sergeant on the death of his father in 1475. He married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir John Savage, of Clifton, knight. Died in 1482. 
2 CONT *   John Davenport, Esq., son of Ralph and grandson of John, was born 1480. Married 1st, Matilda, daughter of '''Sir Andrew Brereton, knight, of Brereton''' ; 2d wife, Jane, daughter of Ralph Arderne, Esq. ; and 3d, Blanch, daught
2 CONC er of Robert Latham, 
2 CONT * http://www.archive.org/stream/historygenealogy51dave#page/27/mode/1up
2 CONT *of Tabley, Esq. He died about 1553, aged 74 years. His children were, 1st, John ; 2d, William; 3d, Thomas; 4th, Roger; 5th, Ralph; 6th, Randle; 7th, Parnell ; 8th, Alice; 9th, Mary; 10th, Katharine ; 11th, Margaret ; 12th, Marger
2 CONC y ; 13th, Ellen*
2 CONT *John Davenport, of Davenport, Esq., son of the preceding John, was born in 1505. Married 1st, to Elleanor, daughter of Thurston Holland, Esq., of Denton County, Lane; 2d wife, Jane, daughter and coheiress of Richard Massey ; 3d w
2 CONC ife, Anne, daughter of Randle Mainwaring, of Carincham, Esq. __________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire (1978)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.74
2 CONT **	BRERETON--BARON BRERETON.
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, who m. Phillppa, dau. of Sir Hugh, and sister of Thomas Hulse, and had issue, 
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, m. Katherine, dau. of Sir John Byron, and d. s. p. 
2 CONT **'''	II. ANDREW (SIR), of whom presently. 
2 CONT **	III. John (Sir), m. 1st Katherine, dau. of Maurice Berkeley, of Reverston, and relict of John, Lord Stourton, and by her had a dau. and heiress, 
2 CONT ***		Werburga, m. 1st to Sir Francis Cheney; and 2ndly, to Sir William Compton. 
2 CONT **	Sir John m. 2ndly, Jane, dau. and heiress of Geoffrey Massy, of Tatton, and relict of Sir William Stanley, and by her had a son, 
2 CONT ***		Philip, who d. s. p. 
2 CONT **	IV. Robert
2 CONT **	V. Roger. 
2 CONT **	VI. Henry.
2 CONT **	VII. Matthew. 
2 CONT **	VIII. Hugh, of Wimbersley. m. Anne, dau. of Robert Done. 
2 CONT **	I. Elizabeth, wife of John Radcliffe, of Ordeshall. 
2 CONT **	II. Jane, wife of Cotton, of Rudware. 
2 CONT **	III. Eleanor, m. 1st. Thomas Bulkeley, of Eyton, and 2ndly, to Hugh Cholmondeley. 
2 CONT **	IV. Matilda, wife of Thomas Needham, of Shavington. 
2 CONT *The eldest surviving son. 
2 CONT *'''   SIR ANDREW BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, m. Agnes, dau. of Robert Legh, of Adlington, and had Issue, 
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM (SIR), his heir. 
2 CONT **	II. John, of Leek, co. Stafford. 
2 CONT **	III. Andrew.
2 CONT **	IV. Matthew. 
2 CONT **	I. Ellen, wife of John Fitton, of Gawsworth. 
2 CONT **	II. Alice, wife of William Moreton, of Little Moreton. 
2 CONT **	III. Elizabeth, m. 1st to Philip Legh, of Boothes; and 2ndly, to John Carington, of Carington. 
2 CONT **	IV. Catherine, m. to Thomas Smith, of Hagh. 
2 CONT **	V. Matilda, m. to John Davenport of Davenport 
2 CONT **	VI. Johanna, m. to Lawrence Dutton. of Marshe, brother and hdr of Sir Thomas Dutton, of Dutton. 
2 CONT *The eldest son and heir. 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt.; chief Justice and lord high marshal of Ireland, m. 1st Alice, dau. of Sir John Savage, Knt, of Clifton, and by her had a son, .... etc.
2 CONT *The chief justice m. 2ndly, Eleanor, dau. of Sir Ralph Brereton, of Ipstones, co. Stafford, and widow of -- Egerton, and by her had issue, .... etc. ______________________________
2 CONT *'''Nooks and corners of Lancashire and Cheshire: A wayfarer's notes in the ... By James Croston
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=KgsNAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA297&lpg=PA297&dq=Matilda+de+Arderne+Legh&source=bl&ots=pwMh6fdCn0&sig=pX7bZGFCtY563O3X2fzJ_DhuQrU&hl=en&ei=K1v9S5SkJ4qmM_C00N4H&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CCoQ6A
2 CONC EwCDhQ#v=onepage&q=Matilda%20de%20Arderne%20Legh&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.119
2 CONT *  Edward Fitton died 15 February, 1510-11, leaving, with other
2 CONT *Pg.120
2 CONT *issue, a son John, who succeeded as heir, and who, as appears by the inquisition taken after his father's death, was then 40 years of age. He had married, in 1498, Ellen, daughter of '''Sir Andrew Brereton''', the representative 
2 CONC of a family that had been seated at Brereton from the time of William Rufus. By her he had, with other issue, a son Edward, who succeeded at his death, which occurred on the Sunday after St. Valentine's Day, 1525. .... ___________
2 CONC _________
2 CONT *'''Remains, Historical and Literary, Connected with the Palatine ..., Volume 97
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=cfoMAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA126&lpg=PA126&dq=Robert+Legh++1486&source=bl&ots=HcoDqqXREX&sig=4DTWYCVWXxkRP1Pb39AdCEFCC9Q&hl=en&ei=g_T9S42fL5LONa_Q_NoN&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CC4Q6AEwBw#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Brereton&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.117
2 CONT **	Pedrigree of Legh of Adlington. Pg.115-121
2 CONT *Robert Legh of Adlington. Ob. 1410. = Maud, daughter of (Belgrave). Ob. 1478.; ch: (Pg.118 Robert (m. Isabel Savage & Isabel Stanley), Margery (m. Wm. Davenport), Maud (m. Jno. Mainwaring), '''Agnes (m. Sir Andrew Brereton)''', I
2 CONC sabel (m. Sir Lawrence Warren & Sir George Holford), A... (m. _ Pigot), Margaret (m. Tho. Mere), Elizabeth (m. Robert Duckenfield), Ellen (m. Roger Legh) Legh)
2 CONT **'''Agnes, married to Sir Andrew Brereton of Brereton, who succeeded his father 1482. ___________________
2 CONT *'''Brereton; a family history (1919)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/14/mode/1up
2 CONT *   In 1386, Sir William Brereton, son of the above, married Anylla, daughter of Sir William Venables, a descendant of Gilbert de Venables, first baron of Cheshire, and grantee of the first Brereton estate, three hundred years bef
2 CONC ore. By a second marriage, to Elena, daughter of Sir William Massey of Tatton Hall, in 1426, the Brereton holdings were among the great estates of England, including the manors of Malpas and Picton, with lands in Woodhull, Crouton
2 CONC , Charlton, and Norwich. 
2 CONT *   William de Brereton, son of the above, married Alice, sister and heiress of Sir Richard Corbett of Leighton ; this William died during the life of his father. About this time the "de" was dropped from English names, as it was 
2 CONC simply a descriptive 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/15/mode/1up
2 CONT *term and never a title, nor represented any special honor. 
2 CONT *   In 1409, a record says that King Henry removed the Mayor of Chester and placed Sir William Brereton in charge as military governor. 
2 CONT *   William Brereton, on the death of his grandfather, in 1435, was found heir to the vast estates of Brereton, and also the estates of his step-mother, in Tilston and Herthull, as recorded in 1438. He was knighted in 1485. His so
2 CONC n, William Brereton, died issueless, breaking the line of descent, the succession passing to his nephew, son of '''Sir Andrew Brereton''', in 1507. 
2 CONT *   On December 7, 1496, a deed was recorded to Ralph Brereton, brother of Sir Randle Brereton of Malpas. This Sir Randle was Chamberlain and Knight of the Bedchamber to Henry VII and Henry VIII. His son, John Brereton, about 1534
2 CONC , started the Norfolk branch of Breretons, from which many noted families have sprung. 
2 CONT *   In 1507, Sir William Brereton held vast 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonfamilyhi00brerrich#page/16/mode/1up
2 CONT *estates, and also had control of the appointment of clergymen to churches at Brereton, Malpas, Tilston, and St. John's. 
2 CONT *   As a side-light on court life of the period, there is a record of one Sir William Brereton of Malpas, whom Henry VIII suspected of being too familiar with the Queen, Anne Boleyn. He was confined in the tower of London, and lat
2 CONC er the King gave orders to "muzzle the bear," meaning to take his head off; so Sir William died May 17,1536, and two days later the Queen, mother of Queen Elizabeth, was beheaded. There is a legend that ever since that event the b
2 CONC ear on the Brereton arms has been muzzled, but in free America we have left the bear free also.  ______________________________
2 CONT *	'Brereton02'
2 CONT *Sir William Brereton of Brereton
2 CONT *  m. Philippa Hulse (dau of Sir Hugh Hulse)
2 CONT **	1. William Brereton of Brereton (dsp)
