1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Anthony Throckmorton==
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1542 - Of, Corse Court, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT * Parents:	Thomas Throckmorton, Margaret Whittington
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Much less is known about Anthony than about his older brother the MP, and he is easily confused with a cousin Anthony Throckmorton http://www.geni.com/people/Anthony-Throckmorton/6000000000426799915 who was the youngest son of Sir
2 CONC  George Throckmorton. (And, perhaps, vice versa.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/throckmorton-sir-thomas-15389-1607
2 CONT
2 CONT >"(Thomas) Throckmorton died on 31 Jan. 1607, ‘in happy and peaceable manner’, according to his tombstone. In his will, dated 17 Dec. 1600, he commended his soul to God, ‘beseeching Him that for His Son Christ Jesu’s sake, He will
2 CONC  have mercy on the same’. His body was not to be ‘opened or bowelled’, but buried ‘without pomp or unnecessary charges’. The bulk of his property he left to his surviving son, with small annuities to his daughter, and to his''' ‘r
2 CONC ight honest and loving brother’ Anthony Throckmorton''', who, with Sir Henry Poole, was named as overseer of the will. He was buried at Tortworth, his tomb bearing the inscription, ‘I have fought a good fight, I have finished my c
2 CONC ourse ... henceforth is laid up for me a crown of righteousness’.5
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT * 5. PCC 26 Windebanck; Bristol and Glos. Arch. Soc. Trans. xxx. 137-41.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=janeausten&id=I5290 Jane Austen Project]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/visitationofcoun00inchit#page/162/mode/2up The visitation of the county of Gloucester, taken in the year 1623] by Henry Chitty and John Phillipot as deputies to William Camden, Clarenceux king of arms
2 CONC , with pedrigrees from the herald's visitation of 1569 and 1582-3, and sundry miscellaneous pedigrees / edited by Sir John Maclean and W.C. Heane. Published 1885 in London . Written in English. Edition Notes Series	The publication
2 CONC s of the Harleian society -- v. 21
2 CONT #  http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/throckmortonb1642.htm
