1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Sir William Stanley
2 CONT *Born about 1380 in Wirral Forest, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Son of William Stanley and Margery de Hooton
2 CONT *Husband of Blanche de Arderne, of Alvanley  — married about 1402 
2 CONT * fought at Agincourt (1415)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disambiguation 
2 CONT
2 CONT note on William Stanleys of Hooton, following Richardson (father-to-son succession, 8 generations, earliest first)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Wm Stanley, of Storeton, m Alice Massey
2 CONT #Sir Wm Stanley-488 of Storeton, d 1427/8, m Margery de Hooton (heiress)
2 CONT #Sir Wm Stanley-50, of Hooton, dvp by 1424, m2 Blanche Arderne 
2 CONT #Wm Stanley-4027 Esq, b abt 1405, d aft 1456, m Mary Savage
2 CONT #Wm De_Stanley-3 Esq, b abt 1425, d 1465/6, m Alice Houghton
2 CONT #Sir Wm Stanley-417, b abt 1445, d 1512, m2 Agnes Grosvenor
2 CONT #Sir Wm Stanley-1404, b abt 1474-5, d aft 1528 m Anne Harrington
2 CONT #Sir Wm Stanley-1407..., younger brother Peter Stanley-1406 is father of Anne Stanley-3531 who marries Sutton
2 CONT
2 CONT ——————————
2 CONT
2 CONT Discussion here 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/XYcx7EMCYog
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Supporting data 
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham Published 2005
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA1099&lpg=PA1099&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&source=bl&ots=2Ewbuw0F3N&sig=amyJUT1pP9FfbnhwRw0p_-APrSM&hl=en&ei=AybKTe2VLYm6sAOVxpGMAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=resul
2 CONC t&resnum=2&ved=0CB4Q6AEwATg8#v=onepage&q=Stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 303
2 CONT *  10. MARY SAVAGE, married (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral) and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, Sheriff of Cheshire, son and heir of ''''''William Stanley, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral)
2 CONC  and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire by his 2nd wife, Blanche, daughter of John Arderne, Knt.'''''' He was born about 1405 (aged 23 in 1428). They had four sons, William, Esq., John, Richard, and Thomas. In 1424 his
2 CONC  widowed mother, Blanche, released her rights to the manor of Stanley, Staffordshire and lands in Chorlton and Le Moels (both in Wirral), Cheshire to him.  He was heir in 1428 to his grandfather, William Stanley, Knt. In 1432 he g
2 CONC ranted lands in Pulton Launcelyn, Bromburgh and le Spitall to Edward de Hoghton and others. In 1434 Richard Coly of Chester granted him lands in Pennesby and Thingwall. In 1437 king ordered the constable of Windsor Castle to take 
2 CONC William Stanley, his brother-in-law, John Savage, Knt., Randolph Brereton, and Urian Brereton into custody for an unspecified offence. In 1439 Richard Bolde was appointed the marriage of Richard Donne, the king's ward, by mainpris
2 CONC e of William Stanley, of Hooton, Cheshire, Esq., and another. He was granted a pardon by the king in 1446. 
2 CONT *Pg. 304
2 CONT **  11. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral), and Storeton, Cheshire, Stanley, Staffordshire, etc., son and heir, born say 1425. He married ALICE HOGHTON (or HOUGHTON), daughter of Richard Hoghton, Knt., of Hoghton (in Ley
2 CONC land), Lancashire, by his wife, Margaret. They had one son William, Knt., and one daughter Isabel (wife of John Marchumley). In 1450 he fought for the king against the traitor, Jack Cade, of Kent. In 1454 John Hertcombe granted au
2 CONC thority to John Savage the younger, William Stanley esquires, and Thomas Kendale to cause a deed to be made in his name regarding the castle, lordship and manor of Mold, Flintshire. In 1460 he was pardoned L166 in arrears as late 
2 CONC receiver of Richard, Duke of York, of the lordship of Denbigh in Wales. In 1462 he and others were appointed to take muster of Roland Fitz Eustace, Knt., and 300 archers at some convenient place near Chester. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq.
2 CONC , died 17 FEb 1466. His wife, Alice, was living 11 March 1465/6.
2 CONT ***  12. WILLIAM STANLEY, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral), Roveacre, and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, son and heir, born about 1445. He married (1st) MARGARET BROMLEY, daughter and co-heiress of John Bromley, Knt., 
2 CONC of Badington (in Acton), Cheshire, by Joan, daughter and co-heiress of William Hexstall, Knt. They had one daughter, Margery. His wife, Margaret, died in 1469. He married (2nd) in 1470 AGNES GROSVENOR, daughter and co-heiress of R
2 CONC obert Grosvenor, Esq., of Holme, Cheshire, by Joan, daughter of Lawrence Fitton, Knt. They had a son, William, Knt. William was knighted about 1484. He was an executor c.1492 of the will of Mr. Henry Medwall, master of St. Giles. 
2 CONC SIR WILLIAM STANLEY died in 1512. His widow, Agnes, died in 1520-1.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham Published 2004
