2 CONT *11. MARY SAVAGE, married (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton, and Storeton, Cheshire, and Hooton, and Stanley, Staffordshire, Sheriff of Cheshire, ''''''son and heir of William Stanley, Knt., of Hooton and Storeton
2 CONC , Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire by Blanche, daughter of John Arderne, Knt.'''''' He was born about 1405 (aged 23 in 1428). They had four sons, William Esq., John, Richard, and Thomas. ''''''In 1424 his widowed mother, Blanc
2 CONC he, released her rights to the manor of Stanley, Staffordshire and lands in Chorlton and Le Moels (both in Wirral), Cheshire to him''''''.
2 CONT *Pg. 291
2 CONT *He was heir in 1428 to his grandfather, William Stanley, Knt. He married (2nd) ALICE DE HOGHTON, daughter of Richard de Hoghton, Knt. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., died 17 Feb. 1466.
