2 CONT ==Parents 
2 CONT
2 CONT “there also seems confusion regarding the Margery or Blanche who married William Stanley of Hooton. We hope to investigate these matters further in due course.”  Detached as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Peter-Ardern
2 CONC e-Kt/6000000008295956753?through=6000000007605562174 & https://www.geni.com/people/Cecily-de-Bredbury/6000000004351853008?through=6000000007605562174, 30 March 2024.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Blanche Arderne''', also seen as Margaret or Margery, married Sir William Stanley, son of Sir William Stanley and Margery de Hooton, in 1402. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche Arderne was born at “of” Elford or Alvanley, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: Sir William Stanley of Hooton  d. 1417
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT *Isabella Stanley+.  Married Robert Legh, Esq., son of Robert Legh and Matilda.  
2 CONT *Maud Stanley+ b. c 1400.  Married Sir John Launcelyn, son of William Lancelyn (Launcelyn).
2 CONT *William Stanley, Esq., Sheriff of Cheshire+2 b. c 1405, d. a 6 Feb 1456.  Married Mary Savage, daughter of Sir John Savage.
2 CONT *Katherine de Stanley+ b. c 1408.  Married Ralph Arderne, son of Henry de Arderne and Ellen Whetenhall,
2 CONT *Margery Stanley+ b. c 1415.  Married Thomas Venables, son of William Venables and Blanche.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed origins 
2 CONT ''Last updated 30 March 2024''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Seen as daughter of John de Arderne and Margaret Pilkington 
2 CONT *Seen as Margery or Blanche, daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Peter-Arderne-Kt/6000000008295956753?through=6000000007605562174 and https://www.geni.com/people/Cecily-de-Bredbury/6000000004351853008.
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Arderne-1 Has her “uncertainly” as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Arderne/6000000016699689615, son of Peter & Cecily. (In other words, a generation later.)
2 CONT *Seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Arderne-Kt/6000000000232615633 and https://www.geni.com/people/Ellen-Arderne/6000000003827876256 (In other words, a generation earlier.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche Arderne1,2 
2 CONT *F, #19344
2 CONT *Father     Sir John de Arderne2 d. 1349
2 CONT *Mother     Elena de Wasteneys2 d. bt 13 Jul 1349 - 23 Dec 1349
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://cybergata.com/roots/8442.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanch married Sir William de Stanley Knight, son of Sir William de Stanley Knight and Margaret de Houghton 713,310.,866 (Sir William de Stanley Knight was born in 1386 in Stanley, Staffordshire, England 721 and died in 1427-1428 
2 CONC in England 721.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Boyer's Medieval English Ancestors of Robert Abell, p. 229, she was a widow in 7 Henry VI (1428-1429) 721
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Archaeologia Cambrensis, Vol XIV, 4th Series, 1883, p. 70, In an article titled "Sir William Stnanley" refers to Blanche as either Margaret or Blanche Ardern, daughter of Sir John Arderne of Hawarden or Harden. 864
2 CONT
2 CONT This is how I figured out just how Blanche Arderne fit into the Arderne family:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580, 527 p. 18, shows (2)Sir John Arderne, father of (3) Blanche who married William Stanley, to be of Hawarden. He is shown as the son of another (1)Sir John Ardern of Harwarden, and brothe
2 CONC r and heir to his elder brothers, (2)Walter and (2)Thomas, who both died without issue. Besides having a daughter, (3)Blanche who married William Stanley, (1) Sir John is shown with a son named (3)Hugh Arderne, who has a son (4)Ra
2 CONC lph Arderne, married to ______Stanely of Hooton. (4)Ralph Arderne sons shown are (5)Thomas of whom the Arderne of Leicestershire desended, and (5)John married to a daughter of Thomas Davenport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comparing this to the pedigree chart given by Ormerod for the Ardernes in History of Cheshire, Vol. II,, 713 pp. 85-86, I find that rather than being named John, there is a (2)Peter, son of (1)John Arderne & Alice Venable daughter
2 CONC  of Hugh Venables (his first wife, his third wife, being Ellen Wastney). Peter's half-brothers are (2)Sir Thomas & (2)Walkelyn (Walter) and his other brother is named (2)John, all who died without issue. (2)Peter is married to Cec
2 CONC ily, daughter and heiress of Adam de Bredbury (marriage settlement on 5 Edward III). Their son, (3) Hugh de Arderne of Harden whose son, (4) Ralph is married to Katherine, daughter of Sir William Stanely of Hooton, and their sons 
2 CONC are, (5) Thomas (Arderne's of Leicestershire) and (5) John who has a son, (6) Ralph who is married to Margaret, daughter of Thomas Davenport.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT See this discussion from < [https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/XYcx7EMCYog soc.gen.medieval] > about the parentage of Blanche Arderne
2 CONT
2 CONT > ….If William Stanley was b. c. 1400, then his mother Blanche Arderne could easily be born c. 1370, which would fit the identification of Blanche as daughter Peter de Arderne and Cicely de Bredbury ( see Earwaker, "History of Eas
2 CONC t Cheshire," p. 474).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/aa/arderne1.php
2 CONT
2 CONT * (i)	Sir John de Arderne of Alford, Alderley and Alvanley (d c1349) 	m. Alice de Venables (dau of Hugh de Venables of Kinerton by Agatha Vernon)
2 CONT **	(b)	Peter de Arderne of Harden and Alvanley (b 1327, d 1378-9)	m. Cicely de Bredbury (dau of Adam de Bredbury of Harden Hall)
2 CONT *** 	((1))	Charles de Arderne of Timperley 	The following comes from Visitation (Cheshire, 1580, Ardern of Timperley). 	m. Elizabeth Radcliffe (dau of Richard Radclffe of Timpley, "younger brother of the Tower")
2 CONT ***  	((2))	Hugh de Arderne of Harden Hall (b 1350, d c1420) 	m1. Agnes de Hulme 	m2. Cecily de Hyde (dau of Ralph de Hyde)
2 CONT ***  	((3))	John de Arderne [@@ We are concerned about possible confusion between the following Charles of Timplerley and the Charles shown above (who m. Elizabeth Radclyffe). Some web sites show the husband of Cicely de Bredbury 
2 CONC as John rather than Peter, shown as father of the above Charles of Timplerley, whilst there also seems confusion regarding the Margery or Blanche who married William Stanley of Hooton. We hope to investigate these matters further 
2 CONC in due course.]
2 CONT ***  	((4))	Matilda de Arderne
2 CONT *** 	((5))	Blanche de Arderne	m. William Stanley of Hooton probable duplication - see note @@ just above
