1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173426903969 Stanley 1 (May 10, 2024; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Magna Carta ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham  Published 2005
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wHZcIRMhSEMC&pg=PA1099&lpg=PA1099&dq=Magna+Carta+ancestry:+a+study+in+colonial&source=bl&ots=2Ewbuw0F3N&sig=amyJUT1pP9FfbnhwRw0p_-APrSM&hl=en&ei=AybKTe2VLYm6sAOVxpGMAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=resul
2 CONC t&resnum=2&ved=0CB4Q6AEwATg8#v=onepage&q=Stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 303
2 CONT *''''''  10. MARY SAVAGE, married (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral) and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, Sheriff of Cheshire, son and heir of William Stanley, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral)
2 CONC  and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire by his 2nd wife, Blanche, daughter of John Arderne, Knt. He was born about 1405 (aged 23 in 1428). They had four sons, William, Esq., John, Richard, and Thomas. In 1424 his widow
2 CONC ed mother, Blanche, released her rights to the manor of Stanley, Staffordshire and lands in Chorlton and Le Moels (both in Wirral), Cheshire to him.  He was heir in 1428 to his grandfather, William Stanley, Knt. In 1432 he granted
2 CONC  lands in Pulton Launcelyn, Bromburgh and le Spitall to Edward de Hoghton and others. In 1434 Richard Coly of Chester granted him lands in Pennesby and Thingwall. In 1437 king ordered the constable of Windsor Castle to take Willia
2 CONC m Stanley, his brother-in-law, John Savage, Knt., Randolph Brereton, and Urian Brereton into custody for an unspecified offence. In 1439 Richard Bolde was appointed the marriage of Richard Donne, the king's ward, by mainprise of W
2 CONC illiam Stanley, of Hooton, Cheshire, Esq., and another. He was granted a pardon by the king in 1446. 
2 CONT **Pg. 304
2 CONT **  11. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton (in Wirral), and Storeton, Cheshire, Stanley, Staffordshire, etc., son and heir, born say 1425. He married ALICE HOGHTON (or HOUGHTON), daughter of Richard Hoghton, Knt., of Hoghton (in Ley
2 CONC land), Lancashire, by his wife, Margaret. They had one son William, Knt., and one daughter Isabel (wife of John Marchumley). In 1450 he fought for the king against the traitor, Jack Cade, of Kent. In 1454 John Hertcombe granted au
2 CONC thority to John Savage the younger, William Stanley esquires, and Thomas Kendale to cause a deed to be made in his name regarding the castle, lordship and manor of Mold, Flintshire. In 1460 he was pardoned L166 in arrears as late 
2 CONC receiver of Richard, Duke of York, of the lordship of Denbigh in Wales. In 1462 he and others were appointed to take muster of Roland Fitz Eustace, Knt., and 300 archers at some convenient place near Chester. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq.
2 CONC , died 17 FEb 1466. His wife, Alice, was living 11 March 1465/6.
2 CONT ***  12. WILLIAM STANLEY, Knt., of Hooton (in Wirral), Roveacre, and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, son and heir, born about 1445. He married (1st) MARGARET BROMLEY, daughter and co-heiress of John Bromley, Knt., 
2 CONC of Badington (in Acton), Cheshire, by Joan, daughter and co-heiress of William Hexstall, Knt. They had one daughter, Margery. His wife, Margaret, died in 1469. He married (2nd) in 1470 AGNES GROSVENOR, daughter and co-heiress of R
2 CONC obert Grosvenor, Esq., of Holme, Cheshire, by Joan, daughter of Lawrence Fitton, Knt. They had a son, William, Knt. William was knighted about 1484. He was an executor c.1492 of the will of Mr. Henry Medwall, master of St. Giles. 
2 CONC SIR WILLIAM STANLEY died in 1512. His widow, Agnes, died in 1520-1.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *''''''Plantagenet ancestry: a study in colonial and medieval families By Douglas Richardson, Kimball G. Everingham  Published 2005
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=p_yzpuWi4sgC&pg=PP1&lpg=PP1&dq=Plantagenet+ancestry&source=bl&ots=RRsM2STbba&sig=n4fyHWGDQZODK9D1BzNoVJisVpE&hl=en&ei=KRvKTeTDBISisAOaj9SeAw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CCQQ6AEwAjg
2 CONC K#v=onepage&q=Stanley&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 290
2 CONT *''''''11. MARY SAVAGE, married (as his 1st wife) WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., of Hooton, and Storeton, Cheshire, and Hooton, and Stanley, Staffordshire, Sheriff of Cheshire, son and heir of William Stanley, Knt., of Hooton and Storeton
2 CONC , Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire by Blanche, daughter of John Arderne, Knt. He was born about 1405 (aged 23 in 1428). They had four sons, William Esq., John, Richard, and Thomas. In 1424 his widowed mother, Blanche, released
2 CONC  her rights to the manor of Stanley, Staffordshire and lands in Chorlton and Le Moels (both in Wirral), Cheshire to him.
2 CONT *Pg. 291
2 CONT *''''''He was heir in 1428 to his grandfather, William Stanley, Knt.'''''' He married (2nd) ALICE DE HOGHTON, daughter of Richard de Hoghton, Knt. WILLIAM STANLEY, Esq., died 17 Feb. 1466.
2 CONT **12. WILLIAM STANLEY, Knt., of Hooton and Storeton, Cheshire, and Stanley, Staffordshire, son and heir, born about 1439. He married (1st) say 1460 MARGARET BROMLEY, daughter and co-heiress of John Bromley, Knt., of Badington (in 
2 CONC Acton), Cheshire, by Joan, daughter and co-heiress of William Hexstall, Knt. They had one daughter, Margery. His wife, Margaret, died in 1469. He married (2nc) in 1470 AGNES GROSVENOR, daughter and co-heiress of Robert Grosvenor, 
2 CONC Esq., of Holme, Cheshire, by Joan, daughter of Lawrence Fitton, Knt. They had a son, William, Knt. He was knighted about 1484. He was an executor c.1492 of the will of Mr. Henry Medwall, master of St. Giles. SIR WILLIAM STANLEY di
2 CONC ed in 1512. His widow, Agnes, died in 1520-1.
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *''''''William Stanley, Esq., Sheriff of Cheshire1,2
2 CONT *''''''M, b. circa 1405, d. after 6 February 1456
2 CONT *Father Sir William Stanley2 d. 2 Feb 1428 
2 CONT *Mother Blanche Arderne2 
2 CONT *''''''     William Stanley, Esq., Sheriff of Cheshire was born circa 1405 at of Hooton & Stanley, Staffordshire, England; Age 23 in 1428.2 He married Mary Savage, daughter of Sir John Savage and Maud Swynnerton, circa 1424; They 
2 CONC had 4 sons (William, John, Richard, & Thomas).2 William Stanley, Esq., Sheriff of Cheshire died after 6 February 1456.2
2 CONT *''''''Family Mary Savage b. c 1400 
2 CONT *Children 
