1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT "Robert Leigh, of Adlington, who left, at his decease, (Inq. p. 111., 3 IlsNnv V.,) by Matilda, his wife, (remarried to William de Honford,) four sons and one dau., viz., RoBERT; James, Rector of Rostherne, in 1456; William; Peter
2 CONC ; and Ellen, the wife of Roger Legh, of Ridge."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----  
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 4th May, 1431, Robert Legh made proof of age, when his mother's second husband, William Honford, “aged 60 and upwards," was one of the witnesses, and testified “that the said Robert was born at Adlynton, and baptized in the
2 CONC  church at Prestbury, the Tuesday on the feast of the Annunciation of the Blessed Virgin Mary (March 25, 1410), and was aged 21 on the feast of the Invention of the Holy Cross (May 3) then last past ; and that he, William, was pre
2 CONC sent at Prestbury the day when Robert Hyde, his godfather, came to the church at Prestbury with the said Robert.” (Earwaker.) ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ....  In 1478 his mother, Matilda, who had survived her first husband sixty-three years, and had also outlived her second husband, William de Honford, died. She must have been very old, for in the inquisition taken after her death
2 CONC  her son Robert was said to be sixty-eight years of age. He had livery of the lands held by her in dower, but did not long enjoy possession of them, for his death occurred on the 21st January following. ...  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----  https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/G52Y-RCZ/matilda-maud-norley-1390-1478
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
