2 CONT ◾6. Sir Laurence Warren, knight, known to be living in 1459 but died before his father (1474). ◾+ Isabel daughter of Sir Robert Legh of Adlington, knight, married before 1459. She later married Sir George Holford of Holford, knigh
2 CONC t, in 1475. This couple had two sons, John and William. Source: East Cheshire Past and Present by J.P. Earwaker, London, 1877 (CRO, Knutsford). This is widely regarded as the best work on East Cheshire of the 19th century. It is u
2 CONC seful for family trees of landed families.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Laurence de Warren, Knight married Isabel, daughter of Robert Leigh of Adlington, Cheshire before 1458.  He was knighted soon after the accession of Edward IV.  He was the Lord of the Manors of Stockport, Poynton, Wode Plumpto
2 CONC n, Fornely, Rotteley, Boton, and Skegeton.  He died in the lifetime of his father, and his widow married Sir George Holford in 1475.  This Sir Laurence had Sir John, and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> The Genealogy of the Warren Family of Poynton Chesire: http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT He was "bailli of Cotentin and bailli of Coutances" in the occupation of northern France.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT was one of 30 spearsmen summoned
2 CONT
2 CONT for the defense of the kingdom, out of the county of Chester, 7th of Henry V (1420)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Warren married Isabel Stanley (1408-1431) who was daughter of Isabel de Lathom and John de Stanley
2 CONT
2 CONT their son Sir Lawrence Warren (1433-1474) married Isabel Legh in 1440
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT born in Poynton, Cheshire
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT D: Bef. 1474 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1458 in England to Isabel Leigh   
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Children John & William
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From Janice Carol Dehod (age 51, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada): Notes on Warren family of Poynton & Stockport taken from Earwaker's East Cheshire. Family 1st acquired manors of Poynton & Stockport when Sir Edward de Warren, knight, 
2 CONC illegitimate son of last Earl of Warren & Surrey m Cicely dtr & finally heiress of Sir Nicholas de Eton of Poynton & Stockport. Sir Edward de Warren d bef 1369. Simplified version of family tree, concentrating on heirs: •1. Sir Ed
2 CONC ward de Warren, knight, illegitimate son of last Earl of Warren & Surrey by Maud de Nerford, d bef 1369. •+Cicely, dtr & finally heiress of Sir Nicholas de Eton of Poynton & Stockport. ◦2. Sir John de Warren of Poynton & Stockport
2 CONC , knight, b c1343, d 1387 & buried at Boton in Norfolk. Inquisition post mortem in 1392. ◦+Margaret, dtr & heiress of Sir John de Stafford of Wickham, Norfolk, knight. Marriage settlement dated 1371. (She m2 John Mainwaring of Ove
2 CONC r Peover c1387 & d 1418. Monument to her at Over Peover.) Sir John de Warren had son Nicholas & dtr, Margaret. ■3. Nicholas de Warren of Poynton & Stockport, b c1378 d 1413. ■+Agnes dtr of Sir Richard de Wynnington, Cheshire who s
2 CONC urvived her husband. In addition to son Laurence they had dtr Emma who m Hugh Venables of Golborne c1410, & 2nd dtr, Elizabeth mentioned in docs of 1417 & 1422. ■4. Sir Laurence Warren, knight, of Poynton & Stockport, b c1394, d 1
2 CONC 444. ■+Margaret, dtr of Richard Bulkeley by Margery Venables his wife. This couple had 3 sons, John, Randle & Edward but little is known of latter 2. There were 6 dtrs, Margery, Joan, Cicely, Margaret & Elizabeth & one who is know
2 CONC n only for marrying Thurstan de Holland but whose Christian name is unrecorded. ■5. John Warren of Poynton & Stockport, d 1474.■+Isabel dtr of Sir John Stanley of Lathom, marriage article dated Mar 1422. This couple had in additio
2 CONC n to heir Laurence, John Warren, Richard & Henry, who became Rector of Stockport (1473-1492). There were 4 dtrs, Elizabeth, m Robert Rhockley of Rockley in Yorkshire, Joan prob m Sir John Mainwaring of Over Peover (doubted by Earw
2 CONC aker), Margaret m John Hawarden of Arderne & Jane, m John Atherton of Atherton in Lancashire. ■6. Sir Laurence Warren, knight, known to be living in 1459 but d bef his father (1474). ■+Isabel dtr of Sir Robert Legh of Adlington, k
2 CONC night, m bef 1459. She m2 Sir George Holford of Holford, knight, in 1475. This couple had 2 sons, John & William. ■7. Sir John Warren, knight of Poynton & Stockport, succeeded his grdfather, b c1461, knighted at Ripon in 1487 & d 
2 CONC 9 Jan 1518. ■+1st wife, Eleanor, dtr of Sir Thomas Gerard of Bryn, Lancashire. All children are from this wife. There were 6 sons, Laurence, Richard, Nicholas, Jerome, Ralph & George. There was dtr Cicely & possibly 1 whose Christ
2 CONC ian name is unk who m Legh of Lyme. ■+2nd wife, Jane dtr of Ralph Arderne of Harden, Esq, widow of Thurstan Holland of Denton, Lancashire & who m2 John Davenport of Davenport. ■8. Laurence Warren of Poynton & Stockport, d 18 Sep 1
2 CONC 530. http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Genealogy of the Warren Family of Poynton Chesire: http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ◾6. Sir Laurence Warren, knight, known to be living in 1459 but died before his father (1474). ◾+ Isabel daughter of Sir Robert Legh of Adlington, knight, married before 1459. She later married Sir George Holford of Holford, knigh
2 CONC t, in 1475. This couple had two sons, John and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thevalleyfamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I17558562178&tree=fitzvalley
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Laurence De Warren, Knight was born c. 1438 in Poynton, Cheshire, England.  Sir Laurence married (1.) Isabel Leigh on 1458 in Cheshire, England and had 2 children:  Sir John Warren, Knight and William Warren.  He passed away o
2 CONC n 1474.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  SOURCE: Jane MacDaniels Genealogy;
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of the Manors of Stockport, Poynton, Wode Plumpton formely Rotteley, Boton and Skegeton. Laurence was knighted by King Edward 1V before 1458 they had 2 children John & William, marriage contract shows 36Hen6=1458
2 CONT
2 CONT This couple had 2 sons - John and William
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: SOURCE:  http://www.warrenfamilyhistory.com/Docs/Our%20Warrens%20in%20England.htm
