2 CONT * (X) Herbert IV, Count of Vermandois and Valois, died 1080, leaving a daughter
2 CONT * (XI) Adela de Vermandois, married Hugh the Great, son of Henry I, of France, and Count of Vermandois and Valois. They had a daughter
2 CONT * (XII) Elizabeth (Isabel), married William de Warren, second Earl of Surry, and Warrenne and Mortimer in Normandy. He was born about 1040 and died 1130. They had a son
2 CONT * (XIII) Reganal de Warrenne, married Adela, daughter of Roger de Mowbray. They had a son
2 CONT * (XIV) William de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir William de Hayden, and had a son
2 CONT * (XV) Sir John de Warren, who married Alice, daughter of Roger de Townshend, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVI) John de Warrenne, married Joan, daughter of Sir Hugh de Post, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVII) Sir Edward de Warrenne, married Maud, daughter of Richard de Skeyton, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVIII) Sir Edward de Warren, married Cicely, daughter of Sir Nicholas de Eaton, and had a son
2 CONT * (XIX) Sir John de Warren, married Agnes, daughter of Sir Richard Wynnington, and had a son
2 CONT * (XX) Sir Laurence de Warren, married Margery, daughter of Hugh Bulkley Esquire, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXI) John de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir John Stanley, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXII) Sir '''Lawrence de Warren''', married Isabel, daughter of Sir Robert Leigh, in 1458, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXIII) William de Warren, by wife Anne had a son
2 CONT * (XXIV) John de Warren, by wife Elizabeth had a son
2 CONT * (XXV) John Warren of Headbury, Devonshire, England, who had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVI) Christopher Warren, who had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVII) William Warren, married Anne Mable, and had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVIII) Christopher Warren, married Alice Webb, and had 
2 CONT * (XXIX) John Warren, married in England. Margaret, and came to New England in 1630, in the same fleet with Sir Richard Saltonstall. and settled at Watertown, Massachusetts.  
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of John Warren and Isabel Dalton  Husband of Isabel Holford / Warren  Father of William Warren, of Ripple Court; John de Warren, Baron of Stopfords; Isabella Warren; Richard Warren (alias Waller), of Bassingbourne and Agnes Ve
2 CONC sey  Brother of Jane de Warren; Elizabeth de Warren; Joan Mainwaring; Margaret Hawarden; John de Warren; Henry de Warren, Rector of Stockport; Richard de Warren and William Warren 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Laurence de Warren, Knight married Isabel, daughter of Robert Leigh of Adlington, Cheshire before 1458.  He was knighted soon after the accession of Edward IV.  He was the Lord of the Manors of Stockport, Poynton, Wode Plumpto
2 CONC n, Fornely, Rotteley, Boton, and Skegeton.  He died in the lifetime of his father, and his widow married Sir George Holford in 1475.  This Sir Laurence had Sir John, and William.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> The Genealogy of the Warren Family of Poynton Chesire: http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________________________________
2 CONT !Laurence de Warren, Esq., son of Sir John, sold in 1523 the lordships of Boton and Skeleton, also the lordship of Rotley in Warwickshire. He was m. first to Margaret, daughter of Sir Piers or Perkin Leigh of Lyme, Cheshire, Knigh
2 CONC t. The marriage settlement, dated July 1494, Laurence being then eighteen years of age, provides, that if he died before consummation, another son was to marry her. By her he had fourteen children—1st, Cecily, m. to ______ Coleshu
2 CONC ll; 2nd, Mabel, m. to Roger Beke, Sergeant-at-arms; 3rd, Sir Edward, who continued the descent; 4th, Helen, who, according to Vincent's Cheshire, m. Roger Downes of Shrigley, or Worth, Cheshire, Esq.; 5th, Margaret, m. to Robert H
2 CONC yde of Norbury; 6th, Dorothy, m. first to _____ Newton, and secondly to Hugh Davenport, deputy steward of Macclesfield; 7th, Randolph, m. Elizabeth, daughter of Henry Catherall, Esq. He had another wife, whose name is not given. H
2 CONC is children were Laurence, Edward, both married, and George. He was buried at Prestbury, 11th August 1562. 8th, Ann, m. to George Highly of Highly, Yorks, Esq., whose grand-daughter Ann, was m. to William Lord Cavendish, the first
2 CONC  Earl of Devonshire; 9th, Catharine, m. to Nicolas Bradbury of Olierset, Derbyshire; 10th, Jane, m. to George Chatterton; 11th Isabel; 12th, Laurence; 13th, George; 14th, another Edward. Laurence de Warren, Esq., had a second wife
2 CONC , Sibil, who was the widow of William Honford, Esq., and survived her husband. Laurence, but had no issue by him. Thomas Warren, A History and Genealogy of the Warren Family in Normandy, Great Britain and Ireland, France, Holland,
2 CONC  Tuscany, United States of America, Etc. (A.D. 912-1902, with Numerous Pedigrees. Private printing, 1902, p. 38-39. Private printing, 1902, Google Books, online.
2 CONT * https://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
