2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Warren, Knight was born on 1461 in Poynton, Cheshire, England to Sir Laurence De Warren, Knight and Isabel Leigh De Warren.  Sir John married (1.) Eleanor Gerrard on 1480 in Poynton, Cheshire, England and had 7 children: 
2 CONC  Laurence De Warren, Richard De Warren, Nicholas De Warren, Jerome De Warren, Ralph De Warren, Daughter 1 De Warren, and Daughter 2 De Warren.  Sir John married (2.) Jane Arderne of Harden AFTER 1480 in England and had a child:  G
2 CONC eorge Warren.  He passed away on January 11, 1517/18 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: SOURCE: Jane MacDaniels Genealogy:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Warryne, knight Lord of Poynton born 1461 = Baron of Stockport of Stropforde 1489, Master of Lichfield Guild 1489 died January 11, 1517/18 9Hen8
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Eleanor Gerrard 1480, daughter of Sir Thomas Gerrard of Bryn Com, Lancashire. He captured Bodiam Castle for King Richard 111. He was knighted by Henry V11 on St. Bartholomews Day in Rippon, Yorkshire
2 CONT
2 CONT All children from Eleanor: six sons: Laurence, Richard, Nicholas, Jerome, Ralph and George.... There was one daughter, Cicely and possibly one whose Christian name is unknown who married a Legh of Lyme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other Source
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Knighted at Ripon in Yorks by King Henry V11, 1487
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Warryne, Kt. also was married to Joan or Jane Arderne and had 1 Child George Warren b 1516
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Gerrard born 1462 of Bryn, Com, Salop, England 5 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Other source: 1st wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JANE ARDERNE OF HARDEN: Daughter of Ralph Arderne of Harden, Esq, widow of Thurston Holland of Denton, Lancashire and who later married John Davenport
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ELEANOR GERARD: Daughter of Sir Thomas Gerard of Bryn, Lancashire.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About SIR WARREYNN and ELEANOR GERARD: Marriage: 1480
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: SOURCE:  [http://www.warrenfamilyhistory.com/Docs/Our%20Warrens%20in%20England.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Warren, Knight was born about 1461 and was knighted at Ripon in York, by King Henry VII, on Bartholomew's Day 1487. He married about 1480, Eleanor, daughter of Sir Thomas Gerrard of Bryn Com, Lancashire, Knight and die
2 CONC d January 11, 1517. John and Eleanor’s children according to Harleison MS. 1074, Laurence, Thomas and Robert; but the Poynton pedigree lists Laurence; Richard, living in 1529, who married Catherine, daughter of John Moore, of Bank
2 CONC  House, Lancashire; Nicholas, who married Catharine Mainwaring; Jerome; Ralph; and two daughters who died without issue.  Sir John married secondly Joan or Jane daughter of Ralph Arderne of Harden.  By her he had George Warren who
2 CONC  lived at Poynton.  The estate passed to Laurence.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ◾7. Sir John Warren, knight of Poynton and Stockport, succeeded his grandfather, born about 1461, knighed at Ripon in 1487 and died 9 January 1518.
2 CONT
2 CONT ◾+ 1 st wife, Eleanor, daughter of Sir Thomas Gerard of Bryn, Lancashire. All the children are from this wife. There were six sons, Laurence, Richard, Nicholas, Jerome, Ralph and George. There was a daughter Cicely and possibly on
2 CONC e whose Christian name is unknown who married a Legh of Lyme.
2 CONT
2 CONT ◾+ 2 nd wife, Jane daughter of Ralph Arderne of Harden, Esq, widow of Thurstan Holland of Denton, Lancashire and who later married John Davenport of Davenport
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/warren.html
2 CONT
2 CONT East Cheshire Past and Present by J.P. Earwaker, London, 1877 (CRO, Knutsford). This is widely regarded as the best work on East Cheshire of the 19th century. It is useful for family trees of landed families. 
2 CONT
