1 NAME William Warren, of Coverton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1460
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stockport
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 MAY 1496
2 ADDR
3 CITY Caunton
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Warren-of-Ripple-Court/6000000003274524179
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd son  of Sir Lawrence Warren (1433-1474) and Isabel Legh, daughter of Isabel de Stanley Legh (1413-1452) and Sir Robert Legh (c1410-1479).
2 CONT
2 CONT his brothers were Richard and Sir John.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT C. H. B. “Warren of Virginia and Maryland.” The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography 6, no. 2 (1898): 200–203. http://www.jstor.org/stable/4242143.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 200 VIRGINIA HISTORICAL MAGAZINE.
2 CONT WARREN OF VIRGINIA AND MARYLAND.
2 CONT
2 CONT The alleged descent of Richard Warren, the Puiritan, of " Mayflower" fame, from John Warren, died 1525, son and heir of William, of Coverton, Nottinghamshire, second son of Sir Lawrence Warren, of Poynton, Cheshire, and ante I475,
2 CONC  has been many times refuted by genealogists
2 CONT and repudiated by descendants of the " Puritan Father," in spite of Dr. Warren's handsome book on the subject, therefore the connection of the Puritan with the ancient Earls of Warren and Surrey has not been established, as no oth
2 CONC er descent has been substituted for the above.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT *'''William Warren1
2 CONT *'''M, #32976, b. circa 1460, d. 1 May 1496
2 CONT *Father       Sir Laurens Warren b. c 1415, d. b 1475
2 CONT *Mother     Isabel Leigh b. 1440
2 CONT *'''     William Warren married Anne. William Warren was born circa 1460. He died on 1 May 1496 at Caunton, Nottinghamshire, England.
2 CONT *'''Family      Anne b. c 1462, d. 1496
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **John Warren+ b. c 1480, d. 1525
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S74] Brent Ruesch's Research Notes.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1098.htm#i32976
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *'''Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the ..., Volume 4 By William Richard Cutter, William Frederick Adams
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=FM8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA2165&lpg=PA2165&dq=Nicholas+de+Warren&source=bl&ots=P_Uj4objMP&sig=NLxzY64uaohmXJFfilt4XkroDiM&hl=en&ei=RwnES7WPIciDnQfu3NytDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CA4Q6AE
2 CONC wBDgU#v=onepage&q=Nicholas%20de%20Warren&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 2165
2 CONT *(XVIII) Sir Edward de Warren, married Cicely, daughter of Sir Nicholas de Eaton, and had a son
2 CONT *(XIX) Sir John de Warren, married Agnes, daughter of Sir Richard Wynnington, and had a son
2 CONT *(XX) Sir Laurence de Warren, married Margery, daughter of Hugh Bulkley Esquire, and had a son
2 CONT *(XXI) Sir John de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir John Stanley, and had a son
2 CONT *(XXII) Sir Lawrence de Warren, married Isabel daughter of Sir Robert Leigh, in 1458, and had a son
2 CONT *'''(XXIII) William de Warren, by wife Anne had a son
2 CONT *(XXIV) John de Warren, by wife Elizabeth had a son _____________
2 CONT *'''Class memoir of George Washington Warren: with English and American ancestry By Thomas Coffin Amory
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=VTMBAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA27&lpg=PA27&dq=Isabel+LEGH+warren&source=bl&ots=6Kormwveb7&sig=xibvPoDVZbzpcdkyFbuduEJxqlM&hl=en&ei=sYL-S_r4GIG6NsuBhTw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CCUQ6AEwBjgU#v
2 CONC =onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.27
2 CONT * .... The line continued on through Nicholas, whose wife was Agnes de Winnington; Sir Lawrence, who, about 1394, married Margaret Bulkeley; John, born 1414, whose wife was Isabel, daughter of Sir John Stanley of Latham, Knight of
2 CONC  the Garter, to Sir Lawrence, who, by Isabel Leigh of Adlington, had '''William, ancestor of Sir John Borlase Warren, of recent naval celebrity, and to Sir John, who, about 1480, marrying Eleanor Girard, had five sons. ....
2 CONT *Pg.28
2 CONT *   Among the ancestor of this Sir George was Sir Lawrence, who, in 1458, married Isabel, daughter of Robert Leigh, of Adlington, in Cheshire. '''William, his second son, settled in Caunton, Nottinghamshire, and from his descended
2 CONC  Sir John Borlase Warren,  ....
2 CONT *   John, the eldest son of Sir Lawrence, died in 1525, and his younger son, George, removed to Headboro, in Devon. He had Christopher, .... __________________________
2 CONT *'''Representative men and old families of southeastern Massachusetts ..., Volume 3
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=GHIWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1676&lpg=PA1676&dq=Nicholas+Of+Headboro+Warren&source=bl&ots=1n-xacuIYk&sig=_B0O2VBN7ABYc4XsyhR-9dktf1I&hl=en&ei=MvHBS8DONojlnQesnbG6Cg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved
2 CONC =0CBYQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.1676
2 CONT *   Nicholas, son of Sir John and Margaret, daughter of Sir John Stafford.
2 CONT *   Sir Laurence, son of Nicholas and Agnes, daughter of Sir Richard Wymington.
2 CONT *   John, born 1414, son of Sir Lawrence and Margery, daughter of Hugh Birlkley.
2 CONT *   Sir Laurence, son of John and Isabel, daughter of John Stanley of Lotham.
2 CONT *'''   William, son of Sir Laurence and  and Isabel, daughter of Robert Legh of Ablington, in Cheshire (married about 1458).
2 CONT *   John, Sr., son of '''William, who settled in Camton, and wife Ann'''. ___________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT 	6. Sir Laurence Warren, knight, known to be living in 1459 but died before his father (1474). 	+ Isabel daughter of Sir Robert Legh of Adlington, knight, married before 1459. She later married Sir George Holford of Holford, kni
2 CONC ght, in 1475. This couple had two sons, John and '''William.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT East Cheshire Past and Present by J.P. Earwaker, London, 1877 (CRO, Knutsford). This is widely regarded as the best work on East Cheshire of the 19th century. It is useful for family trees of landed families. Now available from th
2 CONC e Family History Society of Cheshire on CD ROM
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT see also Find A Grave Memorial # 88184741
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William Warren was born AFTER 1461 to Sir Laurence De Warren, Knight and Isabel Leigh De Warren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * 1.  Jane MacDaniels Genealogy
2 CONT * 2.  [http://www.warrenfamilyhistory.com/Docs/Our%20Warrens%20in%20England.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=FM8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA2165&lpg=PA2165&dq=Nicholas+de+Warren&source=bl&ots=P_Uj4objMP&sig=NLxzY64uaohmXJFfilt4XkroDiM&hl=en&ei=RwnES7WPIciDnQfu3NytDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CA
2 CONC 4Q6AEwBDgU#v=onepage&q=Nicholas%20de%20Warren&f=false Genealogical and Personal Memoirs] Relating to the Families of the State of Massachusetts, Volume 4 (Google eBook) William Richard Cutter, William Frederick Adams.  Page 2165:
2 CONT
2 CONT * (X) Herbert IV, Count of Vermandois and Valois, died 1080, leaving a daughter
2 CONT * (XI) Adela de Vermandois, married Hugh the Great, son of Henry I, of France, and Count of Vermandois and Valois. They had a daughter
2 CONT * (XII) Elizabeth (Isabel), married William de Warren, second Earl of Surry, and Warrenne and Mortimer in Normandy. He was born about 1040 and died 1130. They had a son
2 CONT * (XIII) Reganal de Warrenne, married Adela, daughter of Roger de Mowbray. They had a son
2 CONT * (XIV) William de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir William de Hayden, and had a son
2 CONT * (XV) Sir John de Warren, who married Alice, daughter of Roger de Townshend, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVI) John de Warrenne, married Joan, daughter of Sir Hugh de Post, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVII) Sir Edward de Warrenne, married Maud, daughter of Richard de Skeyton, and had a son
2 CONT * (XVIII) Sir Edward de Warren, married Cicely, daughter of Sir Nicholas de Eaton, and had a son
2 CONT * (XIX) Sir John de Warren, married Agnes, daughter of Sir Richard Wynnington, and had a son
2 CONT * (XX) Sir Laurence de Warren, married Margery, daughter of Hugh Bulkley Esquire, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXI) John de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir John Stanley, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXII) Sir Lawrence de Warren, married Isabel, daughter of Sir Robert Leigh, in 1458, and had a son
2 CONT * (XXIII) '''William de Warren''', by wife Anne had a son
2 CONT * (XXIV) John de Warren, by wife Elizabeth had a son
2 CONT * (XXV) John Warren of Headbury, Devonshire, England, who had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVI) Christopher Warren, who had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVII) William Warren, married Anne Mable, and had a son 
2 CONT * (XXVIII) Christopher Warren, married Alice Webb, and had 
2 CONT * (XXIX) John Warren, married in England. Margaret, and came to New England in 1630, in the same fleet with Sir Richard Saltonstall. and settled at Watertown, Massachusetts.  
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT “he was married to Joane, and their children were William, John, and John de Warren”
2 CONT
