1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/holford.html
2 CONT
2 CONT . Sir George Holford of Holford, knight, son and heir of Thomas, married Isabel, widow to Lawrence Warren of Pointon in Cheshire, and daughter of Robert Legh of Adlington, Esq. 1475, and had issue John Holford, son and heir; Georg
2 CONC e Holford, another son, 22 Henry VII; Constance who married William son of Edward Bradshaw, 1511. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George had four bastard sons - Thomas, Arthur, from whom the Holfords of Davenham; Raufe, and Robert, also Ellen a base daughter, all living 22 Hen VII. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George was sheriff of Cheshire, 1524. He bore Lostock's coat in his seal, to wit, A Greyhound, over which, corner-ways, on the dexter angle of the escutcheon, on a helmet, wreath and mantle, a Greyhound's head couped, written 
2 CONC above the seal - S. George Holford, militis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ourfamilyhistories.org/getperson.php?personID=I26417&tree=00
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gwgbowen.com/index.php/George_Holford_%28b_1456%29
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir George Holford was born.  Sir George married Isabel Leigh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * 1.  Jane MacDaniels Genealogy
2 CONT * 2.  [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gonefishin&id=I097067]
