1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brereton-8
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Brereton was born around 1468. [Elizabeth had a son William who was 14 in 1527 (18 Henry VIII) therefore born in 1513, if she was 45 (est max age to give birth) when she had him she was born in 1468].
2 CONT Elizabeth was the daughter of Sir Andrew Brereton of Brereton and Agnes DeLeigh, daughter of Robert Ligh of Adlington.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Philip Legh of Bothes, esq, after 14 August, 1506.   Phillip Leigh, who was heir to his nephew, died 2 December, 18 Henry 8 and an Inquisition post mortem was held in 18 Henry VIII.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT 18 Henry Vlll -  -21 April 1526	- 21 April 1527 
2 CONT http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/cal/reg20.htm
2 CONT https://aulis.org/Calendar/Regnal_Years.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth then married John Carrington.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth and Phillip had seven children:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir John Leigh of Bouthes, was 14 in 18 Henry VIII, married Jane, sister of Sir William Snead, and died 1558;[7]
2 CONT # Jane married to (1) Richard Starky of Stretton and (2) Stanley of Bickerstaff;
2 CONT # Ellin married to Sir Rafe Lecester;
2 CONT # Anne (or Amy) who died without children;
2 CONT # William
2 CONT # Edward
2 CONT # Roger
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Supporting data 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth Brereton 
2 CONT *'''F, #44555, b. circa 1470
2 CONT *Father      Sir Andrew Brereton b. c 1440
2 CONT *Mother     Agnes Legh b. c 1445
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Brereton married Philip Legh, son of Sir John Legh. Elizabeth Brereton was born circa 1470 at of Brereton, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT *'''Family      Philip Legh d. 1512
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Anne Legh+1 b. c 1472
2 CONT **Ellen Legh+ b. c 1480
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S10297] Unknown author, History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Omerod, 1819., p. 383.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1483.htm#i44555 ______________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great ..., Volume 2 By John Burke
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/agenealogicalan00austgoog
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalan00austgoog#page/n77/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 45
2 CONT *   JOHN LEGH, of Booths, father of
2 CONT *   SIR JOHN LEGH, of Booths, a staunch Lancastrian, who fell fighting under the Red Rose at Blore Heath, in the 38th of Henry VI. He left two sons,
2 CONT **	I. JOHN, his successor.
2 CONT **'''	II. PHILIP, heir to his nephew.
2 CONT *The elder son,
2 CONT *   JOHN LEGH, of Booths, espoused Emma, daughter and co-heiress of Robert Grosvenor, of Hulme, with whom he acquired the demesne lands of Allostock. He died in 1470, and was s. by his only son,
2 CONT *   JOHN LEGH, esq. of Booths. This gentleman m. Anne, daughter of Sir William Booth, of Dunham Massey, by whom (who m. secondly, Geoffrey Shakerley, esq. of Shakerley) he had an only daughter,
2 CONT **	ELIZABETH LEGH, who was sole heiress to her grandmother's estate at Hulme. She m. Peter Shakerley, esq. of Shakerley. (See vol. i. p. 9)
2 CONT *John Legh dying without male issue, was s. by his uncle,
2 CONT *'''      PHILIP LEGH, esq. who was returned to the estate of Booths by inquisition in the 2nd RICHARD III. He wedded Elizabeth, daughter of Andrew Brereton, of Brereton, by whom (who wedded, secondly, John Carrington, of Carringt
2 CONC on) he left issue,
2 CONT **	JOHN (Sir), his Heir.
2 CONT **	Joan, m. first to Richard Starkey, esq. of Stretton, and secondly to _ Stanley.
2 CONT **	Ellen, m. to Sir Ralph Leycester, of Toft. (See vol. i. p. 74)
2 CONT *'''He died in the 18th of HENRY VIII. and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *   SIR JOHN LEGH, of Booths, who received the honor of knighthood at Leith, 11th May, 1544, at which time the Earl of Hertford, being then general, knighted several Cheshire gentlemen. He espoused Jane, sister of William Sneyd, e
2 CONC sq. of Bradwell, and was s. at his decease by his eldest son, ... ___________________
2 CONT *'''The visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580 (1882)
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/visitationchesh00fellgoog
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/visitationchesh00fellgoog#page/n57/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.41
2 CONT **	Brereton of Brereton Pg. 41-42
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Wm Brereton obijt vivo patre. = Alice d. to Jno Corbet of Leighton sister and heire to Richard.; ch: Sr Wm (m. Phillippa Halse) Brereton.
2 CONT **Sr Wm Brereton of Brereton. = Phillippa d. to Sr Hugh Halse.; ch: Wm, Sr Andrew (m. Agnes Ligh & Anne Done) Brereton (Pg.42 Sr John (m. Katherine Barkley & Jane Massy), Hugh (m. Anne Donn) Brereton)
2 CONT ***Sr Andrew Brereton of Brereton. ch: Katherine (m. Wm Bowyer), Elizabeth (m. John Smith); = 1. Agnes d. to Rob't Ligh of Adlington.; ch: (Pg.42 Sir Wm (m. Alice Savage & Elenor Brereton), Katherine (m. Sr Thomas Smith), '''Eliza
2 CONC beth (m. Phillip Ligh & John Carrington)''', Alice (m. Wm Morton), Maud (m. John Damport) Brereton).; = 2. Anne Done.
2 CONT ****Katherine uxr Wm Bowyer of Knipsley.
2 CONT ****Elizabeth vxr John Smith of Oldlaugh. [Oldhaugh. Harl. 1505.]
2 CONT ****http://archive.org/stream/visitationchesh00fellgoog#page/n58/mode/1up
2 CONT ****Pg.42
2 CONT ****Sir Wm Brereton L. Cheife Justice of Ireland. = 1. Alice d. to Sr John Savage.; ch: Will'm (m. Anne Boothe) Brereton; = 2. Elenor d. to Sr Randoll Brereton of Ipstones.; ch: Richard (m. Thomasine Ashley), Mary (m. Sr . . . .  
2 CONC Warburton) Brereton.
2 CONT ****Katherine vxor Sr Thomas Smith of Hough.
2 CONT ****'''Elizabeth uxor Phillip Ligh of Boothes & after to John Carrington.
2 CONT ****Alice uxr Wm Morton of Morton.
2 CONT ****Maud vxr John Damport of Damport. __________
