1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sir William Brereton1,2 
2 CONT *'''M, #44399, b. 1473
2 CONT *Father      Sir Andrew Brereton b. c 1440
2 CONT *Mother     Agnes Legh b. c 1445
2 CONT *'''     Sir William Brereton was born in 1473 at of Brereton, Cheshire, England. He married Alice Savage, daughter of Sir John Savage and Dorothy Vernon, circa 1498 at of Clifton, Cheshire, England.1 Sir William Brereton married 
2 CONC Eleanor Brereton, daughter of Sir Randle Brereton, Chamberlain of Chester and Eleanor Dutton, circa 1519.3
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Alice Savage b. c 1472
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir William Brereton b. c 1506
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Eleanor Brereton b. c 1498
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Mary Brereton+4,2 b. c 1520
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 559.
2 CONT * 2.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 438.
2 CONT * 3.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 260.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1477.htm#i44399 ________________
2 CONT *'''Rt. Hon. Sir William Brereton
2 CONT *'''M, #354139, b. circa 1483, d. circa February 1541
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Apr 2009 
2 CONT *'''     Rt. Hon. Sir William Brereton was born circa 1483.1 He was the son of unknown Brereton. He married, firstly, Alice Savage, daughter of Sir John Savage.1 He married, secondly, Eleanor Brereton, daughter of Sir Randle Brere
2 CONC ton.1 He died circa February 1541.1 He was buried on 4 February 1541 at Kilkenny, County Kilkenny, Ireland.1
2 CONT *'''     He lived at Brereton, Cheshire, England.1 He was he accompanied Lord Depute Sir William Skeffington to Ireland, to subdue the revolt of 10th Earl of Kildare who he beseiged in Maynooth Castle in 1534.1 In 1538 he returned
2 CONC  to England, but went back to Ireland the following year.1 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Ireland].1 He held the office of Lord Marshal of Ireland in 1540.1 He held the office of a Lord Justice [Ireland].1
2 CONT *'''Children of Rt. Hon. Sir William Brereton
2 CONT ** 1.Margaret Brereton2
2 CONT ** 2.Katherine Brereton2 d. 1559
2 CONT ** 3.Ellen Brereton2
2 CONT ** 4.Anne Brereton2
2 CONT ** 5.Mary Brereton+2
2 CONT *'''Children of Rt. Hon. Sir William Brereton and Eleanor Brereton
2 CONT ** 1.Randle Brereton2
2 CONT ** 2.Richard Brereton+2 d. 20 Aug 1558
2 CONT ** 3.Henry Brereton+2
2 CONT *'''Children of Rt. Hon. Sir William Brereton and Alice Savage
2 CONT ** 1.Sir John Brereton2 d. 1549
2 CONT ** 2.Sir William Brereton+2 b. c 1500, d. 1534
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, editor, Burke's Irish Family Records (London, U.K.: Burkes Peerage Ltd, 1976), page 166. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Irish Family Records.
2 CONT * 2.[S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, Burke's Irish Family Records.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p35414.htm#i354139 _____________________
2 CONT *'''Alice SAVAGE
2 CONT *Father: John SAVAGE (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Dorothy VERNON
2 CONT *'''Married: William BRERETON (son of Andrew Brereton and Agnes Leigh) ABT 1488, Clifton, Cheshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. William BRERETON (b. 1506) (m. Anne Booth)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SAVAGE.htm#Alice SAVAGE5 ____________________
2 CONT *'''Breretons of Cheshire, 1100 to 1904 A. D (1904)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/breretonsofchesh00brer
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/45/mode/1up
2 CONT **THE HALTON BRANCH OF THE MALPAS FAMILY, 
2 CONT *   There is very little recorded of this branch of the family. The Herald's Visitation Record of 1663-4 gives the pedigree commencing with Sir Roger Brereton, of Halton, the founder of the family, about 1540, and shows four gener
2 CONC ations of descent. I think this Sir Roger was the sixth son of Sir Randle Brereton IV., of Malpas, and the younger brother of John Brereton, the founder of the Norfolk branch. His mother was Eleanor, daughter of Sir Piers Dutton, 
2 CONC the Lord of Halton and Dutton, in 1500. Sir Piers was descended from Odard, one of the companions in arms of the Conqueror. He (Odard) assumed the name of Dutton upon receiving a grant of that town from Hugh Lupus, first Earl Roya
2 CONC l of Chester, the ancestor of Lady Ada's mother. Sir Piers was the great grandson of Sir Thomas Dutton, of Dutton, who was the Governor and Receiver of the Castle of Halton in 1330. Sir Piers was the son of Sir Lawrence Dutton, wh
2 CONC o married Johanna, daughter of Sir Andrew Brereton, of Brereton, and from whom are descended the present family of Baron Sherbourne, of Sherbourne, Gloucestershire. The Warburton family, of Arley, were also descended from the same
2 CONC  Odard. Sir Roger Brereton married Katherine, widow of Edward Fulleshurst and daughter of '''Sir William Brereton IX., of Brereton, by his second wife, Eleanor, daughter of Sir Randle Brereton III., of Ipstone and Malpas, and the 
2 CONC widow of Philip Egerton, of Egerton.''' 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/98/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Sir Randle de Brereton II., of Ipstone and Malpas, married Joanna, daughter of William Holford. By her he had two sons : 1, Randle Brereton, founder of the Eccleston and Wettenhall branch : 2, Owen Brereton, of Bar Hill, the a
2 CONC ncestor of Brereton of Coddington. His second wife was Katherine, daughter of William Butheley, of Eaton, Cheshire. By her he had three sons: 1, Randle, his heir, of Ipstone and Malpas; 2, Ralph Brereton, of Iscoyd Castle, Shropsh
2 CONC ire, who had one daughter, wife of John Holford ; 3, Bartholomew Brereton, of Grafton, who had three sons : a, Bartholomew ; b, John ; c, Humphrey, of Malpas, the historian of the War of the Roses. 
2 CONT *   Randle Brereton III., of Ipstone, died in Burgundy, France. His wife was Emma, daughter and heiress of John Carington, of Carington. By her he had two sons and two daughters : 1, Randle, his heir; 2, Humphrey, of Malpas; 3, El
2 CONC len, wife of Nicholas Bruyn, of Tarwin, Cheshire ;'''4, Eleanor, wife of Philip de Egerton, afterwards wife of Sir William de Brerton IX., of Brereton.'''  _____________________
2 CONT *'''The history of the county palatine and city of Chester: .... Vol. III.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyp03orme
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyp03orme#page/51/mode/1up
2 CONT **	BRERETON AND HOLT OF BRERETON. 		Pg.51-52
2 CONT *SIR ANDREW BRERETON, of Brereton, kt. = AGNES, dau. of Robert Legh, of Adlington., ch: '''SIR WILLIAM (m. ALICE Savage & ELENOR Brereton)''', ELLEN (m. John Fitton), ALICE (m. William Moreton), ELIZABETH (m. Philip Legh & John Ca
2 CONC rington), CATHERINE (m. Thomas Smith), MATILDA (m. John Davenport), JOHN, ANDREW, MATTHEW, JOHANNA (m. Laurence Dutton) BRERETON
2 CONT *'''SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, kt. chief justice and lord high marshal of Ireland, bur. Feb. 4, 1541, at Kilkenny in Ireland = 1. ALICE, daughter of sir John Savage., ch:''' WILLIAM (m. Anne Bouth) BRERETON.;''' = ELENOR, 
2 CONC dau. of sir Ralph Brereton of Ipstones, widow of . . . .  Egerton., ch:''' MARGARET (m. William Goodman), HENRY, KATHERINE (m. Edward Fulleshurst), ELEN (m. Robert Dokenfeld), ANNE (m. David Kynaston), JOHN, RALPH (m. Thomasine As
2 CONC hley), MARY (m. sir John Warburton) BRERETON. ___________________________
2 CONT *'''The visitation of Cheshire in the year 1580 (1882)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/visitationchesh00fellgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/visitationchesh00fellgoog#page/n59/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.43
2 CONT **	Brereton of Malpas.		Chart Pg.43-44
2 CONT *Randoll Brereton second sonne to Sr Wm Brereton of Brereton = . . . . d. to . . . . Ipstons of Ipstons in Comitatu Staff.; ch: William (m. _ Wyld), Sr Randoll of Ipstones and Mallpas. Brereton.
2 CONT *Sr Randoll Brereton of Ipstones and Mallpas. = ; ch: Randoll (m. Emma Carington) Brereton
2 CONT *Randoll Brereton. = Emma Heiress to John Carington of Carington.; ch: Sr Randoll (m. Elenor Dutton) Brereton.
2 CONT *Sr Randoll Brereton of Mallpas was made Knight Banerett at the Siege of Tirwin and Tourney and was after Chamberlaine of Chester. = Elenor d. to Piers Dutton of Dutton [In a later hand.]; ch: Sr Randoll (m. Elenor Egerton & Isabe
2 CONC ll Butler, Sr Ric., John, Tho. (a Preist), Peter (a Preist), (Pg.44 Sr Roger (m. Katherine Brereton), Wm. (m. Elizabeth Somerset), Rob't, Sr Urian, '''Elenor (m. Sr William Brereton)''', Jane (m. Sr Jn0 Hanmer), Anne (m. Jn0 Harco
2 CONC urt & Jn0 Persall), Elizabeth (m. Rich. Cholmeley) Brereton.
2 CONT *Sr Randoll Brereton of Mallpas. = 1. Elenor d. to Phill. Egerton of Olton.; ch: Anne.; = 2. Isabell d. to Sr . . . .  Butler of Beausy.; ch: Sr Randoll (m. Mary Griffeth) Brereton. __________________________
2 CONT *Roger Brereton was a Welsh politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1604 to 1611
2 CONT *Brereton the third son of Owen Brereton of Borras near Gresford, Denbighshire.
2 CONT *He sat on the bench as Justice of the Peace for Flintshire from 1582 to 1617 and for Shropshire from 1598 to at least 1604. He was appointed High Sheriff of Flintshire for 1591-92.
2 CONT *In 1604, he was elected Member of Parliament for Flint.[1]
2 CONT *Brereton possibly married Katherine Fulleshurst, widow of Edward Fulleshurst and daughter of '''Sir William. Brereton of Brereton, Lord Chief Justice of Ireland by his second wife.[1]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Brereton ______________________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire (1978)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n94/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.74
2 CONT **	BRERETON--BARON BRERETON.
2 CONT *   RALPH DE BRERETON (son of William de Brereton, and grandson of William de Brereton,) was father (besides a 2nd son, Gilbert, and a dau., Isolda, wife of Gilbert de Stoke,) of an elder son and heir. 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, living temp. JOHN and HENRY III., who m. Margery, dau. of Randle de Thornton, and had a son, RALPH, and a dau., wife of Thurstan de Smethwick. The former 
2 CONT *   SIR RALPH BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt, had two sons, WILLIAM (SIR), and Gilbert, father of Henry and Sibella, wife of William de Bouths. The elder son, 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. the dau. of his guardian. Sir Richard de Sandbach, Knt., and was father of 
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Roesia, dau. of Ralph de Vernon, and had issue, 
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, m. Margery, dau. of Richard de Bosley, and d. in his father's lifetime, leaving issue,
2 CONT ***		1 WILLIAM (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT ***		2. etc.
2 CONT **	II. John. .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir William was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, living 49th EDWARD III., who m. 1st Ellen, dau. of Philip, and sister and finally heiress of David Egerton, of Egerton, and by her had a son and successor,
2 CONT **	WILLIAM.
2 CONT *He m. 2ndly, Margaret, dau. of -- Done, of Utkinton, and widow of John Davenport, and by her had a son and two dau., ..... etc.
2 CONT *The eldest son,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, m. 1st, in 1386, Angella, dau. of Hugh Venables, and by her had issue,
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, d. before his father, having m. Alice, sister and heiress of Richard Corbett, of Leighton, and by her (who m. 2ndly, John Stretley, Esq.,) had issue,
2 CONT ***		1 WILLIAM (SIR), successor to his grandfather.
2 CONT ***		2 ... etc.
2 CONT **	II. .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir William m. 2ndly, Elena, dau. of Sir William Massy, of Tatton, Knt., and by her, who m. 2ndly, Sir Gilbert Halsall, Knt., had a son,
2 CONT **	Thomas, in holy orders, rector of Brereton, 1433.
2 CONT *Sir William d. 4th HENRY VI., and was s. by his grandson,
2 CONT *   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., who m. Philippa, dau. of Sir Hugh, and sister of Thomas Hulse, and had issue,
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, m. Katherine, dau. of Sir John Byron, and d. s. p.
2 CONT **	II. ANDREW (SIR), of whom presently.
2 CONT **	III. .... etc.
2 CONT *The eldest surviving son,
2 CONT *   SIR ANDREW BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt., m. Agnes, dau. of Robert Legh, of Adlington, and had issue, 
2 CONT **'''	I. WILLIAM (SIR), his heir.
2 CONT **	II. John, of Leek, co. Stafford.
2 CONT **	III. Andrew.
2 CONT **	IV. Matthew.
2 CONT **	I. Ellen, wife of John Fitton, of Gawsworth.
2 CONT **	II. Alice, wife of William Moreton, of Little Moreton.
2 CONT **	III. Elizabeth, m. 1st to Philip Legh, of Boothes; and 2ndly, to John Carington, of Carington.
2 CONT **	IV. Catherine, m. to Thomas Smith, of Hagh.
2 CONT **	V. Mathilda, m. to John Davenport, of Davenport.
2 CONT **	VI. Johanna, m. to Lawrence Dutton, of Marshe, brother and heir of Sir Thomas Dutton, of Dutton.
2 CONT *The eldest son and heir,
2 CONT *'''   SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, of Brereton, Knt.; chief justice and lord high marshal of Ireland, m. 1st, Alice, dau. of Sir John Savage, Knt., of Clifton, and by her had a son,
2 CONT **	I. WILLIAM, who m. Anne, dau. of Sir William Booth, of Dunham, and predeceasing his father, left issue,
2 CONT ***		1 WILLIAM (SIR), successor to his grandfather.
2 CONT ***		2 Andrew. m. Catherine, dau. of Sir Andrew FitzSimon, of Dublin, Knt., and had issue.
2 CONT ***		3 Robert.
2 CONT ***		4 Arthur.
2 CONT ***		5 John.
2 CONT ***		6. EDWARD, m. Edith, dau. of William Birche, of Birche, co. Lancaster, and had issue,
2 CONT ****			HENRY BRERETON, ancestor it is believed, of the BRERETONS OF QUEEN'S Co. (see LANDED GENTRY).
2 CONT ***		1 Ellen. m. 1st, to John Carenton; and 2ndly, to Lawrence Winington, of Hermitage.
2 CONT ***		2 Jane, wife of Richard Clyve, Esq., of Huxley.
2 CONT ***		3 Margaret.
2 CONT *'''The chief justice m. 2ndly, Eleanor, dau. of Sir Ralph Brereton, of Ipstones, co Stafford, and widow of --- Egerton, and by her had issue,
2 CONT **	I. John, a captain in Ireland.
2 CONT **	II. Ralph, m. Thomasine, dau. and heiress of George Ashley, of Ashley, and had issue.
2 CONT **	III. Henry.
2 CONT **	I. Margaret. m. 1st, to William Goodman, and 2ndly, to William Mostyn.
2 CONT **	II. Katherine, m. 1st, to Edward Fulleshurst, and 2ndly, to Roger Brereton.
2 CONT **	III. Elen, wife of Robert Dokenfeld, of Dokenfeld.
2 CONT **	IV. Anne, wife of David Kynaston, of Hanney.
2 CONT **	V. Mary, wife of Sir John Warburton, of Arley.
2 CONT *'''Sir William, who was buried at Kilkenny, in Ireland, 4 February, 1541, was s. by his grandson, .... etc. ______________________________
