1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pigot-20
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pigot of Chetwynd (b. 1434; living 1459),[1] was arrested in 1457/8 for threatening his aunt Joan, widow of John Pigot.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Ellen, dau. of Robert de Legh of Adlington, Cheshire and Mabel, dau. of Sir William de Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Issue:
2 CONT # Robert of Chetwynd, sheriff of Shropshire in 1517.[3] m. Margaret, dau. of Sir John Blount (Blunt)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pigott'''
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000194421253831&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Fletcher, W.G.D. (1906). The sequestration papers of Thomas Pigott of Chetwynd. Transactions of the Shropshire Archaeological and Natural History, 29, pp. 71. Google Books.
2 CONT Renaud, F. (1867). Contributions Towards a History of the Ancient Parish of Prestbury inn Cheshire, 97, pp. 69. Google Books. (see pedigree of Pigot of Butley, Chetwynd, and Bonishall, p. 70).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT # ↑ ATL D. 13 Jan 1512.[citation needed]
2 CONT # ↑ Accrding to Renaud (1867), John (dvp), so his son Robert succeeded Richard (d. c. 1440, 19 Hen VI).[1] But Fletcher (1906), says he was still alive in 1459, (p. 71).[2]
2 CONT # ↑ see also Rootsweb: "Robert PIGOTT, of Chetwynd (son & heir of John PIGOTT of Chetwynd, by Ellen de LEGH); granted Fiat for appointment of Escheators, Co Salop, Nov 1513; High Sheriff of Co Salop, 1517; marr Mary or Margaret BL
2 CONC OUNT; issue: 1. Thomas PIGOTT, of Chetwynd. See [A] below. 2. John PIGOTT; b ca 1500 or thereabouts; marr Isabella MALPAS, of Cheshire; issue - a son Robert PIGOTT of Bently (some pedigrees record this son instead as Thomas); & a 
2 CONC 2nd or younger son John PIGOTT (see [D] below)."
