1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pigott-166
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert is the son of:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pigot (b. c. 1434); and Elen, daughter of Robert de Legh of Adlington, Cheshire and Mabel / Isabel, daughter of Sir William Stanley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Renaud (1867), he succeeded his grandfather, Robert of Butley (of Chetwynd after marriage), who died in 1440.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Margaret, daughter of Sir John Blount (Blunt) of Kinlet. They are the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas m. Agnes, dau. of Richard Croft; m. Elizabeth Onley
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation
2 CONT
2 CONT 1517: High Sheriff of Shropshire
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pigott'''
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000194421253831&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fletcher, W.G.D. (1906). The sequestration papers of Thomas Pigott of Chetwynd. Transactions of the Shropshire Archaeological and Natural History, 29, pp. 71. Google Books.
2 CONT # Renaud, F. (1867). Contributions Towards a History of the Ancient Parish of Prestbury inn Cheshire, 97, pp. 69. Google Books.[1]
2 CONT # Tresswell, R. & Vincent, A. (1889). "Pigott of Chetwyn," in Visitation of Shropshire 1623, II, pp. 401. George Grazebrook & John Paul Rylands, Ed. Publications of the Harleian Society. Archive.org.[2]
2 CONT # Wikipedia: High Sheriff of Shropshire#16th century
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT # see also: pedigree of Pigot of Butley, Chetwynd, and Bonishall, p. 70).[1]
2 CONT # Even though Tresswell & Vincent (1889), start the pedigree with Pigot of Willaston, they break it before this Robert; and in the footnotes they explain that Blakeway disputed that lineage and asserted that Robt descends from Ric
2 CONC hard of Butley and the heiress of Chetwynd from the Peshale family.
