1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Our Royal, Noble, Titled and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins [https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p389.htm#i11657 Sir John Manwaring]
2 CONT * "Sir John Manwaring was born in 1395 at of Over Peover, Cheshire, England. He married Margaret Delves, daughter of John Delves, Esq., Sheriff of Staffordshire and Philippa Mainwaring, in 1411.(2,3) 
2 CONT * Sir John Manwaring married Joan Warren, daughter of John Warren, Esq. and Isabel Stanley, circa 1455. Sir John Manwaring died in September 1480." {'''<—''' Note that none of this is footnoted.}
2 CONT * '''Family:''' Margaret Delves {'''<—''' No footnote}
2 CONT * '''Children'''
2 CONT ** Elizabeth (Alice) Manwaring [†]
2 CONT ** Margaret Manwaring [†]
2 CONT ** William Manwaring, Esq.+2,3 b. c 1420, d. b 1476
2 CONT ** Mary Mainwaring+ b. c 1421, d. 1488 [citing "Ancestry.com, Submitted by swedesen."? Non-Sourced!!!]
2 CONT ** Johanna (Jane) Mainwaring+5 b. c 1425
2 CONT ** (Miss) Mainwaring+ b. c 1435 [†]
2 CONT
2 CONT † That the website manager included these names without source attribution is academically slapdash.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mainwaring-5 cites—
2 CONT
2 CONT * von Bonsdorff, Ingrid. “‘Hankyn’ or ‘Haukyn?’” Modern Philology, vol. 26, no. 1, 1928, pp. 57–61. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/433573 – Accessed 4 Oct. 2024.
2 CONT **This article gives by way of example: "This name, Hankyn, is found in a covenant for marriage of William Mainwaring, son of Hankyn Mainwaring, with Elyn, the daughter of Sir John Butler, knt. (1444), contained among the Mainwari
2 CONC ng manuscripts in the John Ryland Library, Manchester. The Mainwarings are a Cheshire family, and, according to Lower [Dictionary of the Family Names of the United Kingdom],' Hankyn was a common name in this and other Cheshire fam
2 CONC ilies of the gentry in the fifteenth century. It was from the same part of the country that the author of Piers Plowman came."
2 CONT * Douglas Richardson, ''Magna Carta Ancestry'', Vol. 3, p. 278. — In turn cites:
2 CONT ** Betham Baronetage of England 5 (1805): 568-578 (sub Mainwaring). Ormerod Hist. of Chester 1 (1819): 371. Burke Gen. & Heraldic Hist. of the Extinct & Dormant Baronetcies (1844): 334-336 (sub Mainwaring). Beamont Annals of the L
2 CONC ords Warrington 1 (Chetham Soc. 86) (1872): 248-262. Paget Lineage & Anc. of Prince Charles 2 (1977) 267, 406.
2 CONT * FindAGrave® [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/81535674/john-mainwaring John Mainwaring]  citing St. Lawrence's Churchyard, Over Peover, Cheshire East Unitary Authority, Cheshire, England; Maintained by (Gail) StorybehindtheSt
2 CONC ones (contributor 47612772).
2 CONT ** INSCRIPTION: Hic jacent corpora d'ni Joh'is Mainwaringe de Peever, et Johannæ ux' ejus, filiæ baronis de Stockport....regni Henri. — Here lie the bodies of John Mainwaringe of Peever, and of Joan his wife, daughter of the baron
2 CONC  of Stockport... of the reign of Henry.
2 CONT * See also: Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 282.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikitree: Research Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT "FindAGrave has that John was married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Margaret Mainwaring nee Delves was mentioned on a [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/185346204/margaret-mainwaring memorial] at St. Lawrence's Churchyard, Over Peover, Cheshire East Unitary Authority, Cheshire, England with a d
2 CONC eath date of 1490.[5] However no picture of tomb or evidence
2 CONT
2 CONT "Joan Mainwaring nee Warren was mentioned on a [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/81535825/joan-mainwaring memorial] at St. Lawrence's Churchyard, Over Peover, Cheshire East Unitary Authority, Cheshire, England.[6] However also 
2 CONC no picture of tomb or evidence"
