1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Elizabeth Brereton1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''F, #10996, d. between 30 November 1545 and 1551
2 CONT *Father      Sir Randle Brereton, Chamberlain of Chester2,8,4,5,9,7,10 d. 1531
2 CONT *Mother     Eleanor Dutton2,8,5,9,10 d. a 1522
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Brereton was born at of Malpas, Cheshire, England. She married James Starkey, Esq., son of Hugh Starkey, Esq. and Margaret Egerton. Elizabeth Brereton married Richard Cholmondeley, Esq., son of Richard Cholmonde
2 CONC ley and Ellen Davenport, after 1514.2,3,5,6,10 Elizabeth Brereton married Sir Randall Mainwaring, son of Sir John Manwaring, Sheriff of Flintshire and Katherine Honford, circa 1518; They had 3 daughters (Margaret, wife of Sir Arth
2 CONC ur Mainwaring; Elizabeth, wife of Peter Shakerley, Esq., & of Christopher Holford, Esq; & Katherine, wife of John Davenport, Esq.).2,3,4,5,6,7,10 Elizabeth Brereton died between 30 November 1545 and 1551 at Cheshire, England.10
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Richard Cholmondeley, Esq. d. 1518
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Sir Randall Mainwaring b. c 1495, d. 6 Sep 1557
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Katharine Mainwaring2
2 CONT **Margaret Mainwaring+11,2,4,5,7,10 b. c 1521, d. b 2 Sep 1590
2 CONT **Elizabeth Manwaring+2 b. c 1535, d. a 1601
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S2803] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, Vol. II, p. 120, 173; Plantagenet Ancestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 208.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 557.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 309.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 94.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 279.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 522.
2 CONT * 7.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 2.
2 CONT * 8.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 308-309.
2 CONT * 9.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 521.
2 CONT * 10.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 283.
2 CONT * 11.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 486.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p366.htm#i10996 _______________________
2 CONT *CHOLMLEY (CHOLMONDELEY), Sir Hugh (by 1513-97), of Cholmondeley, Cheshire.
2 CONT *b. by 1513, '''2nd s. of Richard Cholmley (d.1517/18) of Cholmondeley by Elizabeth, da. of Sir Randall Brereton''' of Malpas; bro. of Ralph. m. (1) Amy or Anne (d.1571), da. of Sir George Darman or Dorman of Malpas, 3s. inc. Hugh
2 CONC † 1da., (2) Mary, da. of Sir William Gruffydd of Penrhyn, Caern., wid. of Sir Randall Brereton of Malpas, s.p. suc. bro. 1539. Kntd. 11 May 1544.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/cholmley-%28cholmondeley%29-sir-hugh-1513-97 _____________________
2 CONT *CHOLMLEY, Ralph (by 1517-63), of St. Dunstan-in-the-West, London.
2 CONT *b. by 1517, '''yr. s. of Richard Cholmley of Cholmondeley, Cheshire by Elizabeth, da. of Sir Randall Brereton''' of Malpas; Cheshire; bro. of Sir Hugh†. educ. L. Inn 1535, called 1543. m. Elizabeth Pickering (d.1562), wid. of Rob
2 CONC ert Redman, printer, of London, s.p.2
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/cholmley-ralph-1517-63 _________________________
2 CONT *'''Breretons of Cheshire, 1100 to 1904 A. D (1904)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/breretonsofchesh00brer
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/n39/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.22
2 CONT *   Sir Randle IV., of Malpas. also, built the Brereton chapel, or chantry, at the south side of Malpas church, in 1522. He and his wife Eleanor were buried in this chapel, and their tomb still exists. The Shocklach manor lies wes
2 CONC t of Malpas. It was purchased by Sir Randle Brereton V., of Malpas, in 1572, from Sir Richard Corbet. Malpas and Shocklach, at the time of the conquest, formed portions of the Barony of Malpas, of which Robert Fitz-Hugh was baron.
2 CONC  He received it from Hugh Lupus, first Earl Royal of Chester. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/n43/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.24
2 CONT *   (2) In the Brereton chapel within Malpas church is the tomb of Sir Randle Brereton IV., of Malpas, and his wife Eleanor, who died 1532. This is a handsome tomb in the south aisle of the church, enclosed with a well carved oak 
2 CONC screen. This chapel now belongs by marriage and inheritance to the Egerton family. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/36/mode/1up
2 CONT **	KNIGHTS AS LORDS OF LAND, 
2 CONT *   In the feudal times in order to become a knight it was pre-requisite to be an owner of lands ; hence, the evidence we have of our original ancestor being the original Lord of Brereton. In those days there were two degrees of k
2 CONC nighthood, one a Knight Bachelor, or lord of a manor; the other a Knight Banneret, a knight who had distinguished himself in battle before his king or his baron ; as such was Sir Randle Brereton IV., of Malpas. He was so knighted 
2 CONC for brilliant bravery at Terouenne, and at Tourney, in France, by Henry VIII. The knight bachelor always carried a penon or pointed flag ; the knight banneret had his penon cut off square by the king. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/45/mode/1up
2 CONT **THE HALTON BRANCH OF THE MALPAS FAMILY, 
2 CONT *   There is very little recorded of this branch of the family. The Herald's Visitation Record of 1663-4 gives the pedigree commencing with Sir Roger Brereton, of Halton, the founder of the family, about 1540, and shows four gener
2 CONC ations of descent. I think this Sir Roger was the sixth son of Sir Randle Brereton IV., of Malpas, and the younger brother of John Brereton, the founder of the Norfolk branch. His mother was Eleanor, daughter of Sir Piers Dutton, 
2 CONC the Lord of Halton and Dutton, in 1500. Sir Piers was descended from Odard, one of the companions in arms of the Conqueror. He (Odard) assumed the name of Dutton upon receiving a grant of that town from Hugh Lupus, first Earl Roya
2 CONC l of Chester, the ancestor of Lady Ada's mother. Sir Piers was the great grandson of Sir Thomas Dutton, of Dutton, who was the Governor and Receiver of the Castle of Halton in 1330. Sir Piers was the son of Sir Lawrence Dutton, wh
2 CONC o married Johanna, daughter of Sir Andrew Brereton, of Brereton, and from whom are descended the present family of Baron Sherbourne, of Sherbourne, Gloucestershire. The Warburton family, of Arley, were also descended from the same
2 CONC  Odard. Sir Roger Brereton married Katherine, widow of Edward Fulleshurst and daughter of Sir William Brereton IX., of Brereton, by his second wife, Eleanor, daughter of Sir Randle Brereton III., of Ipstone and Malpas, and the wid
2 CONC ow of Philip Egerton, of Egerton. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/98/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Sir Randle de Brereton II., of Ipstone and Malpas, married Joanna, daughter of William Holford. By her he had two sons : 1, Randle Brereton, founder of the Eccleston and Wettenhall branch : 2, Owen Brereton, of Bar Hill, the a
2 CONC ncestor of Brereton of Coddington. His second wife was Katherine, daughter of William Butheley, of Eaton, Cheshire. By her he had three sons: 1, Randle, his heir, of Ipstone and Malpas; 2, Ralph Brereton, of Iscoyd Castle, Shropsh
2 CONC ire, who had one daughter, wife of John Holford ; 3, Bartholomew Brereton, of Grafton, who had three sons : a, Bartholomew ; b, John ; c, Humphrey, of Malpas, the historian of the War of the Roses. 
2 CONT *   Randle Brereton III., of Ipstone, died in Burgundy, France. His wife was Emma, daughter and heiress of John Carington, of Carington. By her he had two sons and two daughters : 1, Randle, his heir; 2, Humphrey, of Malpas; 3, El
2 CONC len, wife of Nicholas Bruyn, of Tarwin, Cheshire ; 4, Eleanor, wife of Philip de Egerton, afterwards wife of Sir William de Brerton IX., of Brereton. 
2 CONT *   Sir Randle Brereton IV., of Ipstone and Malpas ; Chamberlain of Chester 1506 to 1532; Knight of the Body to Henry VII. and Henry VIII. ; made a Knight Banneret by Henry VIII., at Boulonge, for Terrouenne and Tournay ; built th
2 CONC e Brereton Chapel in Malpas Church in 1522, in which he was buried in 1532. He married Eleanor, daughter of Sir Piers Dutton, of Halton Castle, Cheshire. By her he had nine sons and three daughters: 1, Randle, his heir; 2, Richard
2 CONC , founder of the Tatton branch ; 3, John, founder of the Norfolk branch ; 4, Thomas ; 5, Peter ; 6, Roger, founder of the Halton branch ; 7, William, succeeded his father as Chamberlain of Chester ; was beheaded by Henry VIII. wit
2 CONC h Queen Anne Boleyn, in 1536; 8, Robert; 9, Urian, founder of the Handford branch. The daughters were : 1, Anne, wife of John Harcourt ; afterwards was wife of John Pershall, of Hordesley ; '''2, Elizabeth, wife of Richard Cholmon
2 CONC deley ; afterwards was wife of Randle Mainwaring, of Over Peevor, Cheshire;''' 3, Jane, wife of Sir Thomas Hanmer, of Hanmer, Flintshire. (See Burosham branch). 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/breretonsofchesh00brer#page/99/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Sir Randle Brereton V., of Ipstone, Malpas and Shocklach, married Eleanor, daughter of Sir Philip Egerton, of Egerton. By her he had one child, Anne, wife of Randall Dod, of Edge. His second wife was Izabel, daughter of Thomas
2 CONC  Butler, of Bewsey. By her he had one son, Randle, his heir, and one daughter, Elizabeth, wife of James Starkey, of Darley. 
2 CONT *   Sir Randle Brereton VI., of Malpas and Shocklach, married Mary, daughter of Sir William Griffith, who was afterwards wife of Sir Hugh Cholmondeley. By her he had three sons: 1, Randle, his heir; 2, Richard, of Mitcham, Surrey;
2 CONC  3, Sir Thomas, of Yard, Somerset. (See these branches). _________________
2 CONT *'''The history of the county palatine and city of Chester: .... Vol. II.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyp02orme
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofcountyp02orme#page/377/mode/1up
2 CONT **	BRERETON OF SHOCKLACH, AND MALPAS.
2 CONT *RANDLE BRERETON, of Malpas, younger son of sir William Brereton of Brereton, kt. by Margaret, daughter of Henry Done of Utkinton. = ALICE, daughter and heiress of Wm. Ipstones of Ipstones.; ch: RANDLE (m. JOANNA Holford & KATHERI
2 CONC NE Bulkeley), WILLIAM, . . . . (m. . . . .  Spurstow) BRERETON.
2 CONT **RANDLE BRERETON, of Ipstones. = ch: RANDLE (of Eccleston), OWEN (of Barrel, or Bar Hill) BRERETON; = 1. JOANNA, daughter of Wm. Holford.; = 2. KATHERINE, dau. to Wm. Bulkeley, of Eaton., ch: RANDLE (m. EMMA Carington), RALPH, BA
2 CONC RTHOLOMEW BRERETON.
2 CONT ***RANDLE BRERETON of Ipstones, died in Burgundy. = EMMA, daughter and heiress of John Carington, of Carington, sister to Hamlet and Thomas., ch: SIR RANDLE (m. ELEANOR Dutton), HUMPHREY, ELLEN (m. Nicholas Bruyn), ELEANOR (m. Phi
2 CONC lip de Egerton) BRERETON.
2 CONT ****SIR RANDLE BRERETON, of Ipstones, Shocklach, and Malpas, kt. chamberlain of Chester, 21 Hen. VII. to 23 Hen. VIII. kt. banneret, and kt. of the body to Henry VII.= ELEANOR, daugh. to Piers Dutton of Hatton, esq. living 1522, b
2 CONC uried at Malpas., ch: Sir RANDLE (m. ELEANOR Egerton & ISABEL Butler), 2. Sir RICHARD, (m. Jane Massey), 3. JOHN (d.1542), 4. THOMAS (d.1511), 5. PETER (a priest), 6. Sir ROGER (m. Katherine Brereton), 7. Sir WILLIAM (m. Elizabeth
2 CONC  dau. of earl of Worcester, beheaded 1536), 8. ROBERT, 9. Sir URIAN (m. Margaret Honford & Alice Trafford), ANNE (m. John Harcourt & John Pershall), '''ELIZABETH (m. Ric. Cholmondeley & Randel Mainwaring)''', JANE (m. Thos. Hanmer
2 CONC ) BRERETON.
2 CONT *****SIR RANDLE BRERETON, of Shocklach and Malpas, knt. = ELEANOR, dau. to sir Philip Egerton of Egerton and Oulton, kt., ch: ANNE (m. Randal Dod) BRERETON; = ISABEL, dau. to Thos. Butler of Bewsey. second wife., ch: Sir RANDLE (m
2 CONC . MARY Griffith), ELIZABETH (m. James Starkey) BRERETON. .... etc.
2 CONT *****2. SIR RICHARD BRERETON, kt. marr. Jane, daughter of Geoffrey Massey of Tatton, died at Islington, 3 and 4 Phil. and Mary. Had issue.
2 CONT *****3. JOHN BRERETON, rector of both moieties of Malpas and of Astbury, Bebington, and of St. Mary's in Chester, died 1542.
2 CONT *****4. THOMAS BRERETON, rector of the higher moiety of Malpas, died 1511.
2 CONT *****5. PETER BRERETON, a priest.
2 CONT *****6. SIR ROGER BRERETON, kt. marr. Katherine daughter of sir William Brereton, of Brereton, kt. widow of Edward Fulleshurst of Crewe.
2 CONT *****7. SIR WILLIAM BRERETON, kt. chamberlain of Chester, and groom of the chamber to Hen. VIII. mar. Elizabeth, dau. of Charles, earl of Worcester, widow of sir John Savage; beheaded May 17, 1635.
2 CONT *****8. ROBERT BRERETON, living 1566.
2 CONT *****9. SIR URIAN BRERETON, of Honford, kt. mar. 1st, Margaret, dau. and heiress of Wm. Honford of Honford, and 2dly Alice, dau. of sir Edmund Trafford, kt.
2 CONT *****ANNE, wife of John Harcourt, and after of John Pershall of Hordesley.
2 CONT *****'''ELIZABETH, wife 1st. of Ric. Cholmondeley, and secondly of Randel Mainwaring of Peover.
2 CONT *****JANE, wife of sir Thos. Hanmer, of Hanmer, kt. ___________________________
