1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Elizabeth Manwaring1,2
2 CONT *'''F, #21651, b. circa 1535, d. after 1601
2 CONT *Father      Sir Randall Mainwaring2 b. c 1495, d. 6 Sep 1557
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Brereton2 d. bt 30 Nov 1545 - 1551
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Manwaring was born circa 1535 at Over Peover, Cheshire, England. She married Peter Shakerley, Esq., son of Geoffrey Shakerley, Esq. and (Miss) Holland, circa 1551.2 Elizabeth Manwaring married Christopher Holfor
2 CONC d, Esq., son of Thomas Holford, Esq. and Margaret Boteler, on 13 July 1561 at of Over Peover, Cheshire, England.2 Elizabeth Manwaring died after 1601.
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Peter Shakerley, Esq. d. 6 Jan 1553
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Dorothy Shakerley b. c 1552
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Christopher Holford, Esq. b. c 1535, d. 27 Jan 1581
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Mary Holford+ b. 20 Jan 1562, d. 16 Aug 1625
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6564] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 495; Burke's Dormant and Extinct Baronetcies, p. 335.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 557.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p721.htm#i21651 _______________________
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth Mainwaring1
2 CONT *F, #574680
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Jan 2013
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Mainwaring married Peter Shakerley, son of Geoffrey Shakerley and unknown daughter Holland.1
2 CONT *'''      Cheshire.1 She lived Over Peover.1 Her married name became Shakerley. Daughter and coheir of Sir Randal Mainwaring.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Elizabeth Mainwaring and Peter Shakerley
2 CONT ** 1.Geoffrey Shakerley+2 d. 1618
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 3, page 3576. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p57468.htm#i574680 _____________________
2 CONT *Lady Mary Cholmondeley (1563-1625) was a litigant in a forty-year-long dispute over her father's estate. She was the wife of Sir Hugh Cholmondeley, the younger and had eight children with him.
2 CONT *She was born in 1563 to '''Christopher Holford and Elizabeth Mainwaring''' in Holford, Great Budworth, Cheshire, England and christened on January 20, 1563.[1] She married Sir Randall Brereton of Malpas but he soon died. Around 1
2 CONC 581, she married Sir Hugh Cholmondeley.[2] They had eight children, named Robert, Hatton, Hugh, Thomas, Francis, Mary, Lettice, and Frances,[1] before Sir Cholmondeley's death in 1601.[3] Mary Cholmondeley died on August 15, 1625 
2 CONC at the age of sixty-three in Vale Royal, Whitegate, Cheshire, England and was buried the next day in Malpas, Cheshire, England.[1] .....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Cholmondeley_(heiress) __________________________
