1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family and Education b. 1577, 1st s. of Edward Mainwaring of Whitmore by Jane, da. of Matthew Craddock of Staffs. educ. Magdalen Hall, Oxf. 1594; M. Temple 1595. m. 1600, Sarah (d.1648), da. and coh. of John Stone,
2 CONC  haberdasher, of Bow Churchyard, London, 2s. 1da. suc. fa. 1604.
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held Mayor, Newcastle-under-Lyme 1609, 1640, 1643; j.p. Staffs. 1615; sheriff 1645-6.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Whitmore was some four miles from Newcastle, for which borough Mainwaring was returned while still at the Middle Temple. He was a parliamentarian in the civil war, and died in 1647. The 1625 MP for Newcastle-under-Lyme w
2 CONC as his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/mainwaring-edward-1577-1647
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was the Sheriff of Staffs in 1646 and espoused the cause of the Parl(y) in the Civil War. He purchased the Manor of Knutton in 1595, and entered the Middle Temple that year. He was MP of Newcastle in 1601 and 1625, mayor of New
2 CONC castle in 1609.
