1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ashton-57
2 CONT
2 CONT Aston, John (c.1571-1615) was the son of Sir Thomas Aston (d. 1613), kt., and his first wife, Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Arthur Mainwaring of Ightfield (Staffs).[1] A lawyer, he was educated at Cliffords Inn and the Inner Temple (
2 CONC admitted 1598). Sewer to Queen Anne of Denmark, consort of King James I. He m. 1598 (licence 21 July), Maud (c.1580-1635), daughter of Robert Needham esq. of Shavington (Shropshire).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Thomas Aston (1600-45), 1st bt. (q.v.);
2 CONT # John Aston (1604-50); responsible for managing the Aston estate after the death of his brother in 1646; died unmarried, 1 April 1650 and was buried at Aston, where he is commemorated by a monument erected in 1697;
2 CONT # Robert Aston (b. 1606); died young;
2 CONT # Maud Aston (b. 1607); married 1st, Thomas Parsons esq. of Cubbington (Warks) and 2nd, 1666, John Shuckburgh (d. 1673) of Upton in Wirral;
2 CONT # Anne Aston (b. 1609); died young;
2 CONT # Elizabeth Aston (1611-28); died unmarried, 1628.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the Aston Hall estate from his father in 1613 & he died 13 May 1615.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT #Howard, J. J. Miscellanea: Genealogica et Heraldica. London, England: Hamilton, Adams and Co., 1886. Volume I, pp 85-86.[[1]]
2 CONT # (221) Aston of Aston Hall, Aston-by-Sutton Landed families of Britain and Ireland
