1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Thomas_Aston,_1st_Baronet
2 CONT
2 CONT He matriculated at Brasenose College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, on 28 March 1617.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Brasenose College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, on 8 July 1619 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was admitted to Lincoln's Inn in 1620.1 He was created 1st Baronet Aston, of Aston [in the parish of Runcorn], co. Chester [England] on 25 July 1628.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Sheriff of Cheshire from 1635 to 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Cheshire from April 1640 to May 1640.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Nantwich on 28 January 1642, where he was defeated by the Parliamentary General, Sir William Brereton, and was captured.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Captain of the troop of horse which he raised for King Charles I.
