1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Jean_Spottswood_%281%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Name 	Lady Jean Spottswood
2 CONT Alt Name 	Lady Jean Spottiswoode
2 CONT Gender 	Female
2 CONT Birth? 	1648 	Rosslyn Castle, Edinburgh, , Scotland
2 CONT Marriage 		to James Sinclair, 19th Baron, of Rosslyn
2 CONT Marriage 		to George Hay
2 CONT Death? 		Y
2 CONT [edit]
2 CONT ▼ Jean Spotswood
2 CONT
2 CONT     Douglass, Robert. The Baronage of Scotland: Containing, An Historical and Genealogical Account of the Gentry of that Kingdom. (London: Cadell & Davies, 1798), Page 248. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     XIX. James Sinclair of Roslin, was a great loyalist, and suffered many hardships on account of his attachment to the interest of the royal family, whereby he greatly incumbered his estate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     He married Jean, daughter of Sir Henry Spotswood, sheriff of Dublin, by whom he had many children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     1. Alexander, his heir. 
2 CONT     2. Thomas, who married Elisabeth, daughter of captain Wauchope, a brother of Niddery, by whom he had two sons, 1. James, who had a company in the French service, married a daughter of commissioner Wedderburn, and had issue. 2.
2 CONC  Francis, who is a general officer, and has the command of two battalions in the Neapolitan service: This Thomas had also two daughters, the eldest whereof was married to _____ Bower of Methie and Kincaldrum, and was mother of the
2 CONC  present Alexander Bower of Kincaldrum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     James had a daughter, Helen, who married to Henry Ker of Graden, Esq; 
2 CONT
2 CONT     He was succeeded by his eldest son, Alexander Sinclair, XX. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ▼References
2 CONT
2 CONT       Douglass, Robert. The Baronage of Scotland: Containing, An Historical and Genealogical Account of the Gentry of that Kingdom. (London: Cadell & Davies, 1798)
2 CONT     Page 248.
2 CONT       Spotswood Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lady Jean Spottiswoode, born in 1648 in Rosslyn Castle, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT     1st married, to George Hay, Esquire [a younger son of John Hay of Barra] who became Lord Register of Scotland. This couple produced issue:
2 CONT     John Hay,
2 CONT     Jean Hay,
2 CONT     Richard Augustine Hay [Father Hay, born 1661],
2 CONT     George Hay, and
2 CONT     Marie Hay.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2nd married, to James Sinclair
2 CONT
