2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Vincent Corbet, 1st Baronet (13 June 1617 – 1657) was an English lawyer and politician who sat in the House of Commons in 1640. He fought on the Royalist side in the English Civil War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Corbet was the son of Sir Andrew Corbet, of Moreton Corbet, Shropshire and his wife Elizabeth Boothby.[1] He was baptized at Morton Corbett on 13 July 1617. He matriculated at Queen's College, Cambridge on 24 October 1634. He was 
2 CONC of Lincoln's Inn in 1637.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Remains of part of Moreton Corbet CastleIn April 1640, Corbet was elected Member of Parliament for Shropshire in the Short Parliament.[3] He supported the King and was created a baronet of Moreton Corbet on 29 January 1642.[2] Mor
2 CONC eton Corbet Castle, the home of the Corbet family was repeatedly damaged during the Civil War[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Corbet died at the age of 40 and was buried at Morton Corbet on 21 January 1657.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Corbet obtained a licence to marry Jane Acton, daughter of John Acton, citizen and goldsmith on 15 July 1642.[2] His wife is recorded as Sarah Monson, daughter of Sir Robert Monson, of Carlton, Lincolnshire, who was created Viscou
2 CONC ntess Corbet for life in 1679.[1]
