3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captured and Killed on the march from Deerfield Massacre: In 1675 Indians sacked and burned the town. Samson and his family fled back to Hatfield where they stayed until about 1680, when he returned to Deerfield to
2 CONC  rebuild his home and plantation. Here he lived and raised his children until Feb 29, 1703/04when French and Indians made a savage attack on the town. This was the historical Deerfield Massacre. Samson and his grandaughter Mercy R
2 CONC oot, age 17, were killed. His wife Mary was captured by the Indians and taken hostage on a long trek to Canada. On the 5th day of the march she faltered and could go no further and was killed by her Indian master. <nowiki>--------
2 CONC ------------</nowiki> Killed and scalped at the Deerfield Massacre
