1 NAME Reana /unknown/
2 GIVN Reana
2 SURN unknown
2 _MARNM Frost
2 NICK Reana James
2 NICK Reana Andrew
2 NICK Reana Daniels
2 NICK Reanna
2 NICK widow Reana Daniel
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1605
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 3 JAN 1676
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cambridge
3 STAE Massachusetts
1 OCCU Arrived in Massachusetts with her husband Edmund James in 1630
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Andrew, mariner of Cambridge, 2nd married the widow Reana James of Watertown. Their marriage contract was dated 11 Aug. 1640.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana had married first to Edmund James before 1640, second to William Andrews (- 1652) c 11 August 1640, and third to Robert Daniel (-1655) 2 May 1654, and then married fourth (after 1669) to "Elder" Edmund Frost (d 1672).
2 CONT
2 CONT The inventory of the widow Reana Frost's estate was taken January 3, 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Some online family trees, without source, claim she was the daughter of Giles James and Agnes Gayyard. This is not recognized in Anderson's Great Migration work.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maiden name and identity of her parents are not known. There is no documentation that she was the daughter of Giles James and Agnes Gayyard.
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of her marriage to her first husband, Edmund James, is unknown. She contracted to marry William Andrews in 1640; she m3 Robert Daniel, then last by 1669 to Edmund Frost as his third wife.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died before 3 November 1675 when an inventory of her state was made. The Middlesex County Probate Files for Reana Frost contain a note stating that an inventory record was in p. 292 Vol 4, dated 1676 - 4 -2[2] It is unclear we
2 CONC ather this indicated June 2 or April 4, or if this is the date of the record or the inventory itself.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no evidence, per Robert Charles Anderson,[3] that she had any children by any of her husbands.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-209216.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana (Unknown) Frost (1614 - bef. 1675) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Reana Frost formerly [surname unknown] aka James, Andrews, Daniels===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1614 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Edmund James — married before 1640 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Andrews — married 11 Aug 1640 (to 1652) [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Robert Daniel — married 2 May 1654 (to 6 Jul 1655) [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Edmund Frost — married before 5 Dec 1665 in Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 3 Nov 1675 in Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown-209216 created 31 Aug 2013 | Last modified 15 Jul 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana (Unknown) Frost migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Paige, Lucius Robinson. History of Cambridge, Massachusetts. 1630-1877: With a Genealogical Register, Volume 2 p. 480. Boston: H. O. Houghton
2 CONT ↑ Middlesex County, MA: Probate File Papers, 1648-1871.Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2014. (From records supplied by the Massachusetts Supreme Judicial Court Archives.)
2 CONT ↑ Anderson, Robert Charles. Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III. (Boston, MA: NEHGS 1995):1072, biography of Edmund Frost.
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT Representative Men and Old Families of Rhode Island: Genealogical Records ... pg 2031 - source for "Cyrene" as her maiden name, without explanation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://archive.org/stream/historichomesan02cuttgoog#page/n151/mode/1up/search/Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Elder Frost appeared in Cambridge as early as 1635. The historian of that town, among many other things, says that he possessed "little besides his homestead, and his pressing wants were relieved by the Church." His descendants in
2 CONC  Cambridge have been numerous. His will, dated April 16. 1672, named his wife '''Reana''': sons Ephraim, Thomas, John and Joseph: and daughters Sarah and Mary; he also left legacies to Jacob French and his wife; to the children of
2 CONC  Golden Moore, to Harvard College and to Mr. Alcock's son there. '''The inventory of his widow Reana was taken January 3, 1675.'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. and Canada, Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s about Reana James
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: 	Reana James
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrival Year: 	1630
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrival Place: 	Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members: 	Wife Reana***
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Publication Code: 	281
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary Immigrant: 	James, Edmond
2 CONT
2 CONT Annotation: 	Over 700 names given, with list of 40 heads of families on the Mary and John, which sailed  with the Winthrop Fleet. See also no. 0388, Bartlett; no. 3323, Hunt; no. 4477, Kuhns; and no. 6600,  Passengers of the Mary 
2 CONC and John, 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Bibliography: 	BANKS, CHARLES EDWARD. The Winthrop Fleet of 1630: an Account of the  Vessels, the Voyage, the Passengers and Their English Homes, from Original Authorities. Boston:  Houghton Mifflin, 1930. 119p. Reprinted b
2 CONC y Genealogical Publishing Co., Baltimore, 1961. Repr. 1983.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: 	76
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Watertown, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana (MNU) James
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana (MNU) James and William Andrew filed marriage intentions on 11 August 1640 in Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.1,2 On 2 May 1654 Reana, married Robert Daniels, in Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.1,2,3 On
2 CONC  3 July 1655 in Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, Reana James was mentioned in the will of Robert Daniels.3,4 On 12 April 1669 Reana, married Elder Edmund Frost.1,2,3
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT #Paige, Lucius R. History of Cambridge, Massachusetts 1630-1877 with a Genealogical Register. 1877. Reprint Bowie, Maryland: Heritage Books, 1986.
2 CONT #Gozzaldi, Mary Isabella. History of Cambridge, Massachusetts 1630-1877 with a Genealogical Register - Supplement and Index. 1930. Reprint Bowie, Maryland: Heritage Books, 1986.
2 CONT #Lawson, Stephen M. "Daniels - Morse Ancestry of Stephen Lawson. Online http://sml.simplenet.com/smlawson/daniels.htm. Printout dated 12 March 1998.
2 CONT #Anonymous. "Will of Robert Daniell", The New England Historical and Genealogical Register volume XXX (1876).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Middlesex County, Massachusetts Probate Index, 1648-1870 about Reana Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Given Name: 	Reana
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname: 	Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Date: 	1676
2 CONT
2 CONT Subject: 	Administration
2 CONT
2 CONT Number: 	8629
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana (MNU) James Marriages:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to William Andrew, p. 18
2 CONT
2 CONT ANDREW, William, mariner, Cambridge, frm. Mar 4, 1633-4. Godly parents brought him up till 17 years of age; was apprenticed at Ipswich, Eng. Came first to Charlestown. In his absence his wife rem. to Cambridge, which pleased him. 
2 CONC [Rel.] Town officer. Sold house, all lands and rights in C. Sept. 25, 1637. Sold land again 2 (2) 1651. Wife Mary d. Jan. 19, 1639-40. He m. 2, (contract Aug. 11, 1640,) Reana James of Watertown.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. in 1652, leaving an only son Samuel, who was adm. chh. Dec. 10, 1658. The widow m. 2, Robert Daniels and 3, Edmund Frost.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Robert Daniel, p. 129
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL, Robert, husbandman, Watertown, propr.; rem. to Cambridge 1G36; frm. March
2 CONT
2 CONT 14, 1638-9. Town officer. Deposed 26 (4) 1652, ae. 60 years and upwards. [Mdx. Files.] Wife Elizabeth d. Oct. 2. 1643; he m. May 2, 1654, Reana, widow of Wm. Andrew. Oh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary b. 2 (7) 1642, Thomas bur. 6 (9) 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. July 6, 1655. Will, dated 3 July, prob. Oct. 2, 1655. Wife Reana to have the est. he rec'd with her and additional. 5 children; eldest dau. Elizabeth now wife of Thomas Fanning; sons Samuel and Joseph, daus. Sarah and Mary; 
2 CONC cousin Anna Newcomen. [Reg. XXX, 459.] The widow m. Edmund Frost.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Edmund Frost, Page 176 
2 CONT
2 CONT FROST, Edmund, Cambridge, frm. March 3, 1635-6; propr. 1636. Ruling elder. Wife Thomasine, "Thomas-Anne;" [Mi.] eh. John, "baptized in England," [Mi.] Thomas b. (1) 1637, Samuel b. (12) 1638, Joseph b. 13 (11) 1639, James b. 9 (2)
2 CONC  1643, Mary b. 24 (5) 1645, Ephraim, Thomas, Sarah. The wife Thomasine d., and he m. before 1669, Reana Daniel, widow successively of — James, Wm. Andrew and Robert Daniel. [Mdx. De. Ill, 364.]
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. July 12, 1672. Will dated 16 April, "stricken in years;" prob. Oct. 1, folg. He beq. to wife Reana; to sons Ephraim, Thomas, John and Joseph; to his two daus. Sarah and Mary; to Jacob French and his wife, and the ch. of Gold
2 CONC en More; to Harvard College and to Mr. Alcock's son there. The inv. of the est. of the widow was taken 3 (11) 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Charles Henry Pope, The Pioneers of Massachusetts, Boston: Charles H. Pope, 1900.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Reana Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Reana Frost died sometime prior to January 3, 1675/76 since a recording of Reana Frost's estate was taken on that date. Her estate was valued at 78 pounds 10 shillings.
2 CONT
