1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT > '''William Bankes''', esq. of Winstanley Hall, ''b.'' 1658; ''m.'' 1687, his cousin Lettice, eldest da. of Richard Legh, esq. of Lyme, but by her (who survived him and married, secondly, Thomas Fleetwood, esq. of Bank.) he had n
2 CONC o issue, and was consequently succeeded by his nephew,
2 CONT
2 CONT > [https://www.geni.com/people/William-Banks/6000000046007232866 William Bankes], esq. of Winstanley Hall, ''b.'' 1695, who ''m.'' Elizabeth, third dau. of Amos Meredith, esq. and sister and co-heir of Sr William Meredith, bart. M
2 CONC .P. of Henbury, co. Chester, by whom he left an only child,
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=6AtBAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA214 ''A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, Enjoying Territorial Possessions Or High Official Rank: But Univested with Heritable Hon
2 CONC ours, Volume 4''] (1838) by John Burke
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT > The last '''William Bankes''' dying in 1689, the manors passed to his brother [https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Banks/6000000045972719029 Thomas]'s [https://www.geni.com/people/William-Banks/6000000046007232866 son] and [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/William-Banks/6000000046013402044 grandson]. Thomas had also a daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Holme-Banks/6000000046007100265 Anne], who married [https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Holme/6000000046
2 CONC 011938877 Hugh Holme] of Upholland in 1732, and their descendants, [https://www.geni.com/people/Meyrick-Bankes/6000000034446460132 assuming the name of Bankes], ultimately acquired possession, retaining it until the death of [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/people/Meyrick-Bankes/6000000034447298019 Meyrick Bankes] in 1881. His daughter, [https://www.geni.com/people/Eleanor-Starkie-Letterewe-Bankes/6000000046016305036 Mrs. Murray, was left a life interest in the estat
2 CONC e, and it was entailed in tail male on her sons. She resumed her maiden name and died December 1907, when her only surviving son [https://www.geni.com/people/George-Bankes/6000000046053705998 George Bankes] came into the property.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.british-history.ac.uk/vch/lancs/vol4/pp87-89 Winstanley], British History Online
2 CONT
