2 CONC l.), 19 May 1670, aged 16; succeeded to the Baronetcy in or before 1670. He, by his extravagence, ruined the family, and sold or mortgaged most of the estates. He died unmarried 6 February 1679/80, and was buried at Hickleton, age
2 CONC d 27."
