1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 6.  June Kinard, comp.  2000.  Early Immigrants to Virginia from the 1500s and 1600s.  The Researchers, Indianapolis, IN (online at Ancestry.com):
2 CONT
2 CONT >VENABLE, ABRAHAM, from England to New Kent Co. about 1685.  Married (1) Sarah ___ (died 1687) (2) Elizabeth Lewis Hicks, daughter of Hugh Lewis.  The widow of John Nicks.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Venable, Nathaniel, and Lyon G. Tyler. “Venable Family.” The William and Mary Quarterly 15, no. 4 (1907): 246–49. *https://doi.org/10.2307/1915563.
2 CONT *https://www.familysearch.org/tree/pedigree/portrait/L25D-GRJ 
2 CONT *Ancestors of Elizabeth Lewis http://www.choicemn.com/trees/gibson-tullis/4744.html 
2 CONT *"Hey, Sugar!" – The Windmills of Barbados  1663  Caribbean Sea http://www.mullinsfamilyhistoryproject.com/map/new_orleans?fbclid=IwAR0Q9hcTCC-_Ima3rcg183eJlOy6NdBIFPEg5f4m-GNKWrRwLNH_LOaNMNA 
2 CONT *Full text of "The Cabells and their kin. A memorial volume of history, biography, and genealogy" 
2 CONT *Genealogies of Virginia Families. United States, Genealogical Publishing Company, 1981. P. 658 https://www.google.com/books/edition/_/55I38FXWyPgC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA658&dq=Abraham+(II)+and+Martha+Davis+Venable
2 CONT *Some Venables of England and America And Brief Accounts of Families Into Which Certain Venables Married Henrietta Brady Brown Kinderton Press Cincinnati, Ohio 1961 Copyright 1961 by Henrietta Brady Brown All rights reserved Kinde
2 CONC rton Press. 636 Dixie Terminal Building, Cincinnati, Ohio. http://www.wallace-venable.name/Venable_Genealogy/Some_Venables_of_England_and_America.pdf
2 CONT *Early Lewises in the Colonies 1600-1790 https://www.senclewises.com/earlylewises.html
2 CONT *Hugh Lewis remix By Linda Mullen January 30, 2007 at 07:04:56 https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/lewis/17668/
2 CONT *https://gw.geneanet.org/diann3?lang=en&pz=nikolas+scott&nz=bass&p=james+or+john&n=nix
2 CONT *https://www.genealogieonline.nl/en/riches-to-rags-family-tree/P9371.php
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/76873678/nathaniel-venable
2 CONT *http://dgmweb.net/FGS/V/VenableAbraham-Sarah_-ElizabethMildredLewis.html
2 CONT *Gregg, Eugene Stuart. A Crane's Foot (or Pedigree) of Branches of the Gregg, Stuart, Robertson, Dobbs and Allied Families. United States, Gregg, 1975. pp. 239, 367  < [https://www.google.com/books/edition/_/_31PAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbp
2 CONC v=0 GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-439411111-1-509289/mary-elizabeth-nix-born-lewis-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-56a2a2dc7cb5397c957766411ab38a7f&mrid=5a4e78175574c5c624cd0f459d8558e8
2 CONC  MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 16 2022, 19:34:09 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT James was born in Barbados, where his father, an English Planter, had moved in 1634. James married an apparent widow, Mrs. James Lewis, in Barbados. Her late husband must have been related somehow to James' mother, Elizabeth Lewis
2 CONC . James and wife became the ancestors of our Nix line, and of most (if not all) of the Nixes of VA, SC, GA, MS, and elsewhere in the US such as those who migrated from GA to CO in the early 1900's. Family tradition in GA says that
2 CONC  somewhere down this line, one Nix wife of VA was related to US Presidents John Adams, and John Quincy Adams.
2 CONT
2 CONT James left Barbados and sailed for New Kent, VA, and died soon after his son James was born there, (about 1665.) He was his only child. This son James had sons George and Edward, also born in VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/pedigree/portrait/L25D-GRJ
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The following comes from Genealogies of Virginia Families, Volume I, Edmunds Family. Abraham Venable came to Virginia about 1685; his second wife, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Lewis, widow of John Hicks, also seen as Nicks or Hix or Nix (daughter of Captain Hugh Lewis, and an older Sister of Abadiah Lewis who married Robert Davis and were the parents of Martha Davis, who married Abraham Venabl
2 CONC e II.
2 CONT
2 CONT James & Mildred Nix Married 1685 in Barbados
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Mildred Elizabeth Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT Mildred Elizabeth Lewis (married James Nicks (20 Oct 1642 - 1687) on 1685) (married Abraham Venable I (12 Jan 1662 - 1710) on 1699) is the mother of 5 children and the grandmother of 2 grandchildren. Listed below are details on up
2 CONC  to five generations of descendants. See Mildred Elizabeth's Family Tree & Genealogy Tools for more views.
2 CONT
2 CONT     James Nix ancestors (1665 - 1687)
2 CONT     John Ncks ancestors (1667 - 1729)
2 CONT     George Nix ancestors descendants (1680 - 02 Nov 1745) m. Elizabeth Mildred Lewis (10 May 1655 - 1693). m. Susannah Burton (11 Feb 1692 - Dec 1750) on 1717.
2 CONT         Mary Nix ancestors (1684 - 1760)
2 CONT         Joseph Nix ancestors (1725 - 1800) m. Georgia B Adams (1735 - 1801).
2 CONT     Edward Nix ancestors (Nov 1686 - 08 Oct 1776)
2 CONT     Joseph Venable ancestors (1702 - 1703)
2 CONT
