1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lydia Perkins''' was born 1616 in Of, St. Albans, Hertfordshire, England and died 3 MAR 1645/46 in Hampton, Rockingham Co., New Hampshire 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Isaac Perkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT # MAR 1636/37 in Hampton, Essex Co., Massachusetts to Francis Peabody b: BET 1613 AND 1614 in St. Albans, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of FRANCIS PEABODY and LYDIA are: 		
2 CONT # LYDIA2 PEABODY, b. August 30, 1640, Hampton, New Hampshire; d. April 30, 1715, Boxford, Massachusetts.
2 CONT # JOHN PEABODY, b: 1642 in Hampton, Rockingham, New Hampshire
2 CONT # JOSEPH PEABODY, b. Abt. 1644, Hampton, New Hampshire; d. Abt. 1722; m. (1) BETHIAH BRIDGES October 26, 1668, Boxford, Massachusetts; m. (2) MARY WHEELER, January 4, 1714/15, Beverly, Massachusetts.
2 CONT # WILLIAM PEABODY, b. March 3, 1645/46, Hampton, New Hampshire; d. March 6, 1699/1700, Boxford, Massachusetts; m. (1) MARY BROWN, December 8, 1680; m. (2) HANNAH HALE, August 14, 1684, Boxford, Massachusetts.
2 CONT # 3. ISAAC PEABODY, b. Abt. 1648, Hampton, New Hampshire; d. 1727, Topsfield, Massachusetts; m. (1) ELIZABETH; m. (2) SARAH ESTES GILL Abt. 1693.Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
2 CONT * www.angelfire.com/ny/chickened/peabodyfamily.html 
2 CONT * http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr02/rr02_301.html#P10139
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 9. Lydia Perkins, baptized 1 Jan 1617/8 in Hillmorton, Warwick, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.boydhouse.com/michelle/hussey/isaacaliceperkins.html
2 CONT * http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=113255165
2 CONT  **************************** Find A Grave Memorial# 113255165; http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=113255165
2 CONT * '''Birth:''' 1617, England
2 CONT * '''Death:''' 1649 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire, USA
2 CONT *   •  dau of 2nd wife
2 CONT *   •  b 1 Jan 1617/18; d. bef 1649 
2 CONT * '''Family links: '''
2 CONT *    '''Parents:'''
2 CONT **        Isaac Perkins (1571 - 1639)
