1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://mayflowercharts.com/pabodie/
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 7630. Capt. John Peabody. Born ca 1642 in Hampton, Rockingham Co., NH. John died on 5 Jul 1720 in Boxford, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT * son of Francis Peabody & Lydia
2 CONT
2 CONT John first married Hannah Andrews, second (Sarah Trescott) Moseley, widow of Increase Moseley.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the first settlers of Boxford, Mass., where he was the first school master. He served as town clerk for 24 years, was selectman for many years and captain of the militia. He was made a freeman in 1674, and was a repr
2 CONC esentative to the General Court 1689-1691. (Velton Peabody, vpeabody {at} aol {dot} com, http://www.pbdy {dot} com/index.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as jury member in Salem witch trials.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the Boxford church February 21, 1703. His house stood on the site of the summer home of Julius A. Palmer, Mrs. Palmer being a lineal descendant. The house itself was torn down about 1865 by Mr. Palmer. It was a large two
2 CONC  story square mansion, and according to the custom the walls were filled with brick. On the front the second story projected about a foot over the lower story. While in the last days of its existence it presented a most forlorn an
2 CONC d dreary appearance. It stood in an open field alone, and in front, near the end, was an old wall over with there was a tangle of vines. (Stearns, p. 476)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr04/rr04_177.html#P10147
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Second Generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN, eldest child of Lieut. Francis and Mary (Foster) Peabody, married (first) Hannah Andrews, Nov. 23, 1665. She died Dec. 24, 1702,* aged about sixty years. He mar- ried (second) Sarah Mosely, of Dorchester, Nov. 26, 1703. Live
2 CONC d in Boxford. Died in 1720. Children, all by his first wife: .John, born Aujj. 28, 1666. Mercy, born in 1668. Thomas, born July 22, 1670. Mary, born April 6, 1672. Lydia, born March 9, 1673. DAVID, born July 12, 1678. Elizabeth, b
2 CONC orn Aug. 13, 1680. Nathan, born July 20, 1682. Hannah, born in 168-. Rath, born Nov. 13, 1684. Moses, born Feb. 27, 1687.
2 CONT ======================
2 CONT
2 CONT Third Generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID, sixth child of Capt. John and Hannah (Andrews) Peabody, married Sarah (Gould) Pope, of Dartmouth. Children: Thomas, born Sept. 22, 1705. Hannah, born Oct. 14, 1707. Sarah, born Sept. 26, 1709. Mercy, born Jan. 23, 1712. JOH
2 CONC N, born April 11, 1714. Deborah, born Sept. — , 1716. Rebecca, born Dec. 3, 1718. Susanna, born May — , 1721. Mary, born Sept. — , 1723 ; died in infancy. David, born Oct. 4. 1724. Mary, born Nov. 1, 1726. En- sign David Peabody d
2 CONC ied April 1, 1726. Sarah (Gould- Pope) Peabody died Sept. 29, 1756, aged 72.
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth JOHN, fifth child of Ensign David and Sarah (Gould- Pope) Peabody, married Mary Chadwick, Feb. 26, 1736. Lived in Boxford. Children : David, born June 27, 1736. Mary, born Dec. 22, 1737. Mehitable, born Sept. 13, 1739. Asa,
2 CONC  born July 1, 1741. Jedediah, born April 11, 1743. MOSES, born Nov. 1, 1744. Ruth, born April 7, 1746. Andrew, born Jan. 20, 1748. Elizabeth, born Feb. 17, 1751. Lucy, born March 23, 1753. John Peabody died April 27, 1765. Mary (C
2 CONC hadwick) Peabody married Ebenezer Killam, July 9, 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT •Burled in Bell Rock Cemetery, Maiden, where her grave-stone is yet (Oct. 4, 1903) preserved.
2 CONT ===================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth MOSES, sixth child of John and Mary (ChadwiclO Pp* body, married Hannah Foster, May 26 1767 Sh*, daughter of Lieut. Jeremiah and Ib^ail C Wool) Foster"
2 CONT =====================
2 CONT
2 CONT Sixth JEREMIAH, fifth child of Dea. Moses and Hannah (Fos- ter) Peabody, married Catharine Kimball, of Bradford, Dec. 23, 1804. She was a daughter of William and Ruth (Kimball) Kimball, and was born Aug. 16, 1782. Four children : 
2 CONC Aro-
2 CONT
2 CONT line, born ; died in infancy or early childhood. Aro-
2 CONT
2 CONT line Emily, born Feb. 15, 1807. Sarah Ann, born in Salem,
2 CONT
2 CONT March 24, 1810. George Frederick, born . Jeremiah
2 CONT
2 CONT Peabody died in Boston, Aug. 5, 1839. Catharine (Kimball) Peabody died .
2 CONT ===========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Seventh SARAH ANN, third child of Jeremiah and Catharine (Kimball) Peabody, married James Cogswell Converse, Jan. 8, 1834. He was born in Weathersfield, Vermont, Sept. 23, 1807. Five children ; Ellen Elizabeth, born in Boston, May
2 CONC  11, 1836; died in Boston, May 13, 1859. Katherine Pea- body, born in Boston, Jan. 20, 1839. Anna Harper, born June 22, 1841. James Blanchard, born in Boston, Feb. 17, 1846. Edmund Cogswell, born Nov. 7, 1849. James Cogs- well Con
2 CONC verse died in Greenfield, May 25, 1891. Sarah Ann (Peabody) Converse died in West Cambridge, May 20, 1866. http://archive.org/stream/genealogyofdesce00perl/genealogyofdesce00perl_djvu.txt
