2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr04/rr04_258.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Pane-Joyce Genealogy Lieut. Francis Peabody (2849) & Lydia [Pabodie] 7963. Lydia Peabody. Born ca 1640 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire. Lydia was baptized in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire, on 30 Aug 1640.1
2 CONC 7 Lydia died in Boxford, MA on 30 Apr 1715.206 Ca 1662 Lydia first married Thomas Howlett (5797) , son of Dea. Thomas Howlett (ca 1606-1677/8) & Alice French (2339) (ca 1610-26 Jun 1666). Born ca 1637 in Ipswich, MA.16 Thomas died
2 CONC  in Ipswich, MA on 22 Dec 1667.17 Their children include: 15500i. Mary Howlett (ca 1664-24 Oct 1727) 15501ii. Alice Howlett (ca 1666-bef Dec 1696) Bef 1677/8 Lydia second married Lieut. Thomas Perley (2864) , son of Allen Perley (
2 CONC 1228) (ca 1608-28 Dec 1675) & Susanna Bokesen (-11 Feb 1692).17 Born ca 1641 in Ipswich, MA.112 Thomas died in Boxford, MA on 24 Sep 1709.206 Their children include: 8057i. Hepzibah Perley (Died young) (14 Apr 1678-2 Mar 1694) 805
2 CONC 8ii. Sarah Perley (ca 1684-17 Jun 1769) 7964. Capt. John Peabody. Born ca 1642 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire. John died in Boxford, MA on 5 Jul 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT John first married Hannah Andrews, second (Sarah Trescott) Moseley, widow of Increase Moseley.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was one of the first settlers of Boxford, MA, where he was the first school master. He served as town clerk for 24 years, was selectman for many years and captain of the militia. He was made a freeman in 1674, and was a repre
2 CONC sentative to the General Court 1689, 1691. On 23 Nov 1665 John first married Hannah Andrews (5932) , daughter of Robert Andrews (2426) (ca Nov 1609-29 May 1668) & Grace (-25 Dec 1701), in Topsfield, MA.205,206 Born ca 1642 in Boxf
2 CONC ord, MA. Hannah died in Boxford, MA on 25 Dec 1700. Their children include: 15810i. John Peabody (Died unmarried) (29 Aug 1666-4 Mar 1693/4) 15811ii. Hannah Peabody (13 May 1668-19 Jan 1764) 15812iii. Thomas Peabody (Died unmarrie
2 CONC d) (22 Jul 1670-30 Nov 1700) 15813iv. Mary Peabody (4 Apr 1672-13 Dec 1731) 15814v. Lydia Peabody (10 Mar 1673/4-ca 1708/9) 15815vi. Francis Peabody (11 Mar 1676-Dec 1704) 15816vii. David Peabody (12 Jul 1678-4 Sep 1726) 15817viii
2 CONC . Elizabeth Peabody (13 Aug 1680-Mar 1740/1) 15818ix. Dea. Nathan Peabody (21 Jul 1682-4 Mar 1733) 15819x. Ruth Peabody (13 Nov 1684-29 May 1759) 15820xi. Moses Peabody (Died young) (27 Feb 1686/7-21 Mar 1703) On 26 Nov 1703 John 
2 CONC second married Sarah Trescott, daughter of William Trescott (ca Jan 1614/5-11 Sep 1699) & Elizabeth Dyer (say 1626-31 Jul 1699), in Dorchester, MA. Born on 13 Sep 1662 in Dorchester, MA. Sarah was baptized on 21 Sep 1662. Sarah di
2 CONC ed in Norwich, CT 7 Jan 1724/5.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah first married Increase Moseley, second John Peabody as his second wife. 7965. Joseph Peabody. Born ca 1644 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire. Joseph died ca 1722. Occupation: wheelwright.
2 CONT
2 CONT John became a freeman in 1677, and resided at Boxford. His will was dated 20 Mar 1721, proved 3 Apr 1722. On 26 Oct 1668 Joseph first married Bethiah Bridges, daughter of Edmund Bridges (ca 1612-13 Jan 1683/4) & Elizabeth Manwarin
2 CONC g (-31 Dec 1664), in Topsfield, MA. Born ca 1645 in Rowley, MA. Their children include: 21410i. Joseph Peabody (16 Apr 1671-1714) 21411ii. Jonathan Peabody (ca 1673-12 Aug 1746) 21412iii. Sarah Peabody (4 Sep 1676-) 21413iv. Samue
2 CONC l Peabody (8 Apr 1678-1 May 1706) 21414v. Bethia Peabody (3 Apr 1681-6 Feb 1741/2) 21415vi. Alice Peabody (4 Jan 1685-29 Jul 1726) 21416vii. Lydia Peabody (4 Feb 1683-9 Mar 1765) 4 Jan 1714/5 Joseph second married Mary Wheeler, da
2 CONC ughter of John Wheeler & Mary, in Beverly, MA. Born in Mar 1685 in Beverly, MA. Mary died aft 1721. 7966. William Peabody. Born on 3 Mar 1646 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire. William died in Boxford, MA 6 Mar 1699/170
2 CONC 0.
2 CONT
2 CONT William first married Mary Brown, second Hannah Hale.
2 CONT
2 CONT William resided at Boxford. In 1676, during King Philip's War, he served as a soldier in Capt. Joseph Gardner's company from Salem. It may or may not have been during this service that he lost the arm referred to in his father's w
2 CONC ill. For his military service, he received a grant of land in the township called “Narragansett, Number 3,” later incorporated as Amherst, N.H. The portion in which his grant was situated later became Milford, N.H., where his son 
2 CONC Stephen and a line of descendants lived for many years. William, who was made a freeman July 21, 1685, was a selectman of Boxford for several years. On 8 Dec 1680 when William was 34, he first married Mary Brown, daughter of Richa
2 CONC rd Brown (-26 Apr 1661) & Elizabeth Greenleaf (-10 Oct 1668). On 14 Aug 1684 when William was 38, he second married Hannah Hale (11279) , daughter of Thomas Hale (ca 1633-22 Oct 1688) & Mary Hutchinson (3806) (ca 1630-8 Dec 1715),
2 CONC  in Boxford, MA.206 Born on 19 Nov 1663 in Newbury, MA.136 Hannah died in Boxford, MA 23 Feb 1732/3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah was of Newbury when she married William.206 Their children include: 21417i. Stephen Peabody (4 Aug 1685-7 Jun 1759) 21418ii. Mary Peabody (4 Apr 1687-24 Jun 1761) 21419iii. Ephraim Peabody (23 Apr 1689-16 Jun 1740) 21420iv.
2 CONC  Richard Peabody (17 Feb 1691-Jan 1769) 21421v. Hannah Peabody (ca 1693-1 Jun 1769) 21422vi. John Peabody (1 Aug 1695-29 Jul 1780) 21423vii. Oliver Peabody (17 May 1698-2 Feb 1752) 21424viii. Abial Peabody (ca 1700-23 May 1791) 79
2 CONC 67. Isaac Peabody. Born ca 1648 in Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire. Isaac died in Topsfield, MA on 21 Oct 1727. Occupation: miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac lived in Topsfield, MA. His father, out of consideration for Isaac’s loss of one of his legs, left to him the principal house and mill. Isaac's wooden leg, after his death, apparently became something of a family relic. In a
2 CONC  letter dated Nov. 22, 1852, and published in the Danvers Centennial Celebration 1852, C. M. Endicott wrote of Francis Peabody's halberd, added: “A wooden leg said to have belonged to the first Isaac was also handed down in the fa
2 CONC mily of Matthew with this halberd, until the generation preceding Joel [1800 1861], when by some means the leg was lost.” Isaac first married Sarah Estey, daughter of Isaac Estey (1627-11 Jun 1712) & Mary Towne (ca 1634-22 Sep 169
2 CONC 2). Born on 30 Jun 1660 in Topsfield, MA. Sarah died aft 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah first married Moses Gill, second Isacc Peabody. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isaac and Sarah (Estey) (Gill) Peabody, born at Topsfield:
2 CONT     i. Francis, b. 1 Dec 1694, m. 27 Jan 1714/5 Dorothy Perkins (d. 3 May 1771 at Middletown, MA);
2 CONT     ii. Mary, bp. 5 Feb 1695/6, m. at Boston 1 Aug 1723 William Jarvis of Boston;
2 CONT     iii. Isaac, b. 15 Mar 1697/8, d. 13 Jan 1739 unmarried;
2 CONT     iv. Philadelphia, b. 28 Sep 1698, d. 23 Oct 1743, m. 27 Feb 1722 Daniel Redington (b. 27 Sep 1687 at Topsfield, d. there 29 Jun 1750, son of Daniel & Elizabeth (Davison) Redington, he m. 2nd at Andover 3 Jul 1746 Mrs Elizabeth
2 CONC  Stevens)
2 CONT     v. Matthew, b. 10 Dec 1699, d. 20 Oct 1777 at Topsfield, m. 12 Apr 1726 Mehitable Averill (d. 6 Jun 1740);
2 CONT     vi. William, b. 26 Jaqn 1701, d. young;
2 CONT     vii. Estes, b. 28 Sep 1702, d. 31 Dec 1770, m. 19 May 1746 Mary Gott (d. 15 Feb 1772), resided at Killingly, CT;
2 CONT     viii. Joseph, b. 14 Jun 1704, d. 7 Jun 1755 at Topsfield, m. 1 Nov 1729 Elizabeth Bradstreet (b. 28 Aug 1712, d. 31 Dec 1751 at Topsfield, dau. of Simon & Elizabeth (Capen) Bradstreet);
2 CONT     ix. Sarah, b. 10 Mar 1705/6, m. Luke Averill of Topsfield (b. 2 Aug 1699 at Topsfield, d. 16 Apr 1776, son of Ebenezer & Susanna (Hovey) Averill)
2 CONT     x. Anne, b. 31 May 1707, d. 5 May1760, m. at Ipswich 13 Dec 1727 John Batchelder (b. 8 Jan 1696/7 at Wenham, d. 2 Feb 1771, son of Joseph & Sarah Batchelder, he m. 2nd 23 Aug 1763 widow Hannah (Borman) Perkins);
2 CONT     xi. Hephzibah, b. 25 May 1709, d. 23 Dec 1783 at Topsfield, m. 31 Jan 1731 Ephraim Wildes Jr (bp. 3 Sep 1692/3 at Topsfield, d. there 13 Apr 1767, son of Ephraim &Mary (Howlett) Wildes of Topsfield); and 
2 CONT     xii. Samuel, b. 3 Jan 1711, d. 23 Jan 1711 at Topsfield. Their children include: 21425i. Francis Peabody (1 Dec 1694-23 Apr 1769) 21426ii. Mary Peabody (5 Feb 1695/6-) 21427iii. Isaac Peabody (15 Mar 1697-13 Jan 1739) 21428iv.
2 CONC  Philadelphia Peabody (28 Sep 1698-) 21429v. Matthew Peabody (10 Dec 1699-20 Oct 1777) 21430vi. William Peabody (26 Jan 1701-bef 1726) 21431vii. Estes Peabody (28 Sep 1702-31 Dec 1770) 21432viii. Joseph Peabody (14 Jun 1704-7 Jun 
2 CONC 1755) 21433ix. Sarah Peabody (10 Mar 1706-) 21434x. Anne Peabody (31 May 1707-bef 1763) 21435xi. Hephzibah Peabody (25 May 1709-) 21436xii. Samuel Peabody (Died soon) (3 Jan 1711-23 Jan 1711) Isaac second married Elizabeth.
2 CONT
