2 CONT Joseph Peabody (1644 - 1721)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Peabody
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1644 in Hampton, Essex County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Francis (Pabodie) Peabody and Lydia (Perkins) Peabody Brother of Lydia (Peabody) Perley, John Peabody, William Peabody, Isaac Peabody, Sarah (Peabody) Howe [half], Hepzibah (Peabody) Ray [half], Mary (Peabody) Eames [half],
2 CONC  Ruth Peabody [half], Damaris Peabody [half], Samuel Peabody [half], Jacob Peabody I [half], Hannah Peabody [half] and Nathaniel Peabody [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Bethia (Bridges) Peabody — married 26 Oct 1668 in Boxford, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Joseph Peabody, Jonathan Peabody, Samuel Peabody, Lydia (Peabody) Bixby and Alice (Peabody) Holt
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1721 in Boxford, Essex County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT 23:27: S (Hill) Willson edited the Biography for Joseph Peabody (1644-1721). (outdent heading) [Thank S for this]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married Bethiah Bridges in 1668 and married second Mary Wheeler in Jan 4, 1714-1715.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph's known children were:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b Apr 16, 1671 Jonathan, b 1673 Sarah, b Sept 4, 1676; m first Benjamin Smith Oct 22, 1700; m second James Johnson Samuel, b Apr 8, 1678 Bethia, b Apr 3, 1681; m Robert Holt Dec 13, 1727; d Feb 6, 1742 Lydia, b Feb 4, 1683
2 CONC ; m Jan 4 1705 or 1708, Joseph Bixby Alice, b Jan 4, 1685; m Thomas Holt Dec 14, 1708; d July 29, 1726 Joseph made his will March 20, 1720-1. In it he named his wife Mary, son Jonathan, daughters Sarah Johnson, Bethia Peabody, Lyd
2 CONC ia Bixby, and Alice Holt, and grandson Moses Peabody, son of son Samuel.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Peabody, Selim Hobart Peabody (Paybody. Pabody, Pabodie) genealogy, published 1909. Reference page 19 ↑ Essex County, MA: Probate File Papers, 1638-1881. Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genea
2 CONC logical Society, 2014. (From records supplied by the Massachusetts Supreme Judicial Court Archives.) Reference Essex Case 20856. Subscription Pope, Charles Henry. The Pioneers of Massachusetts, A Descriptive List, Drawn from Recor
2 CONC ds of the Colonies, Towns and Churches, and other Contemporaneous Documents, Boston, Massachusetts: by the Author, 1900. See also:
2 CONT
