2 CONT no image Privacy Level: Open (White) Sarah (Pabodie) Coe (1656 - 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Coe formerly Pabodie Born 7 Aug 1656 in Duxbury, Plymouthmap ANCESTORS ancestors Daughter of William Pabodie Sr and Elizabeth (Alden) Pabodie Sister of John Pabodie, Elizabeth (Pabodie) Rogers, Mary (Pabodie) Southworth, Mer
2 CONC cy (Pabodie) Simmons, Martha (Pabodie) Fobes, Priscilla Pabodie, Priscilla (Pabodie) Wiswall, Ruth (Pabodie) Bartlett, Rebecca (Pabodie) Southworth, Hannah (Pabodie) Churchill, William Pabodie Jr and Lydia (Pabodie) Grinnell Wife 
2 CONC of John Coe — married 10 Nov 1681 in Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap [uncertain] DESCENDANTS descendants Mother of Lydia (Coe) Bailey, Sarah (Coe) Tompkins, Samuel Coe, Elizabeth (Coe) Burgess, Hannah Coe, John Coe and Joseph 
2 CONC Coe Died 27 Aug 1740 in Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Islandmap Profile managers: Mayflower Project WikiTree private message [send private message] and David Winslow private message [send private message] Profile last modified 14
2 CONC  Oct 2020 | Created 10 Jan 2009 This page has been accessed 2,502 times. The Mayflower. Sarah (Pabodie) Coe was related to a passenger on the Mayflower. Join: Mayflower Project Discuss: MAYFLOWER Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Pabodie was born 7 Aug 1656 at Duxbury, Plymouth. She was the daughter of Elizabeth Alden and William Pabodie.[1] Sarah married John Coe[1] at Duxbury on 10 Nov 1681. He was the son of Matthew and Elizabeth (Whately) Coe of 
2 CONC Portsmouth, N.H. Sarah and John Coe had seven children. Sarah died 27 Aug 1740 at Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Island. John died at the same place 16 Dec 1728, age 79.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Tradition says, Sarah accompanied her father on a trip to Little Compton, probably to make a home for him, and John Coe, a surveyor, came down the river in a boat, landed on the shore near the present location, and helped William
2 CONC  Pabodie lay out the lots, and the next year married Sarah."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Wilbour, Benjamin Franklin. Little Compton Families, Vol. I. Little Compton, Rhode Island. Little Compton Historical Society. 1967. pp. 435-40 Pabodie ↑ Alden.org: Descendants of John Alden - Sarah Pabodie: accessed 27 J
2 CONC an 2018. ↑ Excerpt From: Alden, Mary Langford Taylor. “Elizabeth (Alden) Pabodie and descendants.” Salem, Mass. : E. Putnam, 1897. iBooks. This material may be protected by copyright. Woodworth-Barnes, Esther Littleford and Willia
2 CONC ms, Alicia Crane, Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol 16 Part 1 of 3, John Alden, Boston, Mass.: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2002. Vital Record of Duxbury, Massachusetts - Year 1911.[Page 21]: Sarah pabo
2 CONC die the daughter of william pabodie & Elizabeth his wife was borne august . 7 . 1656. Vital Record of Duxbury, Massachusetts - Year 1911. PABODIE - Plymouth County - Page 114. birth of Sarah, daughter of William & Elizabeth [dup. 
2 CONC Elisabeth], 07 August 1656. World Family Tree Vol. 1, Ed. 1, pre-1600 to present, Brøderbund Software, Inc., 1997, Media: Family Archive CD.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 529
