1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Rouse was born circa 1615 in England and died Dec. 16, 1684, Marshfield, Plymouth County, Massachusetts.  He was a servant who came to Plymouth Colony in 1634 & settled in Marshfield. (When the bounds of the t
2 CONC own of Marshfield were drawn on 7 June 1642, care was taken to include "the lands of John Rowse.") 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married by 1640 Annis Paybody, daughter of JOHN PAYBODY {1637, Duxbury} (in his will of 16 July 1649, "John Paybody of Duxburrow" included bequests to "Annis Rouse my daughter" and to "John Rouse the son of John Rouse."
2 CONT
2 CONT Pope stated that this immigrant "had license to marry 7 January 1638-9." On 7 January 1638/9, Plymouth Colony court records tell us that "John Rowe is allowed to marry, and to have a garden place by Scittuate Path, about Goodman G
2 CONC odfraye's." Only two other records have been found in Plymouth Colony for John Rowe, both of which are associated with the town of Duxbury. 
2 CONT
