2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Rouse was born on 16 Jun 1645 in Rehoboth, Bristol, Massachusetts, son of John Rouse Sr. (~1614 - 1684) and Annis (Pabodie) Rouse (~1618 - 1688). [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon married Christianna Gauntlet (1648 - 1724) in 1667 in Massachusetts. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Rouse (1673 - 1770)
2 CONT James Rouse (1678 - 1742)
2 CONT Mercy (Rouse) Stephens (1681 - )
2 CONT Barbara Rouse (1683 - 1700)
2 CONT Simon Rouse (1685 - 1702)
2 CONT Christianna Rouse (1687 - 1703)
2 CONT John Rouse (1690 - 1756).
2 CONT Simon a prominent man in the development of Little Compton, Massachusetts. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon was allowed by the Court to keep a house of entertainment for strangers and travellers. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon died before 11 November 1724 in Dartmouth, Bristol, aged 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Simon Rouse of Dartmouth was dated 19 December 1723 and proved on 17 November 1724 in Bristol. He mentioned his wife, Christian, and his children, William Rouse, John Rouse (executor), and Marcy Stevens. His inventory 
2 CONC was taken on 11 November 1724 in Dartmouth.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
