1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Thankful Rouse Bullock
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	unknown
2 CONT *'''Death: 	unknown
2 CONT *'''Her surname and parentage is not certain. It could be Rush, Rounds, Reneff, or other variants encountered in the records. The name is not very legible in the Rehoboth,MA records. A strong possibilty is that she was the daughte
2 CONC r''' of John Rouse and Annis Peabody/Pabodie Rouse.
2 CONT *'''Her birth is given as 1648 to 1652'''. A daughter Thankful of John and Annis (Peabody) Rouse is said to have been born in Rehoboth,MA on Oct 4,1652.
2 CONT *'''She was the second wife of Samuel Bullock.
2 CONT *'''Children''': Ebenezer Bullock, Thankful Bullock Martin, Samuel Bullock Jr, Israel Bullock, Daniel Bullock, Richard Bullock, and Seth Bullock.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT *''' Spouse:
2 CONT *'''  Samuel Bullock (1648 - 1718)*
2 CONT *''' Children:
2 CONT **  Thankful Bullock Martin (1681 - 1762)*
2 CONT **  Daniel Bullock (1688 - ____)*
2 CONT **  Seth Bullock (1693 - 1784)*
2 CONT *'''Burial:  Unknown
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 44445936
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=44445936 _______________________
2 CONT *'''BULLOCK, Samuel
2 CONT *b. 19 AUG 1648 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *d. 10 MAR 1716/7 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *Parents:
2 CONT *Father: BULLOCK, Richard
2 CONT *Mother: INGRAM, Elizabeth
2 CONT *Family:
2 CONT *Marriage: 12 NOV 1673 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *Spouse: THURBER, Mary
2 CONT *b. 1648 Stanton, Lincoln, England
2 CONT *d. 4 OCT 1674 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *Parents:
2 CONT *Father: THURBER, John
2 CONT *Mother: Priscilla,
2 CONT *Family:
2 CONT *'''Marriage: 26 MAY 1675 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *'''Spouse: ROUSE, Thankful
2 CONT *'''b. 27 JUN 1657 Marshfield, Plymouth, Mass.
2 CONT *'''d. 22 JUL 1762 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT *'''Parents:
2 CONT *Father: ROUSE, John
2 CONT *Mother: PEABODY, Annis
2 CONT *'''Children:
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Ebenezer
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Mary b. 5 OCT 1678 Rehoboth, Bristol, Mass.
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Thankful
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Samuel
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Israel
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Daniel
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Richard
2 CONT **BULLOCK, Seth
2 CONT *From: http://www.genealogyofnewengland.com/f_88.htm#32 __________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Thankful's last name is ROUSE. The "Reneff" spelling, found in some records, apparently occurred in the 19th century when a researcher, probably unfamiliar with the lax spelling practices and the penmanship of the 17th century, re
2 CONC ad the alternative spelling "Roues" as "Reneff". The letter "n" and "u" were written nearly identically and "s" was written like a long " f ". The name of her father - John Rouse, is a matter of record. Ginny Deagan reported that 
2 CONC in response to an inquiry, the Boston Evening Transcript Genealogical Column (entry #3496) says she was a cousin of Samuel Jones, a son of Richard and Olive Jones, from Somerset, England, who named her in his will as "Thankful Rou
2 CONC es". The Transcript is defunct, but its genealogical query and answer columns reside on the 6th floor of NEHGS. Although she is listed as Reneff in Arnold's Vital Records, she is Rouse in the Plymouth Colony Records.
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Thankful's surname is not written clearly in the Rehoboth marriage records. It has been read as Rouse, Rineff, Rose and Rounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Thankful Roues (Rouse) was called "cousin" by Samuel Jones, son of Richard and Alice Jones, in his will dated 28 May 1661. The word "cousin" then often meant a niece or nephew. Alice ([. . .]) Jones married (2) John Kingsley, of
2 CONC  Dorchester and Rehoboth, Massachusetts. Thankful Rouse might have lived with her uncle Samuel Jones, then after his death, come to Rehoboth with his widow and her second husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that she was a daughter of "John Rouse from Barbadoes of Scituate, Mass., slain in King Philip's War, March, 1676."
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that she was the Thankful Rouse, perhaps a granddaughter of Richard and Alice Jones, of Dinder, co. Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that she was a daughter of Faithfull and Suretrust (Starr) Rouse, of Charlestown, based on the nature of her given name. However, this theory is not supported by the work of H. S. Ballou on the Starr family.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has also been suggested that she was Thankful (Bowen) Rouse, but the compiler of ￼''Ancestral Lines Revised￼'' reports being unable to identify such a person.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has not been established that there was a Thankful Round. However, the connection between Samuel Bullock and John Round is consistent with the two men being brothers-in-law. John Round, said to have come from the Isle of Wight,
2 CONC  first appears in Rehoboth in 1689 on Major Bradford's quit claim deed. John Round, then of Swansea, made his will on 16 October 1710, and died 7 October 1716. The will named Job Winslow, Sr., Samuel Bullock, Sr., and John West as
2 CONC  overseers. The 1761 will of Richard Rounde, of Rehoboth, was witnessed by Stephen Bullock, Daniel Harding and Amos Bosworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________
