2 CONT ----
2 CONT Elizabeth Bourne (Rouse) is your 9th cousin 8 times removed.
2 CONT Janet Milburn 11/18/22
2 CONT memorial
2 CONT Elizabeth Martha Rouse Bourne
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 1590
2 CONT Tenterden, Ashford Borough, Kent, England
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 18 Jul 1660 (aged 69–70)
2 CONT New London, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Old Winslow Burying Ground
2 CONT Marshfield, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT 34321617 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Marshfield town records, Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Bourne, was buried on July 18, 1660, at the age of 70. From this record, it is estimated that she was probably born about 1590. It has been said that Elizabeth died w
2 CONC hile in New London, Connecticut. That is highly plausible, as two of her daughters married men from that area.
2 CONT
2 CONT While there is a cenotaph naming Thomas and Elizabeth Bourne at the Old Winslow Burying Ground, there is no evidence that either Bourne was buried there. At this early time, most settlers were buried on their own land, often in bu
2 CONC rying grounds not locatable now.
2 CONT
2 CONT The most recent and accurate research on Thomas and Elizabeth is available at:
2 CONT http://hdl.handle.net/2027/wu.89067589937?urlappend=%3Bseq=629
2 CONT Jacobus, Donald Lines, 1887-1970, and Edgar Francis Waterman. The Waterman Family. New Haven, Conn.: E.F. Waterman, 19391954.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bourne
2 CONT 1581–1664 (m. 1607)
2 CONT
