1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Sarah Harper (c. 1647–c. 1714/1720) was a colonial resident of the Northern Neck of Virginia. She is documented in primary colonial records primarily through her status as a landowner and widow. Legal records from Richmond County 
2 CONC provide the evidentiary basis for her life, confirming her marriage to Henry Berry and her subsequent role as his executrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Birth: c. 1647 (Location UNKNOWN; no primary record exists).
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: c. 1714–1720 (Location: Richmond County, Virginia; documented as "long before 1714" in legal references to her status as a widow).
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Location UNKNOWN (likely private family land).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage & Family===
2 CONT Father: William Harper (Documented in estate settlements).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Mary Elizabeth Gray (Documented in estate settlements).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse 1: Henry Berry (Documented in Richmond County Order Book, 1696).
2 CONT
2 CONT Documented Children:
2 CONT (Lineage generally accepted in regional genealogical studies, though specific dates remain estimates)
2 CONT 1. Henry Berry III: c. 1675–1725
2 CONT 2. William Berry: c. 1677–1720
2 CONT 3. James Berry: c. 1679–1749
2 CONT 4. Sarah Berry: c. 1681–1732
2 CONT 5. Rosanna "Rose" Berry: 1684–1752; m. Capt. Thomas Ashby Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse 2: John Spiller (Documented in Richmond County records as Sarah's subsequent husband).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT None documented
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Documented Legal Evidence===
2 CONT Richmond County Court Order Book (1696): Records the probate of the will of Henry Berry, identifying Sarah Berry as his widow and executrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate Settlement of William Harper (Richmond County): This is the primary factual document identifying Sarah as the "only sister and heir at law" of William Harper. It also identifies her as the "widow of Henry Berry, Jr." and co
2 CONC nfirms her subsequent marriage to John Spiller.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Historical Note on Documentation===
2 CONT Unlike biographical narratives that rely on estimated dates and inferred lineages, the profile of Sarah Harper is anchored by the Richmond County probate and estate records. These documents directly link her to her father (William
2 CONC  Harper), her brother (William Harper), her husband (Henry Berry), and her later status as a widow and heir.
2 CONT
