1 BURI
2 DATE 20 APR 1746
2 PLAC St Oswalds
2 ADDR
3 CITY Chester
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Francis Bassano of the City of Chester
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in his fathers will 1726
2 CONT
2 CONT Herald Painter made great collections of church notes some of which are in the College of Arms
2 CONT
2 CONT "Randle Holmes manuscripts collection business was taken over by Francis Bassano who was admitted freeman 12 September 1712 'gratis' as he had presented the city of Chester with three pictures then in the Pentice.  The DNB states 
2 CONC that Bassano was descended from a Venetian who had come to England in 1538 as a court musician to Henry VIII, and that the next two generations were also musicians, but that by the 18th Century the Bassano's were deputy heralds; '
2 CONC ''Francis senior, father''' to the Chester Bassano was Deputy Herald for Derbyshire, where he was succeeded by his brother Christopher'
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Our Francis was a friend of Charles Orme a painter in Chester , who became godfather of his son Edward and later accepted Edward as apprentice.  When Bassano died in 1747 he left his business and a large collection of church note
2 CONC s, pedigrees etc to Edward, who became Deputy Herald for Chester in 1761, though he is perhaps better known as the Cathedral organist from 1765 until his death in 1771."
2 CONT
2 CONT The written pages are 198, the first of which are these words : 'Mr Orme of Chester, Fr. Bassano' and then in the handwriting of George, Marquess of Buckingham 'Francis Bassano married ..... daughter of Randle Holmes of Chester, P
2 CONC ursuivant at Arms"
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliotheca ms. Stowensis: A descriptive catalogue of the manuscripts in the ...
2 CONT  By Charles O'Conor, John Stow, British Museum. Dept. of Manuscripts, British Museum
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The daughter of Randle Holme IV is said (apparently erroneously) to have married Francis Bassano, who secured many of the Randle Holme charters and rolls'''
