1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Dorothy Josselyn (Gates)''' born 1508 to parents, Sir Sir Geoffrey Gates and Elizabeth Gates in Loddington, Thorpe Malsor, Northamptonshire, England. She married Sir Thomas Josselyn of Hyde Hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Will and Testament of Dorothy Josselyn (Gates), Vestry Records of Church of Sabbesforde, Essex, England. Attached in documents and media for review. 
2 CONT
2 CONT STEPHEN GATES OF HINGHAM AND LANCASTER, MASSACHUSETTS AND HIS DESCENDANTS, A Preliminary Work Subject To Addition And Correction, compiled by Charles Otis Gates, New York, Willis McDonald & Co., Publishers, 1898 (presented to the 
2 CONC Colorado State Library by Mr. C. O. Gates, New York, NY, February 26, 1904)  (See vol. XIV, Harleian Society, p. 574.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Gates married Sir Thomas Josselyn, of Josselyn Hall.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Dorothy Gates1 
2 CONT *F, #226920
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 Mar 2007
2 CONT *''''''     Dorothy Gates is the daughter of Sir Geoffrey Gates.1 She married Sir Thomas Jocelyn.1
2 CONT *''''''      Her married name became Jocelyn.1
2 CONT *''''''Child of Dorothy Gates and Sir Thomas Jocelyn
2 CONT ** 1.Richard Jocelyn+1 d. 1604
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S1541] Beatrice Potter, "re: Lady Isabella Somerset," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 30 November 2005. Hereinafter cited as "re: Isabella Somerset."
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p22692.htm#i226920
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT **Stirnet 'Gates01'
2 CONT *		i. William Gates this genertation omitted by FMG
2 CONT *		m. Mabell Capdow (dau/heir of Thomas Capdow of High Easter by Agne, dau/heir of (Sir) Thomas Fleming of Essex) called Mirabell by Foster
2 CONT **			a. Sir Geffrey Gates 'of High Roding' of Essex
2 CONT **			m. Elizabeth Clopton (dau. of Sir William Clopton of Kentwell)
2 CONT ***				(1) Sir John Gates (dsp, Captain of the Guard)
2 CONT ***				m. Mary Denny (dau of Sir Edward (sb Edmund?) Denny)
2 CONT ***				(2) Geffrey Gates
2 CONT ***				Foster identifies Geffrey's wife as _ Pasthall of Essex and shows Elizabeth Walsingham (m2. Peter Wentworth) as 2nd wife of his brother Sir John. Berry, who does not mention Elizabeth Walsingham at all, shows Geffrey's wife
2 CONC  as _ Pascall of Essex. We are following Visitation (Gloucester) & FMG in showing Geffrey's wife as ...
2 CONT ***				m. Elizabeth Walsingham (dau of William Walsingham, sister of Secretary-of-State Sir Francis)
2 CONT ***				(3) Sir Henry Gates of Seymer or Seamer, Yorkshire (d 07.04.1589)
2 CONT ***				m1. Lucy Knevett (d 01.10.1577, dau. of Thomas Knevett of Buckenham Castle) .... issue etc. ....
2 CONT ***				m2. (sp) Catherine Vaughan (d 15.11.1594, dau. of Watkyn Vaughan of Bredwardyn, widow of James Boyle of Hereford, m3. Robert White of Aldershot)
2 CONT ***''''''				(4) Dorothy Gates mentioned by FMG & Berry
2 CONT ***''''''				m. Thomas Josselyn of Josselyn Hall
2 CONT ***				(5)+ other issue (dsp) - Alberic/Avery, William
2 CONT *Main source(s): Visitation (Gloucestershire, 1623, Gates) with some support/input as reported bove
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *Sir John GATES of Great Garnetts, Knight
2 CONT *Born: 1504, Great Garnetts, High Easter and Havering-atte-Bower, Essex, England
2 CONT *Died: 22 Aug 1553
2 CONT *Father: Geoffrey GATES (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth CLOPTON
2 CONT *Married: Mary DENNY ABT 1534, Cheshunt, Hetfordshire, England
2 CONT *John Gates of Great Garnetts, High Easter and Havering-atte-Bower, Essex; London, and Syon, Mdx.; first son of Sir Geoffrey Gates of High Roding (b. 1484 - d. 1526) and Elizabeth Clopton; brother of Henry. ....
2 CONT *John Gates's 'father was a man of standing in Essex, an associate of the 13th Earl of Oxford and a regular attendant at court and upon the King until his death. He may have died too early to secure his son a place in the royal ho
2 CONC usehold', and it was probably to the King's favourite Anthony Denny, whose sister he married, that Gates owed his early advancement. ....
2 CONT *''''''His sister Dorothy (b. 1512 - d. BEF 11 Feb 1582) had married in 1524 Thomas Josselyn of Hide Hall, Hertfordshire (b. 1506 - d. 24 Oct 1562). Dorothy Josselyn was at court in the household of Queen Catherine Howard in 1540-
2 CONC 2 and surviving correspondence with her brother, Sir John Gates, indicates that the Queen was not that easy to get along with. “I fear I shall scant content her Grace”, Dorothy wrote on one occasion. Dorothy was probably "a suppli
2 CONC er of dresses” to Queen Catherine Parr. Dorothy regularly wrote letters asking for favors from Sir John. In 1542, she needed his help when her husband was implicated in a case of forgery. She made her will in 1579 but lived for se
2 CONC veral more years.
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Bios/JohnGates.htm •________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Gates of Hingham and Lancaster, Massachusetts, and his descendents : a preliminary work subject to addition and correction http://www.archive.org/stream/stephengatesofhi00gate#page/n18/mode/1up GATES OF ESSEX, ENGLAND. (Se
2 CONC e Vol. XIV. Harleian Society, Page 574). http://www.archive.org/stream/stephengatesofhi00gate#page/n20/mode/1up f. WILLIAM GATES (Sir Geoffrey c, William b, Thomas a) of Essex, England m. Mabel, daugher and heiress of Thomas Capdo
2 CONC w of Higheaster, Essex, and his wife Ann, daughter and heiress of Thomas Fleming of Essex, England. g. SIR GEOFFREY GATES (William f, Sir Geoffrey c, William b, Thomas a), m. Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Clapton, Knight, of 
2 CONC Kentwell, Sussex, England. Children of Sir Geoffrey Gates g. Sixth generation i. Sir John. m. Mary, daughter of Sir Edward Denny. Sir John Gates was Gentleman of the Bedchamber to Henry VIII, and was remembered in the Will of the 
2 CONC King (See Strypes' Annals). He became Master of the Horse to King Edward VI, Chancellor of the Duchy of Lancaster, and of the Privy Council. He lost his head (dying sine prole) for High Treason in the matter of Lady Jane Grey. htt
2 CONC p://www.archive.org/stream/stephengatesofhi00gate#page/n22/mode/1up j. Geoffrey. m. ? Pascall of Essex, England k. Henry. He was of Somer, County York, England and from him the Gates of Yorkshire are derived. l. William. He left n
2 CONC o children '	m. Dorothy. m. Sir Thomas Josselyn, of Josselyn Hall. j. GEOFFREY GATES (Sir Geoffrey g, William f, Sir Geoffrey c, William b, Thomas a), of HIgheaster, Essex, England. m. Pascall of Essex, England. http://www.archive
2 CONC .org/stream/stephengatesofhi00gate#page/n26/mode/1up GATES IN AMERICA. _________________ 'The Journal of American history, Volume 6 By Mabel Thacher Rosemary Washburn, National Historical Society http://books.google.com/books?id=N
2 CONC mgKAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA527&lpg=PA527&dq=Maude+Sutton+1312&source=bl&ots=7j4IO6jmht&sig=K1mwcggloWGyK7_5FHnIBk7E_HI&hl=en&ei=sWbmTtWKOaavsQLjx9D5BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CDsQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Maude%20Sutton%201312&
