1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.archive.org/stream/wentworthgeneal02wentgoog#page/n78/mode/1up '''The Wentworth genealogy: English and American (1878) Vol. 1]
2 CONT *(15) '''Henry Wentworth, of Codham Hall, in Wethersfield, co. Essex''', 
2 CONT ** '''married, first, Elizabeth''', daughter and sole heir of Henry Howard, second son of Sir John Howard; and, 
2 CONT ** '''secondly, Jane,''' daughter and heir of Henry Fitz Simon. 
2 CONT *** She survived her husband and 
2 CONT *** remarried Sir Richard Fitz Lewes, Kt., of West Horndon, do. Essex, whose Will she proved 24 November 1529. 
2 CONT *** '''By his second wife Henry Wentworth had issue only one son, Nicholas'''
2 CONT **** ancestor of the Wentworths of counties Oxford, Bucks, Northampton, Warwick, and Lincoln, of whom hereafter. 
2 CONT ** The said '''Henry Wentworth died 22 March 1482-3''', having had issue by his first wife as follows: --
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/wentworthgeneal02wentgoog#page/n79/mode/1up Before proceeding with the main line, we give the '''descendants of the son by the second wife''', just mentioned, viz.--
2 CONT * (16) '''Nicholas Wentworth, who 
2 CONT ** became Sir Nicholas, being knighted by King Henry VIII in person during his expedition to Boulogne, in August 1544'''. 
2 CONT ** For many years he was "Chief Porter of Calais," then an important government post.
2 CONT ** He possessed numerous estates in the counties of Oxford, Bucks, Northampton, Warwick, and Lincoln, but
2 CONT ** his chief residence was at Lillingstone Lovell, co. Oxford, which manor was given to him by the king in 1546, in exchange for certain lands in Northamptonshire. 
2 CONT ** His '''Will, dated 7 February 1551-2, was proved 24 June 1557''', and he probably died not long before the latter date. 
2 CONT ** He '''married, before 1525, Jane''', 
2 CONT *** '''daughter of''' John Josselyn, Esq., of Newhall-Josselyn, co. Essex, and of Sabridgeworth, co. Herts, and sister of Sir Thomas Josselyn, Kt. 
2 CONT *** She survived him, and was buried at Burnham, co. Bucks, 26 August 1659. 
2 CONT ** '''Their issue were are follows:''' --
2 CONT *** 1. '''Peter''', of whom hereafter.
2 CONT *** 2. '''Henry''', who became a counsellor at law in London, and died in St. Sepulchre's parish 1 January 1613-14. By a first wife, whose name has not been ascertained, he had one daughter, Cicely, who married Francis Michell, of
2 CONC  Theydon Garnon, co. Essex, and had issue. Henry Wentworth married, secondly, Anastacy, daughter and heir of William Hale, Esq., of Maldon, co. Essex. She survived her husband, dying 4 June 1634, without issue and was buried at Ma
2 CONC ldon aforesaid.
2 CONT *** 3. '''Paul''', who was of Burnham, co. Bucks. He was chosen M. P. 1571, and was leader of the opposition party in the time of Queen Elizabeth. Hallam calls him "the most undaunted asserter of civil liberty in this reign." He a
2 CONC nd his brother Peter were repeatedly sent to the Tower. He died 13 January 1593-4, in his 60th year, and was buried at Burnham. He married there, 26 November 1653, Helen, daughter of Richard Agmondesham, Esq., of Heston, co. Middl
2 CONC esex, and widow of William Tyllesley, Esq., of Burnham aforesaid. Her Will, dated 24 August, was proved 8 November 1615. They had issue:  Francis, Paul, Peter, William, Anne, Helen, Elizabeth, & Mary. (More info about each child @
2 CONC  http://www.archive.org/stream/wentworthgeneal02wentgoog#page/n80/mode/1up, pg 29) 
2 CONT *** 4. '''Francis''', whom his father in his Will directed should become a priest. There is no evidence that he did so; and he was buried at Burnham 4 September 1564.
2 CONT *** 5. '''Clare''', only daughter, who married, before her father's death, Edward Boys, Esq., of Fredville, in Nonington, co. Kent, sheriff of that county in 1577. She died before 1586, and he remarried twice, dying 15 February 15
2 CONC 98-9, aged 71.
2 CONT  ______________
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.archive.org/stream/wentworthgenealo01inwent#page/n115/mode/2up '''The Wentworth genealogy, comprising the origin of the name, the family in England, and a particular account of Elder William Wentworth, the emigrant, an
2 CONC d of his descendants (1870)]
2 CONT
2 CONT *CHART - Henry Wentworth, of Codham Hall, Co. Essex; son of Sir Roger, as in Table G. = Jane Fitz Lewes; had only son, '''Nicholas'''
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/wentworthgenealo01inwent#page/n117/mode/2up
2 CONT *CHART - '''Sir Nicholas Wentworth, of Lillingston Lovel, Co. Oxford Will proved 1557 = Jane, daughter of John Josselyne.
2 CONT *children: Peter, Three sons and one daughter.
2 CONT *<nowiki>------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *'''Nicholas WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)'''
2 CONT * '''Born:''' 1482 / ABT 1500, Lillingstone Lovell, Oxfordshire, England
2 CONT * '''Died:''' ABT 1553 / 24 Jun 1557
2 CONT * '''Notes:'''
2 CONT **  Held the office of chief porter of Calais. He is variously styled chief porter, master porter, or knight porter. He was knighted by Henry VIII at the siege of Boulogne, 1544, and died in 1557. He married the sister of Sir Thom
2 CONC as Josselyn, K.B., and lived at Lillingstone Lovell, then a detached bit of Oxfordshire surrounded by Buckinghamshire. Lady Wentworth survived to live with her younger son, Paul Wentworth, at Burnham Abbey, and was burled in Burnh
2 CONC am church. 
2 CONT * '''Father:''' Henry WENTWORTH of Codham (Esq.)
2 CONT * '''Mother:''' Joan FITZSIMON
2 CONT * '''Married:''' Jane JOSSELYN (b. ABT 1482) (dau. of John Josselyn of Hyde Hall) 1525, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT * '''Children:'''
2 CONT **1. Peter WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **2. Henry WENTWORTH
2 CONT **3. Joan WENTWORTH
2 CONT **4. Paul WENTWORTH
2 CONT **5. Francis WENTWORTH
2 CONT **6. Clara WENTWORTH
2 CONT *'''From:''' http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/WENTWORTH.htm#Nicholas WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)1 __________
