1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Joan WENTWORTH
2 CONT *'''Born: 1529, High Estre, Essex, England
2 CONT *Father: Nicholas WENTWORTH (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Mother: Jane JOSSELYN
2 CONT *'''Married: Geoffrey GATES ABT 1558, High Easter, Essex, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter GATES
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/WENTWORTH.htm#Joan WENTWORTH1 ____________________
2 CONT *'''Stephen Gates of Hingham and Lancaster, Massachusetts, and his descendents : a preliminary work subject to addition and correction
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/stephengatesofhi00gate
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/stephengatesofhi00gate#page/n22/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 7
2 CONT *'''Geoffrey Gates was the son of _ Pascall & Geoffrey Gates of Higheaster, Essex, England, he  married Joan Wentworth.  Their children are:
2 CONT *Peter, m. Mary Josselyn; he was of London, England. _____________________
2 CONT *'''The visitations of Essex by Hawley, 1552; Hervey, 1558; Cooke, 1570; Raven, 1612; and Owen and Lilly, 1634 : to which are added miscellaneous Essex pedigrees from various Harleian manuscripts, and an appendix containing Berry'
2 CONC s Essex pedigrees v.14
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/visitationsofess14metc
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/visitationsofess14metc#page/574/mode/1up
2 CONT *          Gates.
2 CONT *Tho. Gates Esq. temp. E. 3. = ; ch: William Gates.
2 CONT *William Gates. = ; ch: Sr Geffrey (m. Agnes Baldington), Raffe, Christopher Gates.
2 CONT *Sr Geffrey Gates of Essex knight. = Agnes d. & heir of Sir Tho. Baldington of Alderbury in com. Oxon.; ch: William (m. Mabell Capdow) Gates.
2 CONT *William Gates son & heir. = Mabel d. & heir of Tho. Capdow.; ch: Sir Geffrey (m. Elizabeth Clopton), Ann (m. Thomas Darcy) Gates.
2 CONT *Sir Geffrey Gates of . . . . in com. Essex knight. = Elizabeth d. of Sr William Clopton of Kentwell in Suff.; ch: Sir John (m. Mary Denny), Geffrey (m. . . . .  Pascall), Sir Henry, William (ob. s.p.) Dorathey (m. Tho. Josselyn) 
2 CONC Gates.
2 CONT *Sir John Gates kt Captain of the Guard to E. 6 Chancellor of the Duchy & one of the Privy Council ob. s.p.; = Mary d of Sr Edward Denny.; ch: Geffrey (m. . . . . Pascall) Gates.
2 CONT *Geffrey Gates. = . . . . d. of . . . .  Pascall of Essex.; ch: '''Geffrey (m. Joane Wentworth)''', Henry, John Gates.
2 CONT **'''Geffrey Gates. = Joane d. of . . . .  Wentworth.; ch: Peter Gates. ______________________________________
2 CONT *'''Joan Wentworth Gates
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	1529  High Easter, Essex, England
2 CONT *Death: 	unknown
2 CONT *'''Married Geoffrey Gates in High Easter, England 
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Spouse:
2 CONT *'''  Geoffrey Gates (1530 - ____)*
2 CONT * Children:
2 CONT **  Peter Gates (1566 - 1610)*
2 CONT *Burial:   Unknown
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 48574177
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=48574177 ________________________________________
2 CONT *          Stirnet 'Gates01'
2 CONT *			a. Sir Geffrey Gates 'of High Roding' of Essex
2 CONT *			m. Elizabeth Clopton (dau. of Sir William Clopton of Kentwell)
2 CONT **				(2) Geffrey Gates
2 CONT **				Foster identifies Geffrey's wife as _ Pasthall of Essex and shows Elizabeth Walsingham (m2. Peter Wentworth) as 2nd wife of his brother Sir John. Berry, who does not mention Elizabeth Walsingham at all, shows Geffrey's wife 
2 CONC as _ Pascall of Essex. We are following Visitation (Gloucester) & FMG in showing Geffrey's wife as ...
2 CONT **				m. Elizabeth Walsingham (dau of William Walsingham, sister of Secretary-of-State Sir Francis)
2 CONT ***					(A) Geffrey Gates of Bury St. Edmunds (a 1623)
2 CONT ***					m. Elizabeth Pinchon (dau of John Pinchon of Writtell)
2 CONT ****'''						(i) Geffrey Gates (b c1593)
2 CONT ****'''						The following comes from Berry's Essex Pedigrees (1878, Gates).
2 CONT ****'''						m. Joane Wentworth
2 CONT ****						(ii)+ other issue (a 1623) - Henry, John, Peter, Paul, 2 sons, 1 daughter
2 CONT ***					(B) Anthony Gates
2 CONT ***					m. Judith Taverner (dau of Roger Taverner of Essex (surveyor of the woods))
2 CONT ***					(C) Joyce Gates
2 CONT ***					m. John Taverner (son of John of Upminster (surveyor general))
2 CONT *Main source(s): Visitation (Gloucestershire, 1623, Gates) with some support/input as reported above _______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate death year 1558.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name may be Joan Jean, or 1st name may be Joan or Jean.
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________
