2 CONT possibly knighted
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT Date of birth might be 1537.
2 CONT
2 CONT alleged twin of John (although Stirnet's "Kirton1" page does not mention John)
2 CONT
2 CONT Supposedly from an unidentified Wikipedia article: "The church (Thorpe Mandeville) houses an impressive monument to Thomas Kirton and his family. The Kirtons lived at the manor house from 1554 to 1685. It is recorded that the mano
2 CONC r was garrisoned by Oliver Cromwell. The current [https://www.geni.com/surnames/horton Horton] stone manor house dates from about the 1770s, replacing an old house which stood west of the church. The south front of the house is sa
2 CONC id to be in the strong style of Thomas [https://www.geni.com/surnames/archer Archer]."
2 CONT
