2 CONT '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LRRQ-RZ4
2 CONT Brief Life History of Truman'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Truman was born in 1712 as the son of William Moore (1677-1732) and Elizabeth S McBride (1679-1727)
2 CONT
2 CONT Truman Moore of Perquimans County, North Carolina, wrote his will on 12 December 1752 and named his wife, Leah, and his son, Samuel, as executors of the will.  Probably because Samuel was only about 15 years old, Leah and Samuel w
2 CONC ent to court to ask for assistance in the division of the estate.  The inventory was presented in court on 20 October 1753. The court itemized the inventory of Truman's estate that would go to his wife, Leah, in January 1754, and 
2 CONC to his children:
2 CONT (1) son William Moore
2 CONT (2) daughter Jane Moore
2 CONT (3) son Jesse Moore
2 CONT (4) son Thomas Moore
2 CONT (5) son Samuel Moore
2 CONT (6) daughter Mary Moore   
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 12/12/1752
