1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LCZQ-QJ4
2 CONT Brief Life History of Thomas'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Thomas Winslow was born on 4 April 1679, in Perquimans, North Carolina, British Colonial America, his father, Timothy P. Winslow, was 25 and his mother, Sarah F. Good, was 22. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Clare on 2 November 1704. They were the parents of at least 11 sons and 4 daughters. 
2 CONT Joseph Winslow 1704–1750
2 CONT Christian Winslow 1706–
2 CONT Mary Christian Winslow 1707–1729
2 CONT Ely Winslow 1707–
2 CONT William Winslow 1708–
2 CONT Thomas Winslow II 1709–1747
2 CONT Timothy Winslow 1712–1752
2 CONT Jesse Winslow 1714–1714
2 CONT Millicent Winslow 1716–
2 CONT Jesse Winslow 1717–
2 CONT John Winslow 1717–1754
2 CONT Obed Winslow 1719–
2 CONT Elisabeth Winslow 1721–1750
2 CONT Joab Winslow 1724–1751
2 CONT Miriam Winslow 1728–1747
2 CONT
2 CONT After Elizabeth's death, he married 2nd wife Leah Pritlow on 7/4/1734 in Perquimans, NC . 
2 CONT They had one daughter: Sarah Winslow 1735-?
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 26 September 1745, in his hometown, at the age of 66.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Thomas Winslow''' was born on August 1, 1682 in Pasquotank County, North Carolina. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-93895818 Timothy Winslow, of Perquimans District] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34802080407 S
2 CONC arah Winslow ({unknown})]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-115940415 Elizabeth Winslow (Clare), (twin)] on November 2, 1704 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-112301513 Joseph Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807298743 Marey &quot;Christian&quot; Bundy (Winslow)];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807298832 Thomas Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-33933778 Timothy Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807298870 Jesse Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-115940207 John Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807298952 Elizabeth Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807298987 Joab Winslow];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34807299084 Miriam Anderson (Winslow)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34631598666 Leah Winslow (Pritlowe)]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34802082915 Sarah Winslow]. She probably died young as she is not named in her father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on November 26, 1745 in Perquimans County, North Carolina, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Timothy Winslow: Second Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.heirsandroots.com/MyFamilies/Winslow.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Thomas WINSLOW (Timothy) was born[2] on 1 Aug 1682 in Pasquotank County, North Carolina. He died[3] on 26 Nov 1745 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. 
2 CONT Thomas married[4] 1st Elisabeth CLARE daughter of Timothy CLARE and Mary BUNDY on 2 Nov 1704 in Perquimans County. Elisabeth was born on 21 Feb 1685/6 in Perquimans. She died before Jun 1734 in Perquimans County. Elisabeth had a t
2 CONC win sister named Mary. Thomas was bond to his future father-in-law and proved his freedom from Timothy Clare in 1702. I believe at that time he would have received 50 acres of land as a sort of payment for his indenture. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas m. 2nd Leah Pritlowe, widow of John Smith 7 Jun 1734 (itm) Quaker Records and they had a daughter, Sarah Winslow b.25 July 1735.  On 5 Apr 1720 Thomas Winslowe received land patent for 400 acres on the N E Side of Perquimon
2 CONC s (sic) river, Joining Timothy Clare and the Desert. Wit: C. Eden, Thos. Pollock, Wm. Reed,
2 CONT
2 CONT Richd. Sanderson and Fras. Foster[5]. A deed executed on 10 Jan 1725, on record at the courthouse in Hertford, North Carolina, which conveyed land to Thomas White was signed by Thomas and Elizabeth with their marks, Thomas (T) Win
2 CONC slow and Elizabeth (E) Winslow. John Winslow, brother of Thomas, used the mark (J) for his name. They also lived near each other. Thomas left Negroes to his children in his will; he seems to have prospered.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the back cover of the bible are listed other names, which are probably slaves, they are: Rose b.12 Feb 1764, Venus b.23 Mar 1766, John Winslow, John Griffin Sept(illegible), Dick Winslow b.16 Mar (covered by repair of binding),
2 CONC  Jim b.25 Mar 1739, Dick b.16 Mar 174(torn), Peter b.13 Apr 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Elisabeth had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # 4 M    i.  Joseph WINSLOW was born on 31 Mar 1706 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. He died about 1750 in Perquimans Joseph married[6] 22 Aug 1729 Pleasant Tomes, the daughter of Francis Toms and Margaret Lawrence (widow Bog
2 CONC ue) at the house of Francis Tomes.
2 CONT # 5 F           ii.  Marey WINSLOW was born on 27 Jun 1707 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. She died before Nov 1745 in Perquimans. Marey (AKA Christian) married 2 6mo 1727 (itm) Samuel Bundy son of Caleb Bundy and Jean Maner
2 CONC s. Caleb was the son of William Bundy and Elizabeth Allen.
2 CONT # 6 M     iii.  Thomas WINSLOW was born on 30 Nov 1709 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. He died in 1747 in Perquimans. Thomas married Sarah Nixon Ratliff 21 Jan 1734/5, Perquimans. She was the daughter of Richard Ratliff and 
2 CONC Damaris Pearce/Perse/Peirc, and the widow of Joseph Peirce. Thomas' will dated 21 Jan 1746/7, proved Apr 1747, show he owned slaves. Sarah married 2nd Joseph Outland 6 Dec 1749.
2 CONT #  7 M      iv.  Timothy WINSLOW was born on 5 Jun 1712 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. He died in 1752 in Perquimans County. Timothy married[11] 9 Mar 1736, Rachel Wilson at the home of Mary Newby in Perquimans. She was the
2 CONC  daughter of Robert Wilson and Rachel Pricklowe. Timothy's will dated 26 Apr 1752, proved Jul 1752, Perquimans County shows he owned slaves.
2 CONT # 8 M       v.  Jesse WINSLOW was born on 12 Mar 1714 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. He died before Nov 1745 in Perquimans.
2 CONT # +          9 M      vi.  John WINSLOW was born on 9 Feb 1717/8. He died on 17 Apr 1754.
2 CONT # 10 F      vii.  Elizabeth WINSLOW was born on 6 Nov 1721 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. She died [12]on 12 Nov 1750 in Perquimans County.
2 CONT # 11 M   viii.  Joab WINSLOW was born on 14 Apr 1724 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. He died[13] on 28 Mar 1751 in Perquimans County. Joab/Job received land in Pasquotank County, North Carolina near Newbegun Creek which he l
2 CONC eft to Josiah the son of John Winslow and Mary Pearson when he died[14].
2 CONT # 12 F       ix.  Miriam WINSLOW was born on 29 Aug 1728 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. Miriam m. Joseph Anderson 1 Apr 1747, Perquimans[15].
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married[16] 2nd Leah PRITLOWE on 7 Jun 1734 in Perquimans County, North Carolina. Leah was born on 4 Jan 1695. She was the daughter of John Pritlowe and Elisabeth [-?-] and the widow of Joseph Smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Leah had the following children:
2 CONT # 13 F        x.  Sarah WINSLOW was born[17] on 25 Jul 1735 in North Carolina. Sarah probably died young, she is not mentioned in her father's will.
2 CONT ----
