1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Describe The Record (Notes)
2 CONT Will of Jacob Perry of Perquimmons County, NC, dated 4 Mar 1775.'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Son of Joseph Perry (1665-1725) and Anne (Lawrence) Perry
2 CONT
2 CONT Where The Record Is Found (Citation)
2 CONT Ancestry.com
2 CONT Describe The Record (Notes)
2 CONT Will of Jacob Perry of Perquimmons County, NC, dated 4 Mar 1775.Lists [2nd]wife- Ann Perry, 
2 CONT son- Jacob Perry, 
2 CONT son- Israel Perry, 
2 CONT son- Reuben Perry, 
2 CONT dau- Priscilah Welch, wife of Demsey Welch, 
2 CONT son- Demsey Perry, 
2 CONT son- John Perry, 
2 CONT dau- Hephzibah Stallings, wife of Hardy Stallings, 
2 CONT dau- Ann Winslow, wife of Caleb Winslow, 
2 CONT grandson- Isaac Willson, son of Isaac Willson [ & unknown daughter?].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/56822180/jacob_lawrence-perry'''
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 1) 12/25/1722 in Perquimans Co., NC to Hepsabeth Lawrence Clare
2 CONT m. 2) 12/05/1754 in Perquimans Co., NC to Anne Elizabeth Lilly
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Issue with Hepsabeth:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Elizabeth "Betsy" Perry (1723-1754)
2 CONT * 2. John Perry (1725-1789)
2 CONT * 3. Jacob Lawrence Perry (1726-1796)
2 CONT * 4. Israel Perry (1728-1779)
2 CONT * 5. Priscilla "Prissy" Perry (1730-1780)
2 CONT * 6. Reuben Perry (1733-1775)
2 CONT * 7. Dempsey Perry (1736-1813)
2 CONT * 8. Hepzibah "Eppie" Perry (1739-1812)
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue with Anne:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9. Anne Elizabeth Perry (1755-1796)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Info comes from the Suppliment to the Welch Journal and Sally's Family Place (sallysfamilyplace.com).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Perry's came to Virginia around 1670 from England. Some of them migrated south to Chowan & Perqumans Counties, NC before 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thos Perry family was from Perquimans County. The Perry's, Lawrence's & Cleare's (Clare) all lived very close to each other.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was a mechanic, which in those days was a carpenter. He was also listed as a wheelwright, which meant the repaired & worked on waggon & carriage wheels with wood & metal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived in the area of Perry's Bridge over the Perquimans River in present day Perquimans Co., NC (2010).
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Perry married 5 Dec 1754 Ann Lilley.
2 CONT Court petition bef. April 1755 court. Jacob Perry m. Ann dau of Thomas Lilly who lived in Piney Woods. Thereby putting Thomas Lilly's land, left to her in his will, in the hands of Jacob Perry by marriage to Ann.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''North Carolina Will book P page 254.
2 CONT Jacob Perry's Will, 4 March 1775 -- died 1777 [recorded 24 Nov 1779]'''
2 CONT In the name of God, amen, March 4, 1775, I, Jacob Perry, of Perquimans County in the province of North Carolina, being weak in body but of sound and perfect memory thanks be given to God for the cause and calling to mind the morta
2 CONC lity of my body and knowing that it is appointed for all men once to die, do make and ordain this to be my last will and testament. That is to say. . . First and principally of all I give and recommend my soul into the hands of Go
2 CONC d that gave it me and for my body I recommend to the earth to be buried in a Christian-like and decent manner, according to the directions of my executors hereafter named, nothing doubting but at the general resurrection I shall r
2 CONC eceive the same by the almighty power of God and as touching such worldly estate wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me within this life, I give, devise and dispose of the same in manner and from the following---that is to say 
2 CONC in the first place...
2 CONT -- I give and bequeath to my son Jacob Perry the land and plantation whereon he now lives in Perquimans County aforesaid to a line of marked trees mentioned in a deed of gift to my son Israel Perry which is supposed to contain abo
2 CONC ut 187 1/2 acres to the same more or less to him, his heirs or assigns forever also such part of my personal estate with which he is now possessed with to him and his disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my son Israel Perry all such part of my estate as he is now in actual possession of meaning among other things, 50 acres of land for which some years past acknowledged a deed of sale to him that through mistake h
2 CONC appened to be without date, to him and his disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my son Reuben Perry all such part of my estate as he is now in actual possession of to him and his disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my daughter, Priscilla Welch, wife of Dempsey Welch, all such part of my estate as she is now in actual possession of to her and her own disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my son Dempsey Perry all such part of my estate as he is now in actual possession of to him and his own disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my son John Perry, [a negro or horse] named Dick and also such part of my estate as he is now in actual possession of to him and his own disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my daughter Hephzibah Stallings, wife of Hardy Stallings, all such part of my estate as she is now in actual possession of to her and her own disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my daughter Ann Winslow, wife of Caleb Winslow, land and plantation and improvements whereon I now live, also one plantation and improvements which I bought of Zachariah Lilley, also one plantation which I bought
2 CONC  of my son Jacob, to her and her heirs forever, only my will is that the true intent and meaning of these presents also is that my well beloved Ann Perry shall have the use of the said lands during the time of her natural life wit
2 CONC hout molestation.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my grandson Isaac Wilson, son of Isaac Wilson, a parcel of land lying on the northwest side of a place called the Little Beaver Dam in Chowan County, containing by estimation 100 acres to him and his heirs and as
2 CONC signs forever.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my well-beloved wife Ann Perry one horse call[ed] Spring, one woman's saddle and bridle, one featherbed and furniture, also the use of the labor of my negro man named Tom and negro woman named Pat during the time
2 CONC  of her natural life or widowhood, also the use of my copper still for the same time.
2 CONT -- Then I give to my 8 children sig: Jacob, Israel, Reuben, Priscilla, Dempsey, John, Hephzibah, and Ann my copper still and negroes Tom & Pat to be equally divided among them after the expiration of the time above limited to them
2 CONC  and their disposal.
2 CONT -- Then I give all the rest of my estate to be equally divided between my wife Ann Perry, and my youngest daughter Ann Winslow, wife of Caleb Winslow, to them and their disposal.
2 CONT -- Then, lastly I do hereby nominate and appoint my well-beloved wife executress and Jacob Perry and Israel Perry and Caleb Winslow executors of this my last will and testament, hereby disannullin and disallowing all and any other
2 CONC  forms, wills and testaments, legacies, bequeaths, or executors before this time by me named, willed and bequeathed, ratifying and confirming this and no other to by my last will and testament.
2 CONT In witness thereof I have hereunto set my name, seal the day and year first above written.
2 CONT Recorded November 24, 1779."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the History of Perquimans County by Winslow,''' Jacob is the brother of Israel Perry [this is an error, I think, as Israel states in his will that his father was Jacob smk] and Phillip Perry and was the son of John
2 CONC  and Mary Perry. There are missing records in Perquimans County from 1712-1721. There is a J. Perry using 200a of Timothy's land mentioned in the will of Timothy Clare probated Nov. 10, 1724, it is unclear whether this is Jacob or
2 CONC  his father, John or uncle James. Jacob is listed on the 1735 quits rents list with 300acres. Also listed are Phillip Perry, Benjamin Perry, and Samuel Perry. The Sr. Jacob Perry's land is mentioned in the will of Daniel Rogerson,
2 CONC  Sr. February 13, 1762. A lawsuit over this land mentioned Jacob Perry, Jr., Benjamin Perry, Jr., Joseph Perry, and Phillip Perry among others swearing oath to have examined the land in question of 65A siezed in fee tail for David
2 CONC  Rogerson valued at 35£. The land was auctioned off and sold to Israel Perry for 65£. David Rogerson left Perquimans county for Martin Co. following this court action, he never signed the deed in question with his mark. He later p
2 CONC urchased land in the then Tyrel (now Martin Co.) Co. from Samuel Perry of Chowan Co. - -note in - "The Roos Family Tree" by Joy Roos on Ancestry.com
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritagefamily-trees?itemId=64202831-15-220&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-4bc037c3152c28d8a2e6190603bbf969&mrid=661cc58c83370eae0893085c5b8423e4 MyHerit
2 CONC age Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 23 2016, 23:06:42 UTC''
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/9061/images/007640069_01804?treeid=&personid=&rc=&usePUB=true&_phsrc=Nfb555&_phstart=successSource&pId=1099511623014
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Web Page (Link to the Record)
2 CONT http://familysearch.org
2 CONT Where The Record Is Found (Citation)'''
2 CONT FHL SLC    Perry line 1600 - 2000  by Charles Mc Grath   digital version online  at Family Search  Books
2 CONT Describe The Record (Notes)
2 CONT North Carolina Will Book P. page 254. Abstract lists Jacob, Israel,
2 CONT Reubin, Dempsey, John, Anne.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the History of Perquimans County by Winslow, Jacob is the
2 CONT brother of Israel Perry and Phillip Perry and was the son of John and
2 CONT Mary Perry.''' There are missing records in Perquimans County from
2 CONT 1712-1721. There is a J. Perry using 200a of Timothy's land mentioned
2 CONT in the will of Timothy Clare probated Nov. 10, 1724 , it is unclear
2 CONT whether this is Jacob or his father, John or uncle James. Jacob is
2 CONT listed on the 1735 quits rents list with 300acres. Also listed are
2 CONT Phillip Perry, Benjamin Perry, and Samuel Perry.
2 CONT It is believed the Jacob Perry joined the Quaker faith before marrying
2 CONT Hepsebeth Clare, though their marriage is not documented in any known
2 CONT Quaker records. There is no disownment in the records that we have
2 CONT either, nor is there any condemnation of their marriage. The marriages
2 CONT of their children are recorded as those of birth right Quakers.
2 CONT  The Sr. Jacob Perry's land is mentioned in the will of Daniel
2 CONT Rogerson, Sr. February 13, 1762. A lawsuit over this land mentioned
2 CONT Jacob Perry, Jr., Benjamin Perry, Jr., Joseph Perry, and Phillip Perry
2 CONT among others swearing oath to have examined the land in question of
2 CONT 65A siezed in fee tail for David Rogerson valued at 35£.  The land was
2 CONT auctioned off and sold to Israel Perry for 65£. David Rogerson left
2 CONT Perquimans county for Martin Co. following this court action, he never
2 CONT signed the deed in question with his mark. He later purchased land in
2 CONT the then Tyrel (now Martin Co.) Co.from Samuel Perry of Chowan Co.
