1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sometime prior to 11 July 1694, he assigned the headrights for importation into North Carolina of himself, (can't see that his wife was listed, so local)  Luke, and Ellinor Mizell to William Charlton who used them 
2 CONC for a Chowan Precinct survey ordered on that date.[16]  He figured in a court case on 28 July 1694 in Chowan Precinct as well.[17]  By 3 December 1696 he was dead, for William Brethit and his wife Bethinia, almost certainly Lawren
2 CONC ce Mizell’s widow, were granted administration of his estate as nearest kin.[18]  It appears that Luke and Ellinor were his children.  Two other Mizells, William and Mary, are surely children as well as both were headrights used f
2 CONC or a 1697 Thomas Clark survey of land adjoining William Charlton’s.<br/>
2 CONT [ Albemarle Book of Warrants and Surveys 1681-1706, p164.] <br/>
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT b: Aft. 1684 in Probably Surry Co VA       d: ABT 1756 in Tyrrell Co., N.C.    
