1 OCCU Captain in the Infantry of King and Queen County, Virginia. He was a planter and the owner of 'Porto Bello' plantation, York County, Virginia., In 1711, Queen Ann granted him land in King and Queen County "for diverse good causes 
2 CONC and considerations."
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Collier, John''' (1685 - 1735) - male b. 3 MAR 1684/85 in king & queen county va d. 24 MAR 1734/35 in Wyanoke, Charles City, Virginia father: Collier, Charles (1660 - 1735) mother: Eyers, Mary (1665 - 1701) Will - [date: 26 SEP
2 CONC  1749] [place: will was dated 1746...may explain why documented child Mary was not in will as well as why possible William of 1754 was not in will.]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Spouse #1: Ballard, Elizabeth (*1686 - ) - m. 31 DEC 1704 
2 CONT *spouse #2: Ironmonger, Frances Elizabeth (*1687 - ) - m. 3 FEB 1705/06 in king & queen county , VA 
2 CONT *Spouse # 3: Nancy Eppes m 6 Oct 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Caution
2 CONT
2 CONT >"FYI. Charles Collier Family Bible is faked. Almost all relationships are undocumented, e.g., esp. marriages. No documentation of most births. Ann Eppes married Wm. Kennon. No documentation that Eppes Collier even existed. Severa
2 CONC l Collier sources (e.g., Goode and Pickens Hardy) are inaccurate, based on unsubstantiated... information."
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Collier-1368
2 CONT
2 CONT John Collier was born in 1685 and passed away in 1735.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John, son of Charles and Mary (Eyers) Collier, was born 3 March 1685.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Family Bible of Charles Collier records three marriages for John Collier:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT *on 31 December 1704, John Collier and Elizabeth Ballard, dau. of Col. Thomas Ballard
2 CONT *on 3 February 1706, John Collier and Mrs. Elizabeth Gaines, dau. of Francis Ironmonger, Esq.
2 CONT *on 6 October 1713, John Collier and Anne Eppes, dau. of Col. Francis Eppes
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bible records the following births:[2]
2 CONT # John, son of John and Elizabeth Collier, born 28 February 1707
2 CONT # Elizabeth, son of John and Elizabeth Collier, born 3 April 1709
2 CONT # Thomas, son of John and Anne Collier, born 1 December 1714
2 CONT # Francis, son of John and Anne Collier, born 30 September 1716
2 CONT # Henry Isham Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, born 30 June 1718
2 CONT # Cornelius Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, born 16 November 1720
2 CONT # Mary Collier, daughter of John and Anne Collier, born 14 January 1723
2 CONT # William Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, born 10 February 1724
2 CONT # James Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, born 26 May 1726
2 CONT # Eppes Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, 30 April 1728
2 CONT # Benjamin Collier, son of John and Anne Collier, born 1 January 1730
2 CONT # Frances Collier, daughter of John and Anne Collier, born 31 March 1735
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.curtisit.com/curtis/colyer/wgo3.html#I243
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1st., ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Frances Elizabeth (Ironmonger) Collier
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2nd., ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Nancy Anne (Eppes) Collier
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son, Thomas Collier (m. Rebecca Hunt)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=74922011
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Lt. Colonel of New Kent County The first of the King and Queen County Collier family was William Collier, "Citizen and Weaver of London," who came to York County, Va.,in 1670, and later settled in New Kent County, where in 1675 h
2 CONC e appears as. lieutenant-colonel of the county militia. He is said to have been the ancestor of a numerous progeny in the counties of New Kent, King William, King and Queen and Charles City. Among his sons was Charles Collier of K
2 CONC ing and Queen, born in 1660, probably in England, and died in King and Queen in 1735. He had a son''' John Collier''' (shown by will of John Collier, Jr., probated in Hanover in 1749), who was born in 1685 and died in 1765 [?].--D
2 CONC ates from "Colonial Families of the Southern States."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://smithharper.org/collier-family-of-king-and-queen-county-va/
2 CONT
2 CONT >page 149 Capt. John Collier of “Porto Bello”, King and Queen Co. and later Hanover Co., VA; b. 1707; made will Sept 1749 in which he names his sons, Thomas, John, and Joseph, daughters Elizabeth Ironmonger Collier, Frances and Sa
2 CONC lly; and in which he leaves “to my mother-in-law, Ann Collier of King and Queen County, the part of that tract that was given me by my''' grandfather, Charles Collier''', of King and Queen”. - from Colonial Families of the South –
2 CONC  Collier Family of King and Queen County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
