2 CONT
2 CONT Collier Barksdale's profile cites an 1895 family genealogy, which says "'''We do not know who Collier Barksdale married'''".[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Collier Barksdale in 1739 in Charlotte County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah  and Collier Barksdale
2 CONT * Joseph Barksdale, born in 1741, died in 1800, married Hannah Ford.
2 CONT * Nathan Barksdale, born in 1743, died in 1812, married Mary Allen.
2 CONT * William Barksdale, no further information is available.
2 CONT * Mary Barksdale, no further information is available.
2 CONT * John Barksdale, born in 1751, died in 1803, was born in Virginia and died in Warren County, Georgia. He married Susan Burnley.
2 CONT * Lucy Barksdale, born in 1756 in Virginia, died around 1803 in Warren County, Georgia. She married (1) John Smith Davenport, killed at the Battle of Guilford Courthouse. She married (2) Henry Burnley
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Collier Barksdale wrote his will in 1766[4] and it was proven in court in 1774.[5] Inventory[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family named in the will
2 CONT
2 CONT * son John Barksdale
2 CONT * son William Barksdale
2 CONT * daughter Lucy Barksdale
2 CONT * daughter Allen
2 CONT * wife Sarah
2 CONT * all my children, except my son Nathan Barksdale
2 CONT * Exrs: my too (sic) brothers John and Hickson Barksdale, son William Barksdale
2 CONT * Wit: William Holt, Thomas Barksdale
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Previous curator note, removed 20 November 2022.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sarah Randolph, daughter of Henry Randolph III and Elizabeth Sarah Eppes, was born in 1714 in Charlotte County, Virginia. She married Collier Barksdale in 1739 in Charlotte County. She died March 29, 1774 in Petersburg, Dinwiddie
2 CONC  County, Virginia.
2 CONT
