1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of Private.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A006166  DAR Ancestor # A006166]
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR Patriot Index Volume 1 Page 139
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fortsullivan.org/ancestors.htm DAR Chapter If he is in your ancestry then you may be eligible to join the National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution.  Also the Sons of the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War Soldier Capt. Jeffrey Barksdale, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffrey Barksdale B c1755 D 1836 GA Married Phoebe x Soldier GA
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hillgenealogy.com/getperson.php?personID=I0092&tree=001&PHPSESSID=8a7376b943c79185fc63f98391c55eb7
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mr. Barksdale was born in Georgia, fought on the bloody fields of the Revolutionary War, also in many wars previous to that, and died in his native State, leaving many descendants."
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1830 Census for Hancock Co., GA shows Jeffrey and wife still living there with two slaves, one male between 45-100, and one female, 24-35. (page 145 of 1830 census, per descendant Shirley Drake, sdrake@goldrush.com, correspond
2 CONC ed 7/7/1999)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to descendent, Jennifer Cone, jennycone@aol.com, Jeffrey died Nov. 1832* (*This date is incorrect, see info later in notes) in Hancock Co., GA, and had at least one son, William Barksdale. (1/21/99)
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted on GenForum by Jennifer Cone on January 21, 1999 at 19:39:14:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jeffrey BARKSDALE, RS, d. Nov., 1832 in Hancock Co., GA. He and wife Phebe (I have no other info on her) were parents of William Barksdale. William m. Nancy LONG 9 Nov. 1808 in Hancock Co. Children were Martha, Green B., Alfred, 
2 CONC Andrew J., John, William, James M., Edwin J., Madison Franklin, and Alva H. Barksdale. Nancy died 30 Jan. 1848 and was buried at Bethel Baptist Church cemetery near Sparta. William married Martha DUGGAN in Washington Co., GA. 6 Fe
2 CONC b. 1851. Their son, Virgil Alexander BARKSDALE, was my g.g.grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jennifer Cone" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Another source, Grace Bates, Gbates1015@aol.com, 7/22/99 writes: "Died in Hancock County, on the 28 ult., Captain Jeffrey Barksdale, at an advanced age. He was a Revolutionary soldier" THE GEORGIA MESSENGER, Macon, Georgia, Octobe
2 CONC r 25, 1832. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I found a confirmation article of the above in the book, "Obituaries from the Macon Messenger", abstracted originally by Judge Huxford between 1961 and 1970, and published by Rev. Silas Emmett Lucas in 1989. (Feb. 2004, book found
2 CONC  at the library in Americus, Sumter Co., GA) Since the abbreviation "ult." means the previous month, that means Jeffrey Barksdale died on the 28th of SEPTEMBER, 1832, since the article was published in Oct. of 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffrey Barksdale, called Jeffy, born in Virginia C. 1755, served as a soldier (private) in Capt. Joseph Smith's Company, Gist's Regiment, and Ensign William Triplett's Company, Colonel William Grayson's Regiment, Continental Troo
2 CONC ps, from March 1, 1777 for three years pay of 6 2/3 dollars per month (Revolutionary Records 4137, 4138, 4139, 4142, National Archives). Served in Pennsylvania and Virginia based on his being paid in Pennsylvania and Virginia mone
2 CONC y, bought land (185 acres, Bradley's Creek from James Baber in Halifax Co, VA., May 17, 1781 (Bk 12, page 110, Halifax Co, VA Deeds),
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffrey married to Phoebe Brantley, listed as Head of Family, Halifax Co, VA in 1782 with 2 whites and 1 black. Sold land (185 acres on Bradley's Creek, Halifax Co, VA to Robert Tucker, October 16, 1783 (Bk. 12, Page 368, Halifax 
2 CONC Co, VA Deeds) while a resident of NC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffrey moved on to GA appearing in the land court in Wilkes Co, GA and on January 4, 1785, he was granted a tract of land of 500 acres, 200 acres on his own headright, 200 acres on the headright of Charity Brantley and 100 acres 
2 CONC on the headright of Lewis Brantley. This tract was on the Little Ogechee River in what was then Wilkes Co, but later cut off into Warren Co, and may now be in Taliaferro Co. His application in Richmond Co, GA stated that he had a 
2 CONC family of three, including himself, a wife and a negro girl. Jeffrey Barksdale listed as a defaulter in Hancock Co, GA for the year 1798, Capt. Kirk's District. Church membership records show Jeffrey and his family in the Church o
2 CONC f Christ Baptist Church, Williams Creek , Warren Co, GA and Bethel Baptist Church, Hancock Co, GA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffrey appears in Capt. Coleman's District in the 1820 Hancock, Co, GA Federal Census and also in the 1830 Hancock Co, GA Census where he and his wife are between 70 and 80 years of age. When Jeffrey died, the old family home was
2 CONC  located near Sparta, Hancock Co, GA in the vicinity of old Bethel Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jeffrey and Phoebe Barksdale were: Sarah m. Micajah Pickard, William m. Nancy Long (daughter of Littleton Long, Revolutionary Soldier), Daniel m. Phoebe H. Pruitt, John m. Frances Wilkes, Mary, Caroline m. Lawson Under
2 CONC wood, and Hannah m. Alford Long (1) (son of Littleton Long) and Anthony Jones (2). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the information on Jeffrey Barksdale was researched by George Edward Barksdale, now deceased." 
2 CONT
2 CONT The fourth day of the GA 1827 lottery on 09 MAR 1827 living in Hancock Co GA is Jeffry 
2 CONT
2 CONT BARKSDALE, R. S. residing in the 113th District he won land lot 110 in district 05 in Carroll Co GA. (posted July 8, 1999 on GenForum by John Michael O`Melia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Update Oct. 13, 1999 per descendant Mary Perkins, email: MiiMi4@worldnet.att.net through information provided her by Ken Chapman, email: kchapman@wes.colin.cc.ms.us.
2 CONT
2 CONT "JEFFREY BARKSDALE (74) appears to be the son of Collier Barksdale. Many references are made to a Jeffrey Barksdale in the minutes of the Bethel Baptist Church (Hancock County) which have been given to the Baptist Historical Colle
2 CONC ction of Mercer University. Jeffrey Barksdale was in Halifax County, Virginia, in 1781, in North Carolina in 1783, and got a grant of 200 acres in Wilkes County, Georgia (in that part which later became Warren County) in 1785. He 
2 CONC was at Williams Creek Church in 1787 (now in Warren County) and it appears that he was in Hancock County by 1794. Jeffrey Barksdale owned 407 1/2 acres in Hancock County on the Oconee River in 1808. He also owned land (319 acres) 
2 CONC in Putnam County as well as having been deeded land in Richmond County on March 11, 1789, by James Bishop and his wife Phoebe (page 194, Deed Book A-2, Richmond County, Georgia). The land (100 acres) was located on Middle Creek. T
2 CONC he Hancock County tract was sold by William and Alford Long in 1825 without an intervening deed of gift of sale of the land. References to a Captain William Barksdale of Hancock County who ran a ferry (Barksdale Family and Genealo
2 CONC gy and History of Tift County) possibly refer to Jeffrey or to his son, William. Jeffrey was a Captain GMD 113 as late as 1806." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following from the website of Alan Barksdale, http://www.zebra.net. 1/5/00
2 CONT
2 CONT "Letter from Edward Jasper Barksdale dated 07/28/1906: "My grandfather, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeffery Barksdale, died in Hancock County, Ga. in 1836. " (Another date?) 
2 CONT
2 CONT "After his death, William Barksdale, my father, occupied the old family 
2 CONT
2 CONT home and he and his brother, John, managed the large plantation near 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparta and in the vicinity of old Bethel Church." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter-Written by Nellie Viola Barksdale Brawner (04/04/1950): "Our 
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary ancestor is Jeffery Barksdale, who came to Hancock County, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ga. In 1779, with a land grant for his service as a soldier. He was also 
2 CONT
2 CONT a soldier of the War of 1812. His record being on file at our State 
2 CONT
2 CONT Capitol. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He managed his property well and bought additional lands. When he died, 
2 CONT
2 CONT about 1834, he owned property in eleven different counties of Georgia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His estate was administered by his son John Barksdale, their homeplace 
2 CONT
2 CONT near Sparta, Ga. (Hancock County). Receipts for his estate were signed 
2 CONT
2 CONT by Grandpa Barksdale and his brothers and several of the Patterson 
2 CONT
2 CONT family. All on file in the Court House at Sparta. I have not been to 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparta, but Uncle Matt Barksdale's daughter went and copied much of the 
2 CONT
2 CONT data there for me." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources cited:
2 CONT
