2 CONT
2 CONT Ga. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HANCOCK CO, GA, Inferior Court sitting for ordinary purposes, Monday, 2nd 
2 CONT
2 CONT JAN 1837, Present their Honors, Joel Crawford, J. W. Rabun, Wilkins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith, Justices, John Barksdale has made application for administration 
2 CONT
2 CONT on the estate of Jeffrey Barkesdale, dec'd, late of said 
2 CONT
2 CONT county,..........Whereupon the said John Barkesdale executed his bond in 
2 CONT
2 CONT the sum of $2000.00 with John G. Gilbert, his 
2 CONT
2 CONT security,.............received letters of administration in the premises. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturday, 20th MAY 1837, Court ordered that John Barkesdale have leave to 
2 CONT
2 CONT sell the real estate of said deceased........19th FEB 1838, John 
2 CONT
2 CONT Barkesdale, Adm .......says the foregoing account sales land are just and 
2 CONT
2 CONT true. Henry Rogers CCC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT May 12, 2002. From packet of documents from TX State Archives, Austin, TX sent to me by Robert Steele of Dallas, email RSteele185@aol.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcriptions of letters between Mrs. James Monroe Hill and Mrs. H. A. Iverson written in 1904 and transcribed in 1935 by Hill granddaughter Lucy Amanda Hill Jones, states that Mrs. H. A. Iverson "...was the daughter of of Mrs. G
2 CONC arland Dawkins, who was a SISTER of Mrs. Elizabeth (Barksdale) Hill and aunt of Jas. M. Hill." It further states that "Phebe Ann Barksdale, daughter of Jeffrey and Phebe Barksdale, and sister of Mrs. Elizabeth Barksdale Hill, was 
2 CONC born in Hancock Co., GA March 14, 1800. Was married to Garland Dawkins in Jasper Co., GA in 1824. Died in Alabama Sept. 30, 1864."
2 CONT
2 CONT The fourth day of the GA 1827 lottery on 09 MAR 1827 living in Hancock Co GA is Jeffry BARKSDALE, R. S. residing in the 113th District he won land lot 110 in district 05 in Carroll Co GA.
