1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.anamericansancestry.com/getperson.php?personID=I7650&tree=test1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT AI Overview 
2 CONT Based on Barksdale family history, several genealogical records indicate that a Mary Barksdale (sometimes referred to as Mary Elizabeth or Mary "Polly" Barksdale) married a man named William Lindsey (or James William Lindsey) in t
2 CONC he mid-18th century, with records often placing the event in Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Key details regarding this marriage and family line include: 
2 CONT * Identity: Mary Barksdale (1734/1743–1834) was the daughter of Henry Barksdale and Judith (possibly Judith Dudley Claiborne). 
2 CONT * Marriage: She married William Lindsey (or Caleb William Lindsey) around 1754–1759 in Caroline County, Virginia. 
2 CONT * Children: They were the parents of several children, including Jesse Lindsey, Sarah Lindsey, and Caleb Lindsey. 
2 CONT * Migration: The family was associated with Virginia and later records indicate some members moved to Indiana. 
2 CONT * Evidence: The marriage is substantiated by wills and genealogical records. For instance, a 1778 will of Henry Barksdale references "my daughter Mary Lindsey". Some research notes also mention a second marriage for Mary to a Capt
2 CONC ain John Hurst. 
2 CONT * There are two primary entries in genealogical databases that seem to represent this person: 
2 CONT * Mary Elizabeth Barksdale (1743–1834): Born in Louisa, Virginia; married William Lindsey in 1759, died in Indiana. 
2 CONT * Mary "Polly" Barksdale (1734–1804): Born in Virginia; married William/Caleb Lindsey. 
2 CONT * These records are often cited in Barksdale family history, particularly in genealogies tracing the descendants of early Virginia settlers.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
