1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW HAMPSHIRE  with the rank of COLONEL.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A037860  DAR Ancestor # A037860]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy was a Colonel in The Continental Army from 1775 to 1783. He with his sons fought at the battle of Bunker Hill on June 16-17 1775. He was also a vetren of the French and Indian wars. (1754-1763). After retiring from militar
2 CONC y service, he was a member of the New Hampshire House of Representatives in 1776. He died in Keen, N.H. in 1817 at age 93.
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from "A History of the Town of Keene [New Hampshire] from 1732"
