1 NAME Ichabod /Thayer/ Sr.
2 GIVN Ichabod
2 SURN Thayer
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Thayer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 31 MAR 1721
2 PLAC Mendon, Worcester, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 MAR 1796
2 PLAC Massachusetts, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT In Mendon. Vital record does not name the mother, but it must be Mary, Isaac's second wife[1] Isaac's age makes it possible for him to be either the so of Isaac Sr. (b 1664) or Isaac Jr. b 1695. Isaac Sr.'s will written in 1754 na
2 CONC mes Ichabod as the last of his living six sons.[2] There is no mention of a son Ichabod in the probate records of Isaac Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichabod Thayer married the widowed Hannah Bigelow Cheney in 1742. The 17 year disparity between the ages of widowed Hannah, 38, and her young husband Ichabod, just 21, seems very unlikely, especially back then. But their stone in 
2 CONC Milford's Pine Hill Cemetery supports the match. And there is this romantic tale, recorded 140 years after the event, possibly too good to be true: Adin Ballou relates the following in his History of Milford from 1882: "There come
2 CONC s down a bit of traditional romance concerning the courtship that led to this marriage. Ichabod had become of age and was looking around for a sweetheart. He had become slightly acquainted with a prepossessing lass, who dwelt in t
2 CONC he extreme northerly part of what is now Milford, and resolved to offer her his hand, should she be willing to accept it. So he started from old Mendon in the early winter, near the close of the week, on his connubial mission. But
2 CONC  a driving snow-storm opened upon him; and when he arrived at what is now the homestead of Justin H. Eames, the storm continued with unabated severity for two or three days. Meantime there sprang up a mutual attraction between the
2 CONC  widow and her gallant guest. She was twenty yrs. the oldest, but still ruddy and agreeable; and as Cupid is not easily thwarted, he planted his arrows in their hearts so effectually that a match was ere long consummated. The snow
2 CONC -storm gave Mrs. Hannah an acceptable and willing prisoner. He went no further in pursuit of a wife."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Bigelow Thayer died in Milford in December 1791
2 CONT Ichabod, now referred to as Ichabod Sr., married Dorcas Burnett in Milford on 16 Jan 1794.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichabod and Hannah Thayer had, in the part of Mendon that became Milford: [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah, b. 20 Mar 1742-3
2 CONT Ichabod, b. 6 Mar 1745, bp. 7 Apr 1745 in Milford
2 CONT Elijah, b. 4 June 1747, bp. 5 July 1747 in Milford
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT In Milford, on 10 Mar 1796, aged 74[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Thayer-3554
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichabod Thayer (1721 - 1796) I
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Ichabod Thayer===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 31 Mar 1721 in Mendon, Worcester, Massachusetts Bay Province
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Isaac Thayer and Mary (Unknown) Thayer
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Mercy (Thayer) Thompson [half], Isaac Thayer [half], Ebenezer Thayer [half], Comfort (Thayer) Keith [half], Mary (Thayer) Keith, John Thayer, Nathaniel Thayer, Moses Thayer, Samuel Thayer, Joseph Thayer, Jerusha (Thayer
2 CONC ) Crary and Patience (Thayer) Davison
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Bigelow) Thayer — married about 1742 in Milford, Worcester, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Ichabod Thayer and Elijah Thayer
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 10 Mar 1796 at age 74 in Milford, Worcester, Massachusettsm
2 CONT
