2 ADDR
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT He emigrated in May1760 on the ship "Wolfe" to Cornwallis, NS, and is
2 CONT mentioned as one (of) the grantees of 100,000 acres of land granted by George
2 CONT II, after the expulsion of the French. There are five Woodworths named in
2 CONT this list of grantees: Amasa, Benjamin, Silas, Thomas, and William.
2 CONT (Descendents of Walter Woodworth, by William Atwater Woodworth)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "Nova Scotia Immigrants", Silas Woodworth received lot 2 (66
2 CONT acres), Div. 4, Cornwallis Township Grant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Silas had 10 children, eight of them sons, so certainly a good part of the
2 CONT Bay of Fundy Woodworths were his doing.
2 CONT
2 CONT I hope this helps.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruce Woodworth
2 CONT BruceW22@aol.com
