2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope (Darling) Wilson (1742)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope Wilson formerly Darling
2 CONT Born 25 Aug 1742 in Bellingham, Norfolk County, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Daughter of Samuel Darling Sr. and Penelope (Brown) Darling
2 CONT Sister of Samuel Darling Jr [half], Michael Darling [half], Abigail (Darling) Draper [half], John Darling [half], Nathaniel Butterworth [half] and Joshua Darling [half]
2 CONT Wife of Israel Wilson — married 18 Jul 1765 in Cumberland, Providence County, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Mother of Penelope (Wilson) Arnold
2 CONT Died [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Barry Smith private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 25 Apr 2023 | Created 1 Jul 2018
2 CONT This page has been accessed 200 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope was born in 1742 in Bellingham, Massachusetts, the daughter of Samuel Darling and Penelope Brown.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married first, Israel Wilson in Cumberland, Rhode Island in 1765.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT son Joseph born June 23, 1766
2 CONT son Benjamin born June 22, 1767
2 CONT son Israel born July 14, 1768. A record of the birth is made in Mendon.
2 CONT daughter Penelope who married Thomas Arnold in 1787.
2 CONT She married second, William Burlingame in 1776.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope appears as head of household in Coventry in the 1774 census of Rhode Island.[4] Her household distribution and inferred attributions are as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT three white males under 16: sons Joseph, Benjamin, and Israel
2 CONT one white female over 16: householder Penelope
2 CONT two white females under 16: daughter Penelope and unknown female
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Bellingham VR, page 32.
2 CONT ↑ Arnold, James N. Vital Record of Rhode Island, 1636-1850. Vol. 2, "Cumberland Marriages." Providence, R.I., Narragansett Historical Pub. Co., 1891, p. 71.
2 CONT ↑ Arnold, James N. Vital Record of Rhode Island, 1636-1850. Vol. 1, "Coventry Marriages." Providence, R.I., Narragansett Historical Pub. Co., 1891, p. 11.
2 CONT ↑ 1774 Rhode Island Census, Coventry, Page 2, Entry 12 -- Penelipa Wilson; citing transcription by Linda L. Mathew in Rhode Island Roots 31 p.25, March 2005.
2 CONT "Vital Records of Bellingham, Massachusetts, to the year 1850" in Massachusetts: Vital Records, 1620-1850, database online at American Ancestors.
