1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Adams-15997
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemima Adams
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1 Apr 1740 in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts Bay Province
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Henry Adams Esq. and Jemima (Morse) Adams
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Amos Adams, Sarah (Adams) Harding, Enoch Adams, Elizabeth Adams and	Elijah Adams
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Joseph Lovell Jr — married 27 Sep 1764 in Medfield, Norfolk, Massachusetts Bay Province
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Jemima (Lovell) Richardson and Sarah (Lovell) Wood
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 27 Oct 1814 in Medway, Norfolk, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 1 Nov 2017 | Created 1 Jun 2014
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemima was born in medway on April 1, 1740. She was the daughter of Henry Adams and Jemima Morse. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Lovell married Jemima Adams in Medfield on Sept. 27, 1764.[2] They had posted their intentions in Medway on Nov. 12, 1763[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and Jemima had, in Medway: [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b. Dec. 23, 1765, died three months later Jemima, b. June 5, 1767, m. Ezra Richardson Elizabeth, b. June 17, 1769, m. Rev. Stephen Baxter Sarah, b. May 29, 1772, died April 27, 1775 Abigail, b. Jan. 20, 1775, m. Rev. John 
2 CONC Pierce, in Brookline Keziah, b. Mar. 2, 1778, died 1797 Sarah, b. Oct. 31, 1783, d. Sept. 10, 1786 Jemima Adams Lovell died in Medway on October 27, 1814[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Norfolk, Vital Records of Medfield, Massachusetts to the year 1850, p. 11 ↑ Norfolk, Vital Records of Medfield, Massachusetts to the year 1850, p. 112 ↑ Norfolk, Vital Records of Medway, Massachusetts to the year 1850, p. 225 ↑ 
