2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Massachusetts Vital Records Project for Vital Records of Shrewsbury up to 1849, the Birth transcription on page 23, indicates Persis, d.[aughter] of John Bush and Martha Temple, 23 April 1827. Note: no origianal b
2 CONC irth record exists in the Town Clerk's Office as of 6 July 2021.
2 CONT
2 CONT No grave stone found in 1944 nor 2010 surveys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Persis died May 6, 1788 at 61 years of age, having been married 33 yrs and having 11 children. [the 'Massachusetts Spy', May 22, 1788, Vol XVIII, issue 790, pg 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at Boylston on the 6th instant, the amiable consort of the Rev. Ebenezer Morse, aged 61. Her funeral was attended on the 8th, with the greatest decency and solemnity, by a large assembly of friends and acquaintance [sic]; a w
2 CONC ell adapted sermon was preached on the occasion by the Rev. Mr. Bridge of East Sudbury, from the words, Rom. 8, XVIII, 'For I reckon the sufferings of the present-time, are not worth to be compared with the glory that shall be rev
2 CONC ealed to us'
2 CONT
