1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ebenezer Morse, was a Loyalist who moved from Boylston, Mass. (then called North Shrewsbury) to somewhere
2 CONT
2 CONT in New York at the outbreak of the Revolution. There he clearly met Henrietta and they married. At "the Peace" in 1783, they sailed to Shelburne, Nova Scotia and were among the first settlers. Shelburne fell on hard times a few ye
2 CONC ars later, and they moved back to the United States in 1788 to join Ebenezer's siblings who had settled in Williamsville, a part of Newfane, Vermont. At some point, Abraham must have come to Williamsville to be with his sister and
2 CONC  there married Suzanne Thayer.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/117478772/ebenezer_morse
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Morse II
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 10 Jul 1755
2 CONT Shrewsbury, Worcester County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 30 Jun 1813 (aged 57)
2 CONT Williamsville, Windham County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Williamsville Cemetery
2 CONT Williamsville, Windham County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT PLOT
2 CONT Williamsville Old Cemetery
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT  117478772 · 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Morse, son of Rev. Dr. Ebenezer and Persis Morse married Henrietta Siverly, of New York on Sept 22, 1782. They soon after removed to Nova Scotia. About 1788 he came to Newfane, Vermont for the purpose of building a gristm
2 CONC ill.
2 CONT He and his wife had 12 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Mr. Ebenezer Morse died June 30, 1813, ae 57 yrs.
2 CONT While his body sleeps in Jesus we trust. A beneficent God has opned the great scenes of the eternal world to his imortal spirit (sic)
