1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Michael Lovell ==
2 CONT
2 CONT === Profile Naming Protocol & Suffix Audit ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''First Name:''' Michael
2 CONT * '''Last Name:''' Lovell
2 CONT * '''Suffix:''' [Leave Blank]
2 CONT * '''Technical Rationale:''' No numerical suffix (such as "I") or generational modifier (such as "Sr.") should be added to the primary name fields. The insertion of traditional numerical suffixes is an anachronism in 18th-century 
2 CONC New England colonial documentation and frequently causes generation slippage in digital databases. In contemporary colonial records, terms like "Senior" and "Junior" were temporary, fluid designations used locally to distinguish t
2 CONC wo living men of the same name within a town; they were not permanent legal fixtures attached at birth or carried across migrations. To maintain database stability and prevent automated identity smash-ups, distinction must be mana
2 CONC ged entirely through the vital dates and locations fields.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT === Parentage Audit ===
2 CONT The raw profile previously listed four parents: Nathaniel Lovell, Alexander Lovell, Elizabeth (Davis) Lovell, and Lydia (Albee) Lovell. This was an identity smash-up spanning three generations:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Alexander Lovell''' and '''Lydia Albee''' were the grandparents of Michael Lovell (married 1658 in Medfield).
2 CONT * '''Nathaniel Lovell''' and '''Elizabeth Davis''' were his true biological parents (married 1696).
2 CONT
2 CONT === Chronological Firewall ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birth:''' Born March 13, 1699/1700 in Medfield (later Medway), Massachusetts. The alternative birth date of March 13, 1705, belongs to his younger brother, Nathaniel Lovell Jr.
2 CONT * '''Death:''' Died circa 1752 in Worcester, Massachusetts. His estate was entered into probate in Worcester County in 1752 (Case No. 37926). The alternative death date of 1772 belongs entirely to his son, Capt. Michael Lovell, wh
2 CONC o died in Rockingham, Vermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT == Verifiable Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Lovell was born on March 13, 1700, in Medfield, Massachusetts, the son of Nathaniel Lovell and Elizabeth Davis. He was raised in the part of Medfield that became the town of Medway in 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Morse on May 10, 1726, in Medway. She was the daughter of Benoni Morse and Rachel Bullard. Following the birth of their older children, Michael relocated his family westward to Worcester, Massachusetts, during the 
2 CONC early colonial frontier expansion of the 1730s. He established a homestead in Worcester, where he remained until his death in early 1752. His widow Mary survived him and subsequently married John Walker in 1755 (often cited as Dan
2 CONC iel Walker in later secondary sources).
2 CONT
2 CONT == Geni Alignment Data ==
2 CONT
2 CONT === Immediate Family ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Parents:'''
2 CONT * Father: Nathaniel Lovell
2 CONT * Mother: Elizabeth (Davis) Lovell
2 CONT * '''Siblings:'''
2 CONT * Elizabeth (Lovell) Hartshorn
2 CONT * Hopestill Lovell
2 CONT * Nathaniel Lovell Jr.
2 CONT * Lydia (Lovell) Adams
2 CONT * '''Spouse:'''
2 CONT * Mary (Morse) Lovell [later Walker] — ''Married May 10, 1726''
2 CONT * '''Children:'''
2 CONT * '''Capt. Michael Lovell''' — *Often confused with his father; married Hannah Petty; moved to Rockingham, VT.*
2 CONT * '''Ebenezer Lovell''' — *Served as a Representative to the General Court.*
2 CONT * '''Mary (Lovell) Bugbee''' — *Married Daniel Bugbee.*
2 CONT * '''Lois Lovell''' — *Died in childhood.*
2 CONT * '''Maj. Oliver Lovell''' — *Revolutionary War Officer; settled in Rockingham, VT.*
2 CONT * '''Timothy Lovell''' — *Settled in Rockingham, VT.*
2 CONT * '''Jemima (Lovell) Walker''' — *Married Abraham Walker.*
2 CONT * '''John Lovell''' — *Settled in Rockingham, VT.*
2 CONT * '''Elijah Lovell''' (1749–1816) — *Born April 20, 1749, in Worcester; married Abigail Goldsbury; settled in Rockingham, VT.*
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT == Primary Source Documentation ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Vital Records of Medfield, Massachusetts to the Year 1850 (Births, p. 67: "Lovell, Michael, s. Nathaniel and Elizabeth, Mar. 13, 1699-1700.")
2 CONT * Vital Records of Medway, Massachusetts to the Year 1850 (Marriages, p. 222: "Lovell, Michael and Mary Morse, May 10, 1726.")
2 CONT * Vital Records of Worcester, Massachusetts to the Year 1848 (Births, p. 172: "Lovell, Elijah, s. Michael and Mary, April 20, 1749.")
2 CONT * Worcester County, MA: Probate File Papers, 1731-1881 (Case 37926, Michael Lovell, 1752, Administration of Estate).
