2 CONT The Birth Date is a rough estimate. See the text for details.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth (Hill) Holbrook is related to US President William Howard Taft. Here is the trail.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth was apparently born to Eleazer and Sarah Breck Hill, life-long residents of Sherborn, but no birth record for her yet found in that town's records. A birth in 1696, as suggested by Bartlett,[1] fits within the recorded childr
2 CONC en of her parents and would make her one year younger than her husband, age 22 at her marriage, and age 42 at the birth of her last recorded child, all of which seem reasonable.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Hill married John Holbrook in Sherborn on 13 Mar 1718-19.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Holbrooks settled initially in Sherborn, then removed west to Grafton about 1734, judging from the births of their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Holbrook died in Grafton on 12 May 1747.[3]:
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Ruth Holbrook had at least seven children, first five in Sherborn[4] and last two in Grafton:[5]:
2 CONT
2 CONT William, b. 24 May 1719, m. Sarah Batchellor, 25 May 1753, d. 27 May 1792, in 74th year
2 CONT Silence, b. 23 Mar 1723-4, m. Samuel Goodale of Sutton, 20 Oct 1743
2 CONT Ruth, b. 28 Dec 1726, m. Jonathan Eames of Holliston, 12 June 1744
2 CONT Elizabeth, 6 June 1730
2 CONT John, b. 28 Aug 1733, m. (Mrs) Abigail Warrin, 16 Jan 1758
2 CONT Sarah, b. 18 Jan 1734-5, m. Robert Mellen, in Holliston 19 Nov 1761
2 CONT Moses, b. 14 Sep 1738, m. Mary Whipple 15 Jan 1767, d. 20 or 26 Mar 1802, in his 63rd year
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
