1 OCCU Captain of Militia, Comissary of Army, Town Clerk, Representative to the General Court
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR# [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_descendants/?action=list&MyPrimary_Seqn=320819&MyLineageCount=1 A117555]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was captain of Sherborn Militia in Colonial days, Commisary for the army in the revolutionary war, held many offices of honor and trust, and was leading man in Sherborn until suceeded by his junior half-brother, Hon. Daniel Whi
2 CONC tney. By appointment from the General Court, he acted for years as associate guardian for the Natick Indians. He represented, as general agent, the proprietors of Dublin, New Hampshire., and who was largely responsible for the lar
2 CONC ge numbers of settlers who moved to that place from Sherborn and other parts of Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT  [http://reocities.com/Heartland/Ranch/8457/Twitch.html Source]
2 CONT
2 CONT J Twitchell's indian Account book http://digitalcollections.americanancestors.org/cdm/ref/collection/p15869coll36/id/115
2 CONT
2 CONT Original account book for the associate guardian for Natick Indians (as appointed by the General Court). First page has "Joseph Twitchells Book of Indian accounts". Entries include debts and credits concerning the selling of prope
2 CONC rty and estate settlements performed by Twitchell on behalf of the Natick Indians. Entries also include his acquisition of clothing and food.
