1 NAME John /Ball/ Gent.
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Ball
2 NSFX Gent.
2 _MARNM Ball
1 NAME John Ball, of Worcester
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 JUL 1697
2 ADDR
3 CITY Watertown
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts Bay
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE JAN 1756
2 PLAC Worcester Common
2 ADDR
3 CITY Worcester
3 STAE MA
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 JAN 1756
2 ADDR
3 CITY Worcester
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts Bay
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Reportedly of Watertown Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT From Genealogy Research of Ilene Miller 11/16/1985
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the son of James Ball and Elizabeth Fisk
2 CONT
2 CONT A road was layed out through John Ball's land March 5, 1747-8.  He was chosen Grand Juryman ye year ensuing 1750-1.  He was buried in the old burying ground on the common Worcester, Mass.  Insription on his Tombstone:  Here lies b
2 CONC uried the body of Mr. John Ball who died Janry ye 11th 1756 in the 59th year of his age.  Executors of his will were Lydia, James and Samuel Ball.  Inventory Real Estate 430 lbs.  Personal  106lbs. 13s. 11d.  His will dated Jan. 9
2 CONC  1756 mentions wife Lydia, daughters Anna and Mary and sons James (oldest) Daniel, Samuel, Nathan, John, Josiah, Isaac, Jonathan, Jonas, Joseph.  12 children in all (living at this time1756)  Judge John Chandler Esq. probate of wi
2 CONC lls July 1,1759, Worcester, Mass.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ball-4354 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 14 2016, 0:51:00 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Genealogical Problems and Research'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The New England Ball Project is now the best source for all New England Ball families. Run by John G. Ball, and supported by his associates, it encompasses the classic early 20th century study of New England Ball families: Warren 
2 CONC & Ball, Descs. of John Ball of Watertown (1932)[1], as well as the extensive late 20th century research of Dr. Druse, and the latest research available on this interesting family.
2 CONT
2 CONT A good description of this family is found at The New England Ball Project #83 John Ball (1697–1756). [http://www.newenglandballproject.com/g0/p4.htm#i83 link]
2 CONT
2 CONT Warren & Ball, Descs. of John Ball of Watertown (1932)[2], 14, Part I, #53, John Ball confuses this family with 14, Part I, #50, John Ball. This John Ball (1697–1756) and John Ball (1704–1769) have been confused by many as between
2 CONC  1730 and 1738, they were both married to women named Mary, and having children born at Watertown. The clerk there didn't distinguish the two couples, recording all their children as of John and Mary Ball. Fortunately, both Johns 
2 CONC left wills that clarify their families.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Ball's Will'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Careful attention to the language of this will reveals the general structure of this family. John had three wives ("a Green silk gown I had by my second wife I give to my present wife"). John's eldest child, and only surviving chi
2 CONC ld of his 1st wife, Anna (Ball) Bartlett was named first, received only 5 shillings, and is not included in the list of his children who share the residue of his estate. Clearly her inheritance was already taken care of, probably 
2 CONC when she married. James, Samuel and Nathan, the surviving children of John's 2nd wife, are given special bequests of property which "his mother brough[t] me at marriage" and "I had by their Mother at marriage". The remaining child
2 CONC ren were all by his 3rd wife, Lydia. In the Name of God Amen
2 CONT
2 CONT The last Will and Testament of John Ball of Worcester in the County of Worcester[,] Gent[.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT I the said John Ball being sick and week but of sound memory & disposing mind[,] And not knowing how God may dispose of me under my prese[nt] Illnes[s] do make and ordain these presents to be my last Testament. And first of all[,]
2 CONC  I Commend my precious and I[m]mortall Soul into the hands of Almighty God who gave it, hopeing throh ye Merits of Jesus Christ to Receive the full & free pardon of all my Sins & to Inheritt Eternall life my body I comitt to the E
2 CONC arth by decent Christian burial at the discretion of my Executors hereinafter named nothing doubting but at the Genll Resurrection I shall Receive [the] same again by the mighty power of God —
2 CONT
2 CONT And as touching such worldly Estate wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me in this life[,] I give[,] demise and dispose of the same in the following Man[n]er & form —
2 CONT
2 CONT Imprimis[,] my Will is that my Just debts and funerall Charges be paid by my Execrs as soon as may be after my decease[.]
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my Daughter Anna wife of Ebenr Bartlett of Newton five shillings wch with wt I have given heretofore is in full of her portion of my Estate[.]
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my eldest Son James Ball my Silver Tanker which his mother brough[t] me at marriage to his heirs & assigns forever & also [——] silver spoons & [—.]
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my Two Sons Samuell & Nathan Ball my five Silver Spoons and Two Gold [—]ings Which I had by their Mother at marriage to be Equally Divided between them & to their heirs & assigns forever[.]
2 CONT
2 CONT I Give unto my Dear wife Lydia _ _ the sole use & Improvement of all my Estate Reall and personall for her Support & bringing up & Educateing my Children for the Space of four years from the date hereof from the End of which Time 
2 CONC my will is that my said wife forever have & hold to her & her heirs and assigns forever one third of my personall Estate And the use & Improvement of one third of my Reall Estate during life.
2 CONT
2 CONT All the rest and Residue of my Estate I give Equally amongst my Children namely James[,] Samuell[,] Nathan[,] John[,] Josiah[,] Isaac[,] Jonathan[,] Jonas[,] & Joseph[,] & my Daughter Mary[,] Share & Share alike & to their heirs &
2 CONC  assigns forever & at the death of my said wife ye Remaining third of my Reall Estate I give and dispose of Equally to my said Ten Children Last mention[e]d Equally as aforesd and to their heirs & assigns forever except my wearing
2 CONC  apparell I give to my three Eldest Sons and further my will is that a Green silk gown I had by my second wife I give to my present wife notwithstanding [———] & my yellow and white silk gown and [—] coat I give to my Daughter Mar
2 CONC y aforsd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Finelly I make and ordain my Dear wife & my Son James Executrix & Executor of this my Last Will & Testament Revoking all others and Ce[r]tifying this & no other to be my last will and Testament[.] In Witness whereof I have hereto 
2 CONC set my hand & seal this 9th day of January AD 1756[.]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Ball
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed[,] Sealed[,] published[,] pronounced and declared by the Said John Ball to be my Last Will and Testament in [—]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crefon[?] John Green John Chandler
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
