2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah Williams was born on November 1, 1716 in Taunton, Bristol, Province of Massachusetts Bay, daughter of Nathaniel Williams (1679–1726) and Lydia King (~1687–1748).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1732, her mother, Lidia, was appointed guardian of Bethiah and her sisters, Elizabeth and Judith, who were all under the age of 14 years.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah (20) married Noah Williams (19) (born on March 18, 1718 in Taunton, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America; son of Samuel Williams and Abigail (Wood) Williams) on March 23, 1737 in Taunton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah Williams (~1741–1824)
2 CONT Noah Williams (~1743– )
2 CONT Bethiah died on January 21, 1746 in Taunton, aged 29.
2 CONT
