1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Retrieved from http://www.genealogy.com/ftm/p/u/l/Mark-W-Pullen/BOOK-0001/0005-0012.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >Notes for Hannah Sibley:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hannah, was first married to Stephen Southworth. In the Sibley Family in America, volume 1, it states that Hannah married second an unknown Whiting.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hannah Sibley married, first, September 17, 1753, Stephen Southworth, b. January 12, 1731, Freetown, Massachusetts, and d. bef. 1760. They had a son, Solomon, b. abt. 1758. He was eight years old on March 31, 1766, when John Sibl
2 CONC ey, his grandfather, was appointed his guardian. Solomon died March 14, 1829.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A Genealogy of the Southworths (Southards) Descendants of Constant ...By Samuel Gilbert Webber.  Page 208.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=VllVAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA197&dq=Samuel%20Southworth%201690&pg=PA208#v=onepage&q&f=false Googl
2 CONC eBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT >1960 STEPHEN SOUTHWORTH" (Stephen“, William", Constant, Edward'], b. 12 Jan., 1731, in Freetown, Mass.; d. before 1760; m., 27 Sept., 1753, HANNAH SIBLEY, of Sutton, Mass., b. 13 June, 1732, dau. of John. and Hannah (Marsh) Sible
2 CONC y.* He served as private in 1757 in Capt. John Sibley's company, Col. John Chandler, Jr.'s, regiment, for relief of Fort William Henry; and again in 1758 in Capt. John Fry's company, Col. Timothy Ruggles' regiment. After his death
2 CONC  his widow m. (2), 20 March, 1760, Caleb Whiting, of Douglas, Mass. She was alive in 1776. 
2 CONT
2 CONT > Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # SOUTHWORTH i. SOLOMON, 6. about 1758. He was eight years old 31 March, 1766, when John Sibley was appointed his guardian; d. 14 March, 1829.
2 CONT # STEPHEN', b. about 1755. There is some confusion as to this child, whether there was one or two of the name Stephen. A Stephen had a guardian, Caleb Whiting, appointed 3 Dec., 1766, when he was aged eleven years. Also Stephen ha
2 CONC d amguardian, Abner Sibley, 25 Dec., 1767, when he was aged fifteen years. It is possible that Stephen Southworth had two guardians and the discrepancy in dates and age is due to mistakes as to his age.
