1 OCCU surveyor of land, on the board selectmen, town clerk, town treasurer
1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Baxter-3413
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Baxter served with Civil Service, Massachusetts during the American Revolution.
2 CONT John Baxter was born to Joseph and Mary Fiske, November 2, 1708 in Medfield, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Rebekah Fisher, October 13, 1732, in Medfield, Massachusetts.[2]Another source records this marriage on October 12, 1732 in Medfield, Massachusetts.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Baxter was a prominent man in Medfield; he was a surveyor or land, served on the board of selectmen for many years[4], and was town clerk and town treasurer for a lengthy period of time. He owned a house abut the year 1740 in
2 CONC  the north part of town.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Rebekah had the following known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, b 1734
2 CONT Nathan, b and d in 1735
2 CONT Mary, 1737; m Thomas Mason in 1763
2 CONT Richard, 1740; settled in Princeton
2 CONT Moses, 1742; settled in Rutland
2 CONT John, 1746
2 CONT Sarah, 1750-1780; m in 1778 Silas Bullard
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain John Baxter died November 13, 1788, in Medfield, Massachusetts.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Baxter (1708 - 1788)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John Baxter===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 May 1708 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Joseph Baxter and Mary (Fiske) Baxter
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Joseph Baxter, Mary (Baxter) Gardner, Sarah (Baxter) Buckminster, Hannah Baxter, Joseph Baxter and Thomas Baxter
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Rebekah (Fisher) Baxter — married 12 Oct 1732 in Medfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Joseph Baxter, Nathan Baxter, Mary (Baxter) Mason, Richard Baxter, Moses Baxter and John Baxter
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 14 Nov 1788 at age 80 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 7 Dec 2022 | Created 29 Feb 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT
