2 CONT Moses Baxter is a DAR Patriot Ancestor, A007626.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses, son of John Baxter & Rebeckah, was born on 11 November 1742 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[1] .[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses married Mary Moore (of Sudbury) on 1 September 1768 in Sudbury, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[3] At the time of his marriage, Moses resided in Princeton, Worcester, Massachusetts.[4] [5] They had the following childre
2 CONC n in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts:
2 CONT
2 CONT Chloe Baxter, 9 Dec 1769
2 CONT Mary Baxter, 17 Apr 1772
2 CONT Moses Baxter, 21 May 1774, died 23 Dec 1776 in Rutland.
2 CONT Sarah Baxter, 23 Sep 1776
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses died (age 79) on 1 August 1821 in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts, United States.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses served for twelve days as a private in Capt. Thomas Eustis’s co. of the Massachusetts Militia, and marchedto Cambridge on the alarm of April 19, 1775.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1790 census Moses was in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts.[8] In the 1820 census Moses was in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was recorded in Worcester County, Massachusetts.[10] [11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Baxter (1742 - 1821)
2 CONT
