2 CONT {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\cocoartf1187\cocoasubrtf390\cocoascreenfonts1{\fonttbl\f0\fswiss\fcharset0 Helvetica;}{\colortbl;\red255\green255\blue255;}\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\t
2 CONC x6720\pardirnatural \f0\fs24 \cf0 [Newell_Carmean.FTW] \par  \par Sometime around the 1800's a large group of Backuses left Connecticut and settled in Tompkins, Co., New York. About the same time that Martha, wife of Josiah,Jr. di
2 CONC ed Elizabeth Hillard Backus had also died, so by 1836, both Josiah, Sr. and Josiah, Jr. were widowed. It was from Gallia, Ohio, that the Josiah, Sr. wrote the Pension department asking that his pension money be sent to his new add
2 CONC ress in Ohio. He was a veteran of the Revolutionary War.}
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
