2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Sarah Isabelle
2 CONT
2 CONT When Sarah Isabelle Barber was born on 12 February 1744, in Worcester, Worcester, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, her father, John Barber, was 29 and her mother, Lydia Stimpson, was 22. She married Samuel Bulla
2 CONC rd on 13 March 1766, in Rutland, Worcester, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 4 daughters. She died on 18 October 1836, in Franklin, Vermont, United States, at the age
2 CONC  of 92, and was buried in Swanton, Franklin, Vermont, United States.
