1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=68256710&ref=wvr Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jul. 11, 1779 Barre Worcester County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Aug. 30, 1856 Williamstown Berkshire County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Bixby, born 11 July 1779 at Barre, Ma.; died 30 Aug 1856 at Williamstown, Ma. the result of being thrown from his horse; married 1 Oct. 1805, at Barre, Abigail (Nurse), born 15 Feb. 1785, died 16 Sept. 1825, at Wallingfor
2 CONC d, Vt. having been insane for 7 Years. She was daughter of Timothy and Experience (Unknown) Nurse. He married, second, 16 Feb. 1828 at Rutland, Vt. Submit (Kingsley), born there 22 July 1790, died 25 July 1870, at North Adams, Ma.
2 CONC  Daughter of Phineas and Abigail ( Wood) Kingsley of Rutland, Vt. Submit Kingsley was descended from John Kingsley who came from Hampshire, England, to Dorchester, Ma. in 1635 and was one of the "seven pillars" of the church. Her 
2 CONC father served in the war of the Revolution under Ensign Isaac Cushman and Capt. Samuel Williams. He lived at Rutland and was often employed in scouting, going north from Bennington, Vt. to watch the movement of the British, Indian
2 CONC s, and Tories; and also took his turn in garrisoning the rude fortifications at Rutland. After her husband's death in 1856, Mrs. Bixby lived with her son Warren and removed with him to North Adams, Massachusetts, where she died. J
2 CONC onathan Bixby was bound out 25 Sept. 1793 to Samuel Bullard of Barre to learn the "art & mystery of good Husbandry." He lived at Shrewsbury, Vt. and later at Wallingford. The 1850 census lists his occupation as a "Tailor" in Willi
2 CONC amtown, Ma., but he was also a farmer for a time. In March 1836, the family moved to Williamstown, Ma. to secure educational advantages for the children at Williams College. Both Jonathan and Submit are buried in East Lawn Cemeter
2 CONC y, Williamstown, Massachusetts. This next section is taken from Williamstown and Williams College by Perry - Page 535 "Williamstown has an interest in Re. N. E. Pierson because he married, "in 1844 the beautiful daughter of Jonath
2 CONC an Bixby, himself one of the subscribers of 1842. The Bixby's lived at that time on N.W. Hill, directly opposite the farm of Col Samuel Tyler, whose son Samuel's family moved down into Charityville about the same time that the Bix
2 CONC by's moved thither also. The two families thus became neighbors again in the northwestern part of the village." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouses:
2 CONT *Submit Kingsley Bixby (1790 - 1870)
2 CONT *Submit Kingsley (1790 - 1870)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Eastlawn Cemetery Williamstown Berkshire County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
