1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of Joseph Bennet (Bennett) (1731 –) and Sarah Morse (1733 – 1796). She married Enoch Burnham (1760 – 1802) on 11 Feb 1779 in Ipswitch, Essex, Massachusetts. They lived in the part of Ipswitch called Chebac
2 CONC co that latter became the town of Essex. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Moses Burnham 1780 – 1801 died at sea, Apr. or May ––, 1801, a. abt. 21 y. CR4.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Parker Burnham Capt 1781 – 1871 married Mary Polly Hardy 1786 – 1863. They are in Spring Street Cemetery which opened in 1852.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Bennet Burnham 1783 – 1796, Bennett, s. Enoch, drowned at Chebacco, Aug. 19, 1796. [in his 13th y. CR4]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Enoch Burnham 1791 – ?
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Elisha Burnham 1794 – 1827 died of consumption of liver, Mar 24 1827 at 33 y CR. Buried here
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Sally Bryant Burnham 1797 – 1877 married ISAAC ANNABLE 1798 – 1858. They are buried in Spring Cemetery (opened 1852).
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) Betsey Burnham 1800 – 1824 died of consumption CR, Oct 1, 1824 a 24 y [a 23 y. 10m CR]. Buried here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death records show that she was buried in the ancient cemetery on 28 Main St. However, no maker was recorded in the last survey so the monument has probably been destroyed or the family was to poort to afford on (with Enoch Burnha
2 CONC m having died in 1802).
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT     1761 12 Apr 
2 CONT     Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT     Hannah, d. Joseph, bp. Apr. 12, 1761. CR2 Ipswich - Births Image of page 37 http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Essex/Ipswich/aBirthsB.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism
2 CONT     1761 12 Apr 
2 CONT     Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Enoch Burnham 5
2 CONT     1779 11 Feb Age: 17
2 CONT     Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT     1829 27 Aug Age: 68
2 CONT     Essex, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT     Hannah wid Enoch Aug 27 1829 a 70 y CR note 1761 is the older bp and this closest to match this record
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT     Essex, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT     The old graveyard is located at 28 Main Street behind the Essex Shipbuilding Museum and dates back to 1680. http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~macessex/cemetery/NAMES.htm Find A Grave Memorial# 150258704 
