3 STAE NH
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 AUG 1888
2 PLAC Winchester, Cheshire County, New Hampshire, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} died aged 87y 11m 20ds; married; carpenter
2 CONT
2 CONT *son of David Morse (1745-1808) & Esther (Sager) Morse (1742-1805)
2 CONT
2 CONT *m. 1) Eliza Merriam Eliza d. 30 March 1824 ae 20y
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 2) Sybil Kingman 11 Nov 1824 at Winchester, N.H.
2 CONT
2 CONT children (at least): child b. 15 Jul 1826  Virgil K b. 03 May 1828  Sidney b. 27 Jan 1833 Lucien b. 1 Sept 1839 
2 CONT
2 CONT "John G Morse, born in Winchester in 1799, married Eliza Mariam, who bore him one daughter, Mrs J. A. Lasure. For his second wife he married Sybil Kingman, in 1824, who has borne him three sons Virgil K, Sydney M, and Lucian G. Mr
2 CONC  Morse and his wife now reside with their son Sydney, on road 51, aged respectively eighty-six and eighty-eight years." [Gazetteer of Cheshire County, N.H., 1736-1885. Syracuse, N.Y.:H. Child, 1885, town of Winchester page 550] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * from The history of Dublin, N.H.: containing the address by Charles Mason, and the proceedings at the centennial celebration, June 17, 1852, with a register of families. Dublin, N.H., by L.W. Leonard, published by The town, 1920
