0 @N6000000000929941262@ NOTE !In the 1520's, married Agnes Collyer. He (Richard) was granted his 
1 CONT estate ab out
1 CONT 1530 by henry VIII.  Richard wrote his will 3 Nov. 1579, proved Jan 13,
1 CONT  1580
1 CONT
1 CONT Will of Richard Whicker of Knowel in the Parish Colyton, Yoeman, names:
1 CONT
1 CONT To daughter Margaret, a cupboard or 40 pounds from Hercules, my son.
1 CONT To da ughter Peternell, a table board.
1 CONT The same to my son Walter.
1 CONT To daughter Susan , a crocke.
1 CONT To daughter Jane, a farme.
1 CONT To Agnes, wife, My house i now dwell i n, grounds called the strewse haye,
1 CONT two crofts, pyples, also a pece called Wes t Nylls, she to pay my
1 CONT daughters 5 pounds each.
1 CONT To son Richard, Trently Close , Trenty Meade and black acres at the new
1 CONT dyche
1 CONT beside Pucknige Garden.
1 CONT To son Walter, land called Playne Whyles also 12 acres upon Cawkesdown
1 CONT which
1 CONT I had of William Weston.
1 CONT To son John, land called Fyldes Woode, Knowle Mead.
1 CONT To  son Hercules, Knowle Hill.
1 CONT Son John to pay 16 pounds to my daughters.
1 CONT Son Ri chard to pay 16 pounds.
1 CONT Son Walter 8 pounds.
1 CONT To my sister Margaret Cappy (Cup py), to be heiress of all my childern who
1 CONT die.
1 CONT
1 CONT Residuary legatee & Exectour , Angus my wife.
1 CONT Overseers, brother Robert Whicker.
1 CONT Brother-in-law John Fayto n, brother-in-law John Cranyn and my cousin John
1 CONT Luttyn.
1 CONT
1 CONT Wit:  Tristram Gup py, John Tucker, parson of Southleigh, and Nicholas
1 CONT Beare.
