0 @N6000000006348351823@ NOTE NOTE: Capt. John Darling was son of Dennis (or Denice), born in Braintree, Sept. 2, 1664 and died at Bellingham May 29, 1753 in his 90th year. He was a great business man and landed proprietor. He headed the petition for setting o
1 CONC ff the town of Bellingham which was incorporated in 1719. He had land in Mendon as early as 1691. He had three wives (1) Elizabeth Thompson (2) Anne Rockwood and (3) Elizabeth Morse. By the latter he had eleven children, the young
1 CONC est of whom was Deborah, wife of Henry Bosworth.
1 CONT
