1 CONT minister of Scarborough ME 1728. Last will drawn up on January 13th,
1 CONT 1759.  Will was probated 10-1-1759.  Mentioned as his children William,
1 CONT Anna, and John.  He gave his son William a valuable tract of land at Oak
1 CONT Hill, and also assisted William with money to purchase another tract of
1 CONT land on Stroud Water River.  He also gave William a piece of Thatch land
1 CONT bought from Captain John Libby near Libby's river.. Also he gave William
1 CONT 1/2 of the ThatchLand bought from Jonathan Libby.  He also gave him half
1 CONT of his interest in the common & undivided lands in Scarboro., also his
1 CONT best yoke of oxen.
1 CONT He gave to John the other half of his rights in common lands of
1 CONT Scarboro..  He gaveJohn and Anna equal shares of his estate not disposed
1 CONT of..  He appointed, His wife Anna Executrix, son William an Executor, and
1 CONT also son John another Executor.
1 CONT He graduated Harvard College in 1718 and was an ordained minister of
1 CONT Scarborough, Maine in 1727.  Died at age 60.
1 CONT Pastor of First church in Scarborough.  He was greatly loved by
1 CONT townspeople of Scarborough, ME
