0 @N6000000002116357567@ NOTE Several IGI records show that Katherine was the daughter of Sir Andrew Brereton.  Sir Andrew had by his wife Agnes Legh, a daughter, Katherine, who married Sir Thomas Smith, b. abt. 1468.  Katherine appears to have had eight child
1 CONC ren by Sir Thomas starting in abt. 1516.  This really precludes her from being the same Catherine who married William Bowyer of Knypersley before 1495, by whom a daughter Anne Bowyer was b. not later than 1495 (and probably earlie
1 CONC r).  As William Bowyer lived on until 1541, there would need to have been a divorce from William Bowyer to enable Katherine to remarry Sir Thomas Smith.  Nevertheless several records link this Katherine into both marriages.  In lo
1 CONC oking for an alternative Katherine Brereton, born earlier, there is a record of a Katherine Brereton the daughter of Andrew Brereton and Anne Done (or Donne|.  The records indicate that this was the same Sir Andrew Brereton, who m
1 CONC arried first Anne Done and secondly Agnes Leigh.  While this seems plausible, except that it is unlikely that Sir Andrew would have had two surviving daughters named Katherine, Anne Done, indisputably married Sir Andrew's younger 
1 CONC brother, Hugh Brereton, although there is no record of children.  If Hugh Brereton died young then it is possible (but again quite unlikely) that Sir Andrew would have married his younger brother's widow, before a marriage to Agne
1 CONC s Legh.   Sir Andrew married Agnes Legh when he was about 27, making it less likely that he married Anne Done beforehand.  There is yet another record that shows that Sir Andrew married Agnes Leigh in 1475 and married Anne Done in
1 CONC  1490.  This seems much more likely, although there is no record of a marriage between Sir Andrew and Anne Done in the published family trees.  Yet if this is the case Sir Andrew could not be the father of Anne Done's daughter Kat
1 CONC herine, and none of the genealogical tables show it.  On the balance of probabilities, it is assumed that the Katherine, who married William Bowyer is the daughter of Hugh Brereton and Anne Done, and perhaps the step-daughter of S
1 CONC ir Andrew Brereton, but there is no record to verify this.
