1 CONT Court prove by the Oaths of Two Sufficien t Evidences upon the holy
1 CONT Evangelists
1 CONT of Almighty God that they had each of them respectively lawful and
1 CONT authentick
1 CONT Indentures for four years time as af oresaid, therefore tis ordered that
1 CONT the
1 CONT said Thomas Whickers and George Spil lers (sic) of and from Richard Aylisse
1 CONT their master shall be free and that the  said Richard Aylisse shall pay
1 CONT each of
1 CONT them their corn and clothes with all  country dues respectively with all
1 CONT loss at
1 CONT Execution."
1 CONT
1 CONT About 1690, Thoma s married a second time, but her name is not found.  She
1 CONT died Before 1704.  It  appears Thomas sent Benjamin to England before 1704
1 CONT when
1 CONT he wrote his will in Westmoreland County.
1 CONT Thomas Wicker was one of five witness to the will of J ohn Scott of
1 CONT Westmoreland County 20 May 1700.  A Codicil was proved by Charles 
1 CONT Tankersley
1 CONT and Thomas Whickers on November 26, 1701.
1 CONT There dose not seem t o be any relationship, but among the Provisions of
1 CONT this will was one that Scot t's son John, when age 8 or 9 years, was to be
1 CONT sent
1 CONT to England to his uncle Gustavus to be educated.  It may be that Benjamin
1 CONT Wicker was sent to England a t the same time.
1 CONT
1 CONT Will of Thomas Whicker, dated 4 April 1704, Westmoreland Co unty, Virginia
1 CONT proved 26 July 1704. Reads:
1 CONT
1 CONT In the name of God Amen!  I, Tho mas Wicker of Appamattox in Westmoreland
1 CONT County,
